const e={P2000:["NOx Adsorber Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","A NOx adsorber (lean NOx trap) collects nitrogen oxides while a lean-running engine produces them and turns them into nitrogen during short rich purges. P2000 reports that the trap on bank 1 no longer stores or converts enough NOx; CARB wants this flagged before tailpipe NOx passes a fixed multiple of the standard.",["Sooted or drifting oxygen sensors that misjudge trap loading and purges","NOx trap poisoned by sulphur or aged by heat","Engine software that sets the code without a real fault (update available on some models)","Rich purges or desulphation not completed, e.g. because of short trips"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often accompanied by oxygen sensor codes P2A00/P2A01","No noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2001","P2A00","P2A01"],""],P2001:["NOx Adsorber Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","P2001 belongs to the second cylinder bank: the NOx storage catalyst fed by bank 2 has lost so much capacity that it no longer holds and reduces the nitrogen oxides of lean running. The code is only possible on V or boxer engines that give each bank its own trap. No manufacturer documents P2001 publicly;",["Bank 2 NOx trap poisoned by sulphur or thermally aged","Oxygen or NOx sensor on bank 2 reading wrongly","Rich purges on bank 2 repeatedly interrupted"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Driveability usually unchanged"],2,1,["P2000","P2A03"],""],P2002:["Diesel Particulate Filter Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","P2002 means the particulate filter on bank 1 lets too much soot through, typically because the substrate is cracked, partly melted, emptied or bypassed. CARB requires diesel OBD to flag a filter whose filtering performance lets PM emissions exceed the limit.",["Filter substrate cracked or melted, often after an uncontrolled regeneration","Filter removed, emptied or bypassed","Faulty differential pressure sensor or leaking sensor hoses on pressure-based systems"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Usually no change in driveability","Visible soot at the tailpipe in severe cases"],3,1,["P2003","P2463","P2453","P24AF"],""],P2003:["Diesel Particulate Filter Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","P2003 is set when the particulate filter of bank 2 lets too much soot slip through, which almost always points to a cracked, partly melted, hollowed-out or bypassed core. Separate filters per bank are uncommon, so the code is rare. No manufacturer documents P2003 publicly;",["Bank 2 filter core cracked or melted after an overheated regeneration","Filter on bank 2 removed, emptied or bypassed","PM sensor or differential pressure measurement on bank 2 giving false values"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Visible soot at the tailpipe with a large leak","Engine performance normally unaffected"],3,1,["P2002","P2465","P24AF"],""],P2004:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Open (Bank 1)","Intake manifold runner control (IMRC) uses flaps in the intake manifold; petrol engines switch runner length or tumble, diesels close swirl flaps at low load. P2004 means the flaps on bank 1 stay open when the ECM has commanded them closed, judged from the position feedback. Ford checks commanded against actual plate position after coolant exceeds 40 °F (about 4 °C) and needs four events to set the stuck code;",["Flap shaft sticking, worn or separated inside the manifold","Runner control valve contaminated or corroded","Vacuum hose or actuator diaphragm leaking"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Weaker low-speed torque"],2,1,["P2005","P2006","P2008","P2014","P2015"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2005:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Open (Bank 2)","P2005 is the bank 2 version of the stuck-open check, so it only exists on V and boxer engines with a flap set per cylinder bank. The ECM has commanded the flaps on bank 2 closed, but the position feedback says they stayed open. Ford runs it on vacuum-operated V engines once coolant is above 40 °F and logs it after four failed events;",["Cracked or loose vacuum hose to the bank 2 flap actuator","Moisture in the flap potentiometer giving a false position (Audi 4.0 TFSI)","Flap shaft corroded or seized in the open position","Torn diaphragm in the vacuum actuator"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Less pulling power at low engine speed","Rpm limit on some Audi V8 engines"],2,3,["P2004","P2007","P2011","P2020","P200B"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2006:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Closed (Bank 1)","P2006 means the intake manifold runner or swirl flaps on bank 1 stay closed when the ECM has commanded them open. Closed flaps choke the engine at higher load, so this is the case that costs power.",["Flaps or shafts seized by deposits or wear","Runner control valve stuck from contamination","Electric actuator or its linkage failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Loss of power at higher rpm","Limp mode on some diesels"],2,3,["P2004","P2007","P2008","P2015","P20F8"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 1)"],P2007:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Closed (Bank 2)","P2007 reports that the runner or tumble flaps of bank 2 have not opened although the ECM asked for it. Because closed flaps narrow the intake path, the fault shows up mainly as missing power near the top of the rev range. On the 2013 Audi 3.0 TFSI (A6, A7, S4, S5, Q5, Q7) a torn diaphragm in one vacuum actuator caused P2006 or P2007;",["Torn diaphragm in the bank 2 vacuum actuator","Flap shaft seized by corrosion or deposits","Grease leaking from an integrated tumble valve actuator (Subaru Impreza/Crosstrek)","Vacuum supply or control valve not working"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slight loss of power at high rpm"],2,3,["P2005","P2006","P2011","P2020","P200B"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 2)"],P2008:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1)","P2008 is the general circuit and open-circuit code for whatever drives the bank 1 flaps: a vacuum solenoid, a motor or a smart swirl actuator. GM's 2018 diesels with a feedback swirl actuator set it when the output stage sees more than 200 kΩ load in 12 of 15 samples (Type B, two trips), with the relay supply above 11 V;",["Spread or corroded terminal in the actuator or valve connector","Broken control or supply wire to the bank 1 actuator","Open winding in the solenoid valve or actuator motor","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Flaps stay in their rest position, less low-end torque or top-end power"],2,1,["P2009","P2010","P2011","P200A","P2016","P2017"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2009:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P2009 narrows the bank 1 flap control fault down to a low signal, which in practice means the control line has found a path to ground. GM's 2018 diesel tables flag a resistance to ground below 0.5 Ω in 12 of 15 checks every 100 ms (Type B), and the 2014 Cruze diesel waits until the short has lasted more than 3 s.",["Control wire chafed through and touching ground","Internal short in the solenoid or actuator motor","Leaking integrated tumble valve actuator (Subaru Impreza/Crosstrek)","Water or corrosion in the actuator connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Flaps cannot be switched, uneven running at low speed"],2,1,["P2008","P2010","P2012","P200A"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P200A:["Intake Manifold Runner Performance (Bank 1)","P200A is the functional check of the bank 1 flaps: the circuit is fine, but the flaps do not reach or report the expected positions. GM's 2018 diesels learn both end stops at key-off and fail if the closed stop lies outside 81–92 percent or the raw signal outside 25–40 percent of 5 V, or if a stroke takes over 5 s (coolant at least 60 °C, Type B).",["Flap actuator worn, slow or failed","Broken or sticking linkage or flap inside the manifold","Weak battery disturbing the actuator relearn (Kia V6)","Control software that needs an update (FCA 3.0 diesel)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Weaker response at low or high engine speed"],2,1,["P200B","P2004","P2006","P2008","P2015","P201D"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P200B:["Intake Manifold Runner Performance (Bank 2)","P200B judges whether the flaps of bank 2 move as commanded and settle where they should; it needs a V engine whose second bank has its own flap set or position feedback. The clearest public user is FCA's 3.0 V6 EcoDiesel: bulletins for the Jeep Grand Cherokee and Ram 1500 from 2014 onward, and 18-002-23 for the 2020 Ram 1500 with the third-generation engine, list P200A and P200B together and cure them by…",["Engine software with an available update (FCA 3.0 EcoDiesel)","Bank 2 actuator slow or failed","Flaps on bank 2 sticking from soot or carbon"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often no noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P200A","P2005","P2007","P2011","P201E","P2D2E"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P200C:["Particulate Filter Over Temperature (Bank 1)","P200C reports that the exhaust at the bank 1 particulate filter has become hotter than the filter may tolerate, typically when a heavily loaded filter burns off during regeneration. GM's diesel tables set it as Type A, MIL on the first trip: the 2018 group uses more than 850 °C in regeneration and 800 °C otherwise ahead of the filter (30 of 40 samples), the 2020 table 900 °C behind it, the 2025 table 800 °C from 300…",["Excess soot load burning off too fast during regeneration","Too much fuel reaching the exhaust (leaking injector, post injection, exhaust brake or injector problems)","Leaking charge-air ducting upsetting combustion and soot model","Faulty exhaust temperature sensor near the filter"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration aborted or blocked","Possible power reduction to protect the exhaust system"],3,3,["P200D","P200E","P2002","P2463","P2428"],"מסנן חלקיקים — חום יתר (בנק 1)"],P200D:["Particulate Filter Over Temperature (Bank 2)","P200D is the overheating code for a particulate filter on bank 2 and therefore only appears where the exhaust of the second bank has its own filter and temperature sensors. No manufacturer documents P200D publicly; the published diesel layouts of GM, Ford and Hino run one filter and report its overheating as P200C.",["Bank 2 filter overloaded with soot before regeneration","Leaking injector or excess fuel on bank 2 cylinders","Exhaust temperature sensor on bank 2 reading too high"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration stopped","Power may be limited"],3,3,["P200C","P200F","P2003","P2429"],"מסנן חלקיקים — חום יתר (בנק 2)"],P200E:["Catalyst System Over Temperature (Bank 1)","P200E means the catalyst on bank 1 has run hotter than its design limit. On diesels this is the oxidation catalyst ahead of the particulate filter. GM reads the sensor behind the close-coupled DOC and stores a Type A code above 850 °C in its 2020 table and above 800 °C in 2025, each confirmed over hundreds of samples.",["Unburnt fuel reaching the catalyst (leaking injector, post injection, misfire)","Parked regeneration with high soot load running too hot","Charge-air duct loose or leaking","Exhaust temperature sensor behind the catalyst faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration interrupted, possibly with reduced power","Hot smell or heat from the exhaust area"],3,3,["P200F","P200C","P2428","P2080"],"מערכת ממיר קטליטי — חום יתר (בנק 1)"],P200F:["Catalyst System Over Temperature (Bank 2)","P200F flags excessive temperature in the catalyst of bank 2, so it needs an engine whose second bank feeds its own catalyst with its own temperature sensor. No manufacturer documents P200F publicly; GM and Ford describe only the bank 1 code P200E for their single-path diesels, with limits around 800 to 850 °C behind the oxidation catalyst or a link to a stationary regeneration that runs hot.",["Fuel slipping into the bank 2 exhaust (dribbling injector, misfire)","Bank 2 exhaust temperature sensor reading too high","Regeneration overheating on bank 2"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Possible power reduction"],3,3,["P200E","P200D","P2429","P2082"],"מערכת ממיר קטליטי — חום יתר (בנק 2)"],P2010:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit High (Bank 1)","P2010 is the high-side counterpart of P2009 for the bank 1 flap drive: the control line carries voltage it should not, typically because it touches a supply wire or the actuator is shorted internally. GM's 2018 diesels judge a resistance to supply under 0.5 Ω, again 12 of 15 checks and Type B. The 2014 Cruze diesel looks at the line while the driver is switched on and needs the short for more than 3 s.",["Control wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Shorted winding in the solenoid or actuator motor","Output stage in the engine control module failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Flaps stuck in one position, change in low-speed torque"],2,1,["P2008","P2009","P2013","P200A"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2011:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","P2011 covers the electrical drive of the bank 2 flaps, so it appears only on engines with a separate actuator or solenoid per bank. Ford's petrol summaries list P2011 as the IMRC control circuit of bank 2 on vacuum-operated V engines; the PCM output driver itself reports the fault, the check runs continuously after coolant passes 40 °F and needs 5 s with at least 11 V battery voltage.",["Open wire or loose connector at the bank 2 solenoid","Open coil in the bank 2 control solenoid","Vacuum-driven coolant pump drawing too much vacuum (Audi 3.0 TFSI)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bank 2 flaps do not switch, slight loss of torque or power"],2,1,["P2012","P2013","P2008","P2005","P2007"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2012:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2012 means the ECM reads the control circuit of the bank 2 flap actuator too low, usually a short to ground in the wire or inside the actuator. Subaru is the one maker that names it publicly: on the 2017–2020 Impreza and 2018–2020 Crosstrek, including the plug-in hybrid, lubricant from the tumble generator valve actuator could leak and be drawn into the engine, after which the valve works erratically and P2009 or…",["Integrated tumble valve actuator leaking lubricant (Subaru Impreza/Crosstrek)","Bank 2 control wire shorted to ground","Corroded actuator connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Erratic idle or hesitation on light throttle"],3,1,["P2011","P2013","P2009","P2007"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2013:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","P2013 points to a control line of the bank 2 flap actuator that sits too high, i.e. a short to battery voltage or an actuator whose winding has shorted so the driver sees supply where it expects a load. No manufacturer documents P2013 publicly.",["Bank 2 control wire shorted to a supply wire","Shorted winding in the bank 2 actuator","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bank 2 flaps no longer switch"],2,1,["P2011","P2012","P2010"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2014:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit (Bank 1)","P2014 is the general electrical code for the flap position feedback on bank 1, used when the control unit sees a broken or shorted circuit without, or before, splitting it into low and high. Ford's 2012 summary calls it the IMRC input switch check: with coolant warmer than 40 °F it is checked all the time, and an open or shorted switch must persist for 5 s;",["Runner position sensor (VW G336) failed internally","Sensor wiring broken or shorted","Manifold with integrated flap shaft and sensor damaged (VW 2.0T 2008–2011)","Corroded or loose sensor connector"],["Check engine lamp on","Slightly weaker pull or rougher idle while the flaps are parked"],2,1,["P2015","P2016","P2017","P2018","P2019"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2015:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1)","P2015 means the position feedback of the intake manifold runner or swirl flaps on bank 1 is electrically present but implausible. How it is judged depends on the design. Diesels with a smart swirl actuator send position as a pulse-width signal: GM's 2018 diesels fail a pulse period below 0 or above 64 ms in 52 of 62 samples (Type B), and on the Opel/GM 2.0 CDTi in the Saab 9-5 (2010) the ECM flags a wrong frequency…",["Flap linkage sticking or flap separated inside the manifold","Corroded or faulty flap control valve","Actuator electronics or position sensor faulty","Flap adaptation not performed after repair"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough idle or weaker low-speed torque"],2,1,["P2014","P2016","P2017","P2004","P2020"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2016:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 1)","P2016 says the bank 1 flap position signal sits at the bottom of its range, typically a shorted signal wire or a lost 5 V supply. Ford sets it below 0.24 V after 5 s; the 2014 Touareg 3.0 TDI (CNRB) below 0.15 V.",["Signal wire chafed and grounded","5 V or actuator supply missing (spread terminal, blown fuse)","Position sensor or smart actuator electronics faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Less torque at low revs or flat spot when the runner should switch"],2,1,["P2014","P2015","P2017","P2021","P2008"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2017:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 1)","P2017 is the mirror case of P2016: the bank 1 flap feedback is stuck near the supply rail. With a pulled-up input that happens when the signal or sensor ground opens, or when the signal wire touches a voltage source. Ford's limit is 4.7 V for 5 s, Volkswagen uses 4.85 V on the 3.0 TDI and 4.88 V on the 3.0 TSI hybrid of the 2014 Touareg.",["Open sensor ground or signal circuit","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Spread or corroded terminal in the valve or sensor plug","Position sensor or actuator electronics faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Flaps parked in default position, slightly changed running at part load"],2,1,["P2014","P2015","P2016","P2022","P2008"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2018:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1)","P2018 belongs to bank 1 and covers a flap position signal that drops out or jumps for short moments while it otherwise stays within limits, so neither the low nor the high code matures. Few makers publish it. Mitsubishi lists P2018 for the 2022 and 2023 Outlander with the 2.5 litre PR25DD engine as a bank 1 fault of the sensor that reports where the runner valve stands, logged after two trips with the warning lamp;",["Loose or fretted pins in the sensor connector","Wire cracked by engine movement or heat near the manifold","Worn resistive track in the position sensor"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Often no noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P2014","P2016","P2017","P2023"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2019:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit (Bank 2)","P2019 is the bank 2 counterpart of P2014 and only appears on V or boxer engines with separate flap feedback per cylinder row. It reports an electrical fault in the position circuit without stating its direction. Volkswagen's Touareg hybrid of 2014 (CGFA) stores it once the bank 2 signal drops under 0.2 V.",["Bank 2 sensor wiring open or shorted","Bank 2 position sensor failed","Shared 5 V reference or ground faulty (both banks affected)"],["Check engine lamp on","Mild loss of low-speed torque if the control unit parks the flaps"],2,1,["P2014","P2020","P2021","P2022","P2023"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P201A:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Unit 1)","Engines with two SCR paths give each a DEF dosing valve. P201A concerns the first valve on bank 2: the circuit is not open or shorted, but what the control unit sees while dosing does not fit the command. No manufacturer documents P201A publicly; the pickup and truck SCR systems in the public record use one valve and report this fault as P202E.",["Bank 2 dosing valve sticking from urea crystals or deposits","Corroded connector or harness adding resistance to the valve circuit","DEF pressure at the valve outside the expected range"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF system warning, possibly countdown to speed limitation"],2,3,["P202E","P2050","P208F","P205F"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P201B:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Supply Voltage Low (Bank 1)","P201B does not concern the control signal but the power feed of an electric flap actuator on bank 1. GM's 2025 diesel tables describe it for a swirl valve driven by a DC motor: if the supply seen by the driver falls below 6 V while the powertrain relay itself delivers more than 11 V, and this holds in 240 of 300 samples taken every 12.5 ms, a Type B fault is stored.",["Chafed engine harness shorting or interrupting the actuator feed","Blown fuse in the actuator supply","High resistance at the supply pin of the actuator connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Swirl flaps no longer move, often with other electrical codes"],2,1,["P201C","P201D","P2008","P2009","P2010"],"אספקת מפעיל בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — מתח נמוך (בנק 1)"],P201C:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Supply Voltage Low (Bank 2)","P201C reports that the electric flap actuator of bank 2 is not getting enough supply voltage. It only makes sense on V engines that give each bank its own powered actuator. No manufacturer documents P201C publicly. The bank 1 counterpart P201B is described by GM for its DC-motor swirl drive: the driver supply below 6 V while the relay feed is above 11 V, in 240 of 300 samples, Type B.",["Fuse or relay feeding the bank 2 actuator failed","Damaged supply wire or connector at the bank 2 actuator","Actuator electronics loading the supply down"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bank 2 flaps stop working"],2,1,["P201B","P201E","P2011","P200B"],"אספקת מפעיל בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — מתח נמוך (בנק 2)"],P201D:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Internal Performance (Bank 1)","P201D is for flap actuators with their own electronics: the bank 1 actuator, or the ECM's check of it, has found a fault inside the unit, such as a failed driver, sensor or self-test, while wiring and supply look normal. GM uses the code on its 2017 and 2018 diesels with a smart swirl actuator, but only as a member of the fault group that orders swirl control off, next to P2008–P2010, P201B, P2004 and P2006;",["Internal electronics of the smart actuator failed","Actuator overloaded by sticking flaps, internal protection tripped","Actuator or engine software fault"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Swirl control switched off, slightly rougher combustion at low load"],3,1,["P201E","P201B","P200A","P2008","P2015"],"פנימי מפעיל בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P201E:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Internal Performance (Bank 2)","P201E says the electronic flap actuator serving bank 2 has detected or caused an internal malfunction; the wires to it are not the issue. No manufacturer documents P201E publicly, and only engines with a separate smart actuator per bank can set it.",["Electronics inside the bank 2 actuator failed","Bank 2 flaps binding and overloading the actuator","Moisture inside the actuator housing"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Little or no change in drivability"],3,1,["P201D","P201C","P200B","P2011"],"פנימי מפעיל בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P201F:["Reductant Pump A Stuck On","P201F says reductant pump A keeps running or keeps building pressure although the control unit has switched it off, for example when dosing pauses or after the line has been purged at shutdown. No manufacturer documents P201F publicly.",["Pump relay contacts welded or driver stage stuck on","Pump control wire shorted to supply voltage","Internal fault in the pump or dosing control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Pump audible after switching off the engine","Battery discharged after standing"],2,3,["P208A","P208B","P208D","P20E9"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2020:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","P2020 flags a bank 2 position signal that is electrically sound but does not fit what the flaps should be doing. On the CGFA hybrid V6 of the 2014 Touareg, Volkswagen triggers it when commanded and measured flap position are more than 40 % apart or the reported value leaves the 0–100 % window.",["Bank 2 flap shaft sticking or carbon-fouled","Broken lever or linkage between actuator and shaft","Weak vacuum or leaking actuator diaphragm (vacuum systems)","Sensor shifted or adaptation missing after repair"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced pull in the mid range or uneven idle"],3,1,["P2015","P2019","P2005","P2007","P2011"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2021:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2021 is the low-signal code for the bank 2 runner position sensor. Ford documents it for vacuum-operated runner control on its V engines in the 2020–2023 summary: the position input below 0.24 V for 5 s, monitored continuously once coolant exceeds 40 °F. In the 2024 edition the same fault is shown as P2019 with failure byte 11.",["Bank 2 signal wire grounded","5 V reference to the bank 2 sensor open","Bank 2 position sensor internally shorted"],["Check engine lamp on","Slight loss of low-end torque"],2,1,["P2016","P2019","P2022","P2011"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2022:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 2)","P2022 sets when the bank 2 flap position input reads close to the supply voltage. Ford's limit is above 4.7 V for 5 s on its V engines with vacuum-operated runners (shown from 2024 as P2019 with failure byte 15); for the Touareg hybrid engine CGFA (2014) Volkswagen gives more than 4.88 V.",["Bank 2 sensor ground or signal open","Signal wire touching a 5 V or battery feed","Bank 2 position sensor open internally"],["Check engine lamp on","Little or no change in drivability"],2,1,["P2017","P2019","P2021","P2023"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2023:["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","P2023 is meant for a bank 2 flap position signal that briefly drops out or jumps without staying out of range long enough for P2021 or P2022. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; Ford's V-engine summaries stop at low, high and over-travel for bank 2, and Volkswagen's Touareg tables skip it.",["Bank 2 sensor plug with loose or corroded contacts","Harness rubbing through near exhaust or valve cover","Worn bank 2 position sensor giving dropouts"],["Warning lamp appears now and then","Usually no change in how the engine drives"],2,1,["P2018","P2019","P2021","P2022"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2024:["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit","The fuel vapor temperature sensor tells the ECM how warm the vapor in the tank and canister is, which matters for leak tests that judge pressure or vacuum as the fuel cools after shutdown. P2024 is the unspecified electrical code for that circuit. On recent Audi models the sensor is built into the leak detection unit J909 at the charcoal canister.",["Open or shorted wiring to the temperature sensor or leak detection unit","Misassigned fault entry in the ECM software (Audi 2022–2025)","Leak detection unit with integrated sensor faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","EVAP readiness not set, possible inspection failure"],2,1,["P2025","P2026","P2027","P2028","P0450"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אדי דלק אדי דלק (EVAP) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2025:["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Performance","P2025 means the vapor temperature reading is electrically valid but does not make sense against other inputs or over time. Audi documents a real-world cause on 2016–2018 A6 and A7 with the 3.0 litre engine: water gets into the tank ventilation path, runs past the leak detection pressure switch (NVLD) into the canister and turns to ice in cold weather.",["Water or ice in canister and NVLD switch (Audi A6/A7 3.0)","ECM software setting the code falsely (VW Jetta/Taos 2022)","Temperature sensor drifted or slow to respond"],["Check engine lamp on","Fuel nozzle shuts off repeatedly when filling the tank","EVAP readiness incomplete"],2,1,["P2024","P2026","P2027","P0441","P0451","P0453"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אדי דלק אדי דלק (EVAP) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2026:["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Voltage","P2026 reports a vapor temperature signal stuck near 0 V. With the usual NTC thermistor and pull-up resistor, a low voltage corresponds to an extremely hot reading, so the code nearly always points to a signal wire touching ground or a shorted sensor rather than real heat.",["Sensor signal wire shorted to ground","Temperature sensor or leak detection unit shorted internally","Moisture bridging pins at the canister-mounted connector"],["Check engine lamp on","Implausibly high vapor temperature in live data"],2,1,["P2024","P2025","P2027","P2028"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אדי דלק אדי דלק (EVAP) — מתח נמוך במעגל"],P2027:["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit High Voltage","P2027 is the high-voltage counterpart of P2026: the signal sits near the reference, which an NTC sensor would only produce at a temperature far below anything plausible. In practice the sensor circuit is open – a broken wire, an unplugged connector, a corroded pin – or the signal line is shorted to a voltage source.",["Open circuit – broken wire or unplugged connector","Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Temperature sensor open internally"],["Check engine lamp on","Vapor temperature shown far below ambient"],2,1,["P2024","P2025","P2026","P2028"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אדי דלק אדי דלק (EVAP) — מתח גבוה במעגל"],P2028:["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent","P2028 covers a vapor temperature signal that jumps or briefly drops out instead of changing smoothly, as vapor temperature normally does. Public manufacturer documentation for it is lacking: Ford's 2014 list ends with P2027, and the Audi bulletins concern P2024–P2026 only.",["Corroded or loose connector at the canister area","Wire chafing against body or tank straps","Moisture inside the leak detection unit with integrated sensor"],["Warning lamp that switches on and off","EVAP readiness slow to complete"],2,1,["P2024","P2026","P2027"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אדי דלק אדי דלק (EVAP) — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2029:["Fuel Fired Heater Disabled","A fuel fired heater burns a small amount of the vehicle's fuel to warm coolant or cabin air, a common add-on on diesels with little waste heat. P2029 is a state code: the controller has taken the heater out of service, usually after repeated failed starts, flame-outs, overheating or an electrical fault.",["Lock-out after repeated failed starts or flame-outs (fuel supply, glow plug, combustion air)","Heater shut down after overheating, e.g. low coolant flow","Supply voltage too low or wiring fault to the heater"],["Little or no auxiliary heat, slow warm-up","Heater does not start when requested","Warning lamp depends on the manufacturer"],2,0,["P2030"],""],P202A:["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit/Open","DEF freezes at about −11 °C, so the tank carries an electric, often PTC-type heater that thaws enough fluid for dosing after a cold start. P202A covers the control circuit of that heater with the emphasis on an open circuit: when commanded on, practically no current flows.",["Tank heater element burnt through","Loose or burnt connector at the tank, or blown heater fuse","Interrupted wire between control unit and tank"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","In frost, DEF system warning and inducement countdown"],2,3,["P202B","P202C","P209F","P205B"],"גוף חימום מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P202B:["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit Low","P202B belongs to the electric heater in the DEF tank and reports a low reading in its control circuit. Generically that means a signal sitting too low, for example a grounded wire or a drive output pulled down. Volkswagen gives a concrete test on the 2014 Touareg 3.0 TDI: right at the start of heating the element's conductance must reach a minimum, and a value under 0.30 S, i.e. more than about 3.3 Ω, sets P202B.",["Corroded heater connector pins adding resistance","Heater element partly damaged, resistance too high","Control wire chafed through to ground"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF stays frozen longer after cold starts"],2,3,["P202A","P202C","P209F"],"גוף חימום מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P202C:["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit High","P202C is the high-side fault of the DEF tank heater circuit: the module sees a value above the allowed range, as when the wire touches battery positive or an element that conducts far too well. On the Touareg 3.0 TDI of model year 2014, Volkswagen flags it when the element's conductance at the start of heating exceeds 0.62 S, below roughly 1.6 Ω, which hints at an internal short.",["DEF control unit calibration (software update on some models)","Heater element with internal short, resistance too low","Heater control wire shorted to battery voltage"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Service DEF message, later speed limited","Heater fuse may blow"],2,3,["P202A","P202B","P209F","P20BC"],"גוף חימום מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P202D:["Reductant Leakage","P202D reports that DEF is escaping somewhere between pump and dosing valve, which the controller typically notices as a pressure that cannot be held. Volvo and Mack use it on their 2014 and later trucks (OBD13 onwards). A 2015 tech tip handles it together with P208E and P20E8 and names poor electrical contact, which makes the pressure reading look low, and contamination that really lowers it.",["Dosing valve weeping or crusted with crystals","Leaking DEF line, fitting or seal","Poor electrical contact faking a pressure loss","Contaminated DEF lowering system pressure"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","White crystalline deposits on DEF lines or dosing valve","Higher DEF consumption, later inducement warnings"],2,3,["P208E","P20E8","P204F"],""],P202E:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Unit 1)","P202E concerns the first DEF dosing valve on bank 1, which in most SCR systems is the only one. The circuit itself is intact, but the valve does not behave as commanded. GM's 6.6 L LML (2014 table) checks what the valve driver was told to do against the actual state of its circuit and sets a Type A code after more than ten mismatches within 80 injections, checked only with the coil between about −7 and 100 °C.",["Dosing valve sticking from urea crystals or a clogged tip","Dosing or engine control unit software (updates available on some models)","Corroded valve connector or harness","DEF pressure at the valve outside the expected range"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF system warning, possibly countdown to speed limitation","Possibly additional SCR efficiency codes"],2,3,["P201A","P2047","P208E","P204F","P20EE"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P202F:["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit Range/Performance","P202F covers the commanded supply stage that feeds the reductant system or, in some layouts, the regeneration hardware, typically a supply pump or its power feed. The circuit is electrically present, but its behaviour does not match the command, for instance current or voltage that drifts outside the window expected for the requested state.",["Weak relay or fuse contact in the supply feed","Supply pump drawing excessive current (wear, blockage)","Fault in the dosing or pump control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF system warning, dosing reduced or stopped"],2,3,["P208A","P208B","P21CB","P20EA"],""],P2030:["Fuel Fired Heater Performance","P2030 is the functional check of a fuel fired heater: it is wired and commanded, but does not ignite, keep its flame or deliver the heat expected. Hino uses the code on 2011–2014 conventional trucks with the J08 engine, where a burner heats the exhaust for particulate filter regeneration. Its burner control unit confirms ignition through a flame temperature sensor and logs P2030 as burner misfire;",["Fuel starvation at the heater (dosing pump, filter, line)","Worn glow pin or contaminated flame sensor","Combustion air inlet or exhaust of the heater blocked, sooted chamber","Control unit software misjudging the flame (update on some models)"],["Heater fails to start or goes out","White smoke or fuel smell from the heater exhaust","Burner-assisted filter regeneration does not complete"],2,1,["P2029"],""],P2031:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","Exhaust gas temperature sensor 2 on bank 1 usually sits between the oxidation catalyst and the particulate filter, where the ECM uses it to control regeneration temperature. Under the generic circuit title, manufacturers set P2031 for different faults.",["Sensor failed or reading off from the model","Water or corrosion in the sensor or harness connector","Wiring open or shorted near the hot exhaust"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DPF regeneration inhibited"],2,1,["P2032","P2033","P2084","P0544","P2034"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2032:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P2032 means the signal of exhaust gas temperature sensor 2 on bank 1 is below its valid range. What that means electrically depends on the sensor type. On the Opel/GM 2.0 CDTi in the Saab 9-5 (2010) sensor 2 sits in the particulate filter and its voltage falls as it gets hotter, so a reading below 0.4 V for more than 1 s points to a short to ground; the code is Type A there.",["Signal wire chafed to ground on the exhaust","Internal sensor failure","Damaged or corroded connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DPF regeneration inhibited, soot load rises"],2,1,["P2031","P2033","P2035","P0545"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2033:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P2033 means the signal of exhaust gas temperature sensor 2 on bank 1 is above its valid range. On the Opel/GM 2.0 CDTi in the Saab 9-5 (2010) the sensor in the particulate filter reads high voltage when cold, so more than 1.6 V for over 1 s means an open circuit, an unplugged connector or a short to voltage; it is Type A.",["Sensor element open after heat cycling","Connector unplugged, loose or corroded","Signal wire shorted to voltage"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DPF regeneration inhibited, soot load rises"],2,1,["P2031","P2032","P2036","P0546"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2034:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P2034 is the general electrical fault of the second exhaust temperature sensor on bank 2, so it only appears where the second bank has its own measuring point downstream. GM does not use it: the 2018 diesel tables number every exhaust temperature sensor on bank 1 (P0545/P0546, P2032/P2033, P242C/P242D, P2470/P2471), as one aftertreatment line serves the whole engine.",["Sensor lead open or shorted where it runs along the hot exhaust","Sensing element failed after many heat cycles","Water or corrosion in the sensor connector","Sensor ground or supply from the control unit faulty"],["Engine warning lamp on","DEF dosing or particulate filter regeneration restricted","Engine power reduced on some applications"],2,3,["P2035","P2036","P2086","P2087","P2031"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2035:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P2035 reports that the signal of temperature sensor 2 on bank 2 has dropped below its plausible floor. Whether that is a short or an open depends on the sensor curve: with a thermistor pulled up by the control unit a grounded wire drags the voltage down, whereas some circuits read near zero when the loop is broken. No manufacturer documents P2035 publicly.",["Signal wire chafed through to ground on the exhaust or frame","Internal short in the sensing element","Water bridging the connector pins"],["Engine warning lamp on","Temperature reading on bank 2 implausibly low or at the limit","Regeneration or DEF dosing limited"],2,1,["P2034","P2036","P2032","P0548"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2036:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P2036 is set when the bank 2, sensor 2 temperature signal climbs above the top of its valid window. On the usual pull-up input that is what an unplugged connector, a broken lead or an element gone open after heat cycling produces, while a short to supply voltage gives the same picture. No manufacturer documents P2036 publicly;",["Sensing element open after repeated heat cycles","Connector unplugged, loose or with pushed-back terminal","Sensor lead broken near the hot exhaust","Signal wire shorted to supply voltage"],["Engine warning lamp on","Bank 2 temperature shows an implausibly high value","Possible protective power reduction"],2,3,["P2034","P2035","P2033","P0549"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2037:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit","Some heavy-duty SCR systems do not spray DEF on their own pressure alone but blow it into the exhaust with compressed air, supplied by a compressor or an existing air system; Bosch's first Denoxtronic generation was built this way. A pressure sensor checks that this air is present before dosing. P2037 is the general circuit fault of that sensor.",["5 V supply or ground of the sensor interrupted or shorted","Damaged harness or corroded connector at the dosing module","Air pressure sensor failed internally"],["Engine or emission warning lamp on","DEF dosing suspended","Engine power derate on trucks and machines"],2,3,["P2038","P2039","P2040","P2041","P209A","P2059"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2038:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2038 does not mean a broken wire. The air pressure sensor A of an air-assisted DEF injector delivers a valid voltage, yet the value does not fit the operating state: it may show pressure while the air supply valve is closed, too little pressure while it is open, or fail to move when air is switched on and off. No manufacturer documents P2038 publicly.",["Leaking or kinked air line between valve and dosing unit","Sensor reading drifted or clogged pressure port","Air supply valve sticking open or closed","Insufficient pressure from the vehicle air system"],["Emission warning lamp on","DEF dosing reduced or stopped","Rising NOx emissions and possible derate"],3,3,["P2037","P2039","P2040","P209B","P209E"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2039:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit Low","P2039 is stored when the signal of injection air pressure sensor A sits below the lowest voltage a working sensor can deliver. Deutz documents it on its EMR L1 controller as P2039-00 under SPN 4335 and lumps two causes together: a grounded signal and an open circuit, since the input is pulled low when the signal wire is interrupted. A loss of the 5 V reference is another common reason for a reading near zero.",["Signal wire open or shorted to ground","5 V reference to the sensor lost","Sensor output stuck low"],["Emission warning lamp on","DEF injection stopped","Power derate after a while on machines with inducement"],2,3,["P2037","P2040","P2038","P209C"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P203A:["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit","P203A is the general circuit code for reductant level sensor A, the first or only fill level element inside the DEF tank. Deutz lists it for the EMR L1 main and secondary ECU: the tank level input (J1939 SPN 1761) stores P203A with failure type 13 when the line is interrupted and with types 21 or 22 when the value drops under or climbs over its valid range.",["Loose, corroded or DEF-contaminated connector at the tank module","Broken or chafed level sensor wiring between tank and control unit","Failed level sensor or level electronics in the tank unit","Fault in the dosing or engine control unit, sometimes fixed by software"],["MIL and DEF system warning in the cluster","DEF level gauge missing, frozen or wrong","Countdown to speed limit or no-restart after some distance"],2,3,["P203B","P203C","P203D","P203E","P21A8","P21AD"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P203B:["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P203B means the level reading of sensor A is electrically present but cannot be trusted. GM's 6.6L LML and 2014 Cruze diesel set it after 5 s (Type B) when the three discrete level contacts report a combination that is physically impossible, e.g. a higher contact wet while a lower one is dry.",["Tank overfilled, so the ultrasonic sensor gets no usable echo","Ice or urea crystals on the sensor after cold soak","Wrong or diluted fluid in the DEF tank","Poor terminal contact at the tank module connector","Level sensor or tank unit defective"],["MIL, often with a DEF service message","DEF gauge stuck, jumping or showing empty with a full tank","Restart countdown on some models"],2,3,["P203A","P203C","P203D","P203E","P21A9","P21AE","P206B"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P203C:["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit Low","P203C reports a level sensor A signal stuck at the bottom of its range. On GM's 6.6L LML and the 2014 Cruze diesel this is level contact 1: the tank electronics apply a test pulse, and a reading under 0.17 V for more than 3 s with over 8 V supply counts as a short to ground (LML Type A, Cruze Type B).",["Signal wire shorted to ground or chafed at the tank","Level sensor or pump/level module internally faulty","DEF crept into the connector and bridges the terminals"],["MIL and DEF warning","DEF gauge reads empty or not at all","Speed or restart limit after a warning period"],2,3,["P203A","P203D","P203B","P21AA","P21AF"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P203D:["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit High","P203D is the high-side fault of level sensor A. On the LML Duramax and the 2014 Cruze 2.0D, GM samples level contact 1 1.5 ms after a test pulse: 3.56 to 4.74 V means an open load, above 4.74 V a short to battery, either one for more than 3 s with Type A.",["Open circuit, unplugged or loose tank connector","Signal wire shorted to supply or battery voltage","Overfilled tank on ultrasonic sensors","Failed level sensor or tank assembly"],["MIL with Service Exhaust Fluid System or similar message","DEF gauge missing or showing full permanently","Speed or restart limit if not repaired"],2,3,["P203A","P203C","P203B","P21AB","P21B0"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P203E:["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P203E stands for a level sensor A signal that keeps dropping out or jumping. FCA explains it best: Ram HD trucks with the 6.7L Cummins (2019–2021) carry an ultrasonic level sensor that needs an air gap above the fluid. Bulletin 18-034-21 and STAR case S2025000001 name an overfilled tank as the main trigger, because the echo no longer returns;",["DEF tank overfilled, no air space for the ultrasonic echo","Residual ice or urea crystals covering the sensor","Intermittent contact at the tank connector","Control unit software needing an update"],["MIL and Service DEF message","DEF gauge jumps or reads 0 % with fluid in the tank","Warning returns after filling or after a cold night"],1,3,["P203A","P203B","P203F","P21AC","P21B1"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P203F:["Reductant Level Too Low","P203F is not a sensor fault but the result of the level monitor: the DEF tank holds too little fluid to keep the SCR system working. CARB requires light and medium duty diesels to flag an empty reductant supply (13 CCR 1968.2 (f)(2.2.3)(B)); a maker can be exempted if a driver inducement prevents running without DEF and every input to it, such as the level sensor, is monitored.",["DEF tank actually low or empty","Frozen fluid or ice covering the level sensor","Leak at tank, lines or pump unit","Level sensor reading too low"],["Low DEF warnings and range countdown","Speed limit or no restart once the countdown ends","MIL on some vehicles"],1,3,["P203A","P203B","P203E","P2BAE"],"מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2040:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit High","With P2040 the injection air pressure sensor A reports a voltage above its upper limit, more than a real air pressure could produce. On Deutz's EMR L1 controller this is P2040-00 under SPN 4335, defined as a short circuit to battery. In practice that means the signal wire touches a powered conductor, the sensor ground is missing so the output floats up to the reference, or the sensor itself has failed high.",["Signal wire shorted to battery or another powered line","Sensor ground open so the output floats high","Sensor failed with output stuck high"],["Emission warning lamp on","DEF injection blocked","Air pressure value shown at maximum"],2,3,["P2037","P2039","P2038","P209D"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2041:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","P2041 catches an air pressure sensor A whose signal keeps dropping out or jumping for brief moments, too short or too irregular to be confirmed as a steady low or high fault. On trucks and machines with air-assisted DEF dosing this typically comes from vibration: a terminal with lost contact tension, a cracked wire inside the loom or moisture entering the connector at the dosing module.",["Terminal with lost contact tension at sensor or controller","Wire broken inside the insulation from vibration","Moisture in the connector"],["Warning lamp coming and going","DEF dosing interrupted at times"],2,1,["P2037","P2038","P2039","P2040"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2042:["Reductant Temperature Sensor A Circuit","P2042 concerns reductant temperature sensor A, which is a different part from the tank temperature sensor of P205A ff. The makers that document it place it outside the tank: Deutz assigns P2042 to the DEF temperature sensor of the SCR system (J1939 SPN 4337), while its tank sensor (SPN 3031) uses P205A; failure type 13 marks an open circuit, F0 a ground fault.",["Open circuit or loose connector at the pump/supply module","False setting at low battery voltage in frost (Volvo/Mack)","Poor sensor ground","Temperature sensor in the pump unit defective"],["MIL and DEF system warning","DEF heating or dosing may be restricted"],2,3,["P2043","P2044","P2045","P2046","P205A","P2ACC"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2043:["Reductant Temperature Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2043 flags a temperature reading from reductant sensor A that is electrically valid but does not fit the other temperatures the system knows. Deutz stores it as P2043-64, a plausibility error of the DEF temperature sensor in the SCR system (SPN 4337), separate from the tank sensor check P205B-64.",["Engine control software, fixed by reprogramming (Ford 6.7L)","Temperature sensor drifting or slow to respond","Frozen or partly thawed DEF around the sensor","Contact resistance in the connector shifting the reading"],["MIL, often without noticeable driving change","DEF heater may run at the wrong time"],2,1,["P2042","P2044","P2045","P205B","P205C","P205D","P2ACD"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2044:["Reductant Temperature Sensor A Circuit Low","P2044 is set when the signal of reductant temperature sensor A sits below its valid voltage window. As with other NTC thermistors, a low voltage corresponds to a hot reading, so a signal wire touching ground makes the fluid look extremely hot.",["Signal wire chafed through to ground","Sensor shorted internally (resistance near zero)","DEF residue in the connector bridging signal and ground"],["MIL and DEF warning","Scan tool shows an implausibly high DEF temperature","Lines may freeze because heating stays off"],2,3,["P2042","P2045","P2043","P205C","P2ACE"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2045:["Reductant Temperature Sensor A Circuit High","P2045 covers the opposite end: the voltage of reductant temperature sensor A is higher than any real temperature would produce. With an NTC element this reads as very cold, which is what an interrupted ground, a disconnected plug or a signal wire touching battery voltage cause. Deutz files P2045-00 as a short to battery for the DEF sensor outside the tank (SPN 4337); an open circuit gets its own entry, P2042-13.",["Open sensor ground or unplugged connector","Signal wire shorted to battery or supply voltage","Sensor element open internally"],["MIL and DEF warning","Scan tool shows DEF temperature near the lower limit","Dosing may start late after a cold start"],2,3,["P2042","P2044","P2043","P205D","P2ACF"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2046:["Reductant Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","P2046 records short dropouts or jumps in the signal of reductant temperature sensor A. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Deutz, the clearest user of the P2042 group, lists only an open line, a ground fault, both shorts and a plausibility error for this sensor, but no intermittent entry.",["Terminal losing contact under vibration","Corrosion from DEF residue in the connector","Harness rubbing through intermittently on the frame"],["MIL that comes and goes","Unsteady DEF temperature in live data"],2,1,["P2042","P2043","P2044","P2045","P205E","P2AD0"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2047:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Unit 1)","P2047 covers the electrical path of the first DEF dosing valve on Bank 1, which in nearly every SCR layout is the only one. The controller watches the valve's low-side driver and flags an open load: a broken wire, an unplugged connector or a burnt-out coil. GM's 6.6 L LML table expects roughly 200 kOhm between pin and load for 3 s (Type A); GM's 2018 diesel table counts 30 faulty samples out of 60.",["Loose, corroded or pushed-out terminals at the DEF injector plug","Harness wire broken or chafed through near the exhaust","Open coil inside the DEF injector","Faulty output stage or software in the engine/dosing control module"],["MIL on, often together with a DEF system warning","Speed limitation countdown after continued driving","Increased NOx, failed emissions inspection"],2,3,["P2048","P2049","P202E","P2050","P2053"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2048:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Low (Bank 1 Unit 1)","P2048 means the control line of the Bank 1, unit 1 DEF injector is pulled toward ground, typically a chafed wire touching the chassis or an internal short in the coil. GM's LML calibration treats less than about 0.5 ohm between signal and ground for 2 s as a failure (Type A). Ford's 2023 diesel logic reports the code once injector current exceeds 1.6 A;",["Control wire chafed against chassis or exhaust bracket","Shorted winding inside the DEF injector","ECM software setting the code without a fault (Nissan Titan XD reflash)","DEF residue or water bridging the connector pins"],["MIL on","DEF dosing suspended, warning in the instrument cluster","Inducement or reduced power after a countdown"],2,3,["P2047","P2049","P2051","P2054"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2049:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit High (Bank 1 Unit 1)","P2049 is the opposite electrical case for the Bank 1, unit 1 DEF injector: the low-side control line sees battery voltage, for instance through contact with a powered conductor or water inside the connector. On the 2014 Cruze diesel GM rates it Type B (two trips), whereas the LML and the 2018 diesel tables treat it as Type A; the 2018 test needs more than 11 V and counts 30 bad samples out of 60 at 100 ms.",["Control wire shorted to a supply wire in the harness","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins at the injector connector","Internal fault of the DEF injector coil","Defective output stage in the control module"],["MIL on (on some GM diesels only after the second trip)","Service emission system message","Higher NOx because no DEF is injected"],2,3,["P2047","P2048","P2052","P2055"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P204A:["Reductant Pressure Sensor Circuit","P204A is the general electrical fault of the sensor that measures DEF pressure between pump and injector; in most systems it is built into the pump module. The secondary ECU of Deutz's EMR L1 uses it for two states that are neither low nor high: a ground fault (failure type F0) and a sensor supply outside its window (1C), while shorts to ground or battery go to P204C and P204D.",["Open signal or ground wire to the pressure sensor","Sensor supply voltage out of range","Pressure sensor inside the DEF pump unit failed"],["MIL on, DEF system warning","No DEF dosing","Power or speed limitation after the countdown"],2,3,["P204B","P204C","P204D","P204E"],"חיישן לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P204B:["Reductant Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P204B is a plausibility test: the DEF pressure sensor is electrically fine, but its value disagrees with the system state. GM uses moments when the true pressure is known. The 6.6 L LML sets it if more than 50 kPa appears while the line is empty and unpressurised (Type A, Type B on the 2014 Cruze diesel);",["Pressure sensor offset drift inside the pump module","Dosing control unit software misjudging the reading (Hino SB-16-015)","Line not emptied at shutdown, e.g. afterrun interrupted or frozen DEF"],["MIL on, possibly only after a second trip","Emission service message","Often no noticeable driveability change"],2,3,["P204A","P204C","P204D","P204E","P20E8"],"חיישן לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P204C:["Reductant Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P204C means the DEF pressure sensor output has fallen below its valid range, which points to an open signal wire, a short to ground or a missing 5 V supply. On the 6.6 L LML, GM fails anything under 0.41 V lasting 0.4 s, GM's 2018 diesel table a raw value under 5 % of the supply, and the 2025 DEF controller less than 0.45 V in 6 of 100 samples, each Type A. Ford's 2023 diesels set it under 0.2 V.",["Water intrusion in the reductant harness connectors (Ford TSB 19-2315)","Signal wire open or shorted to ground","Missing 5 V reference to the sensor","Failed sensor in the pump/heater assembly"],["MIL on","DEF dosing stopped, DEF warning messages","Further reductant codes stored at the same time"],2,3,["P204A","P204D","P204B","P204E"],"חיישן לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P204D:["Reductant Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P204D is the high-side counterpart: the pressure signal sits near or above the supply voltage, typically because the signal wire touches 5 V or battery voltage, the sensor ground is open, or the sensor has failed internally. Published limits are 4.80 V on GM's 6.6 L LML, 98 % of the supply in GM's 2018 diesel table, 4.90 V in GM's 2025 DEF controller and 4.85 V on Ford's 2023 diesels.",["Open sensor ground or corroded ground terminal","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Internal failure of the pressure sensor in the pump module"],["MIL on (after two trips on some GM diesels)","DEF pump stopped, no dosing","DEF warning and later inducement"],2,3,["P204A","P204C","P204B","P204E"],"חיישן לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P204E:["Reductant Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P204E covers a DEF pressure signal that jumps around although it stays inside the electrical limits, as with a loose terminal, a cracked wire or a sensor with an internal contact problem. GM's 2025 DEF controller is the public calibration: it adds up all absolute pressure changes over a moving window of 100 readings taken every 10 ms and counts a failure when that sum passes 1500 kPa while pumping forward, 1000 kPa…",["Loose or fretted terminal at the pressure sensor connector","Wire breaking intermittently under vibration","Air in the DEF line or uneven pump delivery","Pressure sensor with internal intermittent fault"],["MIL on, fault may come and go","Dosing interrupted at times","Accompanying DEF pump or pressure codes"],2,3,["P204A","P204B","P204C","P204D"],"חיישן לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P204F:["Reductant System Performance (Bank 1)","P204F (Bank 1) is the functional check of the whole DEF delivery path: the parts are electrically intact, yet the system cannot build or hold the pressure needed for dosing. GM's 6.6 L LML stores a Type A code if the pump module stays at or below 350 kPa after 30 build-up and venting attempts of at least 10 s each; the 2014 Cruze diesel uses 375 kPa and 20 attempts. GM treats P204F as a tamper fault.",["DEF line clogged by crystals or frozen","Worn DEF pump that cannot reach target pressure","Air leak on the suction side or loose line couplings","Dosing unit faults repaired but SCR memory not reset (Hino)","Control module software needing an update (Ram 3.0 L)"],["MIL and DEF warning on","Countdown to speed or power limitation","Code returns after clearing until the cause is fixed"],3,3,["P205F","P20E8","P20E9","P202E","P208B","P218F"],"מערכת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2050:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Unit 1)","P2050 reports an open circuit at the first DEF injector of Bank 2, the cylinder bank opposite cylinder 1. The code only makes sense on engines whose two exhaust banks each feed their own SCR branch with a separate valve. No manufacturer publicly documents P2050;",["Unplugged or corroded connector at the Bank 2 injector","Broken wire in the harness of the second exhaust branch","Open coil in the Bank 2 DEF injector"],["MIL on","Higher NOx from the Bank 2 branch","DEF warning, later inducement possible"],2,3,["P2051","P2052","P2047","P201A","P2056"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2051:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Low (Bank 2 Unit 1)","P2051 reports a ground fault on the drive wire of the DEF injector assigned to Bank 2, unit 1. Like its siblings P2050 and P2052, it presupposes a twin-bank SCR system with a dedicated valve per exhaust branch, and no manufacturer publishes a calibration or bulletin for it.",["Insulation melted or chafed near the Bank 2 exhaust","Shorted coil in the Bank 2 injector","DEF crystals in the connector creating a path to ground"],["MIL on","Dosing on Bank 2 switched off","Possible NOx efficiency code for Bank 2 later"],2,3,["P2050","P2052","P2048","P2057"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2052:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit High (Bank 2 Unit 1)","P2052 tells that battery potential is present on the switched line of the first Bank 2 injector, for example through a short to a powered wire or moisture bridging connector pins. It belongs to twin-bank SCR layouts in which each cylinder bank owns an injector; publicly, no manufacturer documents this code or its thresholds.",["Control line of the Bank 2 injector touching a supply wire","Moisture bridging pins in the Bank 2 injector plug","Faulty output stage for the Bank 2 valve"],["MIL on, possibly after two trips","No DEF on Bank 2","Higher tailpipe NOx"],2,3,["P2050","P2051","P2049","P2058"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2053:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Unit 2)","P2053 concerns a second DEF injector on the same exhaust line as Bank 1, unit 1, used where a manufacturer doses at two points, for instance ahead of two separate catalysts. GM's 2025 table (25OBDG04B, which also covers an inline-six diesel) monitors this DEF metering valve 2 with the same open-load logic as valve 1: more than 11 V, 30 faulty samples out of 60 at 100 ms, Type A;",["Disconnected or corroded plug at DEF injector 2","Broken wire between control module and injector 2","Open coil in injector 2"],["MIL on","Slightly higher NOx, little noticeable otherwise","DEF system message"],2,3,["P2054","P2055","P2047","P2056"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2054:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Low (Bank 1 Unit 2)","P2054 flags a ground short in the switched circuit of the second DEF injector in the Bank 1 line. GM's 2025 diesel table (25OBDG04B) checks DEF metering valve 2 for this with the key on, the engine not cranking and more than 11 V, then sets a Type A code after 30 of 60 samples. Deutz uses P2054 on EMR5 engines for metering unit 2 with failure type 11, voltage below normal.",["Pinched or chafed wire to injector 2 touching ground","Coil resistance too low due to shorted turns (Ford definition)","Water or DEF in the injector connector"],["MIL on","Dosing at the affected valve stopped","DEF warning message"],2,3,["P2053","P2055","P2048","P2057"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2055:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit High (Bank 1 Unit 2)","P2055 is set when the control line of DEF injector 2 on Bank 1 is shorted to battery positive. In GM's 2025 diesel table (25OBDG04B) the power stage of metering valve 2 reports the short; with more than 11 V and 30 faulty readings out of 60 the ECM stores a Type A fault, just as P2049 does for valve 1.",["Control line of injector 2 shorted to battery positive","Coil resistance too high, corroded terminals (Ford definition)","Defective output stage for valve 2"],["MIL on","Second dosing point inactive","Increased NOx emissions"],2,3,["P2053","P2054","P2049","P2058"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2056:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Unit 2)","P2056 refers to the fourth possible DEF injector position: the second valve in the Bank 2 exhaust line. It requires both a twin-bank layout and two dosing points per bank, a combination hardly any production engine uses; no manufacturer publicly documents the code.",["Connector of the Bank 2 second injector unplugged or corroded","Broken wire in the Bank 2 dosing harness","Open injector coil"],["MIL on","Reduced NOx conversion on Bank 2"],2,3,["P2057","P2058","P2053","P2050"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2057:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Low (Bank 2 Unit 2)","P2057 is the short-to-ground case for the second DEF injector of Bank 2. As with P2056 and P2058, it exists in the code list for engines with two exhaust banks and two dosing points each, yet no manufacturer publishes a calibration or service bulletin for it.",["Harness clamped against frame or exhaust bracket","Shorted windings in the injector coil","DEF residue in the connector"],["MIL on","Valve switched off, NOx conversion reduced"],2,3,["P2056","P2058","P2054","P2051"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2058:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit High (Bank 2 Unit 2)","P2058 indicates that the second DEF injector on Bank 2 sees battery voltage on its switched line. Like the other Bank 2, unit 2 codes it is reserved for twin-bank engines with two dosing points per bank, and no manufacturer documents it publicly.",["Moisture in the injector plug","Short to a neighbouring supply wire","Failed output stage in the control module"],["MIL on","No dosing at the Bank 2 second valve"],2,3,["P2056","P2057","P2055","P2052"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2059:["Reductant Injection Air Pump Control Circuit/Open","The air that atomizes DEF in an air-assisted system comes either from a small dedicated compressor or from an existing compressed-air system through a supply valve. P2059 concerns the driver circuit of that pump or valve, above all an open circuit: the output is switched on but no current flows.",["Open coil in the air valve or pump motor","Connector unplugged or corroded, wire broken","Fuse or relay in the supply path failed","Shorted valve coil causing overcurrent shutdown"],["Emission warning lamp on","No DEF dosing, NOx rises","Power derate on trucks and machines"],2,3,["P2060","P2061","P2037"],"משאבת אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P205A:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor A Circuit","P205A is the general circuit code for the temperature sensor inside the DEF tank, usually built into the level or heater unit; the separate sensor in the supply path uses P2042 ff. Deutz assigns the tank temperature (J1939 SPN 3031) to P205A: failure type 13 for an open circuit, 21 and 22 for values under or over the valid range, while the SCR-side DEF sensor (SPN 4337) stays with P2042.",["Open circuit or loose tank connector","Tank temperature sensor in the sender unit defective","Corroded terminals from DEF exposure"],["MIL and DEF warning","Tank heating not working in frost","Speed or restart limit on some models"],2,3,["P205B","P205C","P205D","P205E","P2042","P2ADE"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P205B:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P205B is the rationality check of the DEF tank temperature: after a long cold soak every sensor should read about the same, so a tank value far off the rest is flagged. GM's 6.6L LML compares it with fuel temperature after 28,800 s engine off (beyond +35/−35 °C, Type B);",["Calibration error, fixed by reprogramming","Tank temperature sensor reading off (offset or gain)","Frozen tank or low fill level distorting the reading","Faulty reference sensor (fuel, exhaust or quality sensor)"],["MIL, sometimes with an emissions service message","Usually no change in driving"],2,1,["P205A","P205C","P205D","P205E","P2043","P2ADA"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P205C:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor A Circuit Low","P205C reports the DEF tank temperature signal at the bottom of its range. For voltage-read NTC sensors that means implausibly hot: Ford's 2023 diesels set it below 0.165 V, VW's Touareg below 0.30 V, GM's 2025 DEF controller below 0.3 V (about 75 °C) and GM's 2018 diesel table below 200 Ω, each as short to ground.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Faulty sensor in the heater/sender assembly","DEF in the connector bridging the terminals"],["MIL and DEF warning","Tank temperature in live data stuck at an extreme","Tank heater not working in frost"],2,3,["P205A","P205D","P205B","P2043","P2ADB"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P205D:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor A Circuit High","P205D is the top-of-range fault of the tank's temperature sensor. On voltage-read NTC sensors a high signal looks like extreme cold and typically comes from an open circuit, a lost ground or a short to supply: Ford's 2023 diesels set it above 4.3 V, GM's 2025 DEF controller above 4.75 V (about −40 °C, 0.5 s, Type A), and GM's 2018 diesel table above 60,000 Ω.",["Open circuit, unplugged connector or broken ground","Sensor in the heater/sender assembly open internally","Signal wire shorted to supply voltage"],["MIL and DEF warning","Tank heater runs although the tank is warm","Dosing delayed after start"],2,3,["P205A","P205C","P205B","P2043","P2ADC"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P205E:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P205E marks a DEF tank temperature that changes faster than any real tank could. GM describes two versions: the 2018 diesel table (1.6L Cruze, 2.8L Colorado) checks whether the signal's time evolution is plausible and fails after 8 out of 10 samples taken every 500 ms, provided no electrical fault of the sensor is present;",["Engine control software, fixed by reflash (FCA 6.7L)","Loose or corroded contact at the tank connector","Block heater use causing a fast temperature change"],["MIL, often after cold starts","Jumping tank temperature in live data"],2,1,["P205A","P205B","P205C","P205D","P2046","P2ADD"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P205F:["Reductant System Performance (Bank 2)","P205F is the Bank 2 version of the reductant system performance check, meant for engines in which the second cylinder bank has its own SCR branch with separate pressure supply or valve. It applies when that branch is electrically sound but fails to reach or regulate the pressure or quantity the controller asks for. No manufacturer publicly documents P205F;",["Blocked or frozen DEF line to the Bank 2 branch","Bank 2 injector sticking due to DEF crystals","Insufficient pump or metering unit pressure for the second branch"],["MIL and DEF warning on","Higher NOx from Bank 2, possible inducement"],3,3,["P204F","P20E8","P20E9","P201A"],"מערכת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P2060:["Reductant Injection Air Pump Control Circuit Low","P2060 means the control line of the injection air pump or air valve is held at too low a level: when the output tries to switch it on, the voltage collapses because the wire or the load is connected to ground. Deutz defines exactly this on its EMR L1 controller as P2060-00, a high-side short to ground on output SPN 5796, which drives the air pump or valve.",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Valve or pump coil shorted to its housing","Water in the connector bridging to ground"],["Emission warning lamp on","DEF dosing blocked","Possible blown fuse in the air valve supply"],2,3,["P2059","P2061"],"משאבת אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2061:["Reductant Injection Air Pump Control Circuit High","P2061 is the high-side counterpart: the pump or valve output that feeds atomizing air carries voltage when the controller expects it to be off, or the diagnostic sees a level that only a connection to battery positive can explain. Deutz documents it on the EMR L1 controller as P2061-00, short circuit to battery on the high side (SPN 5796).",["Control wire shorted to a powered cable in the loom","Damaged connector with bridged pins","Output stage in the controller failed"],["Emission warning lamp on","Air valve may run continuously, air system loses pressure","DEF dosing blocked"],2,3,["P2059","P2060"],"משאבת אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2062:["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit/Open","J2012 keeps this title deliberately broad: the controlled supply that feeds the reductant system or, in some layouts, the regeneration hardware, mostly a supply pump or the relay powering it. P2062 reports an open control circuit, so the commanded stage draws no current. No manufacturer documents P2062 publicly.",["Blown fuse or relay not closing in the supply path","Broken wire or unplugged connector at the pump","Supply pump with open winding"],["Engine or emission warning lamp on","No reductant pressure, dosing stops","Restart countdown or speed limit on some vehicles"],2,3,["P2063","P2064","P202F","P208A"],""],P2063:["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit Low","P2063 says the reductant or regeneration supply control circuit reads too low, the classic signature of a grounded control line or of a load drawing far more current than it should, which pulls the driver output down. No manufacturer documents P2063 publicly. The comparable component code in Ford's 2023 diesel summary is P208C, set when reductant pump current exceeds 5 A or the pump controller draws more than 15 A;",["Supply control wire shorted to ground near the tank","Pump motor seized or blocked by DEF crystals","Internal short in the pump winding"],["Engine or emission warning lamp on","Fuse for the DEF supply blows repeatedly","Dosing suspended, possible speed or restart limitation"],2,3,["P2062","P2064","P202F","P208C"],""],P2064:["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit High","P2064 closes the supply control group that begins with P2062. The line that switches power to the reductant supply, in a few layouts to regeneration hardware, carries a level that only a connection to a positive feed can explain, or the stage stays live while the controller has it switched off. No manufacturer documents P2064 publicly.",["Control line chafed through and touching a powered wire","Supply relay contact welded closed","Water or corrosion bridging pins in the supply connector","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["MIL and SCR or DEF warning in the cluster","DEF pump audible after it should have stopped","Countdown toward speed limit or no-restart after repeated faults"],2,3,["P2062","P2063","P05F0","P208D"],""],P2065:["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit","Sensor B is the second fuel level sender, used where one sender cannot cover the whole tank: the passive half of a saddle tank, a secondary tank on dual-tank trucks, or the secondary lever-type sender that Mercedes reads through its fuel pump module. Ford explains the saddle layout: a jet pump moves fuel to the active side, and both readings are averaged into one gauge value.",["Loose or corroded connector at the second sender or pump module","Broken wire between sender and the module that reads it","Worn or failed sender card in the tank","Control module software that does not match the tank layout"],["Fuel gauge reads wrong, stuck or jumps","Low fuel warning comes on with a full tank or not at all","MIL on, evaporative monitor may not complete"],2,1,["P2066","P2067","P2068","P2069","P0460","P25B1"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2066:["Fuel Level Sensor B Performance","P2066 flags a second fuel level sender whose reading is electrically valid but does not behave like real fuel. Makers test it differently. GM, on dual-tank trucks with an electric transfer pump, calls it Fuel Level Sensor 2 Performance and looks for a secondary reading that stays frozen while the engine burns 18 L or more, or that barely moves while the pump transfers fuel; Type B, two trips.",["Float arm sticking or sender card worn in one spot","Transfer or jet pump not moving fuel between tank halves","Plausibility logic needing a software update (Jeep, Genesis)","Poor contact causing a noisy signal (Ford definition)"],["Fuel gauge stays put or lags behind real consumption","MIL after refuelling or long drives","Range display and low fuel warning unreliable"],2,1,["P2065","P2067","P2068","P0461","P25B1","P2636"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2067:["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit Low","P2067 sets when the input from the second fuel level sender drops below its valid floor, usually a grounded signal wire or a sender resistance near zero. Ford's saddle-tank trucks flag it below 5 ohms (under one A/D count) and allow 30 s for the electrical check. GM's 2020 table, written for dual-tank vehicles, sets it when the secondary sender reads under 10 % of its 5 V range in 100 of 125 samples;",["Sender signal wire shorted to ground or chafed on the tank strap","Sender card shorted internally","PCM software for the wrong drivetrain or tank version","Diagnostic logic needing an ECM update (Genesis G80)"],["MIL on with no change in driving","Fuel gauge too low, empty or dropping suddenly","Low fuel warning without reason"],2,1,["P2065","P2068","P2069","P0462"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2068:["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit High","P2068 is the upper limit fault of the second fuel level sender: its signal sits above anything a working sender can produce, which normally means an open circuit, a lost sender ground or a short to a supply voltage. Ford reports it above 200 ohms, more than 253 A/D counts, using the same 30 s electrical check as for sender A.",["Open signal or ground wire, unplugged sender connector","Sender card worn through or wiper lifted off the track","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage"],["Low fuel warning or empty gauge with fuel in the tank","MIL on","Range estimate jumps or is implausible"],2,1,["P2065","P2067","P2069","P0463"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2069:["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2069 covers brief dropouts on the second fuel level sender: the signal leaves its valid window for moments and comes back, too short for a hard low or high fault. Mercedes is the one maker found to document it, as P206900 in the FSCM_GEN4 fuel pump control unit, a sporadic malfunction of the secondary fill level sensor;",["Worn spot on the sender card at the usual fuel level","Loose or corroded terminal at the tank flange connector","Harness rubbing on a bracket or tank strap"],["Fuel gauge needle twitches or drops briefly","Low fuel light flickers on and off","Intermittent MIL"],2,1,["P2065","P2066","P2067","P2068","P0464"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P206A:["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit","The quality sensor sits in the DEF (AdBlue) tank, usually inside a module that also holds level and temperature elements, and estimates urea concentration, in GM's case by timing ultrasonic echoes. P206A is the general circuit code: the module cannot deliver a usable quality value, without a finer split into range, low or high.",["Corroded or loose connector at the tank sensor module","Failed quality sensor or tank sensor module","Damaged signal or supply wiring near the tank","Frozen, aerated or heavily contaminated fluid around the sensor"],["MIL and DEF system warning","Countdown to no-restart or speed limit","DEF quality value missing in scan data"],3,3,["P206B","P206C","P206D","P207F"],"חיישן איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P206B:["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P206B means the quality sensor answers, but its result cannot be used or does not fit what the SCR system does. GM sets it in its 2018 diesel table when the DEF controller keeps reporting the sensor as not ready, for instance because the ultrasonic echo is lost on a fouled sensor: 200 failed out of 250 samples, Type A, checked only with over 4 L of DEF and a sensor above 5 °C.",["Air bubbles on the sensor after filling","Deposits or crystals on the ultrasonic sensor","Internal fault in the quality sensor or tank module","Drifting NOx sensor upsetting the rationality check (Hino logic)"],["MIL and Service Emission System or DEF message","Fault appears shortly or hours after refilling DEF","Possible countdown to speed limit"],2,3,["P206A","P206C","P206D","P207F","P203B"],"חיישן איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P206C:["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit Low","P206C is the low-side fault of the quality sensor, read in two ways. GM treats it as electrical: in its 2018 diesel table the piezo input of the ultrasonic sensor below 0.15 V in 40 of 50 samples sets the code, Type A.",["Diluted or wrong fluid in the DEF tank (Ford definition)","Low tank level letting the sensor run dry in curves","Sensor signal shorted to ground or failed sensor element"],["MIL and DEF quality or emission system warning","Reduced power or speed limit on Ford diesels","Warning that appears after a long curve and then clears"],2,3,["P206A","P206B","P206D","P207F"],"חיישן איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P206D:["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit High","P206D is the upper limit counterpart of P206C. In GM's 2018 diesel table it is electrical: the piezo input of the ultrasonic quality sensor above 4.5 V in 40 of 50 samples, Type A. Ford's 2023 diesels set it when filtered urea concentration reads 60 % or more for over 900 s, which real DEF never reaches, so either the sensor or a foreign fluid is to blame.",["Urea crystals around the sensor after freeze and thaw","Sensor signal open or shorted to voltage, failed sensor","Foreign or over-concentrated fluid in the tank"],["MIL and DEF or emission system warning","Fault often after cold nights","Countdown toward speed limit or no-restart"],2,3,["P206A","P206B","P206C","P207F"],"חיישן איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P206E:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Open (Bank 2)","Reserved for engines whose second cylinder bank has its own intake manifold tuning valve, the flap that switches plenum volume or runner length for resonance charging. The code says the bank 2 flap was commanded shut but its position feedback still reports it open. No manufacturer documents P206E publicly; the GM and Ford tables checked cover only a single tuning valve, logged as P2070/P2071.",["Flap or shaft of the bank 2 tuning valve gummed up by oil vapour and carbon from crankcase ventilation","Bank 2 actuator motor or gear worn, cannot drive the flap into the closed stop","Linkage between actuator and flap shaft detached or broken","End positions not relearned after actuator or manifold replacement"],["Check engine light after two drives (manufacturer-dependent)","Noticeably less pulling power in one rpm range","Changed intake sound under acceleration"],2,1,["P206F","P2070","P207A","P207B","P065F"],""],P206F:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 2)","Here the bank 2 tuning valve ignores an open request: the engine computer asks it to swing to the open end stop, yet the feedback still shows the closed position. The code only makes sense on a V-engine with a separately switched flap per bank, and no manufacturer publishes it; GM and Ford describe a single valve and use P2071 for the stuck-closed case.",["Bank 2 flap seized in its closed position by deposits or a dry shaft bearing","Bank 2 actuator internally defective, no longer produces the opening torque","On vacuum-operated designs a leaking hose or check valve leaves the actuator without vacuum","Broken flap seal or foreign object blocking the flap travel"],["Engine feels flat at high rpm","Check engine light (manufacturer-dependent)","Barely noticeable at moderate driving"],2,1,["P206E","P2071","P207A","P0663","P065F"],""],P2070:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Open (Bank 1)","The tuning valve switches the manifold geometry for resonance charging; with a position sensor fitted, the engine computer can see whether the flap obeys. P2070 is logged when it was told to close and stays open. GM uses it in many tables: the 2006 and 2007 V6/four-cylinder sets flag a learn phase of 0.75 s or more, or five or more learn attempts, between 1000 and 3600 rpm;",["Flap shaft sticking from oily carbon deposits fed by crankcase ventilation","Actuator motor or gear worn, flap stops short of the closed position","Actuator unclipped from the shaft or broken coupling","Learn routine of the end stops aborted, e.g. after repairs or low battery voltage"],["Check engine light after the second faulty drive (GM Type B)","Weaker pulling power in the speed range the closed flap is meant for","Louder or different intake noise"],2,1,["P2071","P206E","P2076","P065E","P0660"],""],P2071:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 1)","Counterpart to P2070: the bank 1 tuning valve receives an open command, but the position feedback keeps showing it shut. In GM's 2006 and 2007 tables the check simply compares commanded and actual flap position under load between 1000 and 3600 rpm, Type B. From 2015 on (also engine LWE in 18OBDG03A) GM requires that the open stop is reached within 5 s;",["Flap seized shut by deposits or corroded shaft bushings","Actuator defective, no longer turns the flap against its return spring","Weak supply to the actuator from a corroded connector or relay contact"],["Lack of power at high engine speed","Check engine light (GM Type B, Ford without MIL)","Engine otherwise runs normally"],2,1,["P2070","P206F","P2076","P2077","P0661"],""],P2072:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Ice Blockage (Bank 1)","Not related to the tuning valve: P2072 belongs to the electronic throttle system. If the throttle plate cannot move freely in frost, the controller assumes ice and runs repeated open and close strokes to break it loose; the code records that event. Ford's 2012 OBD summary lists it for second-generation throttle control as a non-MIL fault, and Ford's 2014 code list marks it for the wrench lamp only.",["Water from the crankcase ventilation condensing and freezing at the throttle plate","Frequent short trips in frost leave water in the engine oil and breather","Heater of the breather line or throttle body (where fitted) not working","Water entering the air intake through a loose duct or wet air filter"],["Wrench or engine light after a cold start in frost","Limited engine speed or reduced power","Engine may not start in deep frost"],2,2,["P2110","P2118","P2111","P2112","P2101"],""],P2073:["Manifold Absolute Pressure/Mass Air Flow - Throttle Position Correlation at Idle","The engine computer compares the measured air mass, or the manifold pressure, with what the throttle opening and engine speed predict. P2073 means the two disagree in the idle range. Ford's diesel OBD summary 2023 explains its approach: an airflow adaptation factor is learned in an idle cell and a load cell once per drive cycle; if the idle value ends up outside its band, P2073 is set.",["Unmetered air entering after the air flow sensor (loose clamp, cracked hose, leaking gasket)","Air flow sensor element contaminated or drifted, adaptation runs out of range","Outdated PCM calibration (Ford 6.7L 2011–2012, bulletin 22-2115)","Deposits at the throttle plate distorting the idle air path"],["Check engine light","Unsteady or raised idle","Often no noticeable driving fault"],2,1,["P2074","P0068","P0101","P0106","P00BC"],""],P2074:["Manifold Absolute Pressure/Mass Air Flow - Throttle Position Correlation at Higher Load","Same plausibility idea as P2073, but evaluated above idle, where the measured air mass or manifold pressure must match what throttle opening and rpm predict under load. Ford's diesels learn an airflow adaptation in a load cell; outside roughly +/-20 % (6.7L chassis and 3.0L), or if no stable value is learned within 20 learning events, P2074 is stored.",["Clogged air filter shifting the learned airflow value (Ford 6.7L)","Leak in charge air pipes or intercooler on turbo engines","Calibration issue fixed by software update (Ford 6.7L, Hyundai 2.5L)","Air flow sensor reading drifted at high flow rates"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or limited performance mode (Hyundai)","Hesitation under acceleration"],2,3,["P2073","P0068","P0101","P00BD","P0170"],""],P2075:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit (Bank 1)","General circuit fault of the bank 1 tuning valve position feedback, which may be a potentiometer, a Hall sensor or a simple end-position switch. The code is meant for systems that do not split the fault into low, high or intermittent.",["Corroded or loose connector at the actuator with integrated position sensor","Signal, reference or ground wire chafed or broken near the hot manifold","Position sensor inside the actuator failed"],["Check engine light (manufacturer-dependent)","Flap position monitoring and stuck-valve tests no longer run","Usually no driveability complaint"],1,1,["P2076","P2077","P2078","P2079","P207A"],""],P2076:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1)","The sensor signal is electrically within its limits, but it does not behave plausibly. GM defines this through the learn routine of the actuator in the 2015 and 2018 tables: if the reported position stays between 5 % and 35 % for 5 s or more while learning, or the learn routine starts ten or more times within a single key cycle, P2076 is stored as Type B after supply voltage of at least 11 V and one second of…",["Flap binding so that the actuator cannot complete its learn sweep","Worn potentiometer track giving jumpy readings","Digital (SENT) position message corrupted by wiring or actuator electronics","Incorrect or non-matching replacement actuator"],["Check engine light after two trips (GM Type B)","Actuator audibly cycling at key-on","Slight power loss in parts of the rev range"],2,1,["P2075","P2077","P2078","P2070","P207B"],""],P2077:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 1)","The feedback signal of the bank 1 tuning valve has dropped below its plausible lower edge, typically because the signal is shorted to ground or the line is open with a pull-down. GM states it in percent of the sensor range: in 2006/2007 and again in the 2015/2018 tables a reading of 95 % or more counts as low, so GM's scaling is inverted; once 320 of every 400 checks (one each 12.5 ms) fail, it is stored as Type B.",["Signal wire shorted to ground or chafed against the engine","5 V reference to the sensor interrupted","Actuator with integrated sensor defective (FCA 3.5L, check duty cycle first)"],["Check engine light (GM Type B; Ford without MIL)","Stuck-valve tests P2070/P2071 disabled","Driving often unchanged"],1,1,["P2078","P2075","P2076","P207C","P2071"],""],P2078:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 1)","Opposite of P2077: the bank 1 valve feedback sits above its upper plausible limit. Typical triggers are a short to battery or 5 V on the signal line, or an open sensor ground. Because GM's percentage scale is reversed, its tables treat a position of 5 % or less as high (2007, 2015, 2018; the 2006 table names 0.05 %), with 320 failures in 400 samples and Type B.",["Sensor ground open, e.g. pushed-back pin in the connector","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Electronics of the actuator unit defective"],["Check engine light (GM Type B; Ford without MIL)","Valve monitoring suspended","Possibly less power in one rpm band"],1,1,["P2077","P2075","P2076","P207D","P2070"],""],P2079:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1)","Intended for brief dropouts or jumps in the bank 1 valve feedback that come and go rather than sticking at one limit. No manufacturer documents this meaning publicly. GM's tuning valve tables stop at P2076 to P2078, and Ford's 2014 code list even assigns P2079 to an intake air system leak, an older Ford-specific text that has nothing to do with the position sensor, so scan-tool texts on Ford vehicles can differ.",["Loose or fretted terminals in the sensor connector","Wire broken inside the insulation, contact lost with engine movement","Dead spot on the sensor track"],["Light comes and goes (manufacturer-dependent)","Fault often not present during workshop test"],2,1,["P2075","P2077","P2078","P207E"],""],P207A:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit (Bank 2)","Unspecified circuit failure of the position feedback on the bank 2 tuning valve. It presupposes a second, separately sensed valve, which in practice means a V-engine with one switchable flap per bank. Nobody publishes this code: the GM tables use a single sensed valve (P2076 to P2078), and in Ford's literature only the runner control flaps (IMRC, P2004 onward) are monitored bank by bank.",["Poorly accessible bank 2 connector not latched or corroded","Harness chafed between manifold and bulkhead","Position sensor of the bank 2 actuator failed"],["Check engine light (manufacturer-dependent)","Mostly no change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2075","P207B","P207C","P207D","P207E"],""],P207B:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","On bank 2, the valve feedback is electrically valid yet does not match what the flap should be doing, for instance it changes too slowly, sticks at an intermediate value or disagrees with the commanded state. No manufacturer documents P207B.",["Bank 2 flap binding, movement profile does not match the command","Coupling between sensor shaft and flap slipping","Sensor characteristic drifted with age and heat"],["Check engine light (manufacturer-dependent)","Possibly uneven power delivery"],2,1,["P2076","P207A","P207C","P207D","P206E"],""],P207C:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 2)","Low signal on the position feedback of the bank 2 tuning valve: the controller sees a value below the window it accepts. Typical electrical causes are the signal shorted to ground or a missing 5 V supply. No manufacturer publishes P207C.",["Bank 2 signal wire shorted to ground","Shared 5 V reference pulled down or open","Internal short in the bank 2 sensor"],["Check engine light (manufacturer-dependent)","Other 5 V sensor codes at the same time"],1,1,["P207D","P207A","P207B","P2077"],""],P207D:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 2)","The bank 2 valve position signal reads above the highest value the controller accepts. Electrically that points at a broken sensor ground or a short from the signal to a supply voltage. There is no published manufacturer use of P207D; it mirrors GM's bank 1 code P2078, where 5 % or less counts as high due to the reversed scale, while GM's 2023/2024 logic compares the raw voltage with about 4.8 V.",["Sensor ground open at a heat-damaged connector","Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Bank 2 actuator electronics defective"],["Check engine light (manufacturer-dependent)","No driveability change in most cases"],1,1,["P207C","P207A","P207B","P2078"],""],P207E:["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","Bank 2 version of the intermittent feedback fault: the valve position signal drops out or jumps for short moments, but returns to normal between events. No manufacturer documents P207E, and even its bank 1 twin P2079 has no published OEM use with this meaning.",["Moisture or corrosion in the bank 2 sensor connector","Solder joint or wire breaking open intermittently under heat","Harness not clipped, contact lost under vibration"],["Intermittent warning light (manufacturer-dependent)","Fault not reproducible in the workshop"],2,1,["P2079","P207A","P207C","P207D"],""],P207F:["Reductant Quality Performance","P207F is the verdict that the tank holds something other than proper DEF, which CARB explicitly requires the OBD system to detect. Without a quality sensor the fluid is judged by its effect: GM's 2011 diesel table names the code Incorrect Reductant Composition and compares measured SCR NOx conversion with a limit that depends on temperature and flow, Type B;",["Water, coolant or other fluid in the DEF tank","Old DEF degraded by heat or long storage","NOx sensor reading wrong, faking poor conversion","Partly blocked dosing valve delivering too little fluid"],["Exhaust fluid quality warning in the cluster","MIL and countdown to speed limit or no-restart","Message persists until a quality test or relearn is passed"],2,3,["P206A","P206B","P206C","P206D","P20EE","P2BA9"],"איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2080:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2080 means the first exhaust temperature sensor on bank 1 passes its wiring checks, yet its reading does not fit the engine state. Each maker tests this differently. On the 6.6 L Duramax (GM 15OBDG09) the heat the exhaust flow should bring to the sensor is integrated and compared with what the sensor saw;",["Sensor element drifted or slow after many heat cycles","Sensor loose, bent or not reaching into the exhaust stream","ECM calibration flags a good sensor (software update released, e.g. Nissan)","Exhaust leak upstream of the sensor cools the reading"],["Engine warning lamp on","Particulate filter regeneration blocked or aborted on diesels","Often no noticeable change in driving"],2,3,["P2081","P2082","P2084","P0544","P0545","P0546","P242B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2081:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2081 is set when the signal of exhaust temperature sensor 1 on bank 1 jumps between consecutive readings faster than real exhaust gas can change. GM documents two versions. A diesel in table 18OBDG04 flags a change of more than 10 ohms between two samples taken 100 ms apart and needs 20 such failures out of 40.",["Loose or corroded pin in the sensor connector","Sensor lead chafed or embrittled by exhaust heat, breaking contact on vibration","Cracked sensing element giving unstable resistance","ECM software issue (Infiniti VR30DDTT reprogramming)"],["Engine warning lamp on, sometimes only after the second trip","Exhaust temperature value jumping in live data","Regeneration or turbo protection strategy interrupted"],2,3,["P2080","P2083","P2085","P0544","P0545","P0546"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2082:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2082 is the plausibility fault of the first exhaust temperature sensor on bank 2, the cylinder bank without cylinder 1. It only exists where both banks carry separate sensors ahead of the merge point, which in practice means V-type petrol engines with turbo or catalyst protection. The diesel tables from GM, Ford and VW number every sensor on bank 1 because one aftertreatment line serves the engine.",["ECM calibration error on affected Nissan/Infiniti models (reprogramming)","Bank 2 sensor drifted or contaminated","Exhaust leak on bank 2 ahead of the sensor"],["Engine warning lamp on","Usually no noticeable driving change"],2,1,["P2080","P2083","P2086","P0547","P0548","P0549"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2083:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2083 reports an unsteady signal from exhaust temperature sensor 1 on bank 2: the value changes by more than the exhaust can physically manage between two readings, or briefly drops out. Only one maker documents it publicly.",["Intermittent contact in the bank 2 sensor connector","ECM software (Infiniti VR30DDTT bulletin)","Lead damaged by turbocharger or exhaust heat"],["Engine warning lamp on","Bank 2 exhaust temperature flickering in live data"],2,1,["P2081","P2082","P2087","P0547","P0548","P0549"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2084:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P2084 applies the plausibility check to the second exhaust temperature sensor on bank 1, on diesels usually the one behind the oxidation catalyst or ahead of the particulate filter or SCR stage. GM runs the same tests here as for sensor 1: a heat balance on the 6.6 L Duramax (15OBDG09) and a cold-soak rise check on the 3.0 L LZO (25OBDG04B), both Type B.",["Sensor 2 reads low or responds slowly due to ageing or soot","Sensor connectors swapped with another exhaust temperature sensor after repair","Oxidation catalyst not producing the expected heat, so the reading looks implausible"],["Engine warning lamp on","Particulate filter regeneration or DEF dosing restricted","Reduced engine power on some diesels"],2,3,["P2080","P2085","P2086","P2031","P2032","P2033"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2085:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P2085 marks the signal of exhaust temperature sensor 2 on bank 1 as erratic. GM monitors it with the same logic as sensor 1 but on separate counters. In the diesel table 18OBDG04 a step of more than 10 ohms between two 100 ms samples counts as a failure, and 20 failures within 40 samples set the code; on the 3.0 L LZO (25OBDG04B) a raw jump above 100 °C in 12 of 25 samples is enough.",["Water or road salt in the underbody sensor connector","Lead rubbing on the exhaust or a bracket, intermittent break","Internal fault in the sensor causing unstable resistance"],["Engine warning lamp on after repeated occurrence","Erratic sensor 2 value in live data","Regeneration interrupted"],2,3,["P2081","P2084","P2087","P2031","P2032","P2033"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2086:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P2086 would report an implausible reading from the second exhaust temperature sensor on bank 2. Snap-on's code list confirms the wording. No manufacturer document available to us uses the code: GM, Ford and VW keep all diesel sensors on bank 1, Nissan's per-bank petrol layouts stop at sensor 1, and Ford's 2014 petrol list jumps from P2085 to P2088.",["Bank 2 downstream sensor aged or sooted, reading off","Sensor loose or not reaching into the gas stream","Leak in the bank 2 exhaust ahead of the sensor"],["Engine warning lamp on","Catalyst or filter protection functions limited"],2,1,["P2082","P2084","P2087","P2034","P2035","P2036"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2087:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P2087 is reserved for a bank 2 sensor 2 exhaust temperature signal that is erratic or drops out. No manufacturer publishes it; we checked GM, Ford, VW, Deutz and the NHTSA bulletin index without a hit, and Ford's 2014 petrol list leaves it out.",["Intermittent contact in the bank 2 sensor 2 connector","Lead chafing on the second exhaust pipe","Sensor element with unstable resistance"],["Engine warning lamp on","Unstable exhaust temperature value for bank 2 sensor 2"],2,1,["P2083","P2085","P2086","P2034","P2035","P2036"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2088:['"A" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)',"P2088 concerns the control line of the oil control valve that moves the intake cam phaser (actuator A) on bank 1. On GM engines the ECM feeds the solenoid through a high-side driver; while the output is switched on, a voltage that falls below the controller window means the line has a path to ground (equivalent to less than 0.5 ohms).",["Control wire chafed through to ground, e.g. GM jumper harness at connector X154","Oil control valve coil shorted internally","Engine oil wicked into the valve connector","Damaged output driver in the ECM"],["Engine warning lamp on","Less pull and higher consumption with cam timing fixed","Rough idle on some engines"],2,3,["P2089","P2090","P2092","P0010","P0011","P0012"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2089:['"A" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 1)',"P2089 is the opposite fault on the intake phaser valve (actuator A) of bank 1: the control line carries voltage although the ECM has switched the output off. With GM's high-side driver that means a short to a supply, again judged against a 0.5 ohm equivalent.",["Control wire shorted to a 12 V feed inside the harness","Pinched or chafed jumper harness at the front cover (GM X154)","ECM output stage shorted internally"],["Engine warning lamp on, on some GM engines in the first trip","Intake cam timing no longer adjusted, sluggish response"],2,3,["P2088","P2091","P2093","P0010","P0011","P0012"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P208A:["Reductant Pump A Control Circuit/Open","P208A reports an open or otherwise faulty drive circuit of the main DEF pump, the one that builds dosing pressure. Ford's 2023 diesels flag it when pump voltage sits between 2.6 and 3.4 V or the pump controller supply falls under 6 V, tested with the driver off and confirmed after 8 s. GM's 2018 diesel table takes a phase-open message from the DEF module, 32 of 40 samples, Type A;",["Unplugged, corroded or broken pump connector or wire","Pump controller or ECU software (Volvo/Mack, JLR, GM 23-NA-008)","Low supply to the pump controller from fuse, relay or ground","Pump motor winding open, pump unit failed"],["MIL and DEF dosing malfunction message","No engine restart countdown","Fault often logged at cold start"],2,3,["P208B","P208C","P208D","P20FA","P2062","P05EE"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P208B:["Reductant Pump A Control Performance/Stuck Off","P208B is the functional check of DEF pump A: the circuit is intact, yet the pump ignores its command or stays off. Ford, titling it Reductant Pump Control Range/Performance, sets it on 2023 diesels when pump speed misses its setpoint by over 300 rpm or its speed control sits at a limit for 30 s, detected within 5 s and only after the circuit tests have passed.",["Air trapped in the tank filter or suction side after service","Leaking DEF line or connection between pump and dosing valve","Worn, frozen or crystallised pump","Calibration needing an update (FCA 3.0L diesel)"],["MIL with DEF system message, often with P20E8","White urea crust on lines or fittings","Countdown to no-restart or reduced power"],2,3,["P208A","P208C","P208D","P201F","P20E8","P20FB"],"בקרת משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P208C:["Reductant Pump A Control Circuit Low","P208C sets when the drive of DEF pump A is pulled low, either by a ground fault or by current far beyond normal. Ford's 2023 diesels look for pump current over 5 A or pump controller current over 15 A with the driver off, the same 8 s window as for the open fault P208A. In GM's 2018 diesel table the DEF control module itself reports the phase shorted to ground; 20 out of 25 samples, Type A.",["Pump drive wire shorted to ground near the tank","Seized or crystallised pump drawing excessive current","Software error in the controlling module (JLR Velar)","Water in the pump connector"],["MIL and DEF dosing malfunction warning","Pump fuse found blown","Countdown to no-restart"],2,3,["P208A","P208B","P208D","P20FC","P2063","P05EF"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P208D:["Reductant Pump A Control Circuit High","P208D means the drive of DEF pump A reads high, typically a wire touching battery positive, so the controller has lost authority over the pump. Unlike the open and low faults, Ford checks this one with the driver switched on: on 2023 diesels pump voltage over 16 V or pump controller current above 5 A sets it, confirmed in only 2 s.",["Pump drive wire shorted to a battery feed","Doser control unit software (Ram 6.7L, 18-010-14)","Moisture or corrosion in the pump connector","Internal fault in pump or pump controller"],["MIL and DEF system warning","No DEF dosing, rising NOx","Countdown to speed limit or no-restart"],2,3,["P208A","P208B","P208C","P20FD","P2064","P05F0"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P208E:["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 1 Unit 1)","P208E says the first DEF dosing valve does not open although it is energised correctly. Valve movement shows in the coil current: when the armature lifts, the trace kinks. Ford's 2023 diesels judge every stroke and need 50 failures; the test pauses while P2047 to P2049 report a circuit fault.",["Urea crystals blocking the dosing valve nozzle","Valve needle seized from deposits or heat","Contaminated fluid or debris from a dirty pump filter"],["MIL and DEF dosing warning","DEF consumption drops noticeably","Derate or countdown to no-restart"],2,3,["P208F","P2047","P2048","P2049","P202D","P218F"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P208F:["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 2 Unit 1)","P208F is the Bank 2 version of P208E: the first dosing valve on the second exhaust branch fails to open although its drive circuit is in order. It only applies to engines with two separate SCR branches, each with its own dosing valve, which is rare; most diesel cars and trucks run one valve on Bank 1. No manufacturer documents P208F publicly.",["Urea crystals blocking the Bank 2 dosing valve","Valve needle stuck from deposits or overheating","Restricted supply line to the second valve"],["MIL and DEF or SCR warning","Higher NOx on one exhaust branch","Possible derate or countdown to no-restart"],2,3,["P208E","P2050","P2051","P2052"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2090:['"B" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)',"P2090 refers to actuator B, on engines with twin phasers the exhaust camshaft valve, on bank 1. What Low means depends on how the ECM drives the solenoid. GM's usual high-side output flags a ground short while the valve is energised; the 3.6 L LFX V6 (19OBDG03B) sets P2090 after 20 of 25 samples as Type A, the 2018 hybrid table 18OBDG02 as Type B.",["Exhaust valve control wire shorted to ground or engine block","Shorted coil in the exhaust oil control valve","Damaged or oil-soaked valve connector"],["Engine warning lamp on, immediately on some GM V6 engines","Slightly higher consumption and emissions at part load"],2,3,["P2091","P2088","P2094","P0013","P0014","P0015"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2091:['"B" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 1)',"P2091 says the control circuit of actuator B on bank 1, normally the exhaust phaser valve, sits too high. GM's high-side version on the 3.6 L LFX checks for a short to supply while the output is off and, like P2090, treats it as Type A after 20 of 25 samples; 18OBDG02 uses Type B.",["Exhaust valve control wire touching a supply wire","Incorrect splice or pin swap after earlier wiring repair","Failed output stage in the ECM"],["Engine warning lamp on","Exhaust cam stays at default angle, slightly reduced performance"],2,3,["P2090","P2089","P2095","P0013","P0014","P0015"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2092:['"A" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)',"P2092 is the Low fault of the intake phaser valve (actuator A) on bank 2, which exists only on V and boxer engines with a separate valve per bank. Bank 2 is the side without cylinder 1. GM's 3.6 L LFX V6 in table 19OBDG03B checks this output with the high-side logic known from bank 1: a short to ground while energised, below 0.5 ohms, 20 bad samples out of 25, Type A, lamp in the first trip.",["Bank 2 intake valve wire shorted to ground on the cylinder head","Shorted coil in the bank 2 intake oil control valve","Oil inside the valve connector"],["Engine warning lamp on, immediately on GM LFX","Uneven running between banks, weaker torque"],2,3,["P2093","P2088","P2094","P0020","P0021","P0022"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2093:['"A" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 2)',"P2093 reports too high a level on the control line of the bank 2 intake phaser valve (actuator A). Table 23OBDG07 shows why High and Low are not tied to one wiring fault: that GM controller switches the valve on the ground side, so it checks for voltage with the driver switched on and calls it a short to power after 1 s, with the lamp after two trips.",["Bank 2 intake valve wire shorted to an ignition or injector feed","Fault in a shared engine harness connector","ECM output stage defective"],["Engine warning lamp on","Bank 2 intake timing fixed, reduced low-speed torque"],2,3,["P2092","P2089","P2095","P0020","P0021","P0022"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2094:['"B" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)',"P2094 belongs to the fourth phaser valve of a twin-phaser V engine: actuator B, the exhaust camshaft, on bank 2. It is therefore absent on single-cam pushrod V8s and on inline engines. On GM's 3.6 L LFX the high-side output is checked for a ground short while on and treated as Type A after 20 out of 25 samples of 250 ms (19OBDG03B).",["Bank 2 exhaust valve wire shorted to ground","Shorted coil in the bank 2 exhaust oil control valve","Insulation damaged by heat near the exhaust manifold"],["Engine warning lamp on","Slight loss of efficiency, higher part-load emissions"],2,3,["P2095","P2090","P2092","P0023","P0024","P0025"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2095:['"B" Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 2)',"P2095 closes the series: the bank 2 exhaust phaser valve (actuator B) shows a high level on its control line. For the 3.6 L LFX, GM table 19OBDG03B describes a high-side driver that finds a short to supply with the output off and sets a Type A code after 20 failures in 25 samples.",["Bank 2 exhaust valve wire shorted to a supply wire","Bridged pins in the valve or engine harness connector","ECM output stage defective"],["Engine warning lamp on","Exhaust cam on bank 2 fixed, minor drop in performance"],2,3,["P2094","P2091","P2093","P0023","P0024","P0025"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2096:["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Lean (Bank 1)","Petrol engines run a slow outer control loop on the oxygen sensor behind the catalyst that shifts the mixture target of the front sensor. P2096 means this post-catalyst trim on bank 1 has hit its limit in the lean direction. The name describes the correction, not the engine: the rear sensor keeps reporting rich exhaust, so the loop keeps taking fuel away.",["Rear oxygen sensor skewed rich, for example a contaminated reference air duct","Front sensor reading lean, so the engine actually runs rich","Calibration issue fixed by an ECM update","New catalyst not yet broken in"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2097","P2098","P0420","P0136","P0172"],""],P2097:["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Rich (Bank 1)","P2097 is the opposite limit of the post-catalyst trim on bank 1: the rear oxygen sensor keeps reporting lean exhaust, so the outer loop keeps adding fuel until it reaches its rich limit. GM's Bosch-based 2005 V6 sets it for a correction above +0.03 lambda; GM's 2018 four-cylinders list it as the high limit, with the integral offset at +99 % and total offset at +50 % or more (Type B);",["Exhaust leak ahead of the rear oxygen sensor drawing in air","Rear oxygen sensor skewed lean or aged","Calibration issue fixed by an ECM update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P2096","P2099","P0420","P0137","P0171"],""],P2098:["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Lean (Bank 2)","P2098 is the bank 2 version of P2096 on V and flat engines with a catalyst and rear oxygen sensor per bank. The post-catalyst trim of bank 2 has reached its lean-side limit because the rear sensor of that bank keeps reporting rich exhaust. Ford monitors both banks the same way and sets the code 5 s after the bank 2 rear bias trim reaches -0.083;",["Bank 2 rear oxygen sensor skewed rich","Bank 2 front sensor reading lean"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2096","P2099","P0430","P0175"],""],P2099:["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Rich (Bank 2)","P2099 is the bank 2 counterpart of P2097: the rear oxygen sensor of bank 2 keeps reporting lean exhaust, so the post-catalyst trim of that bank adds fuel until it reaches its rich-side limit. Ford sets it 5 s after the bank 2 rear bias trim reaches +0.087, with the closed loop running, coolant between 160 and 250 °F and at least 15 % fuel in the tank;",["Exhaust leak ahead of the bank 2 rear sensor","Bank 2 rear oxygen sensor skewed lean or aged"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P2097","P2098","P0430","P0174"],""],P209A:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit","Air-assisted DEF dosing, as in Bosch's first Denoxtronic generation of 2004, mixes the fluid with compressed air before it reaches the exhaust, and a pressure sensor confirms that this air is there. A second sensor B can sit in another air branch or serve as a cross-check for sensor A. P209A is the general circuit fault of sensor B, set when its signal or supply cannot be evaluated at all;",["Corroded or loose connector at sensor B, often from DEF residue or road spray","Reference voltage or ground of the sensor interrupted or out of range","Internal electronic failure of pressure sensor B","Input stage in the dosing control unit defective"],["Malfunction indicator lamp or SCR warning on","DEF dosing suspended, higher NOx output","Engine power derate or inducement countdown on trucks"],2,3,["P209B","P209C","P209D","P209E","P2037"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P209B:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","Here the wiring of air pressure sensor B is intact and the voltage lies inside its valid band, yet the reported pressure makes no sense for the moment. Typical checks compare the value with the switching state of the air supply: pressure must rise when air is released to the mixing chamber and fall back when it is shut off, and with the system at rest it should sit near ambient.",["Sensor B drifting or responding sluggishly","Leak in the atomizing air line between valve and dosing module","Sensing port blocked by urea crystals or dirt","Air supply valve sticking, so the expected pressure change does not occur"],["Check engine or SCR warning lamp","Dosing reduced or stopped, possible NOx efficiency codes later","No noticeable change in driving until an inducement starts"],3,3,["P209A","P209C","P209D","P209E","P2038"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P209C:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","P209C means the signal of the second air pressure sensor in an air-assisted DEF system has dropped below the lowest voltage a working sensor can deliver. With common three-wire pressure sensors this points to a signal wire shorted to ground, a lost 5 V reference or a sensor failed internally; with some input circuits an open signal line also reads low.",["Signal wire chafed through and touching ground","5 V sensor supply missing, for example pulled down by another sensor on the same rail","Pressure sensor B internally shorted"],["MIL or SCR warning on","Live data shows pressure at or below zero regardless of air supply","DEF dosing switched off"],2,3,["P209A","P209D","P209B","P2039"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P209D:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","With P209D the second air pressure sensor reports a voltage above the top of its usable range, close to the supply or battery level. A real air pressure that high is not possible in the system, so the controller treats the value as an electrical fault.",["Sensor ground open at the connector or splice","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor B output stage failed high"],["Warning lamp on, dosing stopped","Displayed air pressure stays at an impossibly high value","Inducement countdown on heavy vehicles if not repaired"],2,3,["P209A","P209C","P209B","P2040"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P209E:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A/B Correlation","When an air-assisted DEF system carries two air pressure sensors, the controller can compare them under conditions where both should read alike, for instance with the air supply shut and the lines vented to ambient, or at a steady dosing point. P209E is set when the two values stay apart by more than the calibrated margin even though each lies within its own electrical range.",["One of the two sensors drifted; compare both against a reference gauge","Restriction or crystal build-up in only one air branch","Leak in the air path between the two measuring points","Replacement sensor with a different pressure range fitted"],["SCR or engine warning lamp on","Live data shows clearly different values for sensors A and B at rest","Reduced or suspended DEF dosing"],3,3,["P2038","P209B","P2037","P209A"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P209F:["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit Performance","DEF freezes at about minus 11 °C, so the tank is heated electrically or by engine coolant. P209F is not about a broken wire, which P202A to P202C report, but about the heating not behaving as expected: the tank does not warm up in the allowed time, or the heater or its valve runs too hot. Deutz uses the code on its MD1 controller as tank heater overtemperature with unknown cause (SPN 520312, FMI 11).",["Control unit software detecting a fault that is not there (FCA bulletins 18-091-16, 08-076-26)","Heater element partly degraded or poorly coupled to the fluid","Coolant heating valve sticking on coolant-heated tanks","Tank temperature sensor reading wrong, so heating looks ineffective"],["MIL and DEF system message, mostly in cold weather","Frozen DEF not thawed in time, dosing delayed after cold start","Speed limitation if the fault persists"],2,3,["P202A","P202B","P202C","P205B","P20B9"],"גוף חימום מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P20A0:["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Circuit/Open","After the engine stops, many airless DEF systems suck the fluid out of the line and injector back into the tank so that nothing freezes there. In Bosch's Denoxtronic 2.2 this is done by a 4/2-way valve in the supply module that reverses the flow. P20A0 concerns the drive circuit of this valve, chiefly an interruption.",["Coil of the purge or reversing valve open","Connector at the supply module loose or corroded by DEF","Wire to the valve broken","Output stage in the engine or dosing control unit defective"],["MIL on (GM Type A, first trip)","DEF system or emission service message","Risk of frozen DEF line or injector in winter"],2,3,["P20A1","P20A2","P20A3","P20A5","P208A"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P20A1:["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Performance","P20A1 judges the valve by its effect rather than its wiring. When the purge valve switches the pump into reverse, the pressure in the DEF line must drop. GM's 6.6 L Duramax (LML/LGH, tables 14OBDG10 and 16OBDG08) watches this pressure reduction phase: if the pump pressure at its end is less than 50 kPa below the value at its start, the code is stored, Type A, so the MIL comes on in the first trip.",["Reversing valve in the supply module not shifting, often from crystallized DEF","Dosing control unit software detecting falsely (Hino SB-16-015)","Return or suction path blocked so pressure cannot drop","DEF pressure sensor reading wrong during the test"],["MIL on after shutdown and restart","DEF warning message, possibly with other pump codes","Line not emptied, frost damage possible"],3,3,["P20A0","P20A4","P20A5","P204B","P24DC"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P20A2:["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Circuit Low","The purge valve that reverses the DEF flow at shutdown is usually switched on the ground side. P20A2 reports that its control line is pulled too low, typically a short to ground somewhere between the driver and the coil, which would switch the valve on unintentionally or keep the driver from sensing it.",["Control wire chafed against the frame or tank bracket","Moisture or DEF in the valve connector creating a leakage path","Valve coil shorted to its housing"],["MIL on at once (GM Type A)","Service emission or DEF system message","Dosing possibly disabled"],2,3,["P20A0","P20A3","P20A1","P24DD"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P20A3:["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Circuit High","P20A3 is the high-side fault of the purge valve circuit: the line carries voltage or current where it should not. GM detects it on the 6.6 L Duramax while the low-side driver is switched on; an impedance of less than 0.5 Ω to controller power lasting 3 s triggers it as a Type A fault.",["Valve coil with shorted windings drawing excessive current","Control wire shorted to a battery-fed conductor","Damaged or DEF-contaminated connector bridging pins"],["MIL on in the first trip (GM Type A)","DEF warning and possibly further pump codes","In frost, risk of DEF freezing in the line"],2,3,["P20A0","P20A2","P20A1","P24DE"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P20A4:["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Stuck Open","Stuck open means the purge valve stays in, or leaks into, its emptying position while the system is supposed to dose. Part of the pump output then flows back toward the tank, so working pressure builds slowly, collapses after the pump stops or needs a high pump duty to hold. No manufacturer documents P20A4 publicly;",["Worn or contaminated valve seat leaking internally in the supply module","Urea crystals holding the valve in the purge position","Valve energized permanently by a driver or wiring fault"],["Warning lamp on, often with low DEF pressure codes","Slow pressure build-up after start","Higher NOx, possibly SCR efficiency codes"],3,3,["P20A5","P20A1","P20E8","P24DF"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P20A5:["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Stuck Closed","Stuck closed is the failure in which the purge valve does not switch to the reverse position when the system wants to empty the line. For the CNRB engine of the 2014 Touareg, Volkswagen bases P20A5 on the pressure difference between the start of the pressure reduction and the current value.",["Control module software (Ford 6.7 L, reprogram the glow dosing module)","Valve jammed in the delivery position by crystallized DEF","Return line to the tank kinked or blocked","DEF pressure sensor frozen at one value"],["MIL on, often found after a shutdown cycle","No change in driveability (Ford software case)","Frost damage to line or injector if a real valve fault persists"],3,3,["P20A4","P20A1","P20A0","P24E0"],"שסתום בקרת טיהור אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקוע במצב סגור"],P20A6:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Control Valve Circuit/Open","In an air-assisted DEF system the compressed air must reach the mixing point at a defined pressure, whether it comes from the vehicle's brake air supply or from a separate compressor. A solenoid valve sets or switches this air pressure. P20A6 marks an open circuit in its control: the controller commands the valve, but no current flows, so the atomizing air cannot be regulated.",["Solenoid coil of the air pressure control valve open","Connector unplugged or wire broken near the valve","Fuse or supply feed for the valve missing"],["SCR warning lamp or MIL on","Dosing stops for lack of atomizing air","Power derate on heavy vehicles"],2,3,["P20A7","P20A8","P20A9","P2059"],"שסתום בקרת לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P20A7:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Control Valve Performance","With P20A7 the air pressure control valve is electrically fine, but the air pressure it should produce does not appear. The check relies on the air pressure sensor: after the valve is opened or its duty changed, the measured value must reach the target band within a set time. If pressure stays too low, overshoots or reacts sluggishly, the valve is judged ineffective. No manufacturer documents P20A7 publicly;",["Valve worn or contaminated with oil, water or urea deposits from the air supply","Insufficient supply pressure from the vehicle air system or compressor","Leaking air line or fitting downstream of the valve","Air pressure sensor reading wrong"],["SCR warning, often together with air pressure codes","Poor atomization, possible deposits in the exhaust pipe","Rising NOx and later efficiency faults"],3,3,["P20A6","P20AA","P20AB","P2038"],"שסתום בקרת לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P20A8:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Control Valve Circuit Low","P20A8 says the air pressure control valve's drive circuit sits at too low a level, which normally means a short to ground. Depending on whether the valve is switched on the high or the low side, this either stops the valve from opening at all or energizes it without command. In both cases the controller loses control of the atomizing air.",["Harness chafed through to ground along the frame","Solenoid coil shorted to the valve body","Water in the connector creating a path to ground"],["MIL or SCR lamp on","Blown fuse possible on high-side switched valves","Dosing stopped, derate on trucks"],2,3,["P20A6","P20A9","P20A7","P2060"],"שסתום בקרת לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P20A9:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Control Valve Circuit High","If the control line of the air pressure control valve shows battery voltage or excessive current where it should not, P20A9 is stored. A wire touching a positive feed, a coil with shorted turns or a bridged connector can cause it. On a low-side driven valve the coil would then be live permanently; on a high-side driver the output often detects overcurrent and shuts down.",["Coil with shorted turns causing overcurrent","Control wire shorted to a positive feed in the harness","Output stage in the dosing control unit defective"],["Warning lamp on","Air pressure uncontrolled, often too high or permanently on","DEF dosing suspended"],2,3,["P20A6","P20A8","P20AA","P2061"],"שסתום בקרת לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P20AA:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Control Valve Stuck Open","P20AA describes a mechanical condition: the air pressure control valve lets air through even when it is commanded closed or to a lower setting. The air pressure sensor then shows pressure in phases where it should have fallen, for example after shutdown or during dosing pauses.",["Debris, water or oil from the air system on the valve seat","Worn valve seal or spring","Valve held open electrically by a wiring or driver fault"],["SCR warning lamp","Air pressure remains present with the valve commanded closed","Audible air flow at the dosing module, compressor runs more often"],2,1,["P20AB","P20A7","P20A6","P2037"],"שסתום בקרת לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P20AB:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Control Valve Stuck Closed","The opposite of P20AA: the air pressure control valve does not open although the controller commands it, so no atomizing air reaches the DEF dosing point. The air pressure sensor stays near ambient during dosing requests. Without air, an air-assisted dosing module cannot spray the fluid into fine droplets, and the risk of liquid DEF and deposits in the exhaust grows;",["Valve seized by corrosion or deposits","No supply pressure, for example low air reservoir or closed protection valve","Air line frozen with condensate or kinked"],["MIL or SCR warning on","Air pressure stays at zero when dosing is requested","Power derate or inducement on trucks"],2,3,["P20AA","P20A7","P20A6","P2059"],"שסתום בקרת לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב סגור"],P20AC:["Reductant Metering Unit Temperature Sensor Circuit","P20AC is the general circuit code for the temperature sensor built into the reductant metering unit, meaning the DEF supply or dosing module that pressurises the fluid. The control unit typically relies on this value to judge whether the module has thawed and may start pumping. The code stands for an electrical fault the software cannot assign to a low or high signal;",["Corroded or loose connector at the DEF supply/metering module","Damaged sensor wiring between module and control unit","Temperature sensor inside the metering unit failed (usually replaced with the module)","Input fault in the dosing or engine control unit"],["Malfunction indicator or DEF/SCR warning lamp on","Dosing delayed or stopped in cold weather","Inducement countdown with speed or restart limit"],2,3,["P20AD","P20AE","P20AF","P20B0","P2042","P205B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P20AD:["Reductant Metering Unit Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P20AD covers a metering unit temperature reading that is electrically valid but does not make sense. A typical check compares it after a long cold soak with other temperatures that ought to agree, or watches whether it climbs once the module heater or warm coolant has had time to act.",["Temperature sensor in the metering unit drifted (reads plausible but wrong)","Comparison sensor (DEF tank or coolant temperature) itself faulty","Contact resistance in the connector shifting the signal","Module heating or coolant heating not working, so the expected rise never comes"],["Warning lamp after a cold start or longer drive","DEF dosing starts late or not at all in winter","Live data shows module temperature out of line with tank and coolant"],2,3,["P20AC","P20AE","P20AF","P20B2","P2043","P205C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P20AE:["Reductant Metering Unit Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P20AE is stored when the signal of the metering unit temperature sensor falls below its valid band. If the sensor is an NTC thermistor, the common design, though no maker confirms it publicly for this part, a low voltage stands for a very high indicated temperature. Typical reasons are then a signal wire chafed through to ground, moisture or DEF crystals bridging the connector pins, or a shorted sensor element.",["Signal wire shorted to ground (chafing near tank or frame)","Water or DEF residue bridging the connector pins","Sensor element in the metering unit shorted"],["Warning lamp on immediately after key-on","Module temperature shown far too hot in live data","DEF dosing suspended, inducement countdown possible"],2,3,["P20AC","P20AD","P20AF","P20B0","P2044"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P20AF:["Reductant Metering Unit Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P20AF means the metering unit temperature signal has risen above its permitted band. For an NTC thermistor, the likely design though not publicly confirmed for this part, that looks like an extremely cold module. Electrically it is usually an open signal or ground wire, a terminal backed out of the connector or a short to a voltage source.",["Open signal or ground wire to the temperature sensor","DEF intrusion and corrosion in the pump connector or harness","Sensor element in the metering unit open","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage"],["Module temperature shown far below ambient in live data","DEF warning and delayed or missing dosing","Further SCR codes if the harness is corroded"],2,3,["P20AC","P20AD","P20AE","P20B0","P2045"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P20B0:["Reductant Metering Unit Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P20B0 flags a metering unit temperature signal that jumps or drops out for brief moments instead of failing steadily. Housing, pump and fluid store a lot of heat, so the real temperature cannot change in leaps; the software treats such steps as a signal defect. Loose terminals, a harness rubbing against the frame near the tank and connectors exposed to road splash and thermal cycling are the main suspects.",["Loose or spread terminal in the module connector","Harness chafing intermittently against frame or tank bracket","Moisture entering the connector during wet or freezing conditions"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Temperature value jumping in live data","Fault often not reproducible in the workshop"],2,3,["P20AC","P20AD","P20AE","P20AF","P205E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P20B1:["Reductant Heater Coolant Control Valve Circuit/Open","Many heavy-duty SCR systems thaw the DEF tank and supply module with engine coolant, and an electrically switched valve decides when that warm coolant may circulate; Bosch offers its larger supply modules with either electric or cooling-water heating. P20B1 is set when the control unit finds the drive circuit of this valve open or otherwise defective. No manufacturer documents P20B1 publicly.",["Valve connector unplugged, loose or corroded","Open solenoid coil in the coolant valve","Broken wire between control unit and valve"],["Malfunction indicator and SCR warning on","DEF thaws slowly or not at all in cold weather","Valve does not click during an actuator test"],2,3,["P20B2","P20B3","P20B4","P202A","P205B"],"שסתום בקרת נוזל קירור גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P20B2:["Reductant Heater Coolant Control Valve Performance/Stuck Open","P20B2 is a functional fault of the coolant valve that heats the reductant system: the circuit is intact, but temperatures do not follow the commanded valve position, most often because coolant keeps flowing while the valve should be shut. Hino uses the code in its dosing control unit and covers it in tech tip TT-16-014 for 2011–2017 conventional and 2013–2017 cab-over trucks.",["Wrong DEF tank or pump temperature input misleading the valve check","Coolant valve mechanically stuck open (deposits, debris)","Valve test blocked by other stored SCR faults, valve wrongly condemned"],["Malfunction indicator with no other SCR fault stored","DEF tank temperature runs unusually high","Possible engine power restriction if left unrepaired"],2,3,["P20B1","P20B3","P20B4","P205C","P20AD","P0116"],"שסתום בקרת נוזל קירור גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע פתוח"],P20B3:["Reductant Heater Coolant Control Valve Circuit Low","P20B3 reports a low reading on the control line of the coolant valve that feeds the DEF heating, the classic picture of a control wire shorted to ground or a solenoid with shorted turns. Depending on how the output stage is wired, the valve then stays permanently energised or never responds, so the DEF can get too warm in summer or remain frozen in winter. No manufacturer is known to describe P20B3 publicly;",["Valve control wire shorted to ground","Valve solenoid with shorted turns (low resistance)","Coolant or DEF inside the valve connector"],["Malfunction indicator and SCR warning on","DEF tank overheats or does not thaw, depending on valve position"],2,3,["P20B1","P20B2","P20B4"],"שסתום בקרת נוזל קירור גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P20B4:["Reductant Heater Coolant Control Valve Circuit High","P20B4 is the opposite electrical case to P20B3: the drive circuit of the reductant heater coolant valve reads too high, which points to a short to battery voltage on the control line or, with certain driver designs, an interrupted ground return. The control unit can then no longer switch the valve, and the heating loop stays in whatever position the valve spring holds.",["Valve control wire shorted to battery voltage","Open ground return of the valve circuit","Output stage in the control unit defective"],["Malfunction indicator and SCR warning on","Valve cannot be actuated in an output test","Slow DEF thaw in winter"],2,3,["P20B1","P20B2","P20B3"],"שסתום בקרת נוזל קירור גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P20B5:["Reductant Metering Unit Heater Control Circuit/Open","P20B5 concerns the electric heater inside the reductant metering unit, the element that keeps the pump module from freezing. The control unit sets it when this heater circuit is open or otherwise broken.",["Heater element in the metering unit burnt out (usually module replacement)","Broken heater supply or ground wire","Corroded heater terminals at the module connector"],["Warning lamp mainly in cold weather","DEF dosing starts late after a cold start","Inducement countdown possible"],3,3,["P20B6","P20B7","P20B8","P20B9","P202A"],"גוף חימום יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20B6:["Reductant Metering Unit Heater Control Circuit Performance","P20B6 is the functional check of the metering unit heater circuit: wiring and driver pass the electrical tests, yet the heating falls short of what the control unit expects, for instance the module temperature barely rises during a commanded heating phase or the current drifts away from its target.",["Aged heater element with reduced output","Metering unit temperature sensor reporting a wrong value","Low supply voltage to the heater (weak battery, poor ground)"],["Warning lamp after cold starts only","Long delay before DEF dosing begins in frost"],3,3,["P20B5","P20B7","P20B8","P20BA","P209F"],"גוף חימום יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P20B7:["Reductant Metering Unit Heater Control Circuit Low","P20B7 means the metering unit heater circuit reads low. Volkswagen gives this a concrete meaning for the 2014 Touareg CNRB: the control unit checks heater conductance at the start of heating and flags P20B7 below 0.33 siemens, so the element shows more than about 3 ohms; further stages at 0.18 and 0.04 siemens follow.",["Heater element resistance too high (aged or partly damaged)","Contact resistance at the heater terminals","Heater wire partly broken (few strands left)"],["Warning lamp at the start of a cold-weather heating phase","DEF dosing delayed in winter"],3,3,["P20B5","P20B6","P20B8","P20BB"],"גוף חימום יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20B8:["Reductant Metering Unit Heater Control Circuit High","P20B8 marks the upper limit of the metering unit heater circuit. The 2014 Touareg CNRB table from Volkswagen sets it when the conductance measured at heating start exceeds 0.74 siemens, meaning the element is below about 1.35 ohms, with additional limits at 0.96 and 0.52 siemens.",["Heater element internally shorted (too low resistance)","Heater wires chafed and touching each other","DEF or water bridging the heater terminals"],["Warning lamp as soon as heating is requested","Heater switched off, DEF stays frozen longer","Possibly a blown heater fuse"],3,3,["P20B5","P20B6","P20B7","P20BC"],"גוף חימום יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20B9:["Reductant Heater A Control Circuit/Open","P20B9 flags an open or broken control circuit for reductant heater A, one of the electric elements that keep diesel exhaust fluid liquid in winter. Which element carries the letter A differs by maker: GM's 2025 DEF tables call it heater 1, the tank heater; Ford links the code to the pump/heater assembly in the tank, Deutz to the suction line heater.",["Water or DEF residue inside the heater or tank harness connectors (Ford TSB 21-2336)","Heater A element burnt out, so resistance is far above specification","Broken supply or return wire between control module and heater","Heater output stage in the DEF or engine control module defective"],["Check engine light, often first noticed in cold weather","DEF dosing starts late or not at all after a cold start","DEF system warning followed by a countdown to a speed limit"],2,3,["P20BA","P20BB","P20BC","P20BD","P20C1","P20C5","P21DD"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20BA:["Reductant Heater A Control Circuit Performance","P20BA is the plausibility test for heater A: the circuit is intact, yet the current, resistance or power the element takes does not match the command. GM's 2025 DEF tables compute the resistance of heater 1, the tank heater, and fail it below 1.00 or above 1.80 ohms, or when power strays more than 45 W from the request, after 8 s as Type A; the 2018 tables use a 1.05–1.93 ohm window.",["Aged heater element whose resistance has drifted out of the allowed window","Corroded or loose heater terminals adding resistance under load","Control software setting the code without a defect (FCA 18-028-14 reflash)","DEF pump unable to build pressure because of swapped or blocked lines (Volvo/Mack KC-4)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp with DEF system message","DEF tank stays cold or frozen in winter although the engine is warm","Possible speed limitation after the inducement countdown"],3,3,["P20B9","P20BB","P20BC","P20BE","P20C2","P20C6","P214F","P21DD"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P20BB:["Reductant Heater A Control Circuit Low","A low reading on the heater A control circuit usually means the output or its wire is grounded, or the element pulls far more current than it should. GM's 2025 DEF module checks heater 1 (tank heater 1) in both states: switched on, a low-side drain voltage above 0.45 V or a load current above 95 A counts; switched off, the high-side voltage sitting in a low band near 0.5–0.6 V.",["Heater A wire chafed through and touching ground","Internal short in the heater element, drawing excessive current","DEF control module calibration setting the code falsely (GM 22-NA-112)","Moisture bridging heater pins to ground in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, possibly with a blown heater fuse","Message that speed will be reduced if the system is not serviced","No DEF heating, so dosing is delayed in frost"],2,3,["P20B9","P20BA","P20BC","P20BF","P20C3","P20C7","P214F"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20BC:["Reductant Heater A Control Circuit High","P20BC means the heater A control circuit reads high: the wire or output has picked up battery voltage, so the element may run when it should be off or cannot be switched at all. GM's 2025 DEF tables spot this on heater 1 (tank heater 1) mostly in the off state, when the high-side voltage lies between roughly 2 and 4.3 V instead of near zero; Type A after a 2 s debounce.",["Heater A control wire shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","DEF control unit software fault (FCA 08-076-26 for 2025 Cummins Ram)","Heater output stage or relay stuck switched on"],["Check engine light and DEF system warning","Heater may stay energized, risking overheating or a drained battery","Reduced power or speed limit once the inducement starts"],2,3,["P20B9","P20BA","P20BB","P20C0","P20C4","P20C8","P202C"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20BD:["Reductant Heater B Control Circuit/Open","Heater B's control circuit is open. In GM's tables heater 2 is the DEF line heater; the 2025 version detects the open state with the output off and sets a Type A code after two seconds, while the 2018 version relies on an open status reported by the DEF control module with battery voltage above 11 V. Deutz assigns B to the pressure line heater, the hose from pump to dosing valve.",["Heating wire in the pressure line broken (line assembly replacement)","Corroded or unplugged line heater connector","Harness to the line heater damaged along the frame rail"],["Warning lamp, especially after cold nights","DEF pressure builds slowly or not at all in frost","Inducement countdown with eventual speed limit"],2,3,["P20BE","P20BF","P20C0","P20B9","P20C1","P20C5","P221C"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20BE:["Reductant Heater B Control Circuit Performance","P20BE judges whether heater B, in most designs the heated pressure line, behaves as expected once the wiring itself checks out. GM's 2025 DEF tables flag line heater resistance below 2.80 or above 7.50 ohms, or a power error above 16.5 W, after 8 s (Type A); the 2018 tables accept a voltage-to-current ratio only between 1.51 and 3.57 ohms.",["Pressure line heating wire degraded, resistance outside the window","High-resistance joint at the line heater connector","Engine control software setting the code erroneously (FCA 18-028-14)","Low heater supply voltage distorting the current measurement"],["Malfunction indicator lamp after a heating phase","Ice in the pressure line on cold starts, dosing late","Possible NOx efficiency codes as a consequence"],2,3,["P20BD","P20BF","P20C0","P20BA","P20C2","P20C6","P221C","P221D"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P20BF:["Reductant Heater B Control Circuit Low","For heater B the code stands for a grounded control circuit or an overcurrent. Ford, where B is the pressure line heater, sets it when circuit 2 draws more than 15 A with the power stage on; the glow plug module can report such a short within 250 ms.",["Line heater wire chafed on the frame and grounded","Water in the line heater connector creating a path to ground","Internal short in the heated pressure line"],["Check engine light, sometimes with a blown fuse","DEF pressure fault codes in cold weather","Speed limitation if the fault persists"],2,3,["P20BD","P20BE","P20C0","P20BB","P20C3","P20C7","P221D"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20C0:["Reductant Heater B Control Circuit High","P20C0 reports that heater B's control circuit is high, typically a wire touching a battery feed or a driver that will not switch off. On Ford diesels B is the pressure line heater: with the power stage off, a current below 3 A while the output still carries over 5 V triggers it, and the glow plug module flags the condition in 250 ms.",["Line heater control wire shorted to a positive feed","Heater output stage in the DEF, engine or glow plug module stuck on","Bridged pins in a shared connector next to a supply terminal"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and DEF warning","Line heater may stay on with the engine off, draining the battery","Frozen pressure line once the module disables the heater"],2,3,["P20BD","P20BE","P20BF","P20BC","P20C4","P20C8","P221D"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20C1:["Reductant Heater C Control Circuit/Open","Heater C's control circuit is interrupted. Where the third element sits again depends on the maker: GM's 2025 DEF tables make heater 3 a second tank heater and test it like the others (output off, 2 s, Type A); Deutz assigns C to the return line heater; FCA's EcoDiesel has a heater 3 of its own.",["Heating circuit in the line or tank module open (resistance check at the connector)","Unplugged or corroded heater C connector","Glow plug control module fault where it drives the DEF heaters (GM LML)"],["Warning lamp mainly after cold soaks","DEF dosing delayed after a cold start","SCR warning and countdown if the fault persists"],2,3,["P20C2","P20C3","P20C4","P20B9","P20BD","P20C5","P221E"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20C2:["Reductant Heater C Control Circuit Performance","P20C2 says heater C is connected but does not take the power the control unit expects. In GM's 2025 tables heater 3, the second tank heater, must measure between 1.50 and 2.60 ohms and stay within 29 W of its command; otherwise Type A after 8 s.",["Heater supply below 5 V because of a weak relay, fuse or feed wire (Ford)","Engine control software setting the code falsely (FCA 18-028-14, 18-019-15)","Heater C element resistance outside its window"],["Check engine light after a heating cycle","DEF thaws slowly in cold weather","Further heater codes if the common supply is weak"],2,3,["P20C1","P20C3","P20C4","P20BA","P20BE","P20C6","P221E","P221F"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P20C3:["Reductant Heater C Control Circuit Low","A low C circuit points to heater C being grounded somewhere or drawing excessive current. GM's 2025 DEF module treats heater 3, its second tank heater, exactly like heaters 1 and 2: a low-band voltage with the output off, or drain voltage and current limits with it on, Type A once 2 s have elapsed.",["Outdated DEF control module calibration on 2020–2022 GM diesel pickups (22-NA-112)","Heater C wire grounded through chafing","Shorted heater C element drawing overcurrent"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, possibly with no real fault present","Driver message that speed will be reduced without service","Unheated tank or line section in frost"],2,3,["P20C1","P20C2","P20C4","P20BB","P20BF","P20C7","P221F"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20C4:["Reductant Heater C Control Circuit High","P20C4 marks heater C's control circuit as high, meaning it sees battery voltage where none belongs. GM's 2025 tables test heater 3, a second tank heater, with the output switched off against a raised voltage window and set a Type A fault after 2 s of persistence. GM's LML documentation from 2014 (6.6 L) has the glow plug module react to over 3.5 V on the heater pin while the heater should be off (Type B).",["Heater C control wire in contact with a battery feed","Heater driver in the DEF or glow plug module stuck on","DEF crystals or moisture bridging pins in the heater connector"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","Battery drained overnight if the heater stays powered","Inducement and speed limit if left unrepaired"],2,3,["P20C1","P20C2","P20C3","P20BC","P20C0","P20C8","P221E"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20C5:["Reductant Heater D Control Circuit/Open","P20C5 covers an open control circuit in reductant heater D, the fourth heating element that only a few SCR layouts carry. Deutz is the one maker found that publishes the code: in its EMR5/MD1 fault list D is the downstream line heater, and P20C5 maps to SPN 520471 with FMI 5, an open or too little current.",["Heating wire in the downstream DEF line burnt out or broken","Loose or corroded heater D connector","Wire break in the harness to heater D"],["Warning lamp in cold weather","Dosing delayed while the downstream line thaws"],2,3,["P20C6","P20C7","P20C8","P20C1","P20BD","P20B9"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20C6:["Reductant Heater D Control Circuit Performance","P20C6 is the functional check of heater D. FCA documents it for the 3.0 L EcoDiesel under the name Reductant Heater 4 Control Circuit Performance: bulletin 18-068-20 reflashed 2017 Ram 1500 engine computers that showed it, and a 2021 STAR case for 2020–2021 Ram 1500, Wrangler and Gladiator notes that it turns up mostly in severe cold, often without a defect.",["False detection in extreme cold with a still-frozen tank (FCA STAR S2118000006)","Outdated engine control software (FCA 18-068-20)","Leaking or blocked DEF supply line to the injector","DEF pump unable to build pressure or injector delivering the wrong quantity"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, mostly after very cold nights","DEF system message, sometimes alongside pressure codes","Often no noticeable change in how the vehicle drives"],2,3,["P20C5","P20C7","P20C8","P20BA","P20BE","P20C2","P20E8","P208B"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ D — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P20C7:["Reductant Heater D Control Circuit Low","P20C7 reports that heater D's control circuit is grounded or overloaded with current. Only Deutz publishes the code: for its downstream line heater (SPN 520471) it maps to FMI 4, a voltage that is too low or a short to a low source. No vehicle maker documents thresholds for heater D.",["Heater D wire chafed through to ground","Water in the heater D connector","Internal short inside the heated downstream line"],["Warning lamp, possibly with a blown fuse","Unheated downstream line and delayed dosing in frost"],2,3,["P20C5","P20C6","P20C8","P20C3","P20BF","P20BB"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20C8:["Reductant Heater D Control Circuit High","Diesel exhaust fluid freezes at about -11 °C, so SCR systems carry several electric heating elements in the tank, pump and lines; which one a maker calls heater D varies. P20C8 reports that the control circuit of heater D reads high, meaning the output or its wiring has contact with battery voltage and the element can no longer be switched as commanded.",["Chafed harness letting the heater D control wire touch a battery-voltage feed","Moisture or DEF residue in the heater connector bridging pins","Internal short inside heater D or its integrated pump or line assembly","Faulty heater output stage in the engine or DEF control module"],["Check engine light and DEF or emission system warning","DEF dosing unavailable in cold weather, NOx warning or later speed limitation","Blown fuses and further unrelated codes when a chafed harness is the cause"],2,3,["P20C5","P20C6","P20C7","P20C4","P20C0","P20BC"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20C9:["Reductant Control Module Requested MIL Illumination","P20C9 is a forwarding code. Some diesel trucks use a separate DEF or SCR control module with its own fault memory; when that module detects an emission-relevant fault it asks the engine module to switch on the check engine lamp, and the engine module records P20C9.",["Emission-relevant SCR fault stored in the DEF control module (heater, pump, pressure, sensor)","Failed upstream NOx sensor reported by the DEF module","Outdated or mismatched software between engine and DEF control module"],["Check engine light with only P20C9 visible on a generic scan tool","DEF or SCR warning lamp, depending on the underlying fault","Possible power derate if the underlying SCR fault triggers inducement"],2,3,["P20FF","P2201","P2206","P2207","P0700","P069E"],""],P20CA:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Leakage","Air-assisted dosing, used mainly on older heavy and medium-duty diesels, mixes diesel exhaust fluid with compressed air from the vehicle's air system and blows the mixture through a nozzle into the exhaust. Airless pump systems in passenger cars and most current light trucks, such as Bosch Denoxtronic 2.2, have no air branch and cannot set this code.",["Leaking air hose or fitting between air supply and dosing unit","Worn seal on the air shut-off or pressure control valve","Leak in the vehicle's compressed-air supply feeding the doser","Cracked or poorly sealed dosing unit housing on the air side"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","Audible hissing near the dosing unit or air lines","Poor DEF atomisation, higher NOx and later engine derate"],2,3,["P20E6","P20E7","P20AA","P20AB","P2037","P2038"],""],P20CB:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Control Circuit/Open","The engine computer checks the drive line of the hydrocarbon doser, a separate valve that sprays diesel into the exhaust ahead of the oxidation catalyst so the particulate filter can be heated for regeneration.",["Corroded or loose connector at the doser, which sits under the vehicle in the exhaust area","Heat- or chafe-damaged wire between engine computer and doser","Open solenoid winding inside the doser","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Particulate filter regeneration does not start or is aborted","Soot load warning and, later, reduced engine power"],2,3,["P20CD","P20CE","P20CC","P20D1","P2697","P2463"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20CC:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Control Performance","Unlike the circuit codes, this one judges what the hydrocarbon doser actually does. On the 6.6 L Duramax LML/LGH, GM table 15OBDG09 sets it when the outlet of the oxidation catalyst runs more than 300 °C hotter than its inlet for 180 s although no regeneration is under way and more than 900 s have passed since the last one; that heat can only come from fuel the doser should not be delivering.",["Doser leaking or dribbling fuel into the exhaust while closed","Coked nozzle tip with distorted spray","Exhaust temperature sensor before or after the catalyst reading wrong"],["Check engine light on","Unexpectedly high exhaust temperatures, possibly white smoke or fuel smell","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P20CB","P20CF","P20D0","P20D2","P2698","P20E2"],"בקרת מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P20CD:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Control Circuit Low","Here the control line of the hydrocarbon doser has a short to ground. GM's diesel tables 18OBDG04 and 25OBDG04A test the output while the driver is off: if the voltage drops below about 2 V, the line is touching ground. GM rates it Type A, which lights the MIL after one trip, and the fault only clears after a calibrated count of good tests or a control-module reset. The LML/LGH Duramax lists it as Type B.",["Control wire chafed through against the frame or exhaust","Water or salt in the doser connector bridging to ground","Internal short in the doser solenoid"],["Check engine light on after a single trip","Doser disabled, no active regeneration","Possible fuel smell or smoke from the exhaust"],2,3,["P20CB","P20CE","P20D3","P2699"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20CE:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Control Circuit High","The control line of the hydrocarbon doser is shorted to battery voltage. GM's diesel tables 18OBDG04 and 25OBDG04A detect it while the driver is switched on: current above roughly 8 to 11 A for a set time, or above about 16 to 22 A at once, counts as a short to power. GM rates it Type B, so the MIL follows after two trips; the LML/LGH Duramax (15OBDG09) uses a voltage check in the on state.",["Control wire touching a powered wire in a damaged harness","Doser solenoid with shorted turns drawing too much current","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Active regeneration not possible","Rising soot load, later reduced power"],2,3,["P20CB","P20CD","P20D4","P269A"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20CF:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Stuck Open","The doser that adds diesel to the exhaust for filter regeneration is judged to stay open, so fuel keeps flowing after the command to close. On Volvo and Mack trucks the nozzle sits right at the turbo outlet and is fed by an AHI module; their troubleshooting guide KC-2157 points first to the fuel supply and then to that module.",["Dirt or deposits holding the doser valve off its seat","Upstream shutoff or dosing module letting fuel through","Calibration error, fixed by a software update"],["Check engine light on","White smoke or strong fuel smell from the exhaust","Very high temperatures at catalyst and filter","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P20D0","P20CC","P20DB","P20D5","P24F6"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P20D0:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Stuck Closed","The exhaust fuel doser is commanded to inject but no fuel gets through, typically because the nozzle tip is plugged. Detection usually relies on line pressure that fails to drop or on too little heat build-up across the oxidation catalyst. Volvo and Mack list P20D0 in their AHI troubleshooting guide KC-2157;",["Nozzle tip clogged with carbon","Dosing module or supply valve not passing fuel","Kinked or blocked fuel line to the nozzle"],["Check engine light on","Regenerations fail or are requested constantly","Soot warning and reduced power"],3,3,["P20CF","P20CC","P20DC","P20D6","P24F7","P2463"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A — תקוע במצב סגור"],P20D1:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector B Control Circuit/Open","Injector B is a second exhaust fuel doser, found only on layouts with two dosing points, for example twin exhaust paths. This code reports a broken control line or open coil on that second unit. No manufacturer documents P20D1 publicly; the logic would mirror injector A, where GM's diesel tables look for an off-state output voltage stuck in a mid band (P20CB, Type B).",["Loose or corroded connector at doser B","Broken wire to doser B","Open solenoid winding in doser B"],["Check engine light on","Regeneration incomplete on the affected exhaust path"],2,3,["P20CB","P20D3","P20D4","P20D2"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20D2:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector B Control Performance","With its wiring intact, the second exhaust fuel doser (B) is not delivering what was asked for: too little heat appears across the catalyst during dosing, or heat appears when it should be idle. No manufacturer documents P20D2 publicly. The comparable check for injector A on GM's 6.6 L Duramax (P20CC, 15OBDG09) watches for the catalyst outlet running far hotter than its inlet outside regeneration.",["Partly coked nozzle on doser B","Low or unstable fuel pressure feeding doser B","Exhaust temperature sensor reading wrong"],["Check engine light on","Longer or more frequent regenerations","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P20CC","P20D1","P20D5","P20D6"],"בקרת מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P20D3:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector B Control Circuit Low","The control line of the second exhaust fuel doser (B) is pulled toward ground. No manufacturer documents P20D3 publicly. For injector A, GM's diesel tables detect this by a switched-off output voltage below about 2 V and treat it as Type A with the MIL after one trip (P20CD), because a grounded line can open the valve without command. A similar strict rating is likely for B.",["Chafed control wire to doser B touching ground","Moisture in the doser B connector","Internal short in doser B"],["Check engine light on","Doser B switched off, regeneration impaired"],2,3,["P20CD","P20D1","P20D4"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20D4:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector B Control Circuit High","On the second exhaust fuel doser (B), the control line sits at or near battery voltage, so the driver cannot pull it low to open the valve. No manufacturer documents P20D4 publicly. For injector A, GM's diesel tables flag excess current in the switched-on state as a short to power and rate it Type B (P20CE). With doser B out of action, the share of the exhaust it serves no longer gets enough heat for regeneration.",["Control wire to doser B shorted to a powered circuit","Shorted turns in the doser B solenoid","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Check engine light on","Regeneration impaired, soot load rising"],2,3,["P20CE","P20D1","P20D3"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20D5:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector B Stuck Open","The second exhaust fuel doser (B) keeps passing fuel after it has been told to shut. No manufacturer documents P20D5 publicly; for the single doser A, Volvo and Mack trace the equivalent code P20CF to the fuel supply or the dosing module, and Ram fixed it on Cummins pickups with software.",["Deposits keeping doser B from sealing","Upstream shutoff valve leaking fuel through","Calibration error in the control software"],["Check engine light on","White smoke or fuel smell","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P20CF","P20D6","P20D2"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P20D6:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector B Stuck Closed","The second exhaust fuel doser (B) fails to deliver fuel even though the control unit commands it open. No manufacturer documents P20D6 publicly. For doser A, Volvo and Mack handle the matching code P20D0 by checking the dosing module and replacing the nozzle, whose tip tends to clog with carbon; the same weak spot applies to B.",["Clogged nozzle tip on doser B","No fuel reaching doser B because of a blocked line or closed supply valve","Mechanically seized valve in doser B"],["Check engine light on","Failed or frequent regenerations","Reduced power once the filter is heavily loaded"],3,3,["P20D0","P20D5","P20D2","P2463"],"מזרק דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P20D7:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Supply Control Circuit/Open","Upstream of the exhaust doser sits a valve that releases fuel to it only when a regeneration is wanted, often called the shutoff or fuel cut valve. This code reports an open in its control circuit. Volvo and Mack store it as P20D713 (failure type 13 = open) and, in troubleshooting guide KC-2157, send the technician to the wiring and connector of the AHI module, where this valve is housed.",["Loose or corroded connector at the dosing module","Broken wire in the dosing module harness","Open coil in the fuel shutoff valve"],["Check engine light on","Active regeneration not possible","Soot warning, later reduced power"],2,3,["P20D9","P20DA","P20D8","P20DB","P20DC","P0005"],"אספקת דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20D8:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Supply Control Performance","The supply valve ahead of the exhaust doser is electrically sound, but the pressure it produces in the feed line does not follow its commands. A typical layout, described in a patent assigned to International Engine, measures that line pressure and uses it both to meter the dose and to diagnose the regulating valve. Hino's J08E manual lists P20D8 among the codes to resolve before chasing a regeneration fault;",["Sluggish or contaminated supply valve","Low feed pressure from a clogged fuel filter or weak low-pressure pump","Line pressure sensor reading off"],["Check engine light on","Regenerations take longer or fail"],3,3,["P20D7","P20DB","P20DC","P20DE","P0005"],"בקרת אספקת דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P20D9:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Supply Control Circuit Low","For the fuel supply valve feeding the exhaust doser, the control line reads too low, which points to a short to ground. Volvo and Mack store P20D900 and, in AHI troubleshooting guide KC-2157, group it with the other electrical faults of the AHI module: check the module's connector and wiring harness.",["Chafed wire in the dosing module harness touching ground","Water in the dosing module connector","Internal short in the supply valve coil"],["Check engine light on","Dosing disabled, no active regeneration"],2,3,["P20D7","P20DA","P20DB","P0006"],"אספקת דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20DA:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Supply Control Circuit High","For the supply valve ahead of the exhaust doser, the control line reads too high, typically because it touches battery voltage or, on some drivers, an open line pulled up internally. Volvo and Mack log it as P20DA00 and list it in guide KC-2157 among the AHI module electrical faults, with the instruction to check that module's wiring and connector.",["Valve control wire shorted to a powered line","Damaged coil in the supply valve","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Check engine light on","Active regeneration not possible"],2,3,["P20D7","P20D9","P20DC","P0007"],"אספקת דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20DB:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Supply Control Stuck Open","The supply valve that should isolate the exhaust doser from the fuel system stays open after being switched off, so the feed line remains pressurized when no regeneration is running. If the doser itself then leaks, fuel can reach the hot exhaust unasked. Ram names P20DB together with P20CF (doser A stuck open) on 2025–2026 Ram 2500/3500 trucks with the 6.7 L Cummins HO, where a PCM software update is the fix.",["Supply or fuel cut valve sticking open from wear or dirt","Detection or control calibration error, fixed by software","Contaminated fuel leaving deposits in the valve"],["Check engine light on","Fuel smell or smoke if the doser also leaks","Long cranking after fuel system work"],3,3,["P20DC","P20CF","P20D7","P20D8","P20DE"],"בקרת אספקת דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P20DC:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Supply Control Stuck Closed","The valve feeding the exhaust doser does not open when a regeneration starts, so the doser receives no fuel. A Hino patent shows how this is recognized: a pressure sensor between the shutoff valve and the dosing valve reads far below a threshold that depends on engine speed. Volvo and Mack list P20DC00 in AHI guide KC-2157 and tell technicians to look at the fuel supply first, then follow the guided diagnostics;",["Clogged fuel filter or water and dirt in the fuel","Supply valve seized shut","Internal fault in the dosing module"],["Check engine light on","Regenerations fail, soot load keeps rising","Reduced power in later stages"],2,3,["P20DB","P20D0","P20D7","P20DF","P0005"],"בקרת אספקת דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — תקוע במצב סגור"],P20DD:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit","The pressure sensor in the feed line of the exhaust doser lets the control unit meter fuel and spot a stuck valve or plugged nozzle. This code is the general circuit fault of that sensor; signal too low, too high and unsteady have their own codes (P20DF, P20E0, P20E1).",["Internally damaged harness to the dosing module and its sensor","Loose or corroded sensor connector","Failed pressure sensor"],["Check engine light on","Active regeneration blocked","Further codes for the reference voltage or the dosing system"],2,3,["P20DE","P20DF","P20E0","P20E1"],"חיישן לחץ דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P20DE:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The doser feed pressure sensor gives a signal inside its electrical limits, yet the value does not fit what the system is doing, for example no pressure rise when the supply valve opens. Hino uses the code widely: SB-18-029 (2017–2019 J08 and J05 trucks, MIL on) has a specific sensor batch replaced, earlier notes blame a fuel cut valve that hangs or dirty fuel clogging a filter, and SB-22-007 swaps a 2020 bubbler…",["Restricted fuel or separator filter from contaminated fuel","Sticking fuel cut or supply valve","Pressure sensor outside its specification","Plugged nozzle or leaking fuel/air line"],["Check engine light on","Regeneration interrupted or blocked","Sometimes further fuel pressure codes such as P0087"],2,3,["P20DD","P20DF","P20E0","P20E1","P20DC","P0087"],"חיישן לחץ דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P20DF:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","The signal of the doser feed pressure sensor sits below its lower limit. Electrically that suggests a grounded signal line or a missing reference voltage. Hino describes its P20DF as the line pressure sensor reading too low and shows that real pressure loss can trigger it too: a fuel cut valve that hangs, or dirty fuel restricting the filter ahead of the dosing injector.",["Real low pressure from a restricted filter or contaminated fuel","Signal wire shorted to ground or reference voltage lost","Fuel cut valve sticking","Outdated detection threshold, fixed by a software update"],["Check engine light on","Regeneration blocked"],2,3,["P20DD","P20DE","P20E0","P20E1","P20DC"],"חיישן לחץ דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P20E0:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit High","The doser feed pressure sensor reports a signal above its upper electrical limit. On a typical three-wire sensor this happens when the signal line is open and pulled up, shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage, or when the ground is lost. Volvo and Mack store it as P20E000 and in guide KC-2157 direct technicians to the sensor's wiring and connector.",["Signal wire open or shorted to reference or battery voltage","Lost sensor ground","Sensor from a faulty production batch"],["Check engine light on","Active regeneration blocked"],2,3,["P20DD","P20DE","P20DF","P20E1"],"חיישן לחץ דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P20E1:["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The signal from the pressure sensor in the doser feed line jumps or drops out for short moments, faster than real line pressure could change. Usual reasons are a loose pin, a cracked wire flexing with engine movement, or moisture in the connector. No manufacturer documents P20E1 publicly.",["Loose or fretted pins at the sensor connector","Wire breaking intermittently from vibration","Internal fault in the pressure sensor"],["Check engine light on, possibly coming and going","Regenerations interrupted"],2,3,["P20DD","P20DE","P20DF","P20E0"],"חיישן לחץ דלק טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P20E2:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 1/2 Correlation (Bank 1)","P20E2 flags that bank 1 exhaust temperature sensors 1 and 2 disagree at a moment when both should show nearly the same value. Sensor 1 usually sits ahead of the oxidation catalyst and sensor 2 behind it.",["Exhaust temperature sensor 1 or 2 drifted or aged (offset reading)","Corroded or loose connector adding resistance to one sensor signal","Sensors swapped or a non-matching replacement part installed","Engine control software needing an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, often with no change in driving","Particulate filter regeneration delayed or blocked","Code returns after a long parking period"],2,1,["P20E3","P20E4","P20E5","P2080","P2084","P0544","P2031"],""],P20E3:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 1/3 Correlation (Bank 1)","P20E3 reports that exhaust temperature sensors 1 and 3 on bank 1 do not agree. In the usual diesel order, sensor 1 measures before the oxidation catalyst and sensor 3 after the particulate filter, so this pair brackets the whole aftertreatment line. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Sensor 1 or sensor 3 reading offset or responding sluggishly","Water or corrosion in the connector of the rear sensor","Exhaust leak near one sensor letting outside air cool its tip"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Particulate filter regeneration postponed","Temperature values of sensors 1 and 3 differ noticeably on a cold engine"],2,1,["P20E2","P20E4","P2080","P242B","P24C2","P242A"],""],P20E4:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 2/3 Correlation (Bank 1)","P20E4 covers the pair around the particulate filter: sensor 2 at the filter inlet and sensor 3 at its outlet on bank 1 no longer agree. GM documents the code for the diesel in table 15OBDG04 (also 14OBDG04): after a soak of at least 28,800 s the start-up values of the filter upstream and downstream sensors are compared against a look-up limit, and a larger gap is a Type B fault.",["Filter inlet or outlet temperature sensor aged by heat cycling","Heat-damaged or corroded sensor connector or lead","Heavy soot or ash deposits on a sensor tip slowing its response"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regenerations aborted or happening more often","Filter loading warning in some vehicles"],2,1,["P20E2","P20E3","P2084","P242B","P2031","P242A"],""],P20E5:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 1/2 Correlation (Bank 2)","P20E5 is the bank 2 counterpart of P20E2: on engines with a separate exhaust and aftertreatment path per cylinder bank, sensors 1 and 2 of the second bank disagree after the system has cooled down. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly; the GM tables that use P20E2 cover single-path diesels.",["Bank 2 sensor 1 or 2 reading offset","Contact resistance in a bank 2 sensor connector","Sensor connectors swapped between banks after a repair"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bank 2 sensors show different values on a cold engine"],2,1,["P20E2","P2082","P0548","P2034","P2086"],""],P20E6:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Too Low","This code belongs to air-assisted DEF dosing, where compressed air carries the fluid to the nozzle and breaks it into fine droplets; airless pump systems in cars and most current pickups do not use it. P20E6 means the air pressure in the dosing branch stays below the minimum the control unit needs while dosing is requested.",["Insufficient air tank pressure from a leak or weak compressor","Air shut-off or pressure control valve not opening","DEF crystals restricting the air side of the dosing unit","Leaking, kinked or blocked air line to the doser"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","DEF dosing reduced or stopped, rising NOx emissions","Engine derate after the inducement period"],2,3,["P20E7","P20CA","P20AB","P2038","P2059"],"לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך נמוך מדי"],P20E7:["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Too High","On air-assisted DEF dosing the control unit regulates the compressed air fed into the mixing chamber so that the nozzle sprays a stable mist. P20E7 is set when the measured air pressure climbs above the permitted upper limit, for instance because the pressure control valve no longer throttles and passes full tank pressure, or because the path downstream of the sensor is narrowed so pressure builds up in front of it.",["Air pressure control valve no longer regulating and passing full supply pressure","DEF crystals or deposits restricting the nozzle or mixing path","Air pressure sensor reading too high"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","Irregular DEF spray, deposits in the exhaust and higher NOx","Engine derate if dosing is shut down"],2,3,["P20E6","P20CA","P20AA","P20A7","P2038"],"לחץ אוויר הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך גבוה מדי"],P20E8:["Reductant Pressure Too Low","Airless DEF systems hold the fluid at a set pressure ahead of the dosing valve with an electric pump, read by a pressure sensor. P20E8 means the measured value stays clearly below that target or cannot be built up at all. Ford's 2023 diesel summary (6.7 L and 3.0 L) sets it when the pressure is more than 200 kPa under setpoint or the pump fails to reach pressure control after five attempts;",["Air in the DEF lines or pump that lost its prime, for example after long storage","Clogged pump inlet, suction tube, filter or tank vent, often from contamination","External leak at a DEF line, connector or the dosing valve","Worn, crystallised or superseded DEF pump unit","Empty or frozen DEF tank"],["Check engine light and DEF system warning message","No DEF dosing, rising NOx and a countdown to speed limitation or no restart","Pump can be heard running longer than usual after key on"],2,3,["P20E9","P208B","P204B","P204C","P20FE","P208E"],"לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך נמוך מדי"],P20E9:["Reductant Pressure Too High","P20E9 is the overpressure counterpart of P20E8: during closed-loop control the DEF pressure ahead of the dosing valve rises clearly above its target. Ford's 2023 diesel summary sets it at more than 150 kPa over setpoint; GM's 18OBDG04 table asks for the same 150 kPa excess while the pump runs below 3,200 rpm (Type A), and GM's 2025 DEF table 25OBDG04A uses a 63 kPa window for 4 s.",["Blocked return path, restricted line or dosing valve not opening properly","Debris in the fluid after a damaged filter seal or dirty refilling","Reductant pressure sensor reading too high","Pump control software needing an update"],["Check engine light and DEF system warning","Dosing shut off, NOx warning and later inducement countdown"],2,3,["P20E8","P20FE","P204B","P204D","P208B"],"לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך גבוה מדי"],P20EA:["Reductant Control Module Power Relay De-Energized Performance - Too Early","Many SCR systems supply the reductant control module, and through it pump and heaters, via a power relay. After the key is switched off the relay should stay energised for a short after-run so the pump can empty the lines and the module can save its learned values, and only then drop out on the module's command. P20EA means the supply disappeared before that point.",["Worn relay contacts or coil interrupting the supply early","Loose fuse, terminal or ground in the relay or module feed","Battery disconnected or voltage collapsing right after shut-off","Reductant control module releasing the relay prematurely"],["Check engine light, often without noticeable driving symptoms","DEF lines not purged, risk of frozen or crystallised lines in winter"],2,1,["P20EB","P068A","P068B","P21C7","P056D"],""],P20EB:["Reductant Control Module Power Relay De-Energized Performance - Too Late","Here the opposite of P20EA happens: after the reductant control module has finished its after-run and released the power relay, voltage is still present on the switched side, so the relay opens late or not at all. Typical reasons are welded contacts, a control line shorted to ground that keeps the coil energised, or a module that never ends its shut-down.",["Welded or sticking relay contacts","Relay control line shorted to ground, keeping the coil energised","Reductant control module or network activity preventing shut-down"],["Check engine light","Battery drained after the vehicle has been parked","DEF pump or relay audible long after switching off"],2,1,["P20EA","P068B","P068A","P21C7","P056D"],""],P20EC:["SCR NOx Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 1)","P20EC means the engine computer has registered a temperature in the SCR catalyst of bank 1 above the limit its washcoat can tolerate. The limit depends on the formulation: vanadium-based SCR material starts to sublimate irreversibly above roughly 550 °C, as Navistar's patent US20190232224 and the US rule 40 CFR 1036.115 both state, and US heavy-duty certification requires engine makers to protect such catalysts from…",["Excess heat release during particulate filter regeneration","Unburnt fuel or oil reaching the exhaust (leaking injector, turbo seal)","SCR temperature sensor reading too high","Regeneration or thermal-management calibration needing an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Regeneration interrupted or power reduced to protect the aftertreatment","Later loss of NOx conversion (follow-up code P20EE)"],3,3,["P20ED","P20F0","P20EE","P200C","P200E","P2428"],"ממיר קטליטי NOx SCR — חום יתר (בנק 1)"],P20ED:["SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 1)","P20ED applies to systems with two SCR stages in series: a small pre-catalyst mounted close to the engine, often with its own dosing unit, ahead of the main SCR brick. The code says this front stage on bank 1 got hotter than permitted.",["Heat from oxidation catalyst or filter regeneration reaching the close-coupled stage","Fuel or oil entering the exhaust upstream of the pre-catalyst","Temperature sensor at the pre-catalyst reading too high"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Front SCR dosing stopped or regeneration interrupted","Higher NOx emissions after a cold start"],3,3,["P20EC","P20EF","P20F1","P200E","P2428"],""],P20EE:["SCR NOx Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","P20EE is the main monitor CARB requires for the NOx-reducing catalyst: the share of NOx removed by the SCR catalyst on bank 1, judged by the NOx sensors before and after it, has fallen below what the system needs. Ford's 2023 6.7 L diesel fails it when cumulative efficiency drops under 55 % with the SCR inlet at 200–320 °C.",["Diluted or contaminated DEF, or a clogged or leaking dosing valve","Upstream or downstream NOx sensor reading wrong","SCR catalyst aged, overheated or poisoned","Exhaust leak between the two NOx sensors","Calibration needing an update (several manufacturer bulletins)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF or exhaust fluid quality warning in the instrument cluster","Speed limitation countdown on some vehicles if the fault persists"],3,3,["P20F2","P20EF","P20EC","P207F","P2200","P2201","P2BAD"],""],P20EF:["SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","P20EF concerns the front stage of an SCR arrangement with two stages on bank 1: the pre-catalyst no longer removes enough NOx. CARB allows catalysts in series to be monitored individually or together; this code is used where the front stage is checked separately, which requires a NOx sensor between the two bricks.",["Front DEF dosing valve clogged, crystallised or leaking","NOx sensor before or between the stages reading wrong","Pre-catalyst thermally aged or poisoned","Poor DEF quality"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Higher NOx at low exhaust temperatures, for example after cold starts"],3,3,["P20EE","P20ED","P20F3","P2200","P2201"],""],P20F0:["SCR NOx Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 2)","P20F0 is the bank 2 version of P20EC: the SCR catalyst in the second exhaust line has been exposed to temperatures above its permitted limit. It presupposes a V engine with one aftertreatment path per bank, which is rare; most diesels merge both banks into one SCR line and use only the bank 1 codes. No manufacturer documents P20F0 publicly.",["Leaking injector or misfire on bank 2 sending fuel into the exhaust","Excess heat during particulate filter regeneration on bank 2","Bank 2 SCR temperature sensor reading too high"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Reduced power or interrupted regeneration to protect the catalyst"],3,3,["P20EC","P20F1","P20F2","P200F","P2429"],"ממיר קטליטי NOx SCR — חום יתר (בנק 2)"],P20F1:["SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 2)","P20F1 reports an over-temperature of the SCR pre-catalyst on bank 2, the close-coupled front stage of a two-stage system in the second exhaust line. Both conditions must be met for the code to exist on a vehicle: separate aftertreatment per bank and a split SCR with a front brick near the turbocharger outlet. No manufacturer documents this combination publicly.",["Fuel slip from bank 2 cylinders (injector leak, misfire, post-injection fault)","Pre-catalyst temperature sensor on bank 2 reading too high","Regeneration heat reaching the front stage"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Front-stage dosing or regeneration suspended"],3,3,["P20ED","P20F0","P20F3","P200F","P2429"],""],P20F2:["SCR NOx Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","P20F2 is the bank 2 twin of P20EE: the main SCR catalyst of the second exhaust line removes less NOx than required, judged by NOx sensors ahead of and behind it. CARB requires the NOx catalyst to be flagged once its conversion loss would push emissions past the regulatory multiple of the standard. No manufacturer documents P20F2 publicly; the widely used P20EE logic shows how such a monitor works.",["Poor DEF quality or bank 2 dosing valve fault","Bank 2 NOx sensor reading wrong","Bank 2 SCR catalyst aged or overheated","Exhaust leak between the bank 2 NOx sensors"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF quality warning, possibly with a countdown to reduced speed"],3,3,["P20EE","P20F3","P20F0","P207F","P2BAD"],""],P20F3:["SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","P20F3 states that the SCR pre-catalyst on bank 2 no longer converts enough NOx. It belongs to engines with a separate aftertreatment line per bank and a two-stage SCR in each, with a NOx sensor between front and main brick so that the front stage can be judged on its own, an option CARB grants for catalysts arranged in series. No manufacturer documents P20F3 publicly;",["Bank 2 front dosing valve blocked or crystallised","NOx sensor between the bank 2 stages reading wrong","Bank 2 pre-catalyst damaged by heat or contamination"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Increased NOx after cold starts"],3,3,["P20EF","P20F2","P20F1","P20EE"],""],P20F4:["Reductant Consumption Too Low","The control unit compares the DEF quantity it commands with what the system actually delivers, judged from tank level, pump effort or the long-term correction the NOx feedback needs. P20F4 means too little fluid is really reaching the exhaust. VW's 2014 Touareg TDI data book sets it once the SCR adaptation value reaches 1.79, so dosing had to be raised far above plan;",["Partly blocked or crystallised dosing valve delivering less than commanded","Air pockets in the injector line, as Mercedes reports for the OM654 Sprinter","Leak in tank, pump or line so less fluid reaches the valve","Dosing control unit software requiring an update"],["Check engine light and DEF warning","DEF tank level falls slower than expected","Higher NOx emissions and, if unresolved, inducement countdown"],2,3,["P20F5","P249D","P208E","P202E","P20E8","P20EE"],"צריכת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך נמוך מדי"],P20F5:["Reductant Consumption Too High","P20F5 is set when more diesel exhaust fluid is used, or has to be corrected away, than the control unit planned. In VW's 2014 Touareg TDI data book the trigger is an SCR adaptation value of 0.51 or lower: the NOx feedback keeps cutting the commanded dose because more fluid evidently reaches the catalyst than intended. GM maps the same idea to P249E (factor below 0.41, Type B).",["Dosing valve dripping or not sealing between pulses","External leak at the valve or its supply line","Pressure sensor reading low, causing excess delivery","Dosing control unit software requiring an update"],["Check engine light and DEF warning","DEF tank empties faster than usual, white crust around the dosing valve","Ammonia smell or deposits in the exhaust"],2,3,["P20F4","P249E","P20F6","P20E9","P202E"],"צריכת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך גבוה מדי"],P20F6:["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Open (Bank 1 Unit 1)","Between pulses the dosing valve must seal tightly so DEF only enters the exhaust when commanded. P20F6 means the control unit concluded that the first valve on bank 1 stays open: the pressure collapses, or the pump has to work much harder to hold it than the commanded quantity explains. A Cummins patent describes this kind of check, comparing the measured pump effort with the expected flow;",["Crystals or debris on the valve seat keeping the valve from closing","Mechanically sticking or heat-damaged dosing valve","Control unit software misjudging valve closure, cured by an update","Leaking or detached line at the valve imitating an open valve"],["Check engine light and DEF warning","Higher DEF consumption, white deposits in the exhaust or ammonia smell","Dosing switched off and later inducement"],2,3,["P20F7","P208E","P2047","P202E","P20F5"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P20F7:["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Open (Bank 2 Unit 1)","P20F7 is the bank 2 version of P20F6 and only applies to engines with a second exhaust line that has its own SCR catalyst and dosing valve, typically V engines with separate aftertreatment per bank. The control unit judges that this valve no longer closes, usually because pressure cannot be held or the pump must deliver far more than the commanded dose. No maker documents P20F7 publicly;",["Crystals or debris on the bank 2 valve seat","Mechanically sticking or heat-damaged bank 2 dosing valve","Leaking or detached supply line at the bank 2 valve"],["Check engine light and DEF warning","Higher DEF consumption and deposits in the bank 2 exhaust","Dosing switched off and later inducement"],2,3,["P20F6","P208F","P2050","P201A","P20F5"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P20F8:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit Performance (Bank 1)","P20F8 means the intake manifold runner or swirl flaps on bank 1 do not follow the commanded position, judged by comparing set point and feedback from the position sensor. Unlike P2004/P2006, which state a direction (stuck open or closed), this code reports poor tracking anywhere in the travel.",["Flaps or shaft sticking from carbon and oil deposits (common on diesels with EGR)","Worn or overheating actuator motor or failed position sensor","Control software needing an update (Mazda bulletin 01-003/26)","Wiring or connector fault at the actuator"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough idle or hesitation at low speed","Less torque at low engine speed"],2,1,["P20F9","P2004","P2006","P2008","P2015"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P20F9:["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit Performance (Bank 2)","P20F9 is the bank 2 counterpart of P20F8: the runner or swirl flaps of the second cylinder bank do not track their commanded position. It needs a V engine whose banks have separately driven flaps, each with its own position feedback. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; GM and Mazda only use the bank 1 code P20F8.",["Bank 2 flaps sticking from deposits","Bank 2 actuator or position sensor faulty","Broken or detached linkage between actuator and flap shaft"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Uneven idle or reduced torque at low speed"],2,1,["P20F8","P2005","P2007","P2011","P2019"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P20FA:["Reductant Pump B Control Circuit/Open","P20FA means the controller has found an open or otherwise faulty drive circuit for the second reductant (DEF/AdBlue) pump, called pump B or pump 2. No public service text explains which physical pump carries this letter; it is a driver channel of its own, separate from pump A (P208A).",["Water ingress or corrosion in the pump B connectors or harness","Connector not fully latched after assembly or repair","Open winding or internal break in pump B","Faulty output stage in the engine or DEF control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Service DEF or AdBlue warning with countdown to restart lockout","Other SCR codes stored at the same time (P208A, P20FC, P20FD)"],2,3,["P20FB","P20FC","P20FD","P208A"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P20FB:["Reductant Pump B Control Performance/Stuck Off","P20FB is the functional check of reductant pump B: its circuit is electrically sound, yet the pump does not reach the commanded state or stays off when it should be running. No public threshold exists for pump B. For pump A, Ford's 2023 diesel summary flags P208B when pump speed misses its setpoint by more than 300 rpm or the speed control sits at its limit for 30 seconds, which shows the principle.",["Outdated PCM software (FCA 3.0L EcoDiesel, reflash bulletins)","Pump B worn, seized or blocked by crystallised fluid","Frozen DEF or failed tank heating in cold weather","Clogged pump filter or restricted lines"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF system warning, possibly with countdown to restart lockout","Code returns mainly after cold starts or long parking"],3,3,["P20FA","P20FC","P20FD","P208B"],"בקרת משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P20FC:["Reductant Pump B Control Circuit Low","P20FC sets when the drive signal for reductant pump B reads too low, typically a ground fault on the line or a current draw beyond what the driver allows. Pump B has no published limits. For pump A, Ford's 2023 diesel summary reports the low fault (P208C) when pump current exceeds 5 A or the pump controller draws more than 15 A, checked with the driver off and confirmed after about 8 seconds;",["Chafed wire shorting the pump B control line to ground","Water ingress or corrosion in the pump connectors","Pump B motor drawing excessive current (internal short or tight motor)","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF system warning and reduced or no reductant dosing","Restart lockout after the inducement countdown if left unrepaired"],2,3,["P20FA","P20FB","P20FD","P208C"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P20FD:["Reductant Pump B Control Circuit High","P20FD indicates that the control line of reductant pump B sits too high, for instance shorted to battery voltage, so the controller can no longer regulate the pump properly. No limits are published for pump B.",["Pump B control line shorted to battery or supply voltage","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the pump connectors","Internal electrical fault in pump B","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF system warning, dosing suspended","Countdown to restart lockout in the instrument cluster"],2,3,["P20FA","P20FB","P20FC","P208D"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P20FE:["Reductant Metering Unit 1 Performance","P20FE judges whether the first reductant metering unit actually delivers the quantity the SCR control asks for. GM's 2025 Duramax tables average a delivery compensation factor and set the code, Type A after one trip, once that factor passes 1.44, meaning the expected pressure drop no longer proves correct dosing.",["Partly blocked or crystallised dosing injector","Loose or damaged tank filter letting debris reach pump and sensor","Over-sensitive diagnostic calibration (software update available)","Air in the dosing lines after service or low fluid level"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","AdBlue/DEF system warning in the cluster","Higher NOx, possible SCR efficiency codes (P20EE)"],3,3,["P2EAD","P20F4","P20E9","P20EE"],"יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P20FF:["Reductant Control Module Performance","P20FF is an internal fault of the module that runs the DEF pump and heaters, not of the pump itself. Ford's 2023 6.7L diesel strategy sets it when the pump motor controller exceeds 130 °C or reports an internal error, detected within about 5 seconds as part of the pump function check.",["Internal memory or processor fault in the DEF control module","Software or calibration mismatch after programming","Pump motor controller overheating (Ford, above 130 °C)","Poor power or ground connection causing module resets"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Service DEF System message, on some GM trucks wrongly shown as DEF Low","DEF dosing stops and the inducement countdown may begin"],4,3,["U040F","P21CB","P21CC","P214E"],"מודול בקרת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2100:["Throttle Actuator A Control Motor Circuit/Open","P2100 reports an electrical fault in the drive circuit of the first electronic throttle motor, usually an open line. Ford's 2012 summary uses it for an open circuit or a short to power or ground (no MIL, wrench lamp). GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 checks the bank 1 H-bridge three ways: open load above 200 kOhm, driver overtemperature and short to ground below 0.5 Ohm, each in one trip.",["Moisture or corrosion in the throttle body or ECU connector","Broken or chafed motor wire between ECU and throttle body","Open winding or worn brushes in the throttle motor","Damaged H-bridge output stage in the engine control unit"],["Throttle held in limp position, very low power","Engine or ETC warning lamp on","Little or no response to the accelerator pedal"],2,3,["P2101","P2102","P2103","P2118","P210A","P2106"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2101:["Throttle Actuator A Control Motor Circuit Range/Performance","Here the controller compares where throttle A should be with where its position sensors say it is. GM's 2018 table 18OBDG03A flags a gap of more than 10 percent between measured and modelled position after 15 counts at 12.5 ms each, classed by GM as Type A with immediate MIL; the 2006/2007 tables used 8.4 percent. VW's 2014 data book accepts 4-50 percent deviation or a drive duty cycle above 80 percent.",["Carbon or ice makes the throttle plate stiff or sticky","High resistance at the throttle connector pins","Worn gear train or weak motor inside the throttle body","Deformed inlet duct or leak at the throttle body"],["Reduced engine power message or limp mode","Engine warning lamp on","Hesitation or uneven idle","Stalling in some cases"],2,3,["P2100","P2111","P2112","P2118","P2119","P210B"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2102:["Throttle Actuator A Control Motor Circuit Low","P2102 means the output stage for throttle motor A sees a voltage or current that points to a short toward ground or an overloaded driver. GM lists P2100-P2103 together in its 2018 calibration as faults that limit engine power and default the throttle authority;",["Motor wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Shorted winding or jammed motor drawing excess current","Water in the throttle connector bridging terminals","Faulty throttle driver in the engine control unit"],["Limp mode with throttle at fixed opening","Engine warning lamp on","Pedal input largely ignored"],2,3,["P2100","P2103","P2101","P2118","P210C"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2103:["Throttle Actuator A Control Motor Circuit High","P2103 is the high-side fault of the throttle A drive: the output stage sees a voltage that suggests a short to battery, or on some layouts the supply relay of the throttle motor stays energized when it should be off. GM groups P2100-P2103 as power-limiting faults (18OBDG03A), and its Bosch-based 2012 ECM ties a power-stage short circuit to this range with about 0.1 s detection.",["Motor wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Throttle motor relay sticking on (where fitted)","Damaged or wet throttle connector","Internal fault in the ECU throttle driver"],["Limp mode with very limited power","Engine warning lamp on","Engine may not start or stalls"],2,3,["P2100","P2102","P2101","P2118","P210D"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2104:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Forced Idle","P2104 is a status code: it does not name a broken part but records that the throttle control has switched into a forced-idle failure mode. In Ford's 2012 summary this happens on second-generation ETC systems when two or three accelerator pedal sensor tracks are lost, so the computer can no longer read driver demand; the engine then holds a raised idle and ignores the pedal, with MIL and wrench lamp.",["Failure of two or more accelerator pedal sensor tracks","Pedal sensor wiring or shared 5 V reference fault","ECU input or software fault"],["Engine stays at raised idle, pedal has no effect","Engine and ETC/wrench warning lamps on","Car can only creep to a safe place"],2,3,["P2105","P2106","P2110","P2122","P2127","P2138"],""],P2105:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Forced Engine Shutdown","P2105 is the most severe throttle failure mode: the controller has decided that throttle control can no longer be trusted and stops the engine. In Ford's 2012 summary the trigger is a serious processor fault found by the separate monitoring processor (Ford calls it the Quizzer); all injectors are switched off and the wrench lamp comes on.",["Monitoring processor detects an internal ECU fault","Unstable ECU supply or ground connection","ECU software fault cured by reprogramming"],["Engine shuts off or will not keep running","Wrench or ETC warning lamp, often without MIL"],4,2,["P2104","P2106","P2110","P2107","P0606"],""],P2106:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Forced Limited Power","P2106 tells you the throttle control is running in a reduced-power fallback. Ford's 2012 summary lists the reasons on second-generation ETC: loss of the MAF signal, one throttle position sensor, crank position or transmission speed sensors, a stuck throttle or a throttle motor circuit fault; it sets with MIL and wrench lamp, and a crank sensor code (P0320/P0322) also adds P2106.",["Failed input such as MAF, throttle position or crank sensor","Sticking throttle or fault in the throttle motor circuit","Failed internal check or software in the engine computer"],["Reduced power, sluggish acceleration","Engine and wrench/ETC lamp on","Limited road speed"],2,3,["P2104","P2105","P2110","P2111","P2112","P0122"],""],P2107:["Throttle Actuator A Control Module Processor","P2107 concerns the processor that runs throttle A control, which in most cars sits inside the engine computer rather than in a separate box. Ford's summaries define it as an internal processor fault or lost communication with the main CPU, detected within 60 ms, with MIL after two drive cycles and the ETC lamp at once; from 2024 Ford reports the same check as P2108 with a failure-type byte.",["ECU software fault fixed by a reflash","Voltage dips or poor ECU ground","Internal hardware failure of the engine computer"],["Engine and ETC warning lamps on","Reduced power or limp mode","Possible stalling or no start"],4,3,["P2108","P211E","P2105","P0606","P2111","P2112"],"מעבד מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A"],P2108:["Throttle Actuator A Control Module Performance","P2108 marks a performance problem of the control function for throttle A, as opposed to a pure processor fault (P2107). VW's 2014 Touareg data book gives a concrete case: the time for the throttle to close below a reference point of 11.56 percent must not exceed 0.60 s.",["Throttle closes too slowly (deposits, weak spring)","ECU software issue needing an update","Supply voltage or ground problem at the ECU"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Unstable idle after lifting off the pedal"],2,3,["P2107","P211F","P2119","P2101","P0606"],"מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2109:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor A Minimum Stop Performance","P2109 flags an implausible rest reading on position signal A: with the throttle or pedal resting on its lower mechanical stop, the minimum learned at key-on falls outside the window the calibration accepts. Ford names its first throttle body sensor TP A, so on such layouts the code concerns the throttle.",["Ice or carbon holding the throttle plate off its rest stop","ECM software with oversensitive detection (update available)","Rest position not relearned after cleaning or replacing the throttle body","Sensor A worn or drifted at the closed end of its track"],["Engine warning lamp, often after a cold or wet night","Raised or unsteady idle","Reduced power until the fault clears"],2,3,["P2113","P2114","P0121","P0122","P2119","P2135"],""],P210A:["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit/Open","Throttle actuator B only exists on engines with two electronic throttles, typically one per cylinder bank. P210A reports an electrical fault, mainly an open line, in the drive of that second motor. GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 checks the bank 2 H-bridge just like bank 1: open load above 200 kOhm (0.8 s), driver overtemperature and short to ground below 0.5 Ohm, each one trip.",["Moisture or corrosion in the throttle B or ECU connector","Broken motor wire to throttle body B","Open winding in throttle motor B","Faulty bank 2 output stage in the ECU"],["Reduced power, one bank breathing poorly","Engine warning lamp on","Rough running or limp mode"],2,3,["P2100","P210B","P210C","P210D","P211C"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P210B:["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit Range/Performance","P210B is the position-control check for the second throttle on twin-throttle engines. The controller compares the commanded opening of throttle B with the measured one; GM's 23OBDG07 table flags a deviation beyond a rate-dependent limit for 0.5 s, one trip.",["High resistance at throttle B connector pins","Deposits or ice making throttle B sluggish","Worn gears or motor in throttle body B","Motor leads swapped after repair work"],["Engine warning lamp and reduced power","Uneven running between the two banks","Limp mode"],2,3,["P2101","P210A","P211C","P211D","P211A","P211B"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P210C:["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit Low","P210C is reserved for a low-side fault in the drive circuit of the second throttle motor, for example a grounded motor lead or an overloaded output stage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Throttle B motor wire shorted to ground","Shorted or jammed throttle motor B","Faulty bank 2 throttle driver in the ECU"],["Reduced power and rough running","Engine warning lamp on"],2,3,["P210A","P210D","P210B","P2102"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P210D:["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit High","P210D covers the high-side fault of the second throttle drive: a voltage on the motor B circuit that suggests a short to battery, or a supply that stays live when the stage should be off. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. On twin-throttle engines that publish their logic, GM (23OBDG07) and Ford (2024) collect the electrical faults of throttle B under P210A, so P210D will rarely be seen.",["Throttle B motor wire shorted to battery voltage","Damaged or wet connector at throttle body B","Faulty bank 2 output stage in the ECU"],["Reduced power and uneven running","Engine warning lamp on"],2,3,["P210A","P210C","P210B","P2103"],"מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P210E:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch C/F Voltage Correlation","P210E compares two redundant position signals, C and F, and sets when their voltages stop agreeing within the permitted tolerance. Which physical tracks carry these letters is up to the manufacturer: GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 uses C for the first sensor of a second throttle body, while Ford's summaries assign D, E and F to the three tracks of its pedal, so a C/F pair only arises on unusual layouts.",["One sensor track worn or drifted, so the pair no longer agrees","Corrosion or water in the connector shifting one signal","Fault in a shared ground or 5 V reference line","Faulty input stage in the engine control module"],["Engine or throttle warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Hesitant or delayed response to the pedal"],2,3,["P2136","P2137","P2138","P2139","P2140","P212F"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ C/F — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P210F:["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Forced Limited RPM","P210F is a status code for the second throttle: the controller has capped engine speed because control of throttle B is no longer reliable. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Its bank 1 sibling P2110 is well described: in Ford's 2012 summary it follows the loss of both throttle position sensors or a fault found by the throttle plate controller, sets the MIL and wrench lamp and enforces an rpm limit with…",["Electrical or mechanical fault of throttle B (see companion code)","Loss of the position signals of throttle B","ECU software reacting too strictly"],["Engine will not rev past a fixed limit","Engine and wrench lamp on"],2,3,["P2110","P210A","P210B","P211A","P211B"],""],P2110:["Throttle Actuator A Control System - Forced Limited RPM","P2110 records that engine speed has been capped because throttle A can no longer be controlled safely. Ford's 2012 summary sets it on second-generation ETC when both throttle position sensors fail or Ford's throttle plate controller (TPPC) reports a fault, with MIL and wrench lamp; rpm is then capped by a pedal-dependent limit enforced through fuel and spark.",["Ice on the throttle plate after a cold soak","Loss of both throttle position sensor signals","PCM software setting the code falsely (update available)","Worn or faulty electronic throttle body"],["Engine will not rev beyond a low limit","Engine warning lamp on","Stop/start disabled or hard start in frost"],2,3,["P2104","P2105","P2106","P210F","P2072","P2118"],""],P2111:["Throttle Actuator A Control System - Stuck Open","P2111 means throttle A stays more open than commanded. Ford defines it precisely: the actual throttle angle exceeds the desired angle by more than 6 degrees for about 500 ms, with MIL after two drive cycles and the ETC lamp at once; it also catches a throttle that cannot bring cold-start idle down. Ford's 2020-2023 and 2024 summaries keep it with MIL, the latter as P2100 byte 72.",["Water or ice in the intake behind the throttle","Carbon build-up holding the plate open","Broken return spring or worn gear in the throttle body","PCM calibration needing an update"],["High idle speed or engine hard to slow down","Loss of power in freezing weather","Engine and wrench lamp on"],2,3,["P2112","P2101","P2119","P2107","P211A","P2072"],""],P2112:["Throttle Actuator A Control System - Stuck Closed","P2112 is the mirror image of P2111: throttle A opens less than commanded. Ford sets it when the actual angle stays more than 6 degrees below the desired angle for about 500 ms (MIL after two drive cycles, ETC lamp at once) and lists it in its 2020-2023 and 2024 summaries. Ford's SSM 50203 names it for Ranger/Bronco with ice behind the throttle.",["Frozen condensate locking the throttle plate","Heavy carbon restricting plate movement","Jammed gear or weak motor in the throttle body","PCM logic needing an update"],["Lack of power after a cold start","Low or unstable idle, possible stalling","Engine and wrench lamp on"],2,3,["P2111","P2101","P2118","P2119","P211B","P0638"],""],P2113:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor B Minimum Stop Performance","The engine computer checks whether position signal B reports a plausible value when the throttle or pedal rests against its lower mechanical stop. At key-on many systems learn this minimum and compare it with a tolerance window; a reading outside that window sets the code.",["Carbon deposits or ice keep the throttle plate off its rest stop","Position sensor B worn or drifted at the low end of its track","Minimum position not relearned after cleaning or part replacement","Corroded connector shifting the sensor B signal"],["Engine or ETC warning lamp on","Unstable or raised idle speed","Reduced engine power (limp mode)"],2,3,["P2109","P2114","P0221","P0222","P0223","P2135"],""],P2114:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor C Minimum Stop Performance","This code reports that position signal C does not show a believable value while its throttle or pedal sits on the lower stop. The controller learns or expects a minimum reading within a tolerance band and flags a fault when the learned value falls outside it. Letter C is rarely assigned: Ford and GM use A/B for the throttle and D/E/F for the pedal, so C appears only on layouts with a third sensor.",["Position sensor C worn or drifted near its rest position","Deposits, ice or a damaged stop prevent the rest position","Rest position not relearned after repair","Connector or wiring fault shifting the C signal"],["Engine or ETC warning lamp on","Irregular idle","Reduced power possible"],2,3,["P2109","P2113","P2115","P2136","P2137"],""],P2115:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor D Minimum Stop Performance","Here the controller judges position signal D at the released (minimum) end of travel. On Ford and GM drive-by-wire systems D is the first accelerator pedal sensor, so the code means the pedal's idle reading is outside the expected window, for example because the pedal does not return fully or its sensor track has shifted. No manufacturer documents P2115 publicly;",["Pedal blocked by floor mat or weak return spring","Worn pedal sensor track D at the idle end","Aftermarket pedal tuning module or wrong pedal part","Corroded or loose pedal connector"],["Warning lamp on","Engine does not drop to normal idle when the pedal is released","Dull or limited pedal response"],1,3,["P2116","P2117","P2109","P2120","P2122","P2138"],""],P2116:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor E Minimum Stop Performance","The code covers the rest-position check of signal E. Ford, GM and Mitsubishi assign E to the second accelerator pedal sensor, which on many pedals runs at roughly half the voltage of sensor D (GM: APP 2 between 0.16 and 2.3 V). If the reading with the pedal released lies outside the learned or calibrated window, P2116 can be stored. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Pedal held off its stop by floor mat or sticking pivot","Worn or contaminated sensor track E","Moisture or corrosion at the pedal connector"],["Warning lamp on","Unsteady or raised idle","Limited throttle response"],1,3,["P2115","P2117","P2125","P2127","P2128","P2138"],""],P2117:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor F Minimum Stop Performance","P2117 is the minimum-stop check for signal F. Ford lists F as the third accelerator pedal sensor on its older Gen2 throttle systems (circuit codes P2132/P2133, range P2131), while most current pedals carry only D and E, so the code can only occur on three-track pedals. The ECU flags it when the F reading at the released position lies outside the expected band. No manufacturer documents P2117 publicly.",["Pedal does not return fully to its stop","Worn third sensor track F","Poor contact at the pedal connector"],["Warning lamp on","Idle speed does not settle","Reduced pedal response"],1,3,["P2115","P2116","P2130","P2139","P2140"],""],P2118:["Throttle Actuator A Control Motor Current Range/Performance","P2118 looks at how much current throttle motor A needs. A healthy throttle moves with modest current; a high or abnormal draw means the motor is fighting resistance. Ford lists P2118 with MIL and wrench lamp in its 2020-2023 summary (2024: P2100 byte 1D).",["Ice on the throttle plate after a cold soak","Carbon or sludge loading the motor","Worn throttle motor or gear train","ECM logic too sensitive (software update available)"],["Limp-home mode after a cold start","Engine warning lamp on","No start or poor idle in frost"],2,3,["P2101","P2119","P2072","P2110","P211C","P2100"],"זרם מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2119:["Throttle Actuator A Control Throttle Body Range/Performance","This is a mechanical performance check of the electronic throttle body. GM calls it Throttle Closed Position Performance: after the motor is de-energized the return springs must bring the plate into its default (limp) position, e.g. 1.32-1.90 V on TP sensor 1 in GM's 2006 tables; 15 failed samples in a row set it. A Bosch-based GM ECM times the spring return at key-on (fault above 0.56 s).",["Carbon deposits make the throttle plate stick","Water or ice in the intake behind the throttle body","Weak return spring or worn gear in the throttle body","ECM software that sets the code falsely (update available)"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Hesitation or uneven acceleration","Raised or unstable idle"],2,3,["P2101","P2111","P2112","P2118","P2176","P0638"],"מרכב מצערת בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P211A:["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Stuck Open","P211A means the second throttle on a twin-throttle engine stays further open than requested. Ford documents it in its 2020-2023 and 2024 summaries for applications with an ETB B, with MIL and wrench lamp and detection within 5 seconds; in 2024 it is shown as P210A with failure-type byte 72, matching P2111/P2100-72 for throttle A.",["Ice or carbon holding throttle B open","Broken return spring or gear in throttle body B","Faulty throttle motor B or its position sensor"],["High or hunting idle","Engine and wrench lamp on","Reduced power"],2,3,["P211B","P2111","P210B","P211D","P210A"],""],P211B:["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Stuck Closed","P211B is set when throttle B on a twin-throttle engine opens less than the controller asks for. Ford lists it for its dual-throttle applications in the 2020-2023 summary and in 2024 as P210A with failure-type byte 73, each with MIL, wrench lamp and detection in under 5 seconds; the A-side logic it mirrors is P2112, where actual angle trailing the target by more than 6 degrees counts as a fault.",["Frozen condensate locking throttle B","Heavy carbon restricting throttle B","Jammed gear or weak motor in throttle body B"],["Weak acceleration, limp mode","Rough idle","Engine and wrench lamp on"],2,3,["P211A","P2112","P210B","P211C","P211D"],""],P211C:["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Current Range/Performance","P211C evaluates the current drawn by the second throttle motor. If throttle B needs clearly more current than expected to reach or hold its position, something is loading it mechanically or the motor itself is degrading. Ford names P211C first in its list for the second throttle body of twin-throttle engines (2020-2023) and in 2024 as P210A byte 1D, each with MIL, wrench lamp and detection within 5 seconds.",["Ice or condensate binding throttle B","Carbon build-up increasing motor load","Worn motor or gears in throttle body B"],["Reduced power or limp mode","Engine and wrench lamp on","Uneven running in cold weather"],2,3,["P2118","P210B","P211D","P210A","P211A"],"זרם מנוע בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P211D:["Throttle Actuator B Control Throttle Body Range/Performance","P211D is the mechanical check of throttle body B, the twin of P2119. GM's 23OBDG07 table describes four spring tests for bank 2: the opening and closing springs must bring the de-energized plate back to the defined limp position within set times (about 0.2-0.36 s per path), checked during offset learning and also at cold temperatures, each failing in one trip.",["Weak or broken return spring in throttle body B","Deposits or ice slowing the plate","Throttle adaptation not completed after service"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Unstable idle"],2,3,["P2119","P210B","P211C","P211A","P211B"],"מרכב מצערת בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P211E:["Throttle Actuator B Control Module Processor","P211E is the processor fault for the control of throttle B on engines with two electronic throttles. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The A version P2107 is well described: Ford treats it as an internal processor fault or lost link to the main CPU, detected in 60 ms, with MIL and an ETC lamp, and from 2024 reports it under P2108.",["Control unit software fault (reflash)","Voltage dips or poor ground at the control unit","Internal hardware failure of the control unit"],["Engine and ETC warning lamps on","Limp mode with reduced power"],4,3,["P2107","P211F","P2108","P0606","P210A"],"מעבד מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B"],P211F:["Throttle Actuator B Control Module Performance","P211F covers a performance fault of the control function for throttle B, as distinct from a processor fault (P211E). No manufacturer documents this code publicly. For the A side, VW's 2014 data book gives a measurable example under P2108: the throttle must close below a reference point of 11.56 percent within 0.60 s.",["Throttle B responds or closes too slowly","Control unit software needing an update","Supply or ground problem at the control unit"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode"],2,3,["P2108","P211E","P211D","P2107"],"מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2120:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D Circuit","P2120 is the general circuit check for signal D, which GM, Ford and VW all use for the first accelerator pedal track. GM's 2007 tables call it APP Sensor 1 Circuit: the ECM watches sensor 1 for steady or intermittent opens and shorts within its 0.325-4.75 V window and counts failures every 12.5 ms, setting the code at 19 of 39 counts.",["Poor terminal tension or corrosion at pedal, inline or ECM connectors","Open or short in the sensor 1 signal, reference or ground wire","Internal fault in the pedal sensor, such as a cracked solder joint","ECM input fault"],["Engine warning lamp and reduced power message","Sluggish or capped acceleration","Fault often intermittent and hard to reproduce"],1,3,["P2121","P2122","P2123","P2124","P2125","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2121:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D Circuit Range/Performance","P2121 means pedal signal D is electrically intact but implausible. Ford's 2012 OBD summary sets it only on second-generation ETC systems, whose pedals carry three tracks D, E and F: if sensor D disagrees with the others by more than 1.1 degrees, the PCM stores P2121 without MIL but with the wrench lamp, and pedal response becomes rate-limited using the healthy tracks.",["Worn or dirty track D giving an offset reading","Contact resistance at the pedal connector","Shared reference or ground line shifting one signal"],["Wrench or engine warning lamp on","Softened, delayed acceleration","Idle may rise when the brake is not pressed"],1,3,["P2120","P2122","P2123","P2124","P2126","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2122:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D Circuit Low","P2122 sets when pedal track D falls below its lower voltage limit, typically from a short to ground, a missing 5 V reference or a broken signal wire. Limits differ by maker: Ford uses 0.25 V and since 2020 lights both MIL and wrench lamp (in 2012 only the wrench lamp); GM's 2007 tables use 0.325 V with 19 of 39 counts at 12.5 ms (Type A), GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 0.28 V for 0.2 s;",["Track D signal wire shorted to ground or chafed","Open or shorted 5 V reference feed to the pedal","Pedal sensor fault such as a cracked solder joint","Corroded terminals with high resistance"],["Engine warning lamp and reduced power message","Pedal feels dead or reacts only slowly","Cruise control may be unavailable"],1,3,["P2120","P2121","P2123","P2124","P2127","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2123:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D Circuit High","P2123 is the high-voltage fault on pedal track D, usually an open sensor ground or a short to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage. GM's 2007 tables set it above 4.75 V (19 of 39 counts, Type A), a Bosch-based GM ECM from 2012 above 4.824 V lasting 0.2 s, and the 2014 VW Touareg above 4.89 V; Ford uses 4.75 V.",["Open or high-resistance ground return of the pedal sensor","Track D signal shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Internal pedal sensor fault","Loose or spread terminals at pedal or inline connector"],["Engine warning lamp and reduced power message","Limited throttle opening despite full pedal","Fault may appear and vanish with harness movement"],1,3,["P2120","P2121","P2122","P2124","P2128","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2124:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D Circuit Intermittent","P2124 covers brief dropouts or spikes on pedal track D that come and go too quickly to count as a steady low or high fault. Ford documents it: special service messages 46829 (2015-2017 F-150) and 46880 (2017 Super Duty built up to late August 2017) tie P2124, alongside other pedal codes and wrench, ABS, airbag and hill descent lamps, to a pedal harness routed behind the bracket between brake booster and brake pedal,…",["Pedal harness pinched or chafed by a misrouted path","Loose terminal or weak pin tension at the pedal connector","Worn spot on track D inside the pedal sensor"],["Warning lamps that come and go, sometimes several at once","Brief loss of pedal response while driving","Reduced power mode after repeated dropouts"],2,3,["P2120","P2122","P2123","P2129","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2125:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E Circuit","P2125 reports a general electrical fault in signal circuit E. GM uses it as Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor 2 Circuit: the ECM looks for a continuous or intermittent open or short in the sensor 2 circuit with a counter at 12.5 ms per count (19 of 39 counts). In GM's 2006 tables sensor 2 is valid between about 0.16 and 2.3 V.",["Internal fault in the pedal sensor (e.g. cracked solder joint)","Open or short in the sensor 2 wiring or 5 V reference","Loose or corroded pedal or inline connector","ECM input fault"],["Engine warning lamp and reduced power message","Delayed or limited pedal response","Traction control may be switched off"],1,3,["P2126","P2127","P2128","P2129","P2138","P2120"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ E — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2126:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E Circuit Range/Performance","Signal E is electrically intact but its value does not fit the situation. Ford's 2012 OBD summary uses P2126 for the second pedal sensor on Gen2 throttle systems: it sets when sensors D and E disagree by more than 1.1 degrees, as a non-MIL fault with the wrench lamp. Mitsubishi lists P2126 as accelerator pedal sensor E on the 2022 Outlander. Many newer systems report the same disagreement as P2138 instead.",["Worn or dirty sensor track E giving offset readings","Contact resistance at the pedal connector","Shared reference or ground circuit shifting one signal"],["Wrench or engine warning lamp on","Softened or delayed acceleration","Idle may be raised when braking"],1,2,["P2125","P2127","P2128","P2129","P2138","P2121"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ E — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2127:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E Circuit Low","P2127 reports that pedal track E reads below its lower limit. Because many pedals run the second track at roughly half the voltage of the first, the limit for E can sit lower than for D: GM's 2006 tables flag sensor 2 under 0.1625 V and the 2014 VW Passat under 0.27 V, against 0.61 V for track D.",["Track E signal wire shorted to ground","Open 5 V reference feed for the second track","Worn track E at the closed-pedal end","Corroded or loose pedal connector"],["Engine warning lamp, on newer Fords together with the wrench lamp","Reduced power and slower pedal response","Traction control may be switched off"],1,3,["P2125","P2126","P2128","P2129","P2122","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2128:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E Circuit High","P2128 sets when pedal track E reads above its upper limit, typically from an open sensor ground, a short to 5 V or a broken track. Where E is a half-scale signal the limit lies far below the supply: GM's 2006 tables flag sensor 2 above 2.295 V and the 2014 VW Passat above 2.43 V. Pedals with two full-scale tracks use about 4.75 V (Ford, GM 2007, 19 of 39 counts) or 4.824 V for 0.2 s (GM's Bosch-based 2012 ECM).",["Open or high-resistance ground of the pedal sensor","Track E signal shorted to the 5 V reference","Broken track or solder joint inside the pedal sensor"],["Engine warning lamp and reduced power message","Weak acceleration even with the pedal fully pressed","Often stored together with P2123 if the ground is open"],1,3,["P2125","P2126","P2127","P2129","P2123","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2129:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E Circuit Intermittent","P2129 is meant for short dropouts or spikes in signal circuit E that do not last long enough for a steady low or high fault. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM and Ford, which assign E to the second pedal sensor, catch such glitches inside their circuit codes instead: GM counts failures every 12.5 ms and flags the APP sensor 2 circuit after 19 of 39 counts (P2125/P2127/P2128), Ford uses 0.25/4.75 V…",["Loose terminal or poor pin tension at the pedal connector","Chafed harness making intermittent contact","Worn spot or cracked joint inside the pedal sensor"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Brief hesitation or power loss while driving","Reduced power mode after repeated dropouts"],2,3,["P2125","P2126","P2127","P2128","P2138"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ E — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P212A:["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit","P212A is the general circuit code for throttle position signal G, a letter that only comes into play on engines with more than one electronic throttle or extra position tracks. No manufacturer documents P212A publicly.",["Open or short in the sensor G signal, supply or ground wire","Corroded or loose connector at the throttle body","Failed position sensor inside the throttle body"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Rough idle on twin-throttle engines"],2,3,["P212B","P212C","P212D","P212E","P212F"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת‏ G — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P212B:["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit Range/Performance","P212B means throttle signal G is electrically valid but its value does not fit. GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 applies it to sensor 2 of the bank 2 throttle body on a twin-throttle engine: the code sets when the angle derived from sensor 2 differs from that of sensor 1 by more than about 5-6.25 %, or from the angle modelled from manifold pressure by more than 9 %, in one trip; the 2024 table repeats the check.",["ECM software setting the code without a real fault (update available)","Sensor G drifted or worn, disagreeing with its partner sensor","Deposits or sticking plate making the angle disagree with airflow","Contact resistance at the throttle body connector"],["MIL on, often without noticeable driving problems","Reduced power if the plausibility fault persists","Uneven idle on twin-throttle engines"],2,3,["P212A","P212C","P212D","P212E","P212F","P2135"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת‏ G — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P212C:["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit Low","P212C sets when position signal G reads below its lower electrical limit. The letter G only comes into play on engines with more than one electronic throttle. GM's 2023 and 2024 OBD tables (23OBDG07, 24OBDG07) give it to the second position sensor in the bank 2 throttle body of a twin-throttle engine: a raw voltage under 0.195 V lasting 0.14 s while the ECU is running stores the code within one trip.",["Signal wire of sensor G shorted to ground","5 V reference to the bank 2 throttle body open or pulled low","Worn or damaged track of position sensor G inside the throttle body","Corroded or loose terminals at the bank 2 throttle connector"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced engine power message","Uneven idle or hesitation on one bank"],2,3,["P212A","P212B","P212D","P212E","P212F","P0222"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת‏ G — אות נמוך במעגל"],P212D:["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit High","P212D is the high-voltage fault on throttle position signal G. GM documents it in the 2023 and 2024 tables (23OBDG07, 24OBDG07) for sensor 2 of the bank 2 throttle body on a twin-throttle engine: once the raw voltage climbs above 4.805 V for 0.14 s, the code is stored in a single trip.",["Open sensor ground at the bank 2 throttle body","Signal wire of sensor G shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Broken signal wire or pushed-back terminal","Internal fault in the position sensor of the bank 2 throttle"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced engine power message","Weak or delayed response to the accelerator"],2,3,["P212A","P212B","P212C","P212E","P212F","P0223"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת‏ G — אות גבוה במעגל"],P212E:["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit Intermittent","P212E is reserved for brief dropouts or spikes on throttle position signal G, the kind that clear again before a steady low or high fault can be confirmed. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM, which assigns G to sensor 2 of the bank 2 throttle body on a twin-throttle engine, reacts to such glitches with its range checks instead: P212C below 0.195 V and P212D above 4.805 V each need only 0.14 s.",["Loose or worn terminal at the bank 2 throttle connector","Harness chafed by engine movement, breaking contact now and then","Moisture or corrosion in the connector","Momentary contact loss on the sensor track"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Brief stumbles or power dips","Fault often not present at the workshop"],2,3,["P212A","P212B","P212C","P212D","P0224"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת‏ G — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P212F:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F/G Voltage Correlation","P212F checks whether the two redundant signals F and G still agree in voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and the letters make it an unusual pair: GM's 2004-2005 truck tables use F for the third accelerator pedal track, while GM's 2023 table assigns G to the second sensor of a bank 2 throttle body.",["One sensor track worn or drifted so the pair disagrees","Contact resistance in the connector shifting one signal","Fault in a shared ground or 5 V reference line"],["Engine or throttle warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Hesitant response to the pedal"],2,3,["P212B","P212E","P2130","P2139","P2140","P210E"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ F/G — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2130:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F Circuit","P2130 is the general circuit code for signal F. GM used it on its 2004-2005 pickups and SUVs with a separate throttle actuator control module (TACM) and a pedal carrying three tracks, where F is APP sensor 3. The TACM flags a continuous or intermittent open or short when sensor 3 reads below 1.63 V or above 4.38 V, or when its learned rest voltage exceeds 4.28 V;",["Poor terminal contact or corrosion at the pedal connector","Open or short in the signal, reference or ground wire of track F","Third track inside the pedal sensor worn or failed","Faulty input in the throttle actuator control module or ECM"],["Engine warning lamp on","Softer or delayed response to the pedal","Reduced power message on some models"],1,3,["P2131","P2132","P2133","P2134","P2139","P2140"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ F — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2131:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F Circuit Range/Performance","P2131 means pedal track F is electrically intact but disagrees with the rest of the pedal. Two makers document it for three-track pedals. GM's 2004-2005 truck tables scale APP sensor 3 to the range of the other tracks and set P2131 only when it strays more than 0.26 V from each of the other two sensors, so the majority vote singles out track F;",["Worn or dirty track F giving an offset reading","Contact resistance at the pedal connector","Bent pedal bracket or binding mechanism distorting one track"],["Wrench or engine warning lamp on","Softened, slower acceleration","Often no noticeable change while driving"],1,3,["P2130","P2132","P2133","P2134","P2139","P2140"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ F — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2132:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F Circuit Low","P2132 sets when signal F drops below its lower voltage limit. Ford uses it for the third accelerator pedal track of its second-generation electronic throttle: its 2012 OBD summary treats anything under 0.25 V as a continuity fault and lights only the wrench lamp, not the MIL.",["Signal wire of track F shorted to ground","Open or weak 5 V reference to the pedal sensor","Track F worn at the rest position"],["Wrench or engine warning lamp on","Delayed or rate-limited acceleration","Idle may stay raised until the brake is pressed"],1,2,["P2130","P2131","P2133","P2134","P2122","P2127"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ F — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2133:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F Circuit High","P2133 is the high-voltage fault on signal F. In Ford's second-generation electronic throttle the third pedal track counts as failed once it rises above 4.75 V; the 2012 summary reports it with the wrench lamp and without MIL. FCA lists P2133 in emissions recall T21 for the 2004-2006 Dodge Sprinter among the codes that can show up after the engine computer is reflashed.",["Open ground line of the pedal sensor","Signal wire of track F shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Internal break in track F of the pedal sensor"],["Wrench or engine warning lamp on","Slower, limited acceleration","May appear together with high faults on other tracks if the ground is open"],1,2,["P2130","P2131","P2132","P2134","P2123","P2128"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ F — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2134:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F Circuit Intermittent","P2134 targets short interruptions on signal F that are too brief or too irregular for a confirmed low or high fault. No manufacturer publishes a detection rule for it. FCA does name P2134 in emissions recall T21 for the 2004-2006 Dodge Sprinter, among the codes that may appear once the engine control unit carries the new software.",["Loose or spread terminal at the pedal connector","Pedal harness pinched or chafed near the footwell bracket","Worn spot on track F causing momentary contact loss"],["Warning lamp that appears and clears","Short hesitation when moving the pedal"],1,3,["P2130","P2131","P2132","P2133","P2124","P2129"],"חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ F — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2135:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch A/B Voltage Correlation","P2135 compares the two position tracks of the electronic throttle, A and B, and sets when they no longer describe the same plate angle. GM's 2006-2007 tables allow a 7 % offset at closed throttle rising to 10 % at full opening and count failures every 12.5 ms until 19 of 39 have failed. Ford flags more than 7 degrees of disagreement;",["Worn or contaminated position tracks in the throttle body","Raised contact resistance or corrosion at the throttle connector","ECM calibration prone to false detection (update available on some models)","Fault on the shared 5 V reference or ground of both tracks"],["Engine warning lamp or wrench lamp on","Reduced engine power, limited throttle opening","Rough or raised idle"],2,3,["P2136","P2137","P0121","P0221","P0122","P0222"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2136:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch A/C Voltage Correlation","P2136 reports that position signals A and C disagree. On engines with two electronic throttles, C typically belongs to the second throttle body: GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 assigns C to sensor 1 of the bank 2 throttle.",["Increased resistance in the throttle actuator connector pins","Position sensor in one throttle body drifted or worn","Carbon or ice making one throttle lag behind the other"],["Engine warning lamp on","Possible loss of power","Often stored together with P2135"],2,3,["P2135","P2137","P2AD3","P2AD2","P210E"],"מתח מזגן חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2137:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch B/C Voltage Correlation","P2137 compares position signals B and C and sets when their voltages drift apart beyond the calibrated tolerance. No manufacturer publishes a detection rule for this pair; FCA merely lists P2137 in emissions recall T21 for the 2004-2006 Dodge Sprinter among the codes that may surface after the ECU is reprogrammed.",["High resistance or corrosion at a throttle connector","Track B or sensor C drifted or worn","Fault on a shared 5 V reference or ground"],["Engine warning lamp on","Possible loss of power"],2,3,["P2135","P2136","P2AD2","P0221"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ B/C — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2138:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D/E Voltage Correlation","P2138 is the standard plausibility check of a two-track accelerator pedal: D and E are pedal sensors 1 and 2 at GM, Ford and VW. GM's 2007 tables set it when the tracks differ by more than 10 % or their learned rest values by over 5 % (Type A); the 2023 table uses 0.12-0.18 V for 0.25 s in one trip. Ford flags more than 0.9 degrees and since 2020 lights MIL and wrench lamp; the 2014 VW Passat allows 0.17-0.70 V.",["Water or corrosion in a pedal or inline harness connector","Worn pedal sensor with one track drifting","Poorly crimped or loose terminals raising resistance","Aftermarket equipment tapped into pedal or 5 V reference circuits"],["Engine warning lamp with reduced engine power message","Sluggish, capped acceleration","Traction or stability control may be switched off on some models"],1,3,["P2122","P2123","P2127","P2128","P2139","P2140"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D/E — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2139:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D/F Voltage Correlation","P2139 compares signals D and F, in practice the first and third tracks of a three-track accelerator pedal. No manufacturer publishes a detection rule for this exact code; FCA only lists P2139 in emissions recall T21 for the 2004-2006 Dodge Sprinter among codes that can appear after the ECU update.",["Track D or F of the pedal sensor worn or drifted","Contact resistance at the pedal connector","Fault on a shared ground or 5 V reference"],["Engine or wrench warning lamp on","Softened or delayed acceleration"],1,3,["P2138","P2140","P2131","P2121","P2130","P212F"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D/F — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P213A:["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B/Open","P213A concerns the electrical drive of EGR throttle B, a second motor-driven regulating flap found on some diesel layouts. Such a flap closes partly so that pressure ahead of the intake falls below exhaust pressure and enough exhaust gas can be recirculated; it also cuts air at engine stop.",["Loose, corroded or broken connector or wire at throttle B","Open winding in the throttle B actuator motor","Harness damaged by heat near the exhaust or EGR cooler","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Engine shudder when switched off","EGR readiness not completed"],2,3,["P213B","P213C","P213D","P0487","P0488"],""],P213B:["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B Range/Performance","P213B is the functional check of EGR throttle B rather than an electrical one. The module compares the position it commands with the position the flap actually reaches, or judges whether the feedback is plausible; if the gap persists beyond a set time, P213B is logged.",["Flap stiff or stuck from soot and oil deposits","Worn gear train or weak actuator motor","Implausible position feedback from the flap sensor","Outdated engine software or missing flap adaptation"],["Check engine lamp on","Hesitation, black smoke or reduced power","Clicking or humming from the flap","Filter regeneration may be postponed"],2,3,["P213A","P213C","P213D","P0488","P0401"],"מעגל בקרת מצערת EGR‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P213C:["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B Low","P213C points to a low signal in the drive circuit of EGR throttle B: the output stage sees too little voltage where it expects supply potential, which almost always means a conductor of the flap motor is touching ground. Chafed harness sections near the exhaust, water in the connector or a motor winding shorted to its housing are typical.",["Chafed wire shorting to ground between module and flap","Water or corrosion in the flap connector","Actuator motor winding shorted to housing","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","Engine shudder when switched off"],2,3,["P213A","P213B","P213D","P2141"],"מעגל בקרת מצערת EGR‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P213D:["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B High","P213D is the opposite electrical fault to P213C on EGR throttle B: the drive line carries voltage where the output stage expects ground, or the driver measures excessive current. A wire touching battery positive, a shorted motor winding that pulls too much current, or a mechanically blocked flap that overloads the motor are the usual triggers.",["Drive wire shorted to battery voltage","Shorted turns in the actuator motor causing overcurrent","Flap mechanically blocked, motor overloaded","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power in some operating ranges","EGR readiness not completed"],2,3,["P213A","P213B","P213C","P2142"],"מעגל בקרת מצערת EGR‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P213E:["Fuel Injection System Fault - Forced Engine Shutdown","P213E records that the engine module stopped the engine on purpose because of a fault on the injection side – rail, high-pressure lines, pressure control or injectors. Continuing to run with an external leak, a rail pressure that can no longer be controlled or an injector that keeps delivering could cause a fire or engine damage. No manufacturer documents P213E publicly.",["External leak at rail, high-pressure line or injector seal","Injector stuck open or leaking heavily","Rail pressure control valve or sensor no longer controlling pressure","Engine software misjudging the fault, update available"],["Engine shuts off while running","Engine cranks but does not start again","Fuel smell or visible fuel leak","Check engine lamp with further fuel system codes"],4,3,["P213F","P0148","P0093","P0087","P0088"],""],P213F:["Fuel Pump System Fault - Forced Engine Shutdown","P213F is the supply-side twin of P213E: the engine module shut the engine down because the fuel pump system – electric lift pump, its relay or control module, or the engine-driven high-pressure pump – no longer behaves in a way it can accept. No manufacturer documents P213F publicly, so the trigger is not known in detail.",["Electric lift pump or its control module failed","Pump relay, fuse or wiring fault","Worn or seized high-pressure pump","Clogged filter or empty tank starving the pump"],["Engine shuts off while driving","No restart or very long cranking","Check engine lamp with fuel pump codes"],3,3,["P213E","P0627","P0230","P0087"],""],P2140:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E/F Voltage Correlation","P2140 checks the second and third pedal tracks, E and F, against each other. As with P2139, no manufacturer explains its own trigger for this code, and FCA's emissions recall T21 for the 2004-2006 Dodge Sprinter just includes it in the list of codes that may follow the ECU reflash.",["Track E or F of the pedal sensor worn or drifted","Shared 5 V reference or ground fault shifting one track","Contact resistance or moisture at the pedal connector"],["Engine or wrench warning lamp on","Reduced or delayed pedal response"],1,3,["P2138","P2139","P2126","P2131","P2130","P212F"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ E/F — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2141:["EGR Throttle Control Circuit A Low","P2141 flags a low signal in the drive circuit of EGR throttle A, the main diesel regulating flap that lowers intake pressure so exhaust gas can flow back. A wire of the flap motor touching ground, a winding shorted to the housing or a wet connector are the common reasons. Note how J2012 spreads flap A over two ranges: open circuit and range/performance sit at P0487 and P0488, low and high at P2141 and P2142;",["Chafed wire shorting to ground between module and flap","Moisture or corrosion in the flap connector","Actuator motor winding shorted to housing","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine shudder when switched off","Reduced power or limp mode"],2,3,["P2142","P0487","P0488","P213C"],"מעגל בקרת מצערת EGR‏ A — ערך נמוך"],P2142:["EGR Throttle Control Circuit A High","P2142 reports a high signal or overcurrent in the drive circuit of EGR throttle A. Either a motor lead has contact with battery voltage, or the motor draws more current than the output stage allows – from shorted turns or because carbon has jammed the blade. The driver then shuts down for protection, the flap springs back to its rest position and EGR regulation is lost.",["Drive wire shorted to battery voltage","Flap jammed by carbon, motor overloaded","Shorted turns in the actuator motor","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode","EGR readiness not completed"],2,3,["P2141","P0487","P0488","P213D"],"מעגל בקרת מצערת EGR‏ A — ערך גבוה"],P2143:["EGR Vent Control Circuit/Open","Vacuum-operated EGR valves are often run by a pair of solenoids: one feeds vacuum to the valve diaphragm to open it, the other – the vent solenoid – lets air in to release the vacuum and close the valve. Ford's EEC engine computers had separate outputs for EGR vent and EGR control, and a Kia diesel patent maps both solenoids by duty cycle, using the vent side whenever the measured EGR value is above target.",["Loose connector or broken wire at the vent solenoid","Open coil in the vent solenoid","Blown fuse or missing supply voltage to the solenoid","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough idle or stalling after deceleration","EGR readiness not completed"],1,1,["P2144","P2145","P0403","P0401"],"אוורור EGR — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2144:["EGR Vent Control Circuit Low","P2144 reports a low signal in the circuit that drives the EGR vent solenoid – the valve that bleeds vacuum from a vacuum-operated EGR valve so it can close. With the usual low-side switching, a control wire touching ground keeps the solenoid energised regardless of the command.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Internal short in the vent solenoid coil","Corrosion bridging terminals in the connector","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough idle or hesitation","Emissions test failure because of EGR"],1,1,["P2143","P2145","P0403","P0401"],"אוורור EGR — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2145:["EGR Vent Control Circuit High","P2145 is the high fault in the vent solenoid circuit of the EGR system: the control line shows supply voltage while the module tries to pull it to ground, or the driver detects overcurrent through a shorted coil.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Shorted vent solenoid coil drawing excess current","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","EGR inactive, sometimes pinging under load on petrol engines","EGR readiness not completed"],1,1,["P2143","P2144","P0403","P0401"],"אוורור EGR — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2146:["Fuel Injector Group A Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Direct-injection and common-rail injectors are fed by a high-side driver in the engine module, often shared by several injectors. P2146 is the open or general fault of the first such supply. GM's 2009 Duramax diesel pairs injectors 1 and 4 in group 1 and sets P2146 when the driver sees an open, short or missing load for 6 ms, type A.",["Injector harness chafed through or wire open inside insulation","Loose, wet or corroded injector connector","Open coil or piezo stack in an injector of the group","Faulty high-side driver in the engine control module"],["Misfire on one or more cylinders","Rough running and loss of power","Check engine lamp on"],3,3,["P2147","P2148","P2149","P2155","P0201","P062D"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2147:["Fuel Injector Group A Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P2147 means the common feed of injector group A is pulled toward ground. GM documents it in detail for its 2018 Duramax diesels: the high-side line to injectors 1 and 4 (group 1 on both the 2.8 L four and the 6.6 L V8) shows 0.5 Ω or less to ground while the driver is switched on;",["Injector supply wire chafed and shorted to ground","Injector of the group shorted internally to its body","Water in the injector harness connector","Faulty injector driver in the engine control module"],["Two cylinders misfire at once","Heavy loss of power, rough running","Check engine lamp on immediately"],3,3,["P2146","P2148","P2150","P0261","P062D"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ A — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2148:["Fuel Injector Group A Supply Voltage Circuit High","P2148 flags group A's injector supply as too high. On GM's 2018 Duramax the high-side terminal of injector 1 or 4 shows 0.5 Ω or less to supply potential while the driver is off; same 5-of-10 counting at 100 ms, type A.",["Injector supply wire shorted to battery voltage","Internal fault of the injector boost circuit in the module","Software falsely detecting the fault, reprogramming available","Injector of the group with internal short"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire and rough running on the affected cylinders","Often no drivability complaint when the cause is software"],3,3,["P2146","P2147","P2151","P0262","P062D"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ A — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2149:["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","P2149 is the open or general fault of the second shared injector supply. Group membership depends on the engine: GM's 2009 Duramax places injectors 7 and 6 in group 2 (6 ms, type A), whereas GM's 2018 tables pair injectors 2 and 5 in the V8 – so the cylinders must be looked up for each engine. VW's 2014 TSI and VR6 engines use the same current window as for group A, under 2.6 A or above about 14.7–14.9 A.",["Injector harness damaged or wire open","Water entering an injector harness connector","Open coil or piezo stack in an injector of the group","Low rail pressure from fuel vapour triggering follow-up faults"],["Misfire on the cylinders of group B","Rough running and reduced power","Check engine lamp on"],3,3,["P2146","P2150","P2151","P2152","P0202"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P214A:["SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too High","P214A reports that the exhaust entering the SCR catalyst was hotter than a calibrated ceiling while no particulate filter regeneration was active. The reading normally comes from the temperature sensor between the filter and the urea mixing section.",["Unburnt fuel or engine oil reaching the exhaust (leaking injector, turbocharger seal)","SCR inlet temperature sensor reading too high or wrongly placed after repair","Overfuelling from injection or air-path faults (boost leak, EGR fault)","Engine control software with outdated temperature model"],["Check engine light on","Reduced engine power to limit exhaust temperature","Further codes for exhaust temperature or SCR efficiency"],3,3,["P214B","P214C","P214D","P20EC","P200C","P242B"],"טמפרטורת כניסת ממיר קטליטי NOx SCR — ערך גבוה מדי"],P214B:["SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too High During Particulate Filter Regeneration","P214B is limited to the regeneration phase. To burn soot out of the particulate filter, the engine control adds late injections or uses a separate exhaust fuel injector, and the oxidation catalyst converts that fuel into heat. The code sets when the gas leaving this hot zone arrives at the SCR inlet above the limit allowed during regeneration.",["Exhaust fuel injector leaking or over-dosing during regeneration","Heavily loaded filter burning off too quickly","Excess post-injection quantity from a worn engine injector","Exhaust temperature sensor upstream of the SCR reading too high"],["Check engine light on, regeneration aborted","Filter warning or rising soot load because regeneration cannot finish","Reduced engine power"],3,3,["P214A","P214D","P214C","P20EC","P2080","P200C"],""],P214C:["SCR NOx Catalyst Outlet Temperature Too High","P214C looks at the downstream end of the SCR catalyst: the temperature measured behind it rose above the permitted maximum outside regeneration. California's OBD rule lists SCR intake and outlet temperature as separate data values a diesel must report, so both points are watched on their own.",["SCR outlet temperature sensor faulty or reading too high","Hydrocarbons passing the oxidation catalyst and burning on the SCR","Fuel or oil entering the exhaust from the engine or turbocharger"],["Check engine light on","Reduced engine power","Implausible outlet temperature compared with the inlet value in live data"],2,3,["P214D","P214A","P214B","P20EC","P242B"],"טמפרטורת יציאת ממיר קטליטי NOx SCR — ערך גבוה מדי"],P214D:["SCR NOx Catalyst Outlet Temperature Too High During Particulate Filter Regeneration","P214D sets when the temperature behind the SCR catalyst exceeds its limit while the particulate filter is regenerating. It is the only code of this group with public manufacturer evidence. Ram pickups with the 6.7L Cummins use it: bulletin 18-053-14 (2014 Ram 2500/3500) reprograms the PCM partly to prevent unnecessary MIL events from P214D, and STAR case S2625000004 (2025–2026 Ram 3500 to 5500) groups it with…",["Exhaust temperature sensor behind the SCR faulty, confused with another sensor or affected by low battery voltage","PCM software requiring an update (Ram 6.7L bulletins)","Regeneration fuel slipping through and burning on the SCR"],["Check engine light on","Regeneration aborted or repeated","Additional exhaust temperature sensor codes"],2,3,["P214C","P214B","P214A","P242B","P2471","P0544"],""],P214E:["Reductant Pump A Current Too High","P214E means the electronics driving the DEF (AdBlue) pump motor saw more current than the pump may draw. GM documents it on Duramax diesels: in the 2018 tables the DEF control module reports a motor high-current or current-limit error, and the ECM sets the code after 20 failed of 25 samples with the battery above 11 V;",["Pump motor seized, worn or blocked by crystallised or frozen fluid","Short in the pump motor winding or supply wiring, often after water ingress","ECM or reductant control module software (GM 20-NA-039)","Faulty driver stage in the reductant control module"],["Check engine light on after one trip","DEF system warning, possibly a countdown to speed limitation","Raised NOx emissions because dosing stops"],2,3,["P2C11","P208A","P208B","P208C","P208D","P20FF"],"זרם משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P214F:["Reductant Heater A Current Too High","P214F concerns heater A of the DEF system, which Ford and GM both assign to the heater inside the tank (heater circuit 1). The code says this element consumed more current or power than intended. Ford's 2023 diesel summary performs one check per heating cycle, right after a cold start, and decides within 2.2 s when tank heater power is higher than expected.",["Tank heater element internally shorted (often replaced with the tank sender unit)","Water ingress or corrosion in the heater connector","Chafed heater wiring shorted to ground","Faulty heater driver in the reductant control module"],["Check engine light on","DEF system warning in cold weather","Delayed DEF dosing after cold starts"],2,3,["P21DD","P20B9","P20BA","P20BB","P20BC","P221D"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2150:["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P2150 reports the common feed of injector group B shorted toward ground. In GM's 2018 Duramax tables group 2 holds injectors 2 and 3 on the 2.8 L four-cylinder but injectors 2 and 5 on the 6.6 L V8; the test is the same as for group A – 0.5 Ω or less to ground with the driver on, 5 failed samples out of 10, type A with lamp on the first trip.",["Group B supply wire chafed and shorted to ground","Injector of group B shorted to its body","Moisture in the injector harness connector","Faulty injector driver in the engine control module"],["Two cylinders misfire together","Marked power loss and vibration","Check engine lamp on immediately"],3,3,["P2149","P2151","P2147","P2153","P0264"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ B — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2151:["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Voltage Circuit High","P2151 marks the group B injector supply as too high. GM's 2018 Duramax checks the high-side pins of the bank 2 injectors with the driver switched off and sets the code at 0.5 Ω or less to supply potential, 5 of 10 samples, type A. On Ford's 2023 diesels the same number stands for an internal fault reported by the boost voltage chip of the module, so a harness check alone rarely solves it.",["Internal fault of the injector boost circuit in the module","Software falsely detecting the fault, reprogramming available","Group B supply wire shorted to battery voltage","Injector of group B with internal short"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire on the group B cylinders","Sometimes no noticeable symptom besides the lamp"],3,3,["P2149","P2150","P2148","P2154","P0265"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ B — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2152:["Fuel Injector Group C Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","P2152 belongs to the third shared injector supply, so it appears only on engines with at least three injector groups or, at GM petrol engines, at least three cylinders. GM's 2009 Duramax puts injectors 2 and 5 into group 3 and flags an open, short or missing load after 6 ms, type A.",["Injector harness rubbed through at plenum, bolts or fuel line","Loose or corroded injector connector","Open coil or piezo stack in an injector of the group","Faulty power stage in the engine control module"],["Misfire on the group C cylinders","Rough running, reduced power","Check engine lamp on"],3,3,["P2149","P2153","P2154","P2155","P0203"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ C — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2153:["Fuel Injector Group C Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P2153 reports the third shared injector supply shorted toward ground. GM's 2018 Duramax tables use it only for the 6.6 L V8, where bank 3 feeds injectors 6 and 7; the four-cylinder 2.8 L has just two banks and never sets it. The criterion matches the other low codes – 0.5 Ω or less between a high-side pin and ground while the driver is on, 5 of 10 samples at 100 ms, type A.",["Group C supply wire chafed and shorted to ground","Injector of group C shorted to its body","Moisture in the injector harness connector","Faulty injector driver in the engine control module"],["Misfire on the group C cylinders","Loss of power and vibration","Check engine lamp on"],3,3,["P2152","P2154","P2150","P2156","P0267"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ C — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2154:["Fuel Injector Group C Supply Voltage Circuit High","P2154 is the high fault of injector supply group C. On GM's 2018 Duramax V8 it covers injectors 6 and 7: with the driver off, 0.5 Ω or less from a high-side pin to supply potential in 5 of 10 samples sets it, type A, one trip. Ford's 2023 diesels assign it to an internal error flagged by the module's high-voltage injector driver chip, a strong hint that the control unit itself is at fault.",["Internal hardware fault of the injector driver in the module","Group C supply wire shorted to battery voltage","Injector of group C with internal short"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire on the group C cylinders","Rough running at idle"],3,3,["P2152","P2153","P2151","P2157","P0268"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ C — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2155:["Fuel Injector Group D Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","P2155 is the open or general fault of the fourth shared injector supply. On GM's 2009 Duramax V8 group 4 joins injectors 8 and 3; an open, short or missing load for 6 ms sets the code, type A. The Passat VR6 of 2014 runs four supply groups and checks group D against a high-side current window of under 2.6 A or above 14.9 A. GM petrol direct injection uses it for the high-side control line of cylinder 4.",["Injector harness damaged or wire open","Water entering an injector harness connector","Open coil or piezo stack in an injector of the group","Faulty power stage in the engine control module"],["Misfire on the group D cylinders","Rough running and reduced power","Check engine lamp on"],3,3,["P2146","P2152","P2156","P2157","P0204"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ D — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2156:["Fuel Injector Group D Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P2156 reports the fourth shared injector supply shorted toward ground. GM's 2018 Duramax uses it only on the 6.6 L V8, where bank 4 combines injectors 3 and 8; the high-side pin reading 0.5 Ω or less to ground while switched on sets it after 5 of 10 samples, type A, lamp on the first trip. Ford's 2023 diesel summary stops at group C, so the code does not appear there.",["Group D supply wire chafed and shorted to ground","Injector of group D shorted to its body","Moisture in the injector harness connector","Faulty injector driver in the engine control module"],["Two cylinders misfire together","Strong vibration and power loss","Check engine lamp on immediately"],3,3,["P2155","P2157","P2153","P2147","P0270"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ D — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2157:["Fuel Injector Group D Supply Voltage Circuit High","P2157 flags the group D injector supply as too high. GM's 2018 Duramax V8 tests the high-side pins of injectors 3 and 8 with the driver off; 0.5 Ω or less to supply potential in 5 of 10 samples sets it, type A, one trip, and the 2025 tables require 4 of 8. For GM petrol direct injection, documented in the Saab 9-5 2.0T procedure, it means excess voltage on the high-side control line of cylinder 4.",["Internal hardware fault of the injector driver in the module","Group D supply wire shorted to battery voltage","Injector of group D with internal short"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire on the group D cylinders","Several injector high codes stored together"],3,3,["P2155","P2156","P2154","P2148","P0271"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ D — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2158:["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Circuit","P2158 reports an electrical fault in the circuit of a second vehicle speed signal, sensor B. P0500 is the matching code for sensor A. Which pickup carries the letter B is up to the manufacturer: a transmission output sensor, one of the ABS wheel sensors or another wheel.",["Speed sensor B defective or its tone ring damaged","Broken wire, corroded or loose connector in the sensor circuit","Retrofitted accessory interfering with the speed signal (Ducati anti-theft kit)"],["Check engine light on","Speedometer erratic or dropping out","Cruise control or ABS/traction functions unavailable"],2,1,["P2159","P0500","P0501","P0502","P0503","P215A"],"חיישן מהירות הרכב‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2159:["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2159 means the circuit of speed sensor B is electrically intact, but its signal does not fit: implausible jumps, dropouts or a value that disagrees with other speed sources. Two makers document it. Audi lists P2159 with fault environment code 8099 as a plausibility fault of speed sensor B on the 0B5 S tronic gearbox of the 2010–2014 RS5 and the S4, S5, S6 and S7;",["Faulty speed sensor or transmission sensor module (Audi 0B5)","Damaged tone ring, wrong air gap or metal debris on the sensor tip","Intermittent contact in wiring or connector","Wrong tyre size or speed factor configured"],["Check engine light or gearbox warning on","Erratic shifting or emergency gearbox mode","Speedometer jumping"],3,3,["P2158","P0501","P0500","P215A","P215B"],"חיישן מהירות הרכב‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P215A:["Vehicle Speed - Wheel Speed Correlation","P215A compares the vehicle speed used by the powertrain with the speed derived from the ABS wheel sensors and sets when the two disagree. Volvo and Mack trucks document it most clearly: with I-Shift or mDRIVE gearboxes the code appears once the difference exceeds 12 km/h (7.5 mph), and the advice is to verify the speed factor and the tyre size stored in the brake controller before testing sensors.",["Tyre size or speed factor not matching the vehicle (common after tyre or axle changes)","Faulty wheel speed sensor or damaged tone ring","Poor ABS module ground or wiring fault in the speed signal path","Fault in the transmission-side vehicle speed source"],["Check engine light on","Speedometer dropping out","ABS, traction or cruise control warnings, power dropouts"],2,1,["P215B","P215C","P0500","P0501","P2158","P2159"],""],P215B:["Vehicle Speed - Output Shaft Speed Correlation","P215B checks whether the vehicle speed, as the control unit has chosen it, matches the speed implied by the transmission output shaft. GM uses it widely in hybrids and EVs. The 2011 Volt tables set it, Type A with MIL after one trip, when wheel-based and output-shaft-based speed differ by more than 6.21 mph or when no secured speed source remains, counted over 400 of 800 samples of 25 ms.",["Damaged wheel speed sensor (GM Bolt EV broken anti-click washer)","Faulty transmission output speed sensor or its wiring","Hybrid or transmission control software (FCA Pacifica Hybrid)","Lost speed message from another module on the data bus"],["Check engine light on after one trip","ABS, traction or stability lamps, systems switched off for the drive","Clicking noise from a front wheel (Bolt EV)"],2,3,["P215A","P215C","P0720","P0721","P0722","P0500"],""],P215C:["Output Shaft Speed - Wheel Speed Correlation","P215C compares the transmission output shaft speed with the output speed calculated back from the wheel sensors. Unlike P215B it does not judge the final vehicle speed but the agreement between these two measured sources. GM's 2019 hybrid tables set it as Type B, MIL after two trips, when the output shaft and the average from wheel and motor speeds differ by more than 50 or 60 rpm for 0.23 s.",["Transmission control software too sensitive, for example under braking (FCA bulletins)","Mechanical driveline fault such as a broken transfer unit spline (Jeep Cherokee)","Faulty output shaft speed sensor or wiring","Faulty wheel speed sensor or mismatched tyre sizes"],["Check engine light on","Harsh or irregular shifting","Grinding noise or loss of all-wheel drive (transfer unit damage)"],2,3,["P215B","P215A","P0720","P0721","P0722","P0723"],""],P215D:["Reductant Pump B Stuck On","P215D says the second DEF pump, called pump B or pump 2, keeps running or stays powered although the controller has commanded it off. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Pump B itself is documented: Ford's 6.7L Super Duty trucks of 2023 can store pump B circuit codes P20FA, P20FC and P20FD (SSM 51891), and FCA names the same channel Reductant Pump 2 on 3.0L EcoDiesel models.",["Output stage in the control module no longer switching off","Pump control line shorted so the pump receives power permanently","Welded contacts in the pump supply relay"],["Check engine light on","Pump audible after switching off the engine","DEF system warning, possibly a flat battery after standing"],2,3,["P201F","P20FA","P20FB","P20FC","P20FD"],"משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P215E:["Reductant Heater D Current Too Low","P215E says the fourth DEF heating element, heater D, drew less current than expected while it was switched on, so it is probably not warming the fluid. Which element carries the letter D depends on the maker; many SCR systems stop at three. No maker documents P215E publicly. GM's 2025 Duramax tables and Ford's 2023 diesel summary check only heaters A to C;",["Heating element D open or burnt through, often inside a heated line or pump assembly","Corroded or loose pins at the heater D connector limiting current","Heater feed fuse or relay open, so the element gets no voltage","Weak heater output stage in the engine or DEF control module"],["Check engine light together with a DEF or emission system message","Dosing starts late or not at all after cold starts in frost","Restart countdown or speed limitation if the fault stays active"],2,3,["P215F","P20C5","P20C6","P20C7","P20C8","P21DD","P221C","P221E"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ D — ערך נמוך מדי"],P215F:["Reductant Heater D Current Too High","P215F is set when heater D of the DEF system pulls more current than its design allows, which points to a partly shorted element or a leak path to ground in its wiring. The letter D is assigned by each maker, and many systems have only three heaters. No maker documents P215F publicly.",["Heating element D partly shorted internally","Moisture or DEF crystals in the heater D connector bridging pins","Chafed heater lead touching ground or a neighbouring circuit"],["Check engine light with a DEF or emission system warning","DEF stays frozen in the affected area during cold weather","Blown heater fuse in some cases"],2,3,["P215E","P20C5","P20C7","P20C8","P214F","P221D","P221F"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ D — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2160:["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","P2160 reports that speed signal B shows little or no activity although the vehicle is plainly moving. Which pickup carries the letter B is the manufacturer's choice. GM assigns P2160 to the transfer case output speed sensor of its four-wheel-drive models (table 18OBDG04): with a gear engaged, moderate pedal and torque, no braking and the transmission output turning, a raw sensor reading under 25 rpm for 4.5 seconds…",["Broken signal wire or short to ground between sensor B and the module","Speed sensor B itself delivers no pulses","Corroded or pushed-back pins at the sensor connector","Tone wheel loose or missing after transfer case or driveline work"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","Four-wheel-drive warning or 4WD modes unavailable","Speedometer or cruise control misbehaving on some models"],2,1,["P2161","P2158","P2159","P2162","P0502"],"חיישן מהירות הרכב‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2161:["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic/High","P2161 flags a speed signal B that behaves in ways no real vehicle can: it collapses for a moment, jumps or reads implausibly high. GM documents the code for the transfer case output speed sensor (18OBDG04). While the truck is driven in gear without braking, a drop of the sensor speed larger than a delta threshold starts a 3-second fail timer, and five such counts store the code as Type B.",["Connector contact opening briefly under vibration","Signal wire chafed against the transfer case or frame","Metal debris on the magnetic sensor tip","Chipped or cracked tone wheel"],["Check engine lamp, often only on rough roads","Speedometer needle twitching","Sporadic four-wheel-drive or shift complaints"],2,1,["P2160","P2158","P2159","P2162","P0503"],""],P2162:["Vehicle Speed Sensor A/B Correlation","P2162 means two speed sources, A and B, disagree by more than the calibration permits although each circuit is electrically sound. Depending on the vehicle, A and B can be a transmission output sensor, a transfer case sensor or wheel sensors read through the ABS unit. No manufacturer documents P2162 publicly.",["Tyre size or axle ratio differs from the programmed values","Metal debris or damage on one of the two sensors","Damaged or wrong tone wheel on one shaft or hub","Wheel speed signal from the ABS unit faulty"],["Check engine lamp","Speedometer reading wrong or unsteady","Harsh or mistimed shifts, possibly a fixed-gear fallback"],2,3,["P2158","P2159","P2160","P2161","P0500","P0501","P215A"],"חיישן מהירות הרכב‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2163:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor A Maximum Stop Performance","P2163 concerns position signal A at the upper end of its travel: with the throttle or pedal resting on its maximum mechanical stop, the reading or the learned full-open value lies outside the band the calibration accepts. On Ford layouts A is the first throttle body sensor, while D to F belong to the pedal. Ford lists P2163 for the 2014 Boss 302S with MIL and wrench lamp.",["Carbon or a bent stop keeps the plate from reaching full opening","Sensor A track worn at the full-open end","Replacement throttle body not matching or not relearned","Contact resistance in the sensor connector shifting the signal"],["Check engine and throttle warning lamps on","Engine does not reach full power","Limp mode with limited throttle opening"],2,3,["P2109","P2164","P0121","P2135","P2119"],""],P2164:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor B Maximum Stop Performance","P2164 is the full-travel test for position signal B. When the throttle or pedal is held at its upper stop, sensor B has to report a value inside a calibrated band; a reading or learned maximum outside that band sets the code. Ford and GM call their second throttle body sensor B, so on those designs the code points at the throttle body, yet no manufacturer documents P2164 publicly.",["Sensor B track worn or drifted at the full-open end","Deposits or a damaged stop limit the plate travel","Corroded contact on the sensor B signal or reference pin","End positions not relearned after part replacement"],["Engine warning lamp on","Power limited at high throttle demand","Occasional limp mode"],2,3,["P2113","P2163","P2165","P0221","P2135"],""],P2165:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor C Maximum Stop Performance","P2165 belongs to the rarely used letter C. It is set when position signal C, at the upper stop of its throttle or pedal, reports a value the controller cannot accept as full travel. Since Ford gives A and B to the throttle and D to F to the pedal, C only appears on layouts with a third sensor track or a different naming scheme. No manufacturer documents P2165 publicly;",["Sensor C track worn at the end of travel","Replacement throttle or pedal with a different characteristic","Mechanical obstruction before the upper stop","Resistance in the sensor C wiring or connector"],["Engine warning lamp on","Reduced power at full load"],2,3,["P2114","P2163","P2164","P2136","P2137"],""],P2166:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor D Maximum Stop Performance","P2166 refers to position signal D, which on Ford designs is the first track of the accelerator pedal. The code means the reading with the pedal pressed all the way does not match the calibrated maximum, for instance because the pedal never reaches its stop or the track is worn at the far end. No manufacturer documents P2166 publicly;",["Floor mat or object keeps the pedal from its stop","Pedal sensor track D worn at full travel","Bent pedal arm or damaged pedal bracket","Corroded pedal connector shifting signal D"],["Engine warning lamp on","No kickdown or no full power with the pedal floored","Possible limp mode"],1,3,["P2115","P2167","P2122","P2138"],""],P2167:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor E Maximum Stop Performance","P2167 checks position signal E at maximum travel; on designs that call the pedal tracks D, E and F, E is the second pedal sensor. The code sets when E, with the pedal fully down, reports a value outside the accepted band. Because the second track usually has a different characteristic from the first, checking D and E side by side at full pedal reveals whether only E is off or the pedal itself is blocked.",["Pedal sensor track E worn at the full-travel end","Contact corrosion in the pedal connector","Pedal cannot reach its stop (mat, object, bent bracket)"],["Engine warning lamp on","Limited power with the pedal fully pressed","Possible limp mode"],1,3,["P2116","P2166","P2168","P2127","P2138"],""],P2168:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor F Maximum Stop Performance","P2168 covers position signal F at maximum travel. Letter F only exists where the pedal carries a third sensor track; GM's 2004 engine table, for example, runs a third pedal sensor under the F circuit codes, whereas most current cars make do with two tracks. The code sets when F, with the pedal at its upper stop, reports a value outside the accepted range. No manufacturer documents P2168 publicly;",["Third pedal track F worn at full travel","Poor contact on the sensor F pins","Pedal held short of its stop"],["Engine warning lamp on","Full power not available"],1,3,["P2117","P2167","P2132","P2139","P2140"],""],P2169:["Exhaust Pressure Regulator Vent Solenoid Control Circuit/Open","The name points to a solenoid that lets an exhaust pressure regulator vent, but the only public, code-exact use found is on Jaguar Land Rover petrol models, where this code family belongs to the active exhaust valve: a solenoid in the tailpipe section switches a flap between quiet and sport sound. P2169 is the open or general fault of its control line.",["Broken wire or loose connector at the exhaust valve solenoid, often from heat or road dirt","Vehicle configuration enables an active exhaust valve that is not fitted","Solenoid coil burnt through"],["Check engine lamp on","Exhaust sound no longer changes with the drive mode"],2,1,["P2170","P2171","P0475"],"סולנואיד אוורור וסת לחץ פליטה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P216A:["Fuel Injector Group E Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Injector group E exists only on engines with at least five cylinders or five separately fed injector groups. GM petrol direct injection uses one group per cylinder, and its 2024 tables (24OBDG07) state it plainly: injector E is cylinder 5. The code covers the high-side feed of that injector.",["Injector harness rubbed through at the intake plenum, valve cover bolts or fuel line","Cylinder 5 injector shorted internally","High-side driver in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine lamp on, often with a cylinder 5 misfire code","Rough running and reduced power"],3,3,["P216B","P216C","P216D","P0205","P0305","P2146"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ E — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P216B:["Fuel Injector Group E Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P216B reports the feed of injector group E pulled toward ground. In GM petrol direct injection, group E means the injector of cylinder 5, so the code appears on V6 and V8 engines. GM's 2016 3.6 LGX V6 and 2018 6.2 LT4 V8 tables treat it as the injector 5 high-side line being grounded: while the driver is switched on, 25 A or more flows through it.",["High-side wire of injector 5 chafed through to ground, for example on the transmission","Cylinder 5 injector shorted to its housing","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 5 misfire, noticeable shaking"],3,3,["P216A","P216C","P216E","P0273","P0305","P2147"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ E — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P216C:["Fuel Injector Group E Supply Voltage Circuit High","P216C is the opposite fault of group E: the feed of the cylinder 5 injector carries voltage when it should not. GM tests it while the high-side driver is switched off; if 1 V or less remains between the signal and the controller supply, the line is treated as shorted to power.",["Injector 5 feed chafed against a powered circuit","High-side driver in the engine control module leaking voltage","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the injector connector"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 5 misfire and rough idle"],3,3,["P216A","P216B","P216F","P0274","P0305","P2148"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ E — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P216D:["Fuel Injector Group F Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","P216D is the general fault of injector group F, which GM petrol direct injection equates with cylinder 6; its 2024 tables (24OBDG07) call it injector F. GM uses this code for shorts on the high side rather than opens: the 2008 3.6 LLT sets it for cylinder 6 shorted to ground or battery, while an open on either side goes to P0206;",["Injector harness rubbed through on V6 engines","Water in the bank 2 injector harness connector (Corvette LT6)","Cylinder 6 injector shorted"],["Check engine lamp on, cylinder 6 misfire","With the LT6 several bank 2 codes and fuel pressure faults at once"],3,3,["P216E","P216F","P216A","P217D","P0206","P0306"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ F — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P216E:["Fuel Injector Group F Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P216E marks the feed of injector group F, the cylinder 6 injector on GM petrol direct injection, as shorted toward ground. It therefore concerns GM V6 and V8 engines with direct injection. The 2016 3.6 LGX and the 2018 LT4 tables use a current test: with the driver on, 25 A or more through the high side counts as a short, and 10 failures in 20 samples taken every 100 ms at 11 V or more store a type A code with the…",["Cylinder 6 feed wire chafed through to ground","Cylinder 6 injector shorted to ground","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 6 misfire and loss of power"],3,3,["P216D","P216F","P216B","P0276","P0306"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ F — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P216F:["Fuel Injector Group F Supply Voltage Circuit High","P216F is set when the group F supply, on GM petrol direct injection the high-side line of cylinder 6, shows voltage while the driver is off. GM's criterion in its 2016 (16OBDG07A) and 2018 LT4 tables is 1 V or less between the line and the controller supply, which means the wire is practically at battery level. At 11 V or more, 10 failures out of 20 samples at 100 ms store it as type A, MIL on the first trip.",["Cylinder 6 feed shorted to another powered wire","Engine control module driver fault, especially with several high codes","Moisture in the injector connector"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 6 misfire"],3,3,["P216D","P216E","P216C","P0277","P0306"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ F — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2170:["Exhaust Pressure Regulator Vent Solenoid Control Circuit Low","P2170 reports the control line of the exhaust pressure regulator vent solenoid pulled toward ground. Jaguar Land Rover uses it for the solenoid of the active exhaust valve; its March 2018 shop foreman call lists P2170-11, meaning the line is grounded, on 2018 Discovery Sport and Evoque with active exhaust.",["PCM software with an overly sensitive fault strategy, fixed by an update","Exhaust flap stiff, often from a misaligned heat shield or cold weather","Control wire chafed through to ground near the exhaust"],["Check engine lamp on","Restricted performance message on some models","Exhaust valve heard clicking at start-up"],2,3,["P2169","P2171"],"סולנואיד אוורור וסת לחץ פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2171:["Exhaust Pressure Regulator Vent Solenoid Control Circuit High","P2171 means the module sees too much voltage on the control line of the exhaust pressure regulator vent solenoid, usually because the line touches battery voltage or the solenoid shorts internally. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit","Solenoid coil shorted internally","Output stage in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Exhaust flap stays in one position"],2,1,["P2169","P2170"],"סולנואיד אוורור וסת לחץ פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2172:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Sudden High Air Flow Detected","P2172 is set when the engine abruptly takes in far more air than the throttle opening can explain, as if a large leak had appeared behind the throttle plate. The controller compares measured airflow (MAF or MAP based) with the flow its throttle model expects and reacts to a quick jump in the difference.",["Hose, PCV line or brake booster line slipped off or split","Spread or pushed-out terminals at the MAP sensor connector","Engine software with oversensitive detection (reflash available)","Leaking throttle body gasket"],["Check engine lamp","High or hunting idle, hissing noise from the engine bay","Power reduction or limp mode"],2,3,["P2173","P2174","P0106","P0171","P0101"],""],P2173:["Throttle Actuator Control System - High Air Flow Detected","P2173 reports an air surplus that builds up gradually: across a longer stretch of driving the engine receives more air than the throttle model predicts, which points to a small leak, a cracked vent hose or a plate that no longer seals. FCA calls it High Airflow/Vacuum Leak Detected (Slow Accumulation).",["Cracked or loose crankcase ventilation or oil vapour tube","Small leak at an intake gasket or vacuum hose","Outdated engine software (FCA reflash)","MAP sensor connector with poor contact"],["Check engine lamp after some driving","Jerking or limp mode","Start/stop system deactivated on some models"],2,3,["P2172","P2175","P0171","P0174","P2110"],""],P2174:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Sudden Low Air Flow Detected","P2174 means the airflow fell abruptly well below what the current throttle opening should deliver. The controller sees a fast negative gap between measured airflow and its throttle-model estimate, as happens when the intake is suddenly blocked, the plate jams or a hose collapses under vacuum. No manufacturer documents P2174 publicly.",["Air inlet suddenly blocked by snow, leaves or debris","Intake duct collapsed or kinked","Throttle plate sticking short of the commanded angle","Airflow or manifold pressure sensor reading too low"],["Sudden loss of power","Check engine and throttle warning lamps","Possible limp mode or stalling"],2,3,["P2175","P2172","P0101","P2112"],""],P2175:["Throttle Actuator Control System - Low Air Flow Detected","P2175 tracks an air shortfall that develops slowly: over many operating points the engine receives less air than the throttle position predicts, and the learned correction finally exceeds its limit. A clogged air filter, carbon narrowing the throttle bore, a partly blocked intake or an airflow sensor drifting low are the usual reasons. No manufacturer documents P2175 publicly.",["Carbon build-up narrowing the throttle bore","Heavily clogged air filter or intake restriction","Contaminated airflow sensor reading low","Idle or airflow adaptation not reset after throttle cleaning"],["Check engine lamp","Sluggish response and low power","Unsteady or low idle"],1,3,["P2174","P2173","P0101","P0506","P2119"],""],P2176:["Throttle Actuator A Control System - Idle Position Not Learned","P2176 says the closed rest position of throttle A could not be learned. At key-on or after shutdown the controller drives the plate onto its lower stop and stores the sensor values; if they stay outside the window after the permitted attempts, the code is set.",["Carbon on plate and bore preventing a clean closed position","Ice from a frozen crankcase ventilation holding the plate open","Engine software misjudging the sensor signals (update available)","Idle learn not performed after cleaning or module replacement"],["Check engine lamp right after start","High, surging or unstable idle","Reduced engine power after a cold start"],1,3,["P218A","P2109","P2119","P0121","P0506"],""],P2177:["System Too Lean Off Idle (Bank 1)","P2177 means bank 1's long-term trim has to add too much fuel once the engine is off idle, at part load and while accelerating. Bosch-type systems learn this as a multiplicative factor that scales with airflow, unlike the additive idle part behind P2187. GM's 2005 V6 and 2008 3.6 LLT set it above a factor of 1.23, GM's 2023 and 2024 tables above 1.27, both over two trips.",["Fuel pressure too low under load, for example a weak pump or clogged filter","Air mass sensor reading too low or contaminated","Leak after the air mass sensor, often on the boost side","Calibration error or damaged A/F sensor wiring covered by bulletins"],["Check engine lamp on after two trips","Hesitation or lack of power when accelerating"],2,1,["P2178","P2179","P2187","P0171","P0087"],""],P2178:["System Too Rich Off Idle (Bank 1)","P2178 is the rich-side limit of the bank 1 load adaptation: above idle the long-term trim has to take away more fuel than allowed. GM's Bosch-based V6 engines of 2005 and 2008 set it below a factor of 0.78, the 2023 and 2024 tables below 0.77, each after two trips.",["Air mass sensor reading too high","Fuel pressure too high or injectors over-delivering","Calibration error fixed by a software update","Fuel vapour from purge or boiling fuel in the low-pressure system"],["Check engine lamp on after two trips","Higher fuel consumption, fuel smell"],2,1,["P2177","P2180","P2188","P0172","P0101"],""],P2179:["System Too Lean Off Idle (Bank 2)","P2179 is the bank 2 version of P2177 on engines with a front oxygen sensor for each cylinder bank: the load-dependent, multiplicative share of bank 2's long-term correction has reached its lean limit. GM's 2005 2.8 and 3.6 V6 and the 2008 3.6 LLT use a factor above 1.23, GM's 2024 tables above 1.27, both over two trips.",["Low fuel pressure or air mass sensor fault, usually with P2177 too","Restricted injector on bank 2","Intake leak or front oxygen sensor fault on bank 2"],["Check engine lamp on after two trips","Hesitation under load"],2,1,["P2177","P2180","P2189","P0174"],""],P217A:["Fuel Injector Group G Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Group G only exists on engines with seven or more injector groups, in practice eight-cylinder engines with direct injection. GM's 2023 and 2024 summary tables (23OBDG07, 24OBDG07) name the cylinder 7 injector G and use P217A for a short on its high side: less than 0.5 ohm between the module pin and ground while the driver is off, or to the injector supply while it is on.",["Cylinder 7 injector feed shorted to ground or supply in the harness","Cylinder 7 injector shorted internally","Engine control module driver faulty"],["Check engine lamp on, cylinder 7 misfire","Rough running under load"],3,3,["P217B","P217C","P217D","P0207","P0307"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ G — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P217B:["Fuel Injector Group G Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P217B reports the feed of injector group G as grounded, which on GM's direct-injection V8 engines is the injector of cylinder 7, at the rear of bank 1. GM's 2016 table 16OBDG07A and the 2018 LT4 table of the supercharged 6.2 V8 measure it with the driver switched on: if 25 A or more flows through the high side, the line is grounded somewhere. The check runs every 100 ms as soon as the battery has 11 V;",["Cylinder 7 feed wire grounded at the rear of the engine","Cylinder 7 injector shorted to ground","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 7 misfire, reduced power"],3,3,["P217A","P217C","P217E","P0279","P0307"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ G — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P217C:["Fuel Injector Group G Supply Voltage Circuit High","P217C means the group G injector supply, cylinder 7 on GM's direct-injection V8 engines, is pulled up to supply voltage. GM tests this while the high-side driver is off: if the line sits within 1 V of the controller supply, the module treats it as shorted to power.",["Cylinder 7 feed shorted to a powered wire","Damaged or wet injector connector","Engine control module driver fault"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 7 misfire"],3,3,["P217A","P217B","P217F","P0280","P0307"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ G — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P217D:["Fuel Injector Group H Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Group H is the eighth injector group, on GM petrol direct injection the injector of cylinder 8, the last one on bank 2 of a V8. GM's 2023 and 2024 tables call it injector H and use P217D when its high side shows less than 0.5 ohm to ground with the driver off or to the injector supply with the driver on; two events above 9 V store the code in one trip.",["Cylinder 8 injector feed shorted in the harness","Water in the bank 2 injector harness connector, Corvette LT6","Cylinder 8 injector shorted internally"],["Check engine lamp on, cylinder 8 misfire","Several bank 2 injector codes at once if the connector is wet"],3,3,["P217E","P217F","P216D","P2155","P0208","P0308"],"מתח אספקה קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ H — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P217E:["Fuel Injector Group H Supply Voltage Circuit Low","P217E flags the supply of injector group H as grounded, on GM's direct-injection V8 engines the injector of cylinder 8. GM lists it for the 6.2 LT4 in 2018 and in its 2016 table 16OBDG07A. With the high-side driver switched on, a current of 25 A or more means the line has found a path to ground; at 11 V or more, 10 bad samples out of 20 taken at 100 ms set the code as type A and light the MIL right away.",["Cylinder 8 feed wire chafed to ground","Cylinder 8 injector shorted to its housing","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 8 misfire, engine shakes"],3,3,["P217D","P217F","P217B","P0282","P0308"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ H — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],P217F:["Fuel Injector Group H Supply Voltage Circuit High","P217F is the last code of the injector group series: the feed of group H, cylinder 8 on GM's direct-injection V8 engines, shows supply voltage although the high-side driver is switched off. GM's tables 16OBDG07A, 18OBDG03A for the 6.2 LT4 and 19OBDG03A set it when the line stays within 1 V of the controller supply, counting 10 failures out of 20 samples at 100 ms with 11 V or more, type A, MIL on the first trip.",["Cylinder 8 feed shorted to a powered wire","Moisture or corrosion in the injector connector","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on immediately","Cylinder 8 misfire, possibly rich running on bank 2"],3,3,["P217D","P217E","P217C","P0283","P0308"],"קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ H — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2180:["System Too Rich Off Idle (Bank 2)","P2180 closes the series: bank 2's long-term trim must remove too much fuel above idle, so its multiplicative adaptation sits at the rich limit. GM's 2005 2.8 and 3.6 V6 and the 2008 3.6 LLT use a factor below 0.78, GM's 2024 tables below 0.77, both over two trips. VW's 2014 Touareg 3.0 TSI hybrid and 3.6 VR6 set it below -30 % on bank 2.",["Injector on bank 2 leaking or over-delivering","Fuel pressure too high or air mass sensor over-reading, usually with P2178","Bank 2 front oxygen sensor reading rich"],["Check engine lamp on after two trips","Higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P2178","P2179","P2190","P0175"],""],P2181:["Cooling System Performance","P2181 is the engine computer's verdict that the coolant warms up too slowly or settles below its target, almost always because the thermostat no longer closes. CARB requires the thermostat to be monitored and flags a failure when the warm-up stays more than 11.1 °C under the regulating point. GM (18OBDG03A) compares the block sensor with the radiator sensor during warm-up;",["Thermostat not closing fully because of wear, corrosion or debris on the seat","Engine control software too sensitive, fixed by a reflash on some models (e.g. Kia SA463)","Radiator fan running constantly and overcooling the engine","Low coolant level or air in the system distorting the temperature reading"],["Check engine light, usually without any change in driving behaviour","Temperature gauge rises slowly or stays below normal","Weak cabin heating in cold weather","Higher fuel consumption on short trips"],2,1,["P0128","P0125","P0116","P2183","P00B6","P0597"],"מערכת קירור — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2182:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit","P2182 is the general circuit code for the second coolant temperature sensor: the module sees a fault in its wiring or signal but does not sort it into low, high or erratic. Where sensor 2 sits is up to the maker. Mazda fits it low on the radiator, VW calls it the radiator outlet sender, Ford's Escape plug-in hybrid uses it in the cabin heater loop, GM uses a second engine sensor.",["Loose, corroded or water-damaged connector at sensor 2","Signal or reference wire to sensor 2 open or damaged","Sensor 2 itself defective"],["Check engine light","Radiator fan runs continuously as a precaution","Thermostat or cooling diagnostics unavailable"],1,1,["P2183","P2184","P2185","P2186","P0115","P01E3"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2183:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit Range/Performance","P2183 means sensor 2 delivers a voltage inside the valid band, yet the temperature does not fit the other readings. Most makers test this after a long cold soak, when all temperatures should match. The VW Touareg with engine CNRB sets it when the radiator outlet sensor differs by more than 35 K from intake air, ambient or fuel temperature at start-up.",["Water ingress or internal corrosion in sensor 2 shifting its reading","Control software misjudging soak time, block heater or cabin heater use","Coolant hoses at the sensor loop swapped or air trapped after service","Aged sensor element drifting out of tolerance"],["Check engine light, often right after a cold start","Remote start disabled on some trucks","Engine overheat message without real overheating on some hybrids"],1,1,["P2182","P2184","P2185","P2186","P0116","P01E4","P26C1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 2 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2184:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit Low","Coolant sensors are NTC thermistors: the hotter they get, the lower their resistance and voltage. P2184 therefore reports a signal from sensor 2 so low that it would mean an impossibly hot engine, typically a signal wire touching ground or a shorted sensor. GM's 2019 tables (19OBDG03D) set it when resistance drops below about 47.5 ohms, matching 150 °C, for 5 s within 6 s (Type B, MIL after two trips).",["Signal wire of sensor 2 chafed through and touching ground","Sensor 2 internally shorted","Coolant or water in the connector bridging signal and ground"],["Check engine light after two drives on GM vehicles","Radiator fans running at full speed","Further codes and warnings if a harness is chafed"],1,1,["P2185","P2186","P2182","P2183","P0117","P01E5"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 2 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2185:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit High","P2185 is the high end of the sensor 2 circuit check. With an NTC thermistor a high signal stands for extreme cold, so the usual reason is an open circuit: a broken wire, an unplugged or corroded connector, or a sensor with an interrupted element; a short to voltage is rarer.",["Connector at sensor 2 unplugged, loose or corroded","Signal or ground wire of sensor 2 broken","Sensor element interrupted","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine light","Fans run permanently as a safety measure","Low coolant or temperature warning without a real cause on some models"],1,1,["P2184","P2186","P2182","P2183","P0118","P01E6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 2 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2186:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2186 covers a sensor 2 signal that jumps instead of changing smoothly. Coolant temperature moves slowly because of the mass of the liquid, so a step faster than physics allows points to a loose contact rather than a real change.",["Worn or loose pins in the sensor 2 connector","Wire broken inside its insulation or chafed harness making intermittent contact","Sensor 2 with an intermittent internal fault"],["Check engine light after two drives","Fans switching on and off irregularly","Temperature-related messages that appear and vanish"],1,1,["P2184","P2185","P2182","P2183","P0119","P01E7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 2 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2187:["System Too Lean at Idle (Bank 1)","P2187 means the long-term fuel trim of bank 1 has to add more fuel than allowed in the idle and low-load range. Many systems, especially Bosch ones, split mixture adaptation into an additive part, which dominates at low airflow, and a multiplicative part for load. An air leak adds a fixed amount of unmeasured air, which matters most at idle, so it shows up in the additive part.",["Air leak after the air mass sensor, often at the crankcase ventilation","Damaged front oxygen or A/F sensor wiring","Fuel pressure too low"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough or hunting idle, hissing from the engine bay"],2,1,["P2189","P2177","P0171","P2279","P2188"],""],P2188:["System Too Rich at Idle (Bank 1)","P2188 means the long-term fuel trim of bank 1 has to remove more fuel than allowed in the idle and low-load range, the additive part of the mixture adaptation on Bosch-type systems. GM's 2008 3.6 LLT sets it below -6.0 % at 520 to 1120 rpm and 1.7 to 7.8 g/s, with closed loop and coolant above 60 °C.",["Leaking injector or fuel pressure too high","Fuel vapour from the purge valve or oil-diluted crankcase gases","Air mass or manifold pressure reading wrong"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough idle, fuel smell"],2,1,["P2190","P2178","P0172","P2187"],""],P2189:["System Too Lean at Idle (Bank 2)","P2189 is the bank 2 version of P2187: on engines with a front oxygen sensor per bank, the long-term trim of bank 2 has to add more fuel than allowed at idle and low load. GM's 2005 2.8 and 3.6 V6 set it when the additive correction exceeds 7 %, the 2008 3.6 LLT above 6.1 % at 520 to 1120 rpm, airflow of 1.7 to 7.8 g/s, engine load of 11 to 45 % and coolant above 60 °C, and GM's 2024 tables above about 5.5 % over two…",["Intake gasket or runner leak on the bank 2 side","Shared vacuum leak, usually with P2187 present too","Bank 2 front sensor, its wiring or an injector on that bank"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough or hunting idle"],2,1,["P2187","P2190","P0174","P2179"],""],P218A:["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Idle Position Not Learned","P218A is the throttle B counterpart of P2176: on engines with a second electronic throttle, usually one per cylinder bank, that second unit failed to learn its closed rest position. GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 runs the same three-step learn for bank 2 as for bank 1.",["Carbon or ice keeping throttle B off its closed stop","Weak motor or gear wear in throttle unit B","Position sensors of throttle B outside the learn window","Supply or signal wiring fault at throttle B"],["Check engine lamp","Uneven idle between the banks","Reduced power"],2,3,["P2176","P210A","P2119"],""],P218B:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit","P218B is a general electrical fault in the second throttle/fuel inhibit line, B. An inhibit line carries a signal with which another unit can tell the engine computer to keep the throttle closed or stop fuelling. No manufacturer documents the B line publicly.",["Open or high-resistance inhibit B wire","Corroded or loose pins at the engine or throttle module connector","Fault in the unit that drives the inhibit signal"],["Check engine lamp on the following drive","Possible power limitation"],2,3,["P218C","P218D","P218E","P2552"],""],P218C:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit Range/Performance","P218C means the inhibit B line is electrically within limits, yet its state or response does not fit what the controller expects: it may signal a lock when none is requested, or fail to react during a function test. No manufacturer documents P218C publicly.",["Relay in the inhibit path sticking or switching late","Software versions of the communicating modules do not match","Intermittent contact causing implausible line states"],["Check engine lamp on the next drive","Occasional power reduction without obvious reason"],3,3,["P218B","P218D","P218E","P2553"],""],P218D:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit Low","P218D reports that the voltage on inhibit line B sits below the lowest permitted value, which normally points to a short to ground, a missing supply from the sending unit or an open line pulled down by the input stage. No manufacturer documents P218D publicly.",["Inhibit B wire shorted to ground","Water or corrosion in a connector of the inhibit line","Output stage of the sending module failed"],["Check engine lamp on the following drive","Possible power reduction"],2,3,["P218B","P218C","P218E","P2554"],""],P218E:["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit High","P218E says the inhibit B line carries more voltage than the controller allows, typically because it touches a battery-fed wire or the sending unit's output stage is stuck high. No manufacturer documents P218E publicly. On the A line, GM's 2005 table for the 3.5-litre V6 (L66) uses two limits for P2555: more than 10 V with the ignition on, or more than 4.5 V once the ignition is off, each judged over 4 seconds;",["Inhibit B wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit","Voltage fed back through a faulty module after ignition off","Relay contacts welded, keeping the line energised"],["Check engine lamp on the following drive","Possible power reduction"],2,3,["P218B","P218C","P218D","P2555"],""],P218F:["Reductant No Flow Detected","P218F means the SCR system is dosing on paper, but nothing reaches the exhaust: the expected link between dosing commands, pump effort and line pressure is missing. Ford's 2023 diesel summary, which calls the test a reductant delivery check for clogging, runs it while dosing with the pressure error inside 0.5 bar for 5 s.",["Dosing valve or its nozzle crystallised and blocked","Leak in the DEF line between pump and dosing valve","Partly frozen line in frost or control software that needs an update","Worn DEF pump that cannot keep up delivery"],["Check engine light with a DEF or emission system warning","Restart countdown or speed limitation if the fault persists","DEF consumption lower than usual","White crystalline deposits at the dosing valve or line joints"],3,3,["P20E8","P20E9","P208B","P208E","P204F","P249C","P2047"],""],P2190:["System Too Rich at Idle (Bank 2)","P2190 is the bank 2 counterpart of P2188: the long-term trim of bank 2 has to remove more fuel than allowed at idle and low load. GM's 2008 3.6 LLT sets it below -6.0 % in the same window it uses for P2188 (520 to 1120 rpm, 1.7 to 7.8 g/s, closed loop, coolant above 60 °C, catalyst heating not active), and GM's 2005 2.8 and 3.6 V6 treat it in the same additive adaptation range.",["Leaking injector on bank 2","Shared cause such as air mass error or purge vapour, usually with P2188 too","Bank 2 front sensor reading lean"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough idle, fuel smell"],2,1,["P2188","P2189","P0175","P2180"],""],P2191:["System Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 1)","P2191 sets once bank 1's long-term trim has run into its enrichment limit in the upper load range, so the engine would be lean there without the correction. It is the third load zone next to P2187 (idle) and P2177 (off idle), and it is where a supply that copes at cruise first falls short: a tired fuel pump, a clogged filter, poor pressure regulation, injectors that flow too little, or an air mass sensor that reads…",["Fuel pump or pressure regulation unable to hold pressure at high demand","Clogged fuel filter or strainer","Air mass sensor under-reading at high airflow","Partly blocked injectors on bank 1","Charge-air or intake leak behind the air mass sensor (turbo engines)"],["Check engine light on","Hesitation or flat spot under heavy throttle","Loss of power when climbing or towing","High positive long-term fuel trim at high load only"],2,1,["P2193","P2192","P2177","P2187","P0171"],""],P2192:["System Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 1)","P2192 is the rich-side limit of the bank 1 trim in the upper load zone: the controller has pulled as much fuel as it may and the front sensor still reports excess fuel. Typical sources grow with demand, such as an air mass sensor reading high, fuel pressure above specification, or injectors that over-deliver or drip at high rail pressure;",["ECM calibration issue covered by a software update (e.g. Kia 1.6 GDI)","Air mass sensor reading too high","Injector leaking or over-delivering at high rail pressure","Fuel pressure above specification"],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Fuel smell or dark exhaust under load"],2,1,["P2191","P2194","P2178","P2188","P0172"],""],P2193:["System Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 2)","P2193 reports for bank 2 what P2191 reports for bank 1: in the upper load zone the long-term trim of that bank sits at its enrichment limit. It only exists on engines with a separate front sensor per bank, such as V6, V8 and boxer engines. The useful question is whether bank 1 shows the same.",["Weak fuel supply (pump, filter, pressure regulation), usually with P2191","Restricted injectors on bank 2","Intake gasket or runner leak on the bank 2 side","Exhaust leak ahead of the bank 2 front sensor"],["Check engine light on","Hesitation under heavy acceleration","Bank 2 long-term trim much higher than bank 1 at high load"],2,1,["P2191","P2194","P2179","P2189","P0174"],""],P2194:["System Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 2)","P2194 means bank 2 has reached the lower limit of its trim in the upper load zone: the ECM is removing as much fuel as permitted, yet that bank still runs rich. Because air mass, fuel pressure and canister purge feed both banks, a rich error caused by them usually brings P2192 along.",["Leaking or over-delivering injector on bank 2","Bank 2 front sensor reading lean","Air mass sensor reading high or fuel pressure too high (usually with P2192)"],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Bank 2 long-term trim strongly negative at high load"],2,1,["P2192","P2193","P2180","P2190","P0175"],""],P2195:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 1, Sensor 1)","P2195 means the front oxygen or air-fuel sensor on bank 1 reports a lean mixture that the ECM does not believe, either because it stays lean or because it disagrees with other evidence. On GM's Bosch-based 2005 V6 the rear sensor has to read rich (above 0.85 V) while the front A/F sensor reads leaner than lambda 1.08 and the short-term trim sits at its maximum of 1.25, for about 100 s or 50 s in total.",["Front oxygen or A/F sensor aged or contaminated","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensor","Sensor signal or reference wiring fault"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Possible rough running or higher consumption from wrong fuelling"],2,1,["P2196","P2197","P0131","P0171","P2270"],""],P2196:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 1, Sensor 1)","P2196 means the front oxygen or air-fuel sensor on bank 1 reports a rich mixture that the ECM does not accept. On GM's Bosch-based 2005 V6 this is a cross-check with the rear sensor: the rear sensor reads lean (below 0.15 V) while the front A/F sensor reads richer than lambda 0.92 and the short-term trim has pulled to its minimum of 0.75, for about 100 s or 50 s in total.",["Front oxygen or A/F sensor contaminated or aged","Sensor signal shorted or reference circuit fault"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Possible hesitation or lean running"],2,1,["P2195","P2198","P0132","P0172","P2271"],""],P2197:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 2, Sensor 1)","P2197 is the bank 2 version of P2195 on engines with a front sensor per bank: the bank 2 front oxygen or A/F sensor keeps reporting lean in a way the ECM rejects. GM's Bosch-based 2005 2.8 and 3.6 V6 flag it when the bank 2 rear sensor reads rich (above 0.85 V) while the front sensor reads leaner than lambda 1.08 with short-term trim at its 1.25 maximum, a contradiction a real lean mixture would not produce.",["Bank 2 front oxygen or A/F sensor aged or contaminated","Exhaust manifold leak on bank 2 ahead of the sensor"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Possible rough running or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2195","P2198","P0151","P0174","P2629"],""],P2198:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 2, Sensor 1)","P2198 is the bank 2 counterpart of P2196: the bank 2 front oxygen or A/F sensor reports rich in a way the ECM does not accept. On GM's Bosch-based 2005 2.8 and 3.6 V6 the bank 2 rear sensor must read lean (below 0.15 V) while the front sensor reads richer than lambda 0.92 and the short-term trim has dropped to its 0.75 minimum; the code then sets after about 100 s, or 50 s cumulatively, over two trips.",["Bank 2 front oxygen or A/F sensor contaminated or aged","Sensor signal or reference wiring fault"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Possible hesitation or lean running"],2,1,["P2196","P2197","P0152","P0175"],""],P2199:["Intake Air Temperature Sensor 1/2 Correlation","P2199 compares two intake air temperature readings that should be close, typically one in the air mass sensor and one further downstream in the intake manifold or a combined pressure and temperature sensor. Each circuit can be fine on its own; the fault is the disagreement.",["One temperature sensor drifted or contaminated","Corroded connector or added resistance in one sensor circuit","Calibration issue fixed by a PCM update (e.g. RAM 1500 3.0 EcoDiesel 2020)","Strong heat soak or hot-air leak near one sensor"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable driveability change","Scan data shows two clearly different intake temperatures with the engine cold-soaked"],1,1,["P0111","P0112","P0113","P0096","P0097","P0098"],""],P219A:["Bank 1 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P219A means the ECM sees mixture differences between the cylinders of bank 1 that are large enough to raise emissions, even if the bank average is fine. CARB phased this monitor in from 25 % of 2011 to all 2014 model-year petrol vehicles (13 CCR 1968.2 (e)(6.2.1)(C)).",["One injector clogged, leaking or out of flow tolerance","Compression loss through an intake or exhaust valve","Air leak at one intake runner or gasket","ECM logic or sensor signal issue covered by software or wiring bulletins"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable symptom","Slight rough running or misfire codes when one cylinder is far off"],2,1,["P219B","P219C","P219D","P219E","P219F","P0300","P2195"],""],P219B:["Bank 2 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P219B is the bank 2 counterpart for V and boxer engines. Ford's 2012 summary shows one way to find it: the ECM watches the fast ripple of the bank's wide-band sensor over windows of roughly 50 revolutions and sets the code when more than 75 % of them fail, after 300 to 700 s of driving at 1000 to 3000 rpm and 20 to 60 % load. On one GM 2016 engine the bank 2 limit is 1.15 against 1.05 for bank 1.",["Leaking or contaminated injector on bank 2","Interference or damage in the bank 2 A/F sensor wiring","Intake runner or gasket leak at one bank 2 cylinder","PCM calibration addressed by a software update"],["Check engine light on","Usually no driveability change","Possible misfire codes on bank 2 cylinders"],2,1,["P219A","P0300","P2197","P0174","P0175"],""],P219C:["Cylinder 1 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P219C names cylinder 1 as the one whose mixture departs from the others. Not every system can do that: CARB lets the stored code point only as far as the monitoring method allows, so many engines just log P219A or P219B.",["Cylinder 1 injector clogged, leaking or out of tolerance","Valve leakage on cylinder 1 (leak-down test)","Intake runner or injector seal leak at cylinder 1","False detection fixed by ECM reprogramming (e.g. Subaru Crosstrek Hybrid)"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable symptom","Possible P0301 or rough idle if cylinder 1 deviates strongly"],2,1,["P219A","P219D","P0301","P0201"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 1"],P219D:["Cylinder 2 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P219D singles out cylinder 2. On engines with two banks, whether cylinder 2 sits on bank 1 or bank 2 depends on the maker's numbering, which decides whether P219A or P219B may appear alongside. Bulletins show three very different outcomes.",["Faulty high-pressure injector at cylinder 2 (direct injection)","Charge-air leak upsetting cylinder filling (e.g. RAM 3.0 Hurricane)","Detection logic corrected by software update (e.g. Hyundai Sonata 2.0T)","Compression loss at cylinder 2"],["Check engine light on","Often no driveability change","Reduced power or whistling noise if a charge-air leak is the cause"],2,1,["P219A","P219B","P219C","P219E","P0302"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 2"],P219E:["Cylinder 3 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P219E points at cylinder 3. Two bulletins show that a mixture code does not always mean a fuel part. Audi stored P219C to P21A1, one code per affected cylinder, on 2010 to 2012 S4, S5 and A6 with the 3.0 TFSI because of an incorrect software setting; the fix was new engine software and, in a later revision, a new crankcase pressure regulating valve.",["Exhaust valve leakage at cylinder 3 (e.g. worn guides on Lexus 8AR-FTS)","Cylinder 3 injector delivering the wrong amount","Incorrect ECM software setting (e.g. Audi 3.0 TFSI)","Faulty crankcase pressure regulating valve"],["Check engine light on","Possible P0303 or rough running","Reduced engine power in severe cases"],3,3,["P219A","P219D","P219F","P0303"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 3"],P219F:["Cylinder 4 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P219F singles out cylinder 4, the last cylinder on four-cylinder engines. Infiniti issued a bulletin for 2017 to 2018 QX60 with the direct-injection VQ35DD that stored only P219F without any driveability complaint; the remedy was ECM reprogramming followed by the idle air volume learn.",["Leaking injector at cylinder 4","Oversensitive detection fixed by ECM reprogramming (e.g. Infiniti QX60, Hyundai Sonata)","Fouled spark plug as a consequence of a rich cylinder"],["Check engine light on","Rough running or rattling noise when an injector leaks","No symptom when the cause is software"],2,1,["P219A","P219E","P21A0","P0304","P0172"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 4"],P21A0:["Cylinder 5 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A0 can only occur on engines with at least five cylinders. VW's 2014 specification books for the Golf, Jetta, Passat and Beetle with the 2.5 litre inline five list P219C to P21A0, one per cylinder, all judged the same way: the ECM briefly leans one cylinder, measures how much rougher the engine runs and derives an individual fuel correction; a result below 0.19 or above 1.50 is a fault.",["Cylinder 5 injector out of tolerance","Ignition or compression weakness at cylinder 5 affecting the roughness test","Software setting corrected by an update (e.g. Audi 3.0 TFSI)"],["Check engine light on","Possible P0305 or slight vibration at idle"],2,1,["P219A","P219F","P21A1","P0305"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 5"],P21A1:["Cylinder 6 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A1 marks cylinder 6, the last cylinder of an inline six or V6. The clearest example comes from the 2025 RAM 1500 with the 3.0 Hurricane twin-turbo inline six: the charge-air cooler housing had a loose crimp that let boost escape, the cylinders filled unevenly and P21A1 set together with other cylinder codes, accompanied by a whistle and lower boost; the cooler was inspected and replaced if needed.",["Charge-air cooler or boost leak (turbo engines, e.g. RAM 3.0 Hurricane)","Faulty injector at cylinder 6","Valve leakage at cylinder 6","ECM software setting (e.g. Audi 3.0 TFSI)"],["Check engine light on","Whistling noise and reduced boost with a charge-air leak","Possible P0306 or rough running"],2,1,["P219A","P219B","P21A0","P21A2","P0306"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 6"],P21A2:["Cylinder 7 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A2 places a mixture imbalance at cylinder 7, so it only exists on engines with eight or more cylinders. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the bulletin index of the US safety authority NHTSA contains no bulletin that names it.",["Cylinder 7 injector clogged or leaking","Intake runner or injector seal leak at cylinder 7","Compression loss at cylinder 7"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable symptom","Possible P0307 if the deviation is large"],2,1,["P219A","P219B","P21A1","P21A3","P0307"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 7"],P21A3:["Cylinder 8 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A3 blames cylinder 8, on a V8 the last cylinder in the numbering. No manufacturer documentation of this code is publicly available, and no bulletin in the NHTSA index refers to it; the basis is the general CARB requirement for detecting cylinder imbalance, phased in for 2011 to 2014 model years with an emission threshold of 3.0 times the FTP standard (4.0 for SULEV II) until 2014 and 1.5 times from 2015.",["Cylinder 8 injector out of tolerance","Valve leakage at cylinder 8","Intake leak at the cylinder 8 runner"],["Check engine light on","Usually no driveability change","Possible P0308 with a strong deviation"],2,1,["P219A","P219B","P21A2","P21A4","P0308"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 8"],P21A4:["Cylinder 9 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A4 is reserved for an imbalance at cylinder 9 and can therefore only appear on engines with ten or more cylinders, a small group of V10 and V12 petrol engines. No manufacturer documents the code publicly and no bulletin in the NHTSA index mentions it.",["Cylinder 9 injector clogged or leaking","Intake leak at cylinder 9","Compression loss at cylinder 9"],["Check engine light on","Possible P0309 with a large deviation"],3,1,["P219A","P219B","P21A3","P21A5","P0309"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 9"],P21A5:["Cylinder 10 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A5 flags cylinder 10, which on a V10 is the final cylinder and on a V12 sits near the end of its bank. Public manufacturer material for this code does not exist, and the NHTSA bulletin index has no entry for it. CARB requires detection of any cylinder imbalance that lifts emissions above one and a half times the FTP limit (from 2015) and that the fault code point as precisely as the method allows;",["Cylinder 10 injector out of tolerance","Fault in another cylinder of the same bank shifting the result","Compression loss at cylinder 10"],["Check engine light on","Possible P0310 or uneven idle"],3,1,["P219A","P219B","P21A4","P21A6","P0310"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 10"],P21A6:["Cylinder 11 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A6 assigns the imbalance to cylinder 11, which exists only on twelve-cylinder engines. No manufacturer has published how it detects this code, and no NHTSA bulletin names it, so it is a placeholder that J2012 provides for large engines. The legal frame is CARB's cylinder imbalance monitor (13 CCR 1968.2 (e)(6.2.1)(C)).",["Cylinder 11 injector clogged or leaking","Valve leakage at cylinder 11","Intake leak at cylinder 11"],["Check engine light on","Possible P0311 with a large deviation"],3,1,["P219A","P219B","P21A5","P21A7","P0311"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 11"],P21A7:["Cylinder 12 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P21A7 is the last code of the cylinder series that starts with P219C and points to cylinder 12 of a twelve-cylinder engine. There is no public manufacturer description and no NHTSA bulletin for it.",["Cylinder 12 injector out of tolerance","Intake seal leak at cylinder 12","Valve not sealing at cylinder 12"],["Check engine light on","Possible P0312 or slight vibration"],3,1,["P219A","P219B","P21A6","P0312"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק צילינדר‏ 12"],P21A8:["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit","P21A8 is the general circuit code for the second reductant level sensor, needed only where a DEF tank reports its fill level through more than one sensing element. GM's 6.6L Duramax (LML/LGH) and the 2014 Cruze diesel read three discrete level sensors, numbered 1 to 3 in GM's tables, which corresponds to A to C.",["Damaged or corroded harness or connector at the DEF tank","Level sensor B in the tank assembly failed","Tank level evaluation electronics faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF system warning message in the cluster","DEF level or range display missing or wrong"],2,3,["P21A9","P21AA","P21AB","P21AC","P203A","P21AD"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P21A9:["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P21A9 flags a level sensor B signal that stays inside its electrical limits but does not fit what else the system knows, such as the states of the other level sensors or the fluid consumed. GM's 2018 Cruze diesel (LH7) stores it in the module running the DEF system, under the name Level Sensor 2 Performance.",["Frozen or very cold fluid giving an implausible reading","Level sensor B fouled by crystallised urea or degraded","Control module calibration flagging the sensor too early"],["Check engine light on","DEF level shown wrongly or jumping","Fault appears mainly after cold nights"],2,3,["P21A8","P21AA","P21AB","P203B","P21AE","P206B"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P21AA:["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit Low","P21AA means the second reductant level sensor reads too low a voltage, which GM takes as a short to ground. GM documents it for the 6.6L Duramax LML and the 2014 Cruze 2.0 diesel: the tank level electronics apply a test pulse, and if sensor 2 then shows less than 0.17 V for more than 3 s with over 8 V supply, the ECM receives an error status over CAN.",["Sensor 2 signal wire chafed through to ground","Fluid or water in the tank connector","Internal short in level sensor B (tank assembly)"],["Check engine light on","DEF warning message that stays on","DEF range or level display wrong"],2,3,["P21A8","P21AB","P203C","P21AF"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21AB:["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit High","P21AB is the high-side counterpart: GM sets it when level sensor 2 shows an open load (between 3.56 and 4.74 V, read 1.5 ms after the test pulse) or a short to battery voltage (above 4.74 V), each for more than 3 s, as Type A on the 6.6L LML and the 2014 Cruze diesel.",["Open signal wire or spread terminal at the tank connector","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source","Level sensor B open inside the tank assembly"],["Check engine light on at once","Service Exhaust Fluid System message","Several level sensor codes stored together"],2,3,["P21A8","P21AA","P203D","P21B0"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21AC:["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P21AC reports that the level sensor B signal drops out or jumps for short moments instead of failing steadily. No manufacturer documents criteria for this code publicly. GM's Duramax and Cruze diesel tables cover sensor 2 only with the steady faults P21AA and P21AB, both requiring an error lasting over 3 s, so an intermittent code points to contact losses shorter than that: a terminal that has lost its grip in the…",["Loose terminal in the tank connector","Harness flexing or rubbing near the tank mounting","Corrosion from fluid creeping into the connector"],["DEF warning that comes and goes","Jumping DEF level display","Check engine light, sometimes only stored code"],2,1,["P21A8","P21AA","P21AB","P203E","P21B1"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P21AD:["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit","P21AD covers the electrical circuit of the third reductant level sensor, so it only exists on tanks with at least three level points. GM's 6.6L Duramax and 2014 Cruze diesel are such cases: the tank electronics test sensors 1 to 3 separately and pass each status to the ECM over CAN. GM uses the specific codes P21AF and P21B0 instead of this summary code.",["Fault in a supply, ground or connector shared by the level sensors","Level sensor C in the tank assembly failed","Sensor C signal wire damaged"],["Check engine light on","DEF range message missing or implausible","Further level sensor codes stored"],2,3,["P21AE","P21AF","P21B0","P21B1","P21A8","P203A"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P21AE:["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P21AE stands for an implausible level sensor C signal whose voltage is still electrically valid. No manufacturer describes a separate check for this code in public material. GM shows how such plausibility testing can work: on the 2014 Cruze diesel the ECM compares the readings of all three discrete level sensors after the test pulse and flags combinations that cannot physically occur together, but files the result…",["Crystallised urea on level sensor C","Partly frozen fluid around the sensor","Level sensor C drifting or degraded"],["Check engine light on","DEF level display does not match the refill amount","Possible DEF warning sequence"],2,3,["P21AD","P21AF","P21B0","P21A9","P203B"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P21AF:["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit Low","P21AF is set when level sensor C, called level sensor 3 by GM, reads below 0.17 V right after the tank electronics apply their test pulse, which GM interprets as a short to ground. Supply must be above 8 V and the error must persist for more than 3 s. The 2014 Cruze diesel stores it as Type B, so the MIL lights after the second failing trip;",["Sensor 3 signal wire shorted to ground","Water or fluid bridging contacts in the tank connector","Level sensor C shorted inside the tank assembly"],["Check engine light after two trips","DEF warning message","Implausible DEF level shown"],2,3,["P21AD","P21B0","P203C","P21AA"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21B0:["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit High","P21B0 means GM's level sensor 3 (sensor C) shows an open circuit or a short to battery: either 3.56 to 4.74 V or more than 4.74 V, measured 1.5 ms after a test pulse, for over 3 s. The 6.6L LML and the 2014 Cruze both rate it Type A, lighting the MIL on the first trip. PIP4887B names P21B0 next to P203D and P21AB on 2010–2011 Duramax trucks showing Service Exhaust Fluid System;",["Tank connector loose, unplugged or with spread terminals","Sensor 3 signal wire open or shorted to voltage","Level sensor C open inside the tank assembly"],["Check engine light on at once","Service Exhaust Fluid System message","P203D and P21AB often stored as well"],2,3,["P21AD","P21AF","P203D","P21AB"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21B1:["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P21B1 marks level sensor C signals that come and go. Public manufacturer criteria do not exist; GM's diesel tables describe sensor 3 only through the steady faults P21AF and P21B0, each filtered over 3 s. A stored P21B1 therefore suggests interruptions too short for those monitors, typical of a connector that works loose under tank vibration, fluid seeping into the terminals, or a harness pinched under a tank strap.",["Tank connector loosening under vibration","Fluid seeping into the terminals","Harness pinched under a tank strap"],["Unsteady DEF level display","DEF warning that appears and clears","Stored code without current fault"],2,1,["P21AD","P21AF","P21B0","P21AC","P203E"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P21B2:["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop NOx Adsorber Control","P21B2 is set when the feedback control of a NOx adsorber (lean NOx trap) has not become active within the time the manufacturer allows once its enable conditions are met. CARB requires this check for vehicles with feedback control of the adsorber or its active injection (13 CCR 1968.2 (f)(8.2.3)(A)(i)).",["Fouled or slow oxygen sensor before or after the adsorber","Exhaust not reaching control temperature (short trips, low load)","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensors","Exhaust temperature sensor reporting too low"],["Check engine light on","Regeneration of the NOx trap delayed or skipped","Higher NOx emissions, possible test failure"],2,1,["P21B3","P2000","P2A00","P2A01"],""],P21B3:["Closed Loop NOx Adsorber Control At Limit - Too High","P21B3 means the NOx adsorber feedback loop has reached its upper adjustment limit and still misses its target, the case CARB describes in 13 CCR 1968.2 (f)(8.2.3)(A)(iii). In practice the controller asks for more enrichment or longer rich phases than the calibration permits, because the downstream oxygen signal never shows the expected change or the bed stays below its target.",["NOx adsorber sulphur-loaded or thermally aged","Downstream oxygen sensor responding too slowly","Air leak in the exhaust ahead of the sensors","Too little fuel delivered for the rich phases"],["Check engine light on","Higher fuel consumption from long rich phases","Often stored together with P2000"],3,1,["P21B2","P2000","P2A01"],""],P21B4:["NOx Adsorber - Over Temperature (Bank 1)","P21B4 reports that the NOx adsorber on bank 1 has run hotter than the manufacturer's protection limit. The risk is greatest during desulphation, when the adsorber is heated on purpose: Eaton patent US7251929 gives about 750 °C as the maximum desulphation temperature, beyond which the adsorber ages thermally, while Cummins aims for roughly 650 °C during regeneration (US7594392).",["Too much fuel during regeneration or desulphation","Leaking or dribbling injector on bank 1","Misfire sending unburnt fuel into the exhaust","Exhaust temperature sensor reading too high"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power while the engine protects the catalyst","Strong smell or heat from the exhaust"],3,3,["P21B5","P2000","P2428","P2080"],""],P21B5:["NOx Adsorber - Over Temperature (Bank 2)","P21B5 is the bank 2 version of the adsorber over-temperature fault and therefore only exists where each cylinder bank feeds its own NOx storage catalyst, which in practice means V engines with two exhaust paths. If only bank 2 overheats, the cause most likely sits on that side: an injector delivering too much, misfire limited to that bank, or a faulty temperature sensor there.",["Injector on bank 2 delivering too much fuel","Misfire confined to bank 2","Regeneration overheating both banks (with P21B4)","Bank 2 exhaust temperature sensor reading too high"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power to protect the catalyst","Uneven exhaust temperatures between the banks"],3,3,["P21B4","P2001","P2429"],""],P21B6:["Cold Start Cylinder 1 Injection Timing","After a cold start, petrol direct-injection and diesel engines deliberately move the moment of injection – for example with an extra late pulse – so that more heat reaches the catalyst. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 (e)(11) wants every element of this strategy checked while it runs and reported apart from warm-engine faults. P21B6 pins such a deviation on cylinder 1. No manufacturer documents this code publicly;",["Injector of cylinder 1 responds late or inconsistently when cold","Corroded or loose connector or harness at injector 1","Injector driver stage in the engine control module faulty","Engine module software with an overly strict cold-start check"],["Check engine light after one or more cold starts","Slightly rough idle in the first minute after a cold start","No noticeable fault once the engine is warm"],3,1,["P21B7","P020A","P2B08","P0201","P0301","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 1"],P21B7:["Cold Start Cylinder 2 Injection Timing","P21B7 flags cylinder 2 during the cold-start phase only: the injection timing commanded for catalyst heating did not arrive as intended on that cylinder. The heating phase is brief and ends as coolant and catalyst warm up, so the monitor gets one chance per cold start and may need several cold starts before the code is confirmed.",["Injector of cylinder 2 worn or coked, opening late at low temperature","Chafed or high-resistance wiring to injector 2","Weak battery lowering injector supply voltage during and after cranking"],["Check engine light that appears only after cold starts","Uneven running or slight smoke shortly after starting a cold engine","Code may take several cold starts to return after clearing"],3,1,["P21B6","P21B8","P020B","P2B09","P0202","P0302","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 2"],P21B8:["Cold Start Cylinder 3 Injection Timing","Cylinder 3 is the last cylinder of three-cylinder engines such as Ford's 1.0-litre EcoBoost, a turbo direct-injection unit. There a single cylinder accounts for a third of all combustion events, so a cold-start fault on it tends to be felt more than on larger engines. P21B8 reports that while the cold-start heating strategy was active, the injection timing of cylinder 3 left its tolerance.",["Injector of cylinder 3 with deposits or a weak coil","Moisture or corrosion in the plug of injector 3","Engine software update available for the cold-start calibration"],["Noticeable shaking at cold idle, especially on three-cylinder engines","Check engine light after cold starts","Normal running once warm"],3,1,["P21B7","P21B9","P020C","P2B0A","P0203","P0303"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 3"],P21B9:["Cold Start Cylinder 4 Injection Timing","Four-cylinder petrol direct injection is the most widespread engine type this code can apply to, and cylinder 4 is its last cylinder. Ford's 2011 OBD summary for its first turbo direct-injection engine explains the background: during catalyst heating the injection timing may be specific to that mode, possibly as two injections with one during the compression stroke, which in turn needs a rail pressure window…",["Deposits on the tip of injector 4 changing its opening behaviour","Harness fault on the injector 4 circuit","Rail pressure barely inside its window during cold start, affecting the last cylinder first"],["Check engine light, usually without drivability complaints","Slightly longer catalyst warm-up and possibly higher cold-start emissions","Occasional hesitation right after a cold start"],3,1,["P21B8","P21BA","P020D","P2B0B","P0204","P0304","P053F"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 4"],P21BA:["Cold Start Cylinder 5 Injection Timing","P21BA can only occur on engines with at least five cylinders – inline fives, V6, V8 and larger. GM's 4.3-litre V6 and 5.3/6.2-litre V8 direct-injection engines use a dual-pulse injection in open loop after a cold start; a GM bulletin explains that the module watches crankshaft speed in this mode and sets P050D (cold start rough idle) if it varies too much.",["Injector of cylinder 5 sticking or delivering late when cold","Repair on the wrong injector because of a misread cylinder numbering","Open or high-resistance circuit to injector 5"],["Check engine light after cold starts","Rough idle during the first seconds after a cold start, possibly together with P050D"],3,1,["P21B9","P21BB","P020E","P2B0C","P0205","P0305","P050D"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 5"],P21BB:["Cold Start Cylinder 6 Injection Timing","Cylinder 6 exists on six-cylinder engines and anything larger – inline sixes and V6 units such as Ford's 3.5-litre EcoBoost petrol or the 3.0-litre EcoDiesel in the Ram 1500. For that diesel FCA listed the warm-engine timing codes P020A–P020F together with the over-advanced and over-retarded codes in a 2021 bulletin whose fix was reprogramming the engine module.",["Injector of cylinder 6 worn, coked or with drifting opening delay","Outdated engine module software (analogous timing codes were cured by reprogramming)","Damaged wiring or connector at injector 6"],["Check engine light after cold starts","On diesels, more white smoke or knocking in the first minutes","Hard start or rough idle when cold"],3,1,["P21BA","P21BC","P020F","P2B0D","P0206","P0306","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 6"],P21BC:["Cold Start Cylinder 7 Injection Timing","From cylinder 7 on, the code is limited to engines with at least seven cylinders – in practice V8, V10, V12 and W12. Common petrol V8 with direct injection are GM's 5.3- and 6.2-litre small blocks, which a GM bulletin describes with dual-pulse injection after a cold start, and Ford's 5.0-litre Coyote, which since 2018 combines port and direct injection.",["Direct injector of cylinder 7 slow to open or leaking at low temperature","Chafed or heat-damaged wiring to injector 7","Fault in the high-voltage injector driver of the engine module"],["Check engine light after cold starts","Rough cold idle, sometimes with P050D or a cylinder 7 misfire code"],3,1,["P21BB","P21BD","P021A","P2B0E","P0207","P0307","P050D"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 7"],P21BD:["Cold Start Cylinder 8 Injection Timing","P21BD covers cylinder 8, the last cylinder of a V8. GM's 2025 diesel tables show how close an existing monitor comes to this code: during cold start the module compares requested and scheduled start of injection, with every cylinder from A to H included in the enable checks, and a deviation beyond ±4 in 88 of 176 samples sets the lamp in the first trip.",["Injector of cylinder 8 with slow or varying response","Connector or wiring fault at injector 8","Cold-start calibration in the engine module needing an update"],["Check engine light after cold starts","Rough running or smoke in the first minute after a cold start","No symptoms at operating temperature"],3,1,["P21BC","P21BE","P021B","P2B0F","P0208","P0308","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 8"],P21BE:["Cold Start Cylinder 9 Injection Timing","A ninth cylinder exists only on V10, V12 and W12 engines, so P21BE is limited to a handful of models. Petrol engines in this class with direct injection include the 5.2-litre V10 of Lamborghini and Audi (Huracán, R8, S6 and S8) and the 6.3-litre W12 FSI of the Audi A8, which feeds its injectors from two high-pressure pumps and two rails.",["Direct injector of cylinder 9 with deposits or slow response","Wiring or connector fault at injector 9","Low pressure on the rail feeding cylinder 9 (engines with two rails)"],["Check engine light after cold starts","Slightly uneven idle while the engine is cold"],4,1,["P21BD","P21BF","P021C","P0209","P0309","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 9"],P21BF:["Cold Start Cylinder 10 Injection Timing","Cylinder 10 is the last cylinder of a V10 and exists otherwise only on twelve-cylinder engines. V10 engines are rare: Ford's 6.8-litre truck V10 (firing order 1-6-5-10-2-7-3-8-4-9, in the E-Series until 2019) and the 5.2-litre direct-injection V10 of Lamborghini and Audi. P21BF states that cylinder 10, during the cold-start heating phase, received its fuel at a different moment than targeted.",["Injector of cylinder 10 aged or contaminated","Wiring or connector problem at injector 10","Engine module software needing a cold-start calibration update"],["Check engine light after one or more cold starts","Uneven idle until the engine warms up"],4,1,["P21BE","P21C0","P021D","P0210","P0310","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 10"],P21C0:["Cold Start Cylinder 11 Injection Timing","P21C0 applies only to twelve-cylinder engines (V12 or W12), since passenger-car engines with exactly eleven cylinders do not exist. Examples with direct injection are BMW's N74 twin-turbo V12, found in the BMW 760i and in Rolls-Royce models such as Ghost, Wraith and Dawn, and the 6.3-litre W12 FSI.",["Direct injector of cylinder 11 with changed opening behaviour","Heat-damaged wiring or connector at injector 11","Injector driver for cylinder 11 in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine light after cold starts","Barely noticeable on the road; a twelve-cylinder engine masks a single cylinder well"],4,1,["P21BF","P21C1","P021E","P0211","P0311","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 11"],P21C1:["Cold Start Cylinder 12 Injection Timing","Cylinder 12 is the last cylinder of V12 and W12 engines. Direct-injection V12 include Ferrari's F140 family (FF, F12berlinetta, 812 Superfast) and BMW's N74; among W engines there is the 6.3-litre W12 FSI. P21C1 reports that during the cold-start heating phase the injection timing of cylinder 12 deviated from its target.",["Injector of cylinder 12 with deposits or worn needle","Damaged wiring at the end of the cylinder bank (injector 12)","Cold-start calibration of the engine module out of date"],["Check engine light after cold starts","Hardly any drivability change, at most a slightly uneven cold idle"],4,1,["P21C0","P021F","P0212","P0312","P05EC"],"תזמון הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 12"],P21C2:["Reductant Heater Relay Control Circuit/Open","P21C2 concerns the control line of the relay that supplies current to the DEF heaters. The control module drives the relay coil through an output stage and checks whether the circuit reacts; an open circuit means the coil, its wiring or a connector has lost continuity, so the heaters cannot be energised.",["Relay coil burnt open or relay not seated in its socket","Broken control wire between module and relay","Corroded or loose terminals at relay box or module connector","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["Check engine light on","DEF system warning, especially at low ambient temperature","Frozen DEF thaws slowly, dosing begins late after a cold start"],2,3,["P21C3","P21C4","P21C7","P20B9","P21DD"],"ממסר גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P21C3:["Reductant Heater Relay Control Circuit Low","P21C3 is the low-side fault on the control line of the DEF heater relay: the signal is pulled toward ground, for example by a chafed wire touching the frame or a shorted relay coil, so the relay no longer follows the command.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Relay coil with internal short or welded contacts","Water or salt in the relay or heater connector","Output stage of the controlling module faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF heating inactive or running when not commanded","Blown fuse in the heater supply"],2,3,["P21C2","P21C4","P21C7","P20BB"],"ממסר גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P21C4:["Reductant Heater Relay Control Circuit High","P21C4 means the control side of the DEF heater relay shows voltage when it should be dead. Ford's 2023 diesel summary sets it when the relay stage and all heaters are off and the heater circuit still carries more than 5 V, within at most 5 s; a short to the battery feed or contacts that no longer open are the classic reasons.",["Replacement dosing control unit not programmed or with outdated software (FCA)","Control or heater wire shorted to battery voltage","Relay contacts welded closed","Internal fault in the controlling module"],["Check engine light on","Code appears shortly after a DEF control unit was replaced","Additional communication code such as U11C1 stored"],2,3,["P21C2","P21C3","P21C7","P20BC"],"ממסר גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P21C5:["Reductant Level Sensor A Stuck","P21C5 is a plausibility code: the level sensor A reports valid readings, yet they hardly move when the fluid in the tank should be sloshing. GM spells this out for the ultrasonic sensor in its 2025 diesel tables, where it is sensor 1. While the vehicle is above 5 km/h, accelerating by more than 0.1 m/s², the fluid is liquid and over 5 L remain, a level change below 0.3 mm within one second counts as a failed sample;",["Level sensor calibration in the engine software (update available, e.g. Jaguar)","Ultrasonic level sensor in the tank unit faulty","Crystal deposits or gas bubbles disturbing the echo","Fluid partly frozen or slush around the sensor"],["Check engine light on after two drives","DEF gauge stays at the same value while fluid is being used","DEF warning messages in the instrument cluster"],2,3,["P21C6","P203A","P203B","P21A9"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — תקוע"],P21C6:["Reductant Level Sensor B Stuck","P21C6 applies only to DEF tanks with a second level measurement, labelled B. It is stored when that second reading is electrically fine but stays frozen at one value although the module expects it to change. No manufacturer documents P21C6 publicly.",["Second level sensing element in the tank unit faulty","Float or contact held by crystals or debris","Calibration of the level evaluation needs a software update"],["Check engine light on","DEF gauge implausible or not moving","DEF warning in the instrument cluster"],2,3,["P21C5","P21A8","P21A9","P21AA"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקוע"],P21C7:["Reductant Control Module Power Relay/Relays Control Circuit/Open","P21C7 flags a break in the control line of the power relay, or group of relays, that supplies the DEF control module and the loads behind it. Ford's 2023 diesel summary evaluates it inside the same continuous heater relay check as P21C2 to P21C4, so on that design the relay also feeds the heating circuits.",["Relay defective or missing from its socket","Open control wire or loose terminal between module and relay","Blown fuse in the relay or module feed","Driver in the controlling module faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF heating and dosing do not work","SCR warning and countdown to restricted starting or speed"],2,3,["P21C8","P21C9","P20EA","P20EB","P21C2","P0685"],""],P21C8:["Reductant Control Module Power Relay/Relays Control Circuit Low","P21C8 means the control line of the DEF module's power relay, or relays, sits too close to ground. No manufacturer documents P21C8 publicly. Ford's 2023 diesel summary only shows the open-circuit sibling P21C7, judged by comparing the commanded relay state with the voltage on the switched side; a low-side code follows the same idea with a pin voltage below the expected window.",["Control wire chafed and shorted to ground","Shorted relay coil","Moisture in relay socket or module connector","Output stage in the controlling module faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF system without power or permanently powered","Flat battery after the vehicle has been parked"],2,3,["P21C7","P21C9","P20EB","P0686"],""],P21C9:["Reductant Control Module Power Relay/Relays Control Circuit High","P21C9 is stored when the control line of the DEF module's power relay, or relays, carries more voltage than the driver state allows, typically because the wire touches a battery feed or the driver can no longer pull it down. No manufacturer documents P21C9 publicly. The closest published logic is Ford's 2023 diesel summary for P21C7, which flags voltage on the switched side while the output stage is off;",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","Relay contacts welded, switched side stays live","Driver in the controlling module shorted"],["Check engine light on","DEF pump or module audible or active with the engine off","Battery drained overnight"],2,3,["P21C7","P21C8","P20EB","P0687"],""],P21CA:["Reductant Control Module Supply Voltage Circuit","P21CA is the general code for the supply feed of the DEF control module: the voltage arriving at the module is missing or unusable, without the module assigning it to the low or high case. Volvo and Mack trucks use it, as P21CA00, on the aftertreatment control module that runs the SCR system.",["Loose or corroded battery or ground connections of the module","Weak batteries or insufficient charging voltage","Faulty in-line fuse or damaged supply wire","Control module itself faulty"],["Check engine light on","Several sensor communication codes at the same time","SCR inducement with power reduction"],2,3,["P21CB","P21CC","P056D","P0562","U02A2"],"מודול בקרת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P21CB:["Reductant Control Module Supply Voltage Low","P21CB says the DEF control module receives too little supply voltage. GM measures it as a difference to system voltage: in the 2018 diesel tables a gap above 3 V between battery voltage and the supply of the SCR power module, seen in 40 of 50 samples taken every 100 ms with the powertrain relay in range and cranking excluded, sets the code;",["Voltage drop at fuse, terminal or ground of the module feed","Weak battery or low charging voltage","Damaged or corroded supply wire to the module","Internal voltage measurement of the module faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF dosing or heating drops out intermittently","Further undervoltage or communication codes from the SCR system"],2,3,["P21CA","P21CC","P056D","P0562","P20FF"],"אספקת מודול בקרת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מתח נמוך"],P21CC:["Reductant Control Module Supply Voltage High","P21CC is the overvoltage counterpart of P21CB: the DEF control module sees a supply above what its electronics are designed for. Ford's 2023 diesel summary checks the reductant pump controller in a continuous loop and sets P21CC once its supply exceeds 19 V, deciding within 5 s.",["Alternator voltage regulator overcharging","Jump start or charging with excessive voltage","Loose battery terminal causing voltage spikes","Module's own voltage measurement faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF dosing paused, SCR warning","Battery or charging warning, bulbs unusually bright"],2,3,["P21CA","P21CB","P056D","P0563"],"אספקת מודול בקרת אוריאה (AdBlue) — מתח גבוה"],P21CD:["Reductant Quality Module Supply Voltage Low","The DEF quality module measures the urea concentration in the tank and, on many tanks, shares a housing with the level sensor. P21CD reports that its supply voltage is too low. Ford's 2023 diesel summary sets the code when the quality sensor supply falls below 10 V or rises above 20 V for 15 s, so on Ford the overvoltage case shares this code.",["Water and corrosion in the quality module connector (Ford C4851)","Damaged tank harness or supply wire","Low battery or charging voltage","Quality module internally faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF quality or level warning in the instrument cluster","Communication code for the quality module stored as well"],2,3,["P21CE","U02A2","P206B","P21CB"],"אספקת מודול איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — מתח נמוך"],P21CE:["Reductant Quality Module Performance","P21CE says the DEF quality module as a unit is not working properly: it is supplied and talking to the controller, but its self-test or the plausibility of its output fails, so the controller cannot rely on the concentration it reports. This differs from P206B to P206D, which grade the measured concentration, and from P21CD, which concerns the module supply.",["Contaminated or degraded DEF disturbing the measurement","Quality module internally faulty","Crystals or air bubbles on the sensing element","Poor contact at the module connector"],["Check engine light on","DEF system error message in the display","Erratic DEF level reading"],2,3,["P21CD","P206B","P206C","P206D","U02A2"],"מודול איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P21CF:["Cylinder 1 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21CF flags an open drive circuit of the second injector on cylinder 1. Which of the two injectors is B depends on the maker: Ford gives the letter to the port injector and keeps A, coded P0201, for direct injection, whereas Mitsubishi calls its direct injectors B and files open circuits under the low code P21DB. Ford's 2020 to 2025 gasoline summaries test the B circuits continuously above 11 V and need 5 s.",["Chafed or broken wire in the port injector harness (on the Bronco Sport near the transmission cover)","Open coil in the cylinder 1 port injector","Loose or corroded plug at the injector","Faulty driver stage in the engine module or separate injector module"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle or misfire on cylinder 1, often with P0301","Further harness codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P0201","P21DB","P21DC","P21D0","P21D1","P0301"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 1 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D0:["Cylinder 2 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D0 is the open-circuit code for the B injector of cylinder 2. Where that cylinder sits varies: GM's small-block V8 alternates odd and even numbers between the banks, so cylinder 2 opens the right bank, while Ford's V6 and V8 count one bank first and place it next to cylinder 1. Ford defines B as the port injector, the direct injector being A with P0202.",["Port injector of cylinder 2 with an open winding","Broken wire or pushed-back terminal in the injector harness","Output stage in the engine or injection module failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 2, mainly at idle and light load","Code P0302 stored as well"],2,1,["P0202","P21DE","P21DF","P21CF","P21D1","P0302"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 2 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D1:["Cylinder 3 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D1 concerns the B injector of cylinder 3, which on Ford's 1.5 EcoBoost three-cylinder is the last one in the block. That engine combines port and direct fuel, and Ford names the port injectors B.",["Harness damage affecting several injectors at once (Ford Bronco Sport, transmission cover)","Open coil in the cylinder 3 port injector","Connector not latched or corroded"],["Check engine light on","Rough running or misfire on cylinder 3","With harness damage also transmission codes or no crank"],2,1,["P0203","P21E0","P21E1","P21CF","P21D0","P0303"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 3 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D2:["Cylinder 4 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D2 reports an open in the drive circuit of the B injector on cylinder 4. On four-cylinder engines with dual injection it is the last of the set, for example Ford's 2.0 EcoBoost from 2022 or the 2.3 introduced for the 2024 Mustang, both of which added port injectors to direct injection.",["Open winding in the cylinder 4 port injector","Wire broken at a bend or clip near the intake manifold","Corroded or loose injector connector"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 4 (P0304)","Uneven idle"],2,1,["P0204","P21E2","P21E3","P21D1","P21D3","P0304"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 4 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D3:["Cylinder 5 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D3 can only appear on engines with at least five cylinders and two injectors per cylinder. Documented users are Ford's dual-injection V6 and V8 engines (2.7 and 3.5 EcoBoost of the second generation, 5.0 V8 from 2018) and GM's supercharged LT5 V8. Ford defines B as the port injector; the direct injector of this cylinder is A, coded P0205. GM stores it as Type A once 20 of 25 samples fail.",["Open coil in the cylinder 5 port injector","Broken wire in the bank harness of the port injectors","Output stage in the engine or injection module failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 5 (P0305)","Fuel trim of one bank shifted"],2,1,["P0205","P21E4","P21E5","P21D2","P21D4","P0305"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 5 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D4:["Cylinder 6 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D4 is the last B injector code on a six-cylinder engine. Ford's second-generation 2.7 and 3.5 EcoBoost V6 combine port and direct injection, label the port injectors B and test this circuit together with P21CF to P21D3, continuously above 11 V within 5 s; on these engines cylinder 6 is the rear cylinder of the second bank.",["Port injector of cylinder 6 open internally","Damaged wire at the rear of the engine, hard to inspect","Connector not fully latched after earlier work on the intake"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 6 (P0306)","Slightly rough idle"],2,1,["P0206","P21E6","P21E7","P21D3","P21D5","P0306"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 6 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D5:["Cylinder 7 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D5 belongs to V8 engines with a second injector per cylinder. Two are documented: Ford's 5.0 V8, which gained direct injection alongside its port injectors in 2018, and GM's 2019 LT5, the supercharged Corvette ZR1 engine with primary direct and supplemental port injection. Ford's summary lists P21CF to P21D6 as port injector circuits, continuous above 11 V, 5 s.",["Open winding in the cylinder 7 port injector","Broken wire or terminal in the port injector harness of that bank","Separate fuel injection control module faulty (GM LT5)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 7, on the LT5 mostly under high load","Reduced power at full throttle"],2,1,["P0207","P21E8","P21E9","P21D4","P21D6","P0307"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 7 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D6:["Cylinder 8 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D6 is the highest B injector code that any manufacturer documents publicly: both Ford's port injector check (P21CF to P21D6) and GM's LT5 injection module list end here. On the LT5 the port injectors exist to add fuel under boost beyond what the direct system and its mechanical pump can deliver, so an open cylinder 8 injector shows up mainly at high load, where that cylinder can run lean and lose power;",["Port injector of cylinder 8 open","Wire damage at the rear of the engine near the firewall","Output of the engine or separate injection module failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfire or lean running on cylinder 8 under load","Power loss at wide-open throttle"],2,1,["P0208","P21EA","P21EB","P21D5","P21D7","P0308"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 8 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D7:["Cylinder 9 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D7 would mark an open drive circuit of the second injector on cylinder 9, which presupposes at least nine cylinders. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the published Ford and GM lists stop at cylinder 8 (P21D6).",["Open coil in the second injector of cylinder 9","Broken wire or terminal in the injector harness","Driver stage in the engine control module failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 9 (P0309)"],3,1,["P0209","P21EC","P21ED","P21D6","P21D8","P0309"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 9 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D8:["Cylinder 10 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D8 covers the second injector of cylinder 10, the last cylinder of a V10. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. A V10 with two injectors per cylinder is on record in the Lamborghini Huracán, whose engine combines direct and multipoint injection, yet which of them its software would call B is unknown.",["Second injector of cylinder 10 open internally","Wiring or connector fault at the cylinder 10 injector","Output stage in the engine control module failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 10 (P0310)"],3,1,["P020A","P21EE","P21EF","P21D7","P21D9","P0310"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 10 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21D9:["Cylinder 11 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21D9 is reserved for an open circuit of the second injector on cylinder 11 and therefore only makes sense on twelve-cylinder engines with dual injection. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and no available source names a twelve-cylinder engine that uses it. Its meaning follows from the series: like P21CF to P21D6, it is an electrical check of the injector drive, not of fuel quantity.",["Open coil in the second injector of cylinder 11","Damaged injector harness or loose plug","Faulty driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 11 (P0311)"],3,1,["P020B","P21F0","P21F1","P21D8","P21DA","P0311"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 11 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21DA:["Cylinder 12 Injector B Circuit/Open","P21DA closes the circuit/open series of the second injectors with cylinder 12. It requires a twelve-cylinder engine with two injectors per cylinder; no manufacturer documents this code publicly and no available source names such an engine using it. The fault type is the same as for its documented siblings: the control unit switches the injector and sees no current or an impedance far above normal.",["Second injector of cylinder 12 with open coil","Wire or terminal fault in the injector harness","Output stage of the controlling module failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 12 (P0312)"],3,1,["P020C","P21F2","P21F3","P21D9","P21DB","P0312"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 12 B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P21DB:["Cylinder 1 Injector B Circuit Low","P21DB means the drive circuit of the B injector on cylinder 1 is pulled toward ground. Two makers document it, with opposite meanings of B. Mitsubishi's 2022 Eclipse Cross uses B for the direct high-pressure injector (its port injector faults are P0261 ff.) and sets P21DB when an interruption or a grounded line persists for 2 s with 10 to 16.5 V battery and over 10 V on the injector driver supply.",["Injector wire chafed through to ground","Injector winding open or shorted to its housing","Damaged intermediate or injector connector","Engine or injection control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 1 misfire or shut-off","Reduced torque when several cylinders are affected (Mitsubishi)"],3,3,["P21DC","P21CF","P0261","P0262","P21DE","P0301"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 1 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21DC:["Cylinder 1 Injector B Circuit High","P21DC is the high-side fault of the cylinder 1 B injector: the line carries voltage where the control unit expects it to be low, typically from a short to supply or between the two injector wires. On GM's 2019 LT5 V8 the FICM injection module looks at the low side of the supplemental injector while its driver is off;",["Injector control wire shorted to a supply wire","Both injector wires shorted together in the harness","Injector coil shorted internally","Driver stage of the control module damaged"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 1 runs weak or misfires","Torque limited if more cylinders fail (Mitsubishi)"],3,3,["P21DB","P21CF","P0262","P21DF","P0301"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 1 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21DD:["Reductant Heater A Current Too Low","P21DD means heater A of the DEF system, which Ford and GM both assign to the tank heater (circuit 1), draws less current than expected while switched on, so it is likely open or barely heating. GM's 2025 diesel tables set it when heater 1 current stays below 0.75 A for 40 samples of 0.1 s during a positive command, Type A with MIL after one trip;",["Tank heater element burnt open","Water and corrosion in the pump and heater connector (Ford C3613)","Missing heater supply due to relay, fuse or wiring fault","Heater driver in the control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","DEF stays frozen longer in winter, dosing starts late","DEF warning messages after cold starts"],2,3,["P214F","P221C","P20B9","P20BB","P20BC","P21C2"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — ערך נמוך מדי"],P21DE:["Cylinder 2 Injector B Circuit Low","P21DE is the low fault of the cylinder 2 B injector circuit. In Mitsubishi's 2022 Eclipse Cross manual, B means the direct injector; the code covers both a break and a grounded wire on the two DI lines of cylinder 2, held for 2 s at 10 to 16.5 V, while the port injector of the same cylinder reports P0264.",["Injector line of cylinder 2 touching ground","Injector coil resistance outside specification","Fault at the intermediate connector of the injector harness"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 2 (P0302)","Possible fuel smell or rich running if an injector stays open"],3,3,["P21DF","P21D0","P0264","P21DB","P21E0","P0302"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 2 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21DF:["Cylinder 2 Injector B Circuit High","P21DF is set when the cylinder 2 B injector circuit shows a short toward supply. Mitsubishi's 2022 Eclipse Cross applies it to the direct high-pressure injector and stores it after a 2 s short with the ignition on and the driver supply above 10 V; troubleshooting first inspects the negative DI wire of cylinder 2 up to the engine module and names the injector, the harness and the ECM as possible causes.",["Negative injector line of cylinder 2 shorted to supply","Injector coil shorted","ECM or injection module driver defective"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 2 switched off or misfiring","Less pulling power with multiple faults"],3,3,["P21DE","P21D0","P0265","P21DC","P21E1","P0302"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 2 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21E0:["Cylinder 3 Injector B Circuit Low","P21E0 reports a low circuit state on the B injector of cylinder 3. Mitsubishi lists it for the 2022 Eclipse Cross as the direct injector code and does not use the open code P21D1, so an interrupted wire and a short to ground both end up here once they last 2 s.",["Cylinder 3 injector wire broken or shorted to ground","Injector of cylinder 3 with open or shorted coil","Engine control module output faulty"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 3 (P0303)","Rough idle"],3,3,["P21E1","P21D1","P0267","P21DE","P21E2","P0303"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 3 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21E1:["Cylinder 3 Injector B Circuit High","P21E1 is the high fault on the cylinder 3 B injector circuit. In Mitsubishi's 2022 Eclipse Cross that is the direct high-pressure injector, and the module reacts to a short circuit lasting 2 s, checked with 10 to 16.5 V battery voltage. To confirm a repair, the manual points to its OBD drive cycle pattern 1.",["Cylinder 3 injector line shorted to supply voltage","Shorted injector coil","Damaged driver in the control module"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 3 not firing properly","Torque reduction if several injectors fail (Mitsubishi)"],3,3,["P21E0","P21D1","P0268","P21DF","P21E3","P0303"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 3 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21E2:["Cylinder 4 Injector B Circuit Low","P21E2 is the low fault of the B injector on cylinder 4, the last cylinder of an inline four. It is the final direct injector low code in Mitsubishi's 2022 Eclipse Cross list, which uses B for the high-pressure injectors and sets it for an open or a short to ground lasting 2 s.",["Cylinder 4 injector wire open or shorted to ground","Intermediate connector fault affecting several cylinders","Cylinder 4 injector coil defective"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 4 (P0304)","Noticeably less power with several codes (port injection only)"],3,3,["P21E3","P21D2","P0270","P21E0","P21E4","P0304"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 4 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21E3:["Cylinder 4 Injector B Circuit High","P21E3 marks a high circuit state on the cylinder 4 B injector, normally a short to a supply line. On Mitsubishi's 2022 Eclipse Cross, where B is the direct high-pressure injector, the fault must persist 2 s; it closes the manual's list of direct injector circuit codes for the four cylinders.",["Cylinder 4 injector line shorted to a supply wire","Injector of cylinder 4 shorted internally","Driver stage in the ECM or injection module damaged"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 4 (P0304)","Engine runs with reduced torque if further cylinders are affected"],3,3,["P21E2","P21D2","P0271","P21E1","P21E5","P0304"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 4 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21E4:["Cylinder 5 Injector B Circuit Low","P21E4 flags a low state on the circuit of the second (B) injector serving cylinder 5. The only public OBD summary that lists it is GM's for the 2019 Corvette ZR1, whose supercharged LT5 V8 pairs direct injectors with port injectors and drives the supplemental ones from a separate fuel injection control module (FICM).",["Low-side wire of the cylinder 5 B injector touching ground","Injector winding shorted to its housing","Moisture or corrosion in the injector connector","Driver stage in the injection control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Rich running or fuel trim pulled back on bank 1","Rough idle or misfire on cylinder 5"],3,1,["P21E5","P21D3","P0273","P21E2","P21E6","P0172","P0305"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 5 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21E5:["Cylinder 5 Injector B Circuit High","P21E5 means the cylinder 5 B injector circuit is pulled toward supply voltage. GM documents it for the LT5 V8 of the 2019 Corvette ZR1: the FICM looks at the low side of that injector while its driver is off and treats 0.5 Ohm or less toward power as a short. The test needs a running engine and at least 11 V at the powertrain relay, runs continuously and sets a Type A fault.",["Low-side wire of the cylinder 5 B injector shorted to a supply wire","Supply and control wire of the injector bridged in the harness","Injector coil shorted across its terminals","Damaged output stage in the injection control module"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 5 lean or hesitant at full load","Part-load driving often feels normal"],3,1,["P21E4","P21D3","P0274","P21E3","P21E7","P0171","P0305"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 5 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21E6:["Cylinder 6 Injector B Circuit Low","P21E6 reports that the B injector circuit of cylinder 6 has found a path to ground. In GM's 2019 tables for the Corvette ZR1 LT5, cylinder 6 is the third position on the right bank, which GM counts as bank 2. The FICM samples the switched-off low side every 100 ms and needs 20 bad readings out of 25, so a solid fault is confirmed within about two and a half seconds;",["Cylinder 6 B injector harness chafed against engine metal","Internal short to ground inside the injector","Injection control module output stuck low"],["Check engine light on","Rich condition on bank 2, possibly fuel smell","Fouled spark plug or misfire on cylinder 6"],3,1,["P21E7","P21D4","P0276","P21E4","P21E8","P0175","P0306"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 6 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21E7:["Cylinder 6 Injector B Circuit High","P21E7 is stored when the B injector of cylinder 6 shows a short toward power. GM's 2019 Corvette ZR1 with the LT5 V8 is the documented user; there the FICM checks the low side only in the driver-off state, flags 0.5 Ohm or less to power, and needs at least 11 V at the powertrain relay with the engine running. The result is a Type A fault after one trip.",["Cylinder 6 B injector control wire in contact with a live wire","Shorted turns in the injector coil","Output stage of the injection control module damaged by the short"],["Check engine light on","Lean condition on bank 2 under load","Cylinder 6 misfire at high load"],3,1,["P21E6","P21D4","P0277","P21E5","P21E9","P0174","P0306"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 6 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21E8:["Cylinder 7 Injector B Circuit Low","P21E8 covers a low, ground-side fault on the cylinder 7 B injector. GM lists it for the 2019 Corvette ZR1, where the LT5 V8 carries a direct and a supplemental injector per cylinder and cylinder 7 is the rearmost cylinder of the left bank (bank 1).",["Cylinder 7 B injector wire grounded at the rear of the engine","Injector coil leaking to ground","FICM output faulty"],["Check engine light on","Rich mixture reported for bank 1","Misfire on cylinder 7"],3,1,["P21E9","P21D5","P0279","P21E6","P21EA","P0172","P0307"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 7 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21E9:["Cylinder 7 Injector B Circuit High","P21E9 indicates that the low side of the cylinder 7 B injector carries supply voltage. On GM's 2019 Corvette ZR1 LT5, the FICM declares this when it sees 0.5 Ohm or less to power with the driver off, provided the engine runs and the powertrain relay delivers 11 V or more; Type A, one trip. The rear left cylinder then gets only its direct injector.",["Cylinder 7 B injector control wire shorted to battery voltage","Injector coil with too low resistance","Injection control module driver defective"],["Check engine light on","Bank 1 lean at full throttle","Less power at full throttle"],3,1,["P21E8","P21D5","P0280","P21E7","P21EB","P0171","P0307"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 7 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21EA:["Cylinder 8 Injector B Circuit Low","P21EA is the ground-short code for the B injector of cylinder 8 and the last low code in GM's 2019 FICM table for the Corvette ZR1 LT5, because the V8 ends there. Cylinder 8 is the rearmost of the right bank (bank 2). The module flags 0.5 Ohm or less between the switched-off low side and ground in 20 of 25 samples of 100 ms, with the engine running and 11 V or more at the powertrain relay, as a Type A fault.",["Cylinder 8 B injector wiring chafed through to ground","Water or corrosion in the cylinder 8 injector plug","Injector shorted to its body","FICM driver stuck on"],["Check engine light on","Rich running on bank 2","Hard hot start or misfire on cylinder 8"],3,1,["P21EB","P21D6","P0282","P21E8","P21EC","P0175","P0308"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 8 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21EB:["Cylinder 8 Injector B Circuit High","P21EB is set when the cylinder 8 B injector circuit is shorted toward power. It closes GM's run of B-injector codes for the 2019 Corvette ZR1 LT5: the FICM sees the switched-off low side within 0.5 Ohm of supply in 20 of 25 samples and stores a Type A fault, lighting the MIL in the first trip.",["Cylinder 8 B injector control wire shorted to a feed wire","Shared harness connector shorted when several injectors are affected","Injector coil shorted","Injection control module damaged"],["Check engine light on","Lean bank 2 under boost","Normal behaviour at part load"],3,1,["P21EA","P21D6","P0283","P21E9","P21ED","P0174","P0308"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 8 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21EC:["Cylinder 9 Injector B Circuit Low","P21EC signals a low circuit state, usually a grounded wire or, depending on the maker, also a break, on the B injector of cylinder 9. It can only occur on an engine with at least nine cylinders and two injectors per cylinder. No manufacturer documents it publicly; GM's and Ford's lists stop at cylinder 8. The one such engine on record is Lamborghini's Huracán V10, which combines direct and multi-point injection;",["Cylinder 9 B injector wire shorted to ground","Broken wire, if the maker reports opens under the low code","Injector coil shorted to housing or open","Engine control module output faulty"],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough running on cylinder 9","Mixture deviation on the bank of cylinder 9"],3,1,["P21ED","P21D7","P0285","P21EA","P21EE","P0309"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 9 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21ED:["Cylinder 9 Injector B Circuit High","P21ED is defined for a B injector circuit on cylinder 9 that reads high, meaning the control side is shorted to supply or, on some designs, the two injector wires touch. No manufacturer publishes thresholds or vehicles for it. Only engines with ten or more cylinders and dual injection could set it;",["Control wire of the cylinder 9 B injector shorted to power","Both injector wires bridged in the harness","Injector coil shorted internally","Driver stage in the control unit faulty"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 9 lean in mixed injection operation","Misfire on cylinder 9 (P0309)"],3,1,["P21EC","P21D7","P0286","P21EB","P21EF","P0309"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 9 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21EE:["Cylinder 10 Injector B Circuit Low","P21EE is the low-circuit code for the B injector of cylinder 10, the last cylinder of a V10. In practice that points to a ten-cylinder engine with two injectors per cylinder, of which only Lamborghini's Huracán is documented: its V10 pairs a direct injector with a port injector at each cylinder and was presented as the first V10 to combine both.",["Cylinder 10 B injector wire grounded","Damaged or corroded injector connector on cylinder 10","Injector with internal ground fault","Engine control unit output defective"],["Check engine light on","Rough running or misfire on cylinder 10 (P0310)","Fuel trim deviation on the second bank"],3,1,["P21EF","P21D8","P0288","P21EC","P21F0","P0310"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 10 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21EF:["Cylinder 10 Injector B Circuit High","P21EF stands for a high reading on the B injector circuit of cylinder 10. No public manufacturer document covers it, so the exact threshold is unknown; the closest documented model is GM's LT5 V8, where a switched-off low side within 0.5 Ohm of supply counts as a short and sets a Type A fault.",["Cylinder 10 B injector control wire touching a live circuit","Short inside a connector shared by several injectors","Injector coil shorted","Output stage overloaded by the short"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 10 weak or misfiring under load","Lean mixture on the second bank"],3,1,["P21EE","P21D8","P0289","P21ED","P21F1","P0310"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 10 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21F0:["Cylinder 11 Injector B Circuit Low","P21F0 is reserved for a low state, typically a wire touching ground, in the B injector circuit of cylinder 11. Setting it requires at least eleven cylinders with two injectors each, so in practice a V12 or W12 with combined port and direct injection. No such engine could be confirmed: Lamborghini's V12 family uses multi-point injection only, as do Aston Martin's V12 and Mercedes-AMG's M279.",["Cylinder 11 B injector wire shorted to ground","Injector with internal short to ground","Code read on an engine without a cylinder 11 B injector (scan tool or maker-specific use)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 11 (P0311)"],3,1,["P21F1","P21D9","P0291","P21EE","P21F2","P0311"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 11 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21F1:["Cylinder 11 Injector B Circuit High","P21F1 describes a cylinder 11 B injector circuit that sits too high, i.e. its switched side is shorted to supply. The code exists in SAE J2012 for completeness of the cylinder series, but no public manufacturer source uses it, and no twelve-cylinder engine with two injectors per cylinder could be documented.",["Control wire of the cylinder 11 B injector shorted to power","Injector coil shorted","Control module driver damaged"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 11 lean or misfiring (P0311)"],3,1,["P21F0","P21D9","P0292","P21EF","P21F3","P0311"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 11 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21F2:["Cylinder 12 Injector B Circuit Low","P21F2 is the generic code for a low circuit state, usually a grounded control wire, at the B injector of cylinder 12. It would need a twelve-cylinder engine with two injectors per cylinder, and none could be documented: the V12s from Lamborghini and Aston Martin inject into the ports only. No manufacturer publishes the code in this sense.",["Cylinder 12 B injector wire shorted to ground","Injector with internal ground fault","Manufacturer-specific use of the number (McLaren Artura high-voltage battery)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 12 (P0312)","Hybrid warning instead, if the code is a McLaren battery fault"],3,1,["P21F3","P21DA","P0294","P21F0","P0312"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 12 B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P21F3:["Cylinder 12 Injector B Circuit High","P21F3 ends the B injector series of SAE J2012: a high signal on the cylinder 12 circuit, caused by a short to supply on the switched side. The series runs from P21CF to P21DA for opens and from P21DB to P21F3 for low/high pairs; the A injector equivalent here is P0295.",["Control wire of the cylinder 12 B injector shorted to supply","Injector coil with shorted windings","Driver stage damaged by a lasting short"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 12 lean or misfiring (P0312)"],3,1,["P21F2","P21DA","P0295","P21F1","P0312"],"מזרק צילינדר‏ 12 B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P21F4:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean Off Idle (Bank 1)","P21F4 reports that the second fuel path on bank 1 needs more added fuel than its adaptation may supply once the engine has left idle, in the part-load range. Engines with port and direct injection learn a correction for each path; Ford calls its direct system A and its port system B.",["Outdated engine control software (Audi 2.5 TFSI, bulletin 2059429/1)","Port injectors of bank 1 restricted or delivering too little","Pressure in the low-pressure (port) fuel rail too low","Air mass sensor reading too low"],["Check engine lamp on","Weak performance or hesitation at part load","Often stored together with P2177 or P0087"],2,1,["P21F5","P21F6","P21F8","P21FC","P2177","P2BF0"],""],P21F5:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich Off Idle (Bank 1)","P21F5 is the rich limit for the second fuel path of bank 1 in the part-load zone above idle: the learned correction already removes as much fuel as allowed, yet the front sensor still sees surplus fuel.",["Outdated engine control software (Audi 2.5 TFSI, bulletin 2059429/1)","Port injector on bank 1 leaking or sticking open","Pressure in the low-pressure rail above specification","Air mass sensor reading too high"],["Check engine lamp on","Increased fuel consumption","Fuel smell from the exhaust"],2,1,["P21F4","P21F7","P21F9","P21FD","P2178","P2BF1"],""],P21F6:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean Off Idle (Bank 2)","P21F6 is the bank 2 form of P21F4 and only exists on V or flat engines whose cylinder banks each have their own front oxygen sensor and two injection paths. Here the part-load correction of the second path on bank 2 has reached its lean limit. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Restricted port injector on bank 2","Wiring or connector fault on the bank 2 injector harness","Low pressure in the shared port fuel rail (if bank 1 also lean)"],["Check engine lamp on","Slight hesitation at part load"],2,1,["P21F4","P21F7","P21FA","P21FE","P2179","P2BF2"],""],P21F7:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich Off Idle (Bank 2)","P21F7 sets when the second fuel path on bank 2 has to remove more fuel above idle than its rich limit permits. It needs an engine with two banks, separate front sensors and dual injection; inline engines such as Audi's 2.5 TFSI only have the bank 1 codes. No manufacturer publishes criteria for P21F7.",["Leaking port injector on bank 2","Bank 2 front oxygen sensor reading rich","Low-pressure regulation too high (if bank 1 also rich)"],["Check engine lamp on","Increased fuel consumption"],2,1,["P21F5","P21F6","P21FB","P21FF","P2180","P2BF3"],""],P21F8:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Idle (Bank 1)","P21F8 covers the idle zone: the second fuel path of bank 1 needs more extra fuel at idle than its adaptation allows. Airflow at idle is so small that a fixed amount of unmetered air or a slightly sluggish injector shifts the mixture a lot, which is why makers learn idle separately from part load.",["Outdated engine control software (Audi 2.5 TFSI, bulletin 2059429/1)","Unmetered air entering behind the air mass sensor","Port injector on bank 1 delivering too little","Low pressure in the port fuel rail"],["Check engine lamp on","Unsteady or hunting idle"],2,1,["P21F9","P21FA","P21F4","P21FC","P2187","P2BF0"],""],P21F9:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Idle (Bank 1)","P21F9 reports that bank 1's second fuel path runs rich at idle even though its correction has already reached the lower limit. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; Audi's 2.5 TFSI bulletin lists only the lean idle code P21F8 and the off-idle pair.",["Port injector on bank 1 dripping after closing","Low-pressure fuel regulation holding too much pressure","Fuel vapour entering via crankcase ventilation (fuel-diluted oil)"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough idle and fuel smell","Higher consumption in town traffic"],2,1,["P21F8","P21FB","P21F5","P21FD","P2188","P2BF1"],""],P21FA:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Idle (Bank 2)","P21FA is the bank 2 version of the idle lean check for the second fuel path. It applies to engines with two cylinder banks, a front oxygen sensor per bank and dual injection, such as Ford's 5.0 V8, which has combined port and direct injection since 2018. No manufacturer publishes this code; Ford monitors its port system per bank without separate idle cells and would store the fault as P2BF2.",["Intake leak at bank 2 runners or gasket","Partly blocked port injector on bank 2","Bank 2 front oxygen sensor reading lean"],["Check engine lamp on","Uneven idle"],2,1,["P21FB","P21F8","P21F6","P21FE","P2189","P2BF2"],""],P21FB:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Idle (Bank 2)","P21FB means bank 2's second fuel path is rich at idle while its correction already sits at the rich limit. The code requires an engine with a separate front sensor per bank and two injection paths; no maker documents it publicly. CARB section (e)(6.2.2) is the legal basis: once adaptive fuel control has used up the adjustment the manufacturer allows, a fault must be stored.",["Port injector on bank 2 leaking or sticking open","Bank 2 front oxygen sensor reading rich","Low-pressure regulation too high or fuel from crankcase ventilation (if both banks rich)"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough idle and fuel smell"],2,1,["P21FA","P21F9","P21F7","P21FF","P2190","P2BF3"],""],P21FC:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 1)","P21FC is the lean check of bank 1's second fuel path in the upper load zone, the third cell next to idle (P21F8) and part load (P21F4). Under high load, delivery capacity matters most: a weak lift pump, a clogged filter or a low-pressure rail that sags at high flow show up here first. On engines combining both paths, the share of each depends on the operating point;",["Weak in-tank lift pump or clogged fuel filter","Port rail pressure dropping at high flow","Port injectors on bank 1 flowing too little","Charge air leak behind the air mass sensor"],["Check engine lamp on","Hesitation or power loss at full load"],2,1,["P21FD","P21FE","P21F4","P21F8","P2191","P2BF0"],""],P21FD:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 1)","P21FD sets when the second fuel path on bank 1 is still rich at higher load although its learned correction has already taken away the permitted maximum. No manufacturer documents the code publicly.",["Air mass sensor reading too high at large airflow","Low-pressure regulator holding too much pressure","Port injectors on bank 1 over-delivering"],["Check engine lamp on","Increased consumption, sooty tailpipe"],2,1,["P21FC","P21FF","P21F5","P21F9","P2192","P2BF1"],""],P21FE:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 2)","P21FE is the bank 2 counterpart of P21FC: in the upper load zone the second injection path on bank 2 needs more enrichment than its adaptation may supply. It can only appear on two-bank engines with per-bank sensors and dual injection.",["Restricted port injectors on bank 2","Weak shared supply (lift pump, filter, low-pressure sensor) if both banks lean","Harness or connector fault on bank 2 injectors"],["Check engine lamp on","Loss of pull at full throttle"],2,1,["P21FF","P21FC","P21F6","P21FA","P2193","P2BF2"],""],P21FF:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 2)","P21FF closes the series: bank 2's second fuel path is rich in the upper load range although its correction already removes the largest reduction allowed. No manufacturer publishes criteria for it. Under CARB, a fuel system fault must be stored once adaptive control has exhausted the range the maker allows; threshold, load window and the number of trips are left to the manufacturer.",["Port injectors on bank 2 over-delivering at long pulse widths","Bank 2 front oxygen sensor reading rich","Excessive pressure in the shared low-pressure rail"],["Check engine lamp on","Increased fuel consumption"],2,1,["P21FE","P21FD","P21F7","P21FB","P2194","P2BF3"],""],P2200:["NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2200 is the general electrical fault reported for the front NOx sensor on bank 1, the unit ahead of the SCR catalyst. Such sensors carry their own control unit, which checks the probe wiring and reports the result over CAN. GM's 6.6L Duramax (LML) sets P2200 as a Type A fault once an open-circuit status keeps arriving for more than 0.5 s or 10 s, depending on calibration.",["Internal fault in the NOx probe or its attached control unit","Damaged cable between probe and sensor control unit (heat, chafing)","Moisture or corrosion in the sensor connector","Unstable supply or ground at the sensor control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No NOx value in live data from the upstream sensor","SCR or emissions warning, possibly followed by inducement countdown"],2,3,["P2201","P2202","P2203","P2204","P220A","P229E","P2213","U029D"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2201:["NOx Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","Here the upstream NOx sensor on bank 1 is electrically intact, yet its reading is not believable. Manufacturers test this in different ways. VW's 2014 Touareg TDI compares the reading with modelled engine-out NOx (deviation beyond 60 percent), checks a slow fall from 100 to 60 percent (over 4.5 s) and an offset outside +50/-30 ppm.",["Aged or poisoned NOx sensing element with offset or slow response","Exhaust leak upstream of the sensor letting in outside air","Fault elsewhere (EGR, fuelling, DEF dosing) that shifts real NOx output","Control software calibration (Ford 6.7L 2020-2023, TSB 24-2136/24-2148)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often stored together with SCR efficiency codes such as P20EE","Increased AdBlue consumption or SCR warning"],2,1,["P2200","P2202","P2203","P221A","P229F","P2214","P20EE","P22FB"],"חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2202:["NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2202 means the raw NOx value sent by the upstream sensor on bank 1 has dropped below the lowest figure a working sensor can report. Since the probe talks over CAN, the check concerns the transmitted value rather than a wire voltage. GM's Duramax diesels (6.6L LML and 3.0L LZ0) use a limit of minus 90 ppm, the LZ0 as Type B after two trips with dew point reached and supply in range;",["NOx sensing element drifted low or internally faulty","Engine software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)","Damaged probe lead or connector between element and sensor module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Live data shows a negative NOx value upstream","SCR dosing may switch to a fallback strategy"],2,1,["P2200","P2201","P2203","P2204","P22A0","P2215"],"חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2203:["NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2203 flags a raw NOx value from the upstream sensor on bank 1 that lies above anything the engine can actually emit. The limits differ: GM sets 1,500 or 2,500 ppm on the 6.6L Duramax (LML) and 2,500 ppm on the 3.0L LZ0 (Type B, two trips), VW 1,655 ppm on the 2014 Touareg TDI.",["Upstream NOx sensor reading high due to internal failure","ECM software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0, bulletins 23-NA-193 and 24-NA-094)","Sensing element contaminated by oil ash or DEF deposits"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Implausibly high upstream NOx value in live data","Possible over-dosing of AdBlue or SCR efficiency codes"],2,1,["P2200","P2201","P2202","P2204","P22A1","P2216"],"חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2204:["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2204 describes an upstream NOx sensor on bank 1 whose signal path works most of the time but keeps dropping out. Smart NOx sensors report the state of their measuring circuit (open wire, short or no error) to the engine computer over CAN; when such fault messages come and go faster than a steady circuit fault would allow, this code fits.",["Loose or corroded terminals at the NOx sensor connector","Harness near the exhaust damaged by heat or vibration","Intermittent internal fault in the sensor module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, sometimes going out again","NOx value in live data dropping out briefly","SCR warning that comes and goes"],2,1,["P2200","P2202","P2203","P2212","P2217"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2205:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The ceramic element of a NOx sensor only measures once its built-in heater has brought it to several hundred degrees. P2205 reports a break on the heater control side of the upstream sensor on bank 1. GM's 6.6L Duramax (LML) sets it after the sensor has reported an open heater for over 10 s with at least 11 V; on the 3.0L LZ0 it is an open load on the heater control pin.",["Heater element in the NOx probe burnt through","Broken conductor in the lead between probe and sensor module","Software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after one trip","Upstream NOx sensor never becomes ready","SCR warning on the display"],2,1,["P2206","P2207","P2208","P220E","P22A3","P2218"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2206:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","A NOx sensor needs its ceramic element heated to several hundred degrees before it can measure. P2206 means the heater control circuit of the first (upstream) NOx sensor on bank 1 reads low, typically a short to ground or a driver output stuck low. CARB requires diesel OBD to detect heater circuit opens and shorts that conflict with the commanded state.",["Internal heater or control-unit fault in the NOx sensor","Heater wiring chafed to ground near the exhaust","Moisture or corrosion in the sensor connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","SCR or emissions warning on the display","Usually no change in driveability"],2,1,["P2205","P2207","P2208","P2219","P22A4"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2207:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2207 is the high-side counterpart of P2206: the heater control circuit of the upstream NOx sensor on bank 1 shows a voltage that is too high for the commanded state, typically an open heater element or a short to supply voltage. CARB requires the diesel OBD system to flag such circuit faults that contradict the command.",["Heater element inside the NOx sensor burnt open","Open circuit or short to voltage in the heater wiring","Loose or heat-damaged connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","NOx readiness or SCR efficiency faults may follow"],2,1,["P2205","P2206","P2208","P2220","P22A5"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2208:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","Besides the control line, the NOx sensor heater has a sense or feedback path through which the controller checks how the heater actually responds (current, resistance or element temperature). P2208 marks a general fault in this sense circuit of the upstream sensor on bank 1. GM calls it NOx Sensor Heater Feedback Circuit (3.0L LZ0 diesel);",["Internal fault in the NOx sensor or its control unit","Damaged wiring between sensor element and sensor control unit","Water ingress in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","NOx sensor reports no valid value"],2,1,["P2209","P2210","P2211","P2212","P2205","P2221"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2209:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2209 is the performance check of the NOx sensor heater: the feedback is electrically present but shows that the element does not reach or hold operating temperature as expected. VW's 2014 TDI specification books (Passat, Touareg) set it when NOx control has not become active more than 180 s after the dew point was passed.",["Aged NOx sensor element that heats up too slowly","Low supply voltage or poor ground to the sensor","Prolonged cold or wet exhaust delaying dew-point release"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","NOx sensor not ready for long periods after start","Possible follow-up SCR efficiency faults"],2,1,["P2208","P2210","P2211","P2212","P220E","P2222"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P220A:["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","A smart NOx sensor draws its own operating power, mostly for the probe heater. P220A means the supply reaching the upstream sensor on bank 1 is outside its window. Ford's 6.7L and 3.0L diesels flag above 16.5 V or below 8.5 V; GM's 3.0L Duramax (LZ0) flags below 9.9 V while the engine runs, Type B after two trips.",["Blown fuse, faulty relay or poor ground in the sensor supply","Supply wire chafed, corroded or with high resistance","Supply booster in the glow plug control module (GM 6.6L LML)","Weak battery or charging-system voltage out of range"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Upstream NOx sensor shows no value or no communication","Other NOx sensor codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P220B","P220C","P220D","P2200","U029D"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P220B:["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P220B concerns the second NOx sensor on bank 1, the one behind the SCR catalyst whose reading proves how well NOx is being converted. Its operating voltage is outside the allowed band. Ford applies the same 8.5 to 16.5 V window as for the front sensor; GM's 3.0L LZ0 flags under 9.9 V (Type B), and VW's 2014 Touareg TDI compares battery and sensor supply, faulting a gap above 1.5 V.",["Fuse, relay or ground fault in the downstream sensor supply","Supply wire to the rear sensor damaged under the vehicle","ECM calibration (GM 1.6L LH7 2018, PIP5615A / 19-NA-009)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Downstream NOx sensor shows no value","SCR efficiency monitor stays incomplete"],2,1,["P220A","P220C","P220D","P229E","U029E"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P220C:["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P220C is reserved for an engine with a separate exhaust path per cylinder bank, each with its own NOx sensors, and reports that the upstream sensor on bank 2 is not getting a proper supply voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the diesel pickups and trucks examined (Ford, GM, VW, Volvo/Mack) merge both banks into one SCR line and only use the bank 1 codes.",["Fuse, relay or ground fault in the bank 2 sensor supply","Supply wiring to the bank 2 upstream sensor damaged","System voltage out of range (battery or alternator)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No NOx value from the bank 2 upstream sensor"],2,1,["P220A","P220B","P220D","P2213"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P220D:["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P220D covers the last position in this group: the downstream NOx sensor on bank 2, after that bank's own SCR catalyst, has a supply voltage outside its window. It only exists on engines whose two banks keep separate aftertreatment, which none of the publicly documented diesel applications do; no manufacturer lists the code with thresholds. Ford's bank 1 rear sensor code P220B uses 8.5 to 16.5 V, a useful reference.",["Supply fuse, relay or ground fault for the bank 2 rear sensor","Corroded connector exposed to road spray behind the catalyst","Internal fault in the supply stage of the sensor module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","SCR efficiency monitor for bank 2 not completed"],2,1,["P220A","P220B","P220C","P221B"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P220E:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P220E says the heater of the upstream NOx sensor on bank 1 is not behaving as commanded. Ford's 6.7L and 3.0L diesels bundle several checks under it: an open heater found by the sensor hardware, a short to positive (over 5 V on the heater), a short to ground (0 V), and a duty cycle that differs from the expected one by more than 20 percent.",["Aged heater element in the upstream NOx probe","Sensor and PCM software (Ford 6.7L 2020-2023, TSB 24-2136/24-2148)","Heater wiring or ground with high resistance or shorts"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Upstream NOx sensor slow to become ready after start","Often stored with P2201 or P2209"],2,1,["P220F","P2205","P2206","P2207","P2209","P2201"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P220F:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P220F is the heater check of the rear NOx sensor on bank 1, the one after the SCR catalyst. Ford's diesel summary (it titles the code as a heater sense circuit fault) flags a heater current under 0.4 A, a short to battery or to ground, or a heater duty cycle more than 20 percent away from the expected value.",["Heater of the downstream NOx probe weak or failed","Heater wiring of the rear sensor shorted or with high resistance","Water or salt in the rear sensor connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","SCR efficiency monitor not completing"],2,1,["P220E","P22A3","P22A4","P229E","P220B"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2210:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2210 means the heater feedback signal of the upstream NOx sensor on bank 1 sits below its permitted range. Typical electrical causes are a short to ground in the sense line or a failed measuring stage in the sensor electronics. GM lists the code as NOx Sensor Heater Feedback Circuit Low for the 2024 Silverado/Sierra 3.0L diesel (LZ0).",["Fault in the sensor element or its control unit","Sense line shorted to ground","Corrosion in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No NOx reading in live data"],2,1,["P2208","P2209","P2211","P2212","P2206","P2223"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2211:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2211 flags a heater feedback signal above its permitted range on the upstream NOx sensor of bank 1. An open sense line, a short to supply voltage or an interrupted heater element that the electronics reads as maximum resistance are the usual reasons. GM lists it as NOx Sensor Heater Feedback Circuit High for the 3.0L Duramax (LZ0) in the 2024 Silverado/Sierra.",["Interrupted heater element in the NOx sensor","Open sense line or short to voltage","Loose or heat-damaged connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","NOx sensor stays not ready"],2,1,["P2208","P2209","P2210","P2212","P2207","P2224"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2212:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","Besides driving the heater, the upstream NOx sensor on bank 1 has a sense path that reports back how the heater actually responds; GM measures heater resistance on a separate HTemp pin. P2212 means this feedback keeps dropping out or jumping instead of failing for good. No manufacturer publishes thresholds for P2212;",["Loose or corroded contact in the NOx sensor connector","Cracked conductor in the probe lead that opens with heat or vibration","Intermittent fault in the sensor module's heater measurement"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, possibly intermittent","Upstream NOx value briefly invalid"],2,1,["P2208","P2209","P2210","P2211","P2205","P2204"],"חישת גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2213:["NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 2)","P2213 mirrors P2200 for the second cylinder bank: the NOx sensor serving bank 2 ahead of its SCR catalyst reports a general electrical fault. That presumes an engine whose banks feed separate aftertreatment lines. No manufacturer documents P2213 publicly; even V8 diesels such as GM's 6.6L Duramax, Ford's 6.7L and the Cummins 5.0L in Nissan's Titan XD route both banks into a single SCR line and use bank 1 codes only.",["Internal fault in the bank 2 NOx probe or its sensor control unit","Heat-damaged or chafed lead between probe and sensor control unit","Water or corrosion in the bank 2 sensor connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No NOx value from the bank 2 sensor in live data","SCR warning, possibly with an inducement countdown"],2,3,["P2200","P2214","P2215","P2216","P2217","P220C"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P2214:["NOx Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","Under J2012, P2214 is the plausibility fault of the bank 2 NOx sensor: wiring intact, reading not credible. No maker uses it that way in public documents. Hino does use the number differently: on its J08E inline six (Hino 238, 258, 268 and 338 conventional models, 2011 to 2016) P2214 belongs to NOx sensor 2 behind the SCR catalyst.",["Aged or poisoned NOx element reading with offset or slow response","Sensor heater cracked by condensation (Hino 2015-2016, SB-15-038/SB-16-002)","Diluted DEF or faulty dosing injector distorting the NOx reading","Exhaust leak upstream of the sensor"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often stored with P2201 or SCR efficiency code P20EE","Higher DEF consumption or SCR warning"],2,1,["P2201","P2213","P2215","P2216","P221B","P20EE"],"חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2215:["NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2215 says the NOx value transmitted for bank 2 falls below the smallest figure a healthy sensor can deliver. Because smart NOx sensors talk over CAN, the limit is a concentration in ppm, not a wire voltage. No manufacturer publishes this bank 2 code; the diesels on record send both banks through one SCR system and use P2202 instead.",["NOx element of the bank 2 sensor drifted low","Fault in the measuring electronics of the sensor module","Damaged lead between probe and sensor module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Negative NOx value for bank 2 in live data","DEF dosing switches to a substitute strategy"],2,1,["P2202","P2213","P2214","P2216","P2217"],"חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2216:["NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2)","P2216 is set when the NOx concentration reported for bank 2 exceeds anything the engine could plausibly emit. It belongs to engines with an SCR line per cylinder bank; none of the documented diesels is built that way, and no manufacturer lists P2216 publicly.",["Bank 2 NOx sensor reading too high due to internal failure","Sensing element fouled by oil ash or DEF crystals","Calibration error in the engine or dosing control software"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Implausibly high NOx value for bank 2 in live data","SCR efficiency codes may follow"],2,1,["P2203","P2213","P2214","P2215","P2217"],"חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2217:["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","P2217 describes a bank 2 NOx sensor whose measuring path fails only now and then: the reading drops out or the sensor briefly reports an electrical error, then recovers. A smart NOx sensor evaluates its own probe lines and sends status flags for open or shorted circuits alongside the value over CAN; flags that toggle point to this code rather than to the steady fault P2213.",["Loose or corroded terminals at the bank 2 sensor connector","Lead near the exhaust cracked by heat or vibration","Sporadic fault in the sensor module electronics"],["Malfunction indicator lamp that comes and goes","Bank 2 NOx value briefly invalid in live data"],2,1,["P2204","P2213","P2215","P2216","P2225"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2218:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","A NOx sensor cannot measure until its built-in heater has taken the ceramic cell to several hundred degrees, and the sensor electronics switches that heater itself. P2218 reports a break in the heater control path of the bank 2 sensor, either inside the probe or in the lead to the sensor module. No manufacturer documents the bank 2 version.",["Heater element in the bank 2 NOx probe burnt through","Broken conductor between probe and sensor module","Pushed-back or corroded pin in the sensor connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after one trip","Bank 2 NOx sensor never reports ready"],2,1,["P2205","P2219","P2220","P2221","P2213"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2219:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2219 means the heater control line of the bank 2 NOx sensor is pulled toward ground when it should not be, typically a heater lead chafed against the exhaust or a shorted output stage in the sensor electronics. The control unit then switches the heater off to protect itself. Bank 2 use is not documented by any manufacturer, as known SCR diesels combine both banks.",["Heater lead of the bank 2 sensor chafed through to ground","Shorted heater or output stage inside the sensor","Salt water bridging pins in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Bank 2 NOx sensor stays cold and delivers no value"],2,1,["P2206","P2218","P2220","P2223"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P221A:["NOx Sensor 1/2 Correlation (Bank 1)","P221A compares the two NOx sensors of bank 1, upstream and downstream of the SCR catalyst. When conditions should make both read alike, the gap between them is too large, so the system cannot tell which value to trust. Volvo and Mack list P221A among codes that often lead to needless sensor swaps;",["One of the two NOx sensors (often the outlet sensor) reading wrongly","Exhaust leak between the two sensors diluting the reading","ECM software (Nissan Titan XD 5.0L 2016, NTB16-048)","Faulty DEF dosing distorting the comparison"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often stored with P20EE or other SCR codes","Implausible NOx conversion values in live data"],3,1,["P221B","P2201","P229F","P229E","P22A7","P20EE"],""],P221B:["NOx Sensor 1/2 Correlation (Bank 2)","P221B compares the NOx sensors before and after the SCR catalyst of bank 2. When operating conditions should make them agree, their readings differ by more than the calibration allows, and the controller cannot decide which value is wrong. The code requires a separate SCR line on bank 2, which no publicly documented diesel has; no manufacturer lists P221B.",["One of the two bank 2 NOx sensors reading wrongly","Exhaust leak between the two sensors","Dosing that does not stop or leaks, distorting the comparison"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often stored with SCR efficiency codes","Inlet and outlet NOx values for bank 2 disagree in live data"],3,1,["P221A","P2214","P2213","P220D","P20EE"],""],P221C:["Reductant Heater B Current Too Low","P221C reports that heater B of the DEF system draws too little current while switched on. GM and Ford both assign B to the heated pressure line that carries DEF to the dosing valve. GM's 2025 Duramax tables flag line heater current under 0.75 A with a PWM command above zero, 40 faulty readings spaced 0.1 s apart, Type A with the MIL after one trip.",["Heating element in the DEF pressure line open or burnt","Corroded or loose connector at the heated line","Missing heater supply (fuse, relay or harness)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","DEF line may freeze in winter, dosing starts late","DEF system warning, inducement possible if unresolved"],2,3,["P221D","P20BD","P20BE","P20BF","P20C0","P21DD","P221E"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — ערך נמוך מדי"],P221D:["Reductant Heater B Current Too High","P221D is stored when heater B, the electrically heated DEF pressure line at GM and Ford, takes more current or power than its design permits. That usually means a partly shorted element or a lead touching ground, and the controller cuts the heater to save its driver.",["Partly shorted heating element in the DEF pressure line","Heater lead chafed to ground","Water in the line heater connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after one trip (GM)","Line heater switched off, DEF may stay frozen in cold weather"],2,3,["P221C","P20BD","P20BE","P20BF","P20C0","P214F","P221F"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — ערך גבוה מדי"],P221E:["Reductant Heater C Current Too Low","P221E says DEF heater C pulls too little current while commanded on. Which element is C depends on the system. In GM's 2025 Duramax tables heater 3 is a second tank heater; the code needs a PWM command above zero and trips under 0.75 A after 40 readings taken every 0.1 s, a Type A fault with the MIL after one trip.",["Heater C element open or burnt (tank or supply module, by system)","Corroded or wet connector at the tank or pump unit","Heater supply missing (fuse, relay, harness)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slow DEF thawing in cold weather, dosing starts late"],3,3,["P221F","P20C1","P20C2","P20C3","P20C4","P221C","P21DD"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — ערך נמוך מדי"],P221F:["Reductant Heater C Current Too High","P221F flags excessive current through DEF heater C, pointing to a partial short in the element or its lead. GM's 2025 Duramax tables, where heater 3 is the second tank heater, set the code above 15 A over 40 samples of 0.1 s whenever the vehicle is active, Type A with the MIL after one trip, and zero all heater PWM commands while any heater fault is present.",["Partly shorted heater C element","Heater lead chafed to ground at the tank or pump unit","Water or DEF crystals in the heater connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after one trip (GM)","DEF heating disabled, possible frozen-DEF warnings in winter"],3,3,["P221E","P20C1","P20C2","P20C3","P20C4","P221D","P214F"],"זרם גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2220:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","P2220 is the high-side counterpart of P2219: on the bank 2 NOx sensor, the heater control line carries battery voltage when the heater should be off or regulated, so the element may overheat or the output stage cannot switch. A pinched lead touching a feed wire or a failed driver inside the sensor are the usual causes. The bank 2 code is not documented by any manufacturer.",["Heater control lead shorted to a supply wire","Failed heater driver inside the bank 2 sensor module","Heat-damaged connector with pins bridged"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Bank 2 NOx reading missing or invalid"],2,1,["P2207","P2218","P2219","P2224"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2221:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 2)","Alongside the heater drive, a NOx sensor has a sense path that tells the electronics how the heater is really behaving, usually by measuring its resistance, which tracks cell temperature. P2221 reports a general fault in that sense circuit on the bank 2 sensor.",["Fault in the heater measurement of the bank 2 sensor","Open sense conductor between probe and sensor module","Corrosion in the sensor connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bank 2 NOx sensor not ready"],2,1,["P2208","P2218","P2222","P2223","P2224","P2225"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החישה (בנק 2)"],P2222:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","With P2222 the heater feedback of the bank 2 NOx sensor is electrically present, yet what it reports does not match the heating command: the cell warms too slowly or settles at the wrong resistance. No manufacturer documents this bank 2 code. Two bank 1 descriptions show the approach.",["Aged heater in the bank 2 NOx probe with drifted resistance","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the sensor module","Heater wiring with added resistance"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bank 2 NOx sensor slow to become ready after a cold start","SCR monitor for bank 2 delayed"],2,1,["P2209","P2221","P2223","P2224","P220F"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה (בנק 2)"],P2223:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P2223 indicates that the heater sense line of the bank 2 NOx sensor sits at or near ground potential, so the electronics reads an impossibly low value for heater resistance. A sense conductor rubbed through to the exhaust bracket or a shorted measuring input inside the sensor module are the usual explanations. No manufacturer publishes the bank 2 code.",["Sense lead of the bank 2 sensor shorted to ground","Shorted measuring input in the sensor module","Water ingress in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","No valid NOx value from bank 2"],2,1,["P2210","P2221","P2222","P2224","P2219"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל החישה (בנק 2)"],P2224:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 2)","P2224 is logged when the heater sense signal of the bank 2 NOx sensor is too high, which the electronics sees as a short to supply voltage or as an interrupted heater reading near infinite resistance. The bank 2 code appears in no public manufacturer document.",["Heater element in the bank 2 probe open, read as maximum resistance","Sense lead shorted to a voltage source","Fault in the sensor module input stage"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Bank 2 NOx sensor stays unready"],2,1,["P2211","P2221","P2223","P2225","P2220"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל החישה (בנק 2)"],P2225:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","P2225 covers a heater sense circuit on the bank 2 NOx sensor that fails only for moments: the feedback drops out or jumps, then returns to normal, which a steady open or short code would not describe. No manufacturer documents thresholds for P2225 or for its bank 1 twin P2212.",["Loose or corroded contact in the bank 2 sensor connector","Cracked sense conductor that opens with heat or vibration","Sporadic fault in the heater measurement of the sensor module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp that comes and goes","Bank 2 NOx value briefly invalid"],2,1,["P2212","P2221","P2223","P2224","P2217"],"חישת גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2226:["Barometric Pressure Sensor A Circuit","P2226 is the general circuit code for barometric pressure sensor A, the sensor that tells the engine computer the outside air pressure for air-charge, fuel and boost calculations. Ford's OBD summary for 2024-2025 gasoline engines shows how the code appears in current software: every BARO fault is reported as P2226 plus a failure-type byte, -16 for a low voltage (formerly P2228), -17 for high (P2229), -92 for a…",["Fault of the barometric sensor built into the engine control module","Damaged wiring or loose connector on an external BARO sensor","5 V reference supply of the sensor pulled down by another faulty sensor"],["Check engine light","Auto start-stop no longer works","Failure-type suffix (-16, -17, -92, -1F) shown with the code on newer scan tools"],2,1,["P2227","P2228","P2229","P2230","P222A"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2227:["Barometric Pressure Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2227 means the barometric reading is electrically fine but does not fit the other pressure signals. Ford's 2012 summary compares BARO, throttle inlet and manifold pressure after at least 10 s engine-off; the sensor that disagrees with the other two is blamed. While driving at low airflow BARO must stay within 5.5 inHg of throttle inlet pressure. Ford's 2023 diesels set P2227 for a reading below 50 kPa held for 1 s.",["Ice or sludge in the charge air cooler on turbo engines in severe cold (GM 22-NA-007, 23-NA-002)","BARO sensor reading with an offset or drift","Faulty boost or manifold pressure sensor that skews the comparison","Engine control software that needs an update"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or hesitation in very cold weather on turbo engines","P0299 or misfire codes stored alongside"],2,3,["P2226","P2228","P2229","P2230","P0106","P0236","P222F"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2228:["Barometric Pressure Sensor A Circuit Low","P2228 sets when the voltage from barometric pressure sensor A stays below the lowest value a real atmosphere could produce. Ford's gasoline summaries (2012 and 2020-2023) use under 2.0 V, which would mean an altitude above 15,000 ft, for 5 s; on these engines the sensor is mounted on the PCM circuit board. Ford's 2023 diesels flag under 0.25 V (about 6 kPa) after 0.5 s.",["Signal wire of an external BARO sensor shorted to ground or open","Defective sensor inside the PCM (Ford, Mazda and others), PCM replacement","Low or missing 5 V reference to the sensor"],["Check engine light","Auto start-stop deactivated","Scan tool shows an implausibly low barometric pressure"],2,1,["P2226","P2227","P2229","P2230","P222C"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2229:["Barometric Pressure Sensor A Circuit High","P2229 reports a barometric sensor A voltage above anything plausible for outside air. Ford's gasoline engines judge more than 4.4 V, an altitude below -1,000 ft, over 5 s; the 2023 diesels use 4.85 V (115 kPa) after 0.5 s. GM's 2018 diesel tables look for contact with a voltage source: over 94.1 % of the 5 V range (115.1 kPa) in 320 of 400 readings, Type B.",["Breather filter of a PCM-internal BARO sensor clogged (e.g. engine-bay wax, Mazda 01-008/20)","Signal wire of an external sensor shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Internal fault of the sensor or the control module"],["Check engine light, often only after the engine bay has heated up","Auto start-stop deactivated","Scan tool shows barometric pressure far above the real value"],2,1,["P2226","P2227","P2228","P2230","P222D"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P222A:["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit","P222A is the general circuit code for a second barometric pressure sensor, B. Only some engines carry one. GM's tables for the 3.0 L twin-turbo V6 (LGW, 2018) and for 2023-2024 twin-throttle engines monitor such a sensor B, but they report its circuit faults with the more specific codes P222C (low) and P222D (high) and do not use P222A. No maker documents P222A publicly.",["Damaged wiring or corroded connector at sensor B","Barometric pressure sensor B defective","Fault in the shared 5 V sensor supply"],["Check engine light","Usually no noticeable change in how the engine runs"],2,1,["P222B","P222C","P222D","P222E","P2226"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P222B:["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P222B means sensor B delivers a clean signal whose value is wrong. GM documents two strategies. On the 3.0 L LGW (2018) and a 2016 engine family the ECM estimates outside pressure from boost pressure, airflow and rpm while driving; sensor B fails if it deviates by more than 20 kPa, or 25 kPa once more than 1.24 miles have passed since the last update.",["Sensor B reading with offset or stuck at one value","Leak or restriction in the intake path that distorts the comparison","Boost or manifold pressure sensor fault affecting the estimate"],["Check engine light after two drives","Usually no driveability change"],2,1,["P222A","P222C","P222D","P222E","P222F","P2227"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P222C:["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","P222C flags a sensor B voltage that has dropped too low, as with a signal wire touching ground. GM's 2018 tables for the 3.0 L LGW set the code below 40 % of the 5 V range, equal to about 50.9 kPa, counted in 320 of 400 readings taken every 12.5 ms; it is a Type B fault with the MIL after two trips. GM's 2023-2024 tables for a twin-throttle engine use the pressure value itself: below 50 kPa for 2 s.",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","5 V reference to sensor B open or shorted","Sensor B internally defective"],["Check engine light","Scan tool shows a very low reading for the second barometric sensor"],2,1,["P222A","P222B","P222D","P222E","P2228"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P222D:["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","P222D is stored when sensor B reports an excessive voltage. GM's 2018 tables for the 3.0 L LGW name contact with a supply voltage or a broken line: on that input a broken wire drives the signal up, not down. The limit is 90 % of the 5 V range, about 115 kPa, met in 320 of 400 readings; Type B, MIL after two trips.",["Connector of sensor B unplugged or signal wire broken","Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Sensor B internally defective"],["Check engine light","Second barometric reading stuck near the top of its range"],2,1,["P222A","P222B","P222C","P222E","P2229"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P222E:["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P222E catches a sensor B signal that jitters. Outside air pressure changes slowly, so GM measures noise directly: every 12.5 ms the difference to the previous reading is taken, and the absolute differences over 80 consecutive readings are added up into a so-called string length. If that total exceeds 100 kPa, the one-second sample counts as failed;",["Loose or corroded terminal at sensor B or the ECM","Chafed wire with intermittent contact","Electrical interference, for example from a poorly grounded component nearby"],["Check engine light that may come and go","Second barometric value jumping on the scan tool"],2,1,["P222A","P222B","P222C","P222D","P2230"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P222F:["Barometric Pressure Sensor A/B Correlation","P222F is meant for engines with two barometric sensors whose readings should agree but drift apart, without the software being able to say which of the two is wrong. No maker documents this code publicly.",["One of the two barometric sensors has drifted","Supply or ground offset shifting one sensor's signal","Blocked port or breather of one sensor"],["Check engine light","The two barometric readings differ clearly on the scan tool"],2,1,["P2227","P222B","P0069"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2230:["Barometric Pressure Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2230 flags a barometric pressure (BARO) signal that is electrically present but jumps or drops out for short moments instead of sitting permanently low or high. The engine computer uses BARO for air-charge, fuelling and boost calculations. Ford's 2020-2023 gasoline OBD summary lists P2230 with P2227-P2229 among the BARO faults that inhibit auto start-stop.",["Engine harness chafed against an engine component (e.g. vacuum pump pulley, cam cover)","Loose or corroded pin at the BARO sensor or ECM connector","Barometric pressure sensor with an internal contact problem"],["Check engine light, often coming and going","Auto start-stop inactive","Other sensor codes stored at the same time if a shared harness is damaged"],2,1,["P2227","P2228","P2229","P0106"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2231:["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2231 means the engine computer sees the heater supply of the upstream oxygen sensor on bank 1 leaking into the sensor's signal path - typically an internal short in the sensor or two neighbouring wires touching in the harness. VW's 2014 specification books for the Passat and Tiguan set it when the front sensor signal changes by more than 190 microamps, i.e. the measured sensor current is distorted.",["Internal short between heater and sensing element in the oxygen sensor","Heater and signal wires melted or chafed together (exhaust heat, routing)","Moisture or contamination bridging pins in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption due to open-loop fuelling","Rough idle or hesitation in some cases"],2,1,["P2232","P2233","P2234","P0030","P0130"],""],P2232:["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P2232 reports that the heater supply of the oxygen sensor behind the catalyst on bank 1 is bleeding into that sensor's signal line. A switching sensor only produces up to about 1 V, so the ECM watches its signal at the instant the heater is switched off.",["Internal leakage between heater and sensing element of the rear oxygen sensor","Signal and heater wires fused or chafed together near the exhaust","Water or corrosion bridging pins in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light after two drives","Catalyst monitor not completed or catalyst code stored alongside"],2,1,["P2231","P2233","P2235","P0036","P0137","P0138"],""],P2233:["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P2233 is the heater-to-signal short for sensor 3 on bank 1, a third oxygen sensor that some engines fit after a second catalyst or between two catalyst bricks. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM's checks for the rear-sensor codes P2232/P2235 show how such a fault is normally caught: the signal leaps by more than 2 V within 0.04 s whenever the heater is switched off.",["Internal leakage between heater and sensing element of sensor 3","Sensor 3 wiring melted or chafed along the exhaust or underbody","Corroded underbody connector of the third sensor"],["Check engine light without noticeable driving change","Emissions inspection failed because of the stored code"],2,1,["P2232","P2236","P0042","P0143","P0144"],""],P2234:["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2234 means the heater of the front air-fuel sensor on bank 2 couples into its measuring circuit. On a wide-band sensor the disturbance is small, so the check is finer than on rear sensors. GM's 2005 tables for the Bosch-equipped 2.8/3.6 V6 look for a signal step of 0.08-0.2 V appearing no later than 0.05 s after each heater switching edge;",["Front sensor element cracked by thermal shock (water on the hot sensor)","Heater and signal wires of the bank 2 sensor touching in the harness","Moisture in the sensor connector bridging heater and signal pins"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption when bank 2 runs without lambda control","Other bank 2 front-sensor codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P2231","P2235","P2240","P0050","P0150"],""],P2235:["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P2235 concerns the post-catalyst oxygen sensor on bank 2, found on V engines with a catalyst per bank. The ECM sets it when switching off the heater makes the sensor voltage spike. GM runs the check only once the sensor is past its dew-point phase and the modelled exhaust has been above 250 °C for 90 s (and below 800 °C);",["Internal leakage between heater and sensing element of the bank 2 rear sensor","Sensor wires damaged by heat or chafing near the bank 2 catalyst","Water ingress in the rear sensor connector"],["Check engine light after two drives","Bank 2 catalyst monitor not completed"],2,1,["P2232","P2234","P2236","P0056","P0157","P0158"],""],P2236:["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","P2236 would be set if the heater of the third oxygen sensor on bank 2 leaked into its signal wire. Such a sensor sits furthest downstream and exists only on engines with two catalyst stages per bank. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and Jaguar Land Rover's 2015 list for its V6 with sensors 3 on both banks does not use it either.",["Internal leakage between heater and sensing element of sensor 3 on bank 2","Long underbody wiring to the rear sensor chafed or heat-damaged","Road salt corrosion in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light with normal driving behaviour","Readiness for catalyst or oxygen sensor monitor not set"],2,1,["P2233","P2235","P0062","P0163","P0164"],""],P2237:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2237 points to an open pump-current line (IP or APE) on the front wide-band sensor of bank 1. With that wire broken the output freezes near its stoichiometric value of roughly 1.5 V and lambda stops moving. Ford sets it on Bosch sensors when 20 s of fuel-control steps and reference-current pulses shift lambda by 0.05 or less; NTK interface chips report the open line directly.",["Broken pump-current wire or pushed-back pin between sensor and ECM","Pump cell of the wide-band sensor damaged, for example by catalyst-heating strategy or thermal shock","Engine software that sets the code falsely (update available for some models)"],["Check engine light","Lambda reading stuck at 1.0 in live data","Higher fuel consumption in open-loop fuelling"],2,1,["P2238","P2239","P2240","P2243","P2251","P0130","P0134"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2238:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2238 is the low-side fault of the pump-current circuit of the front wide-band sensor on bank 1. Saab's 9-5 2.0 turbo (2010) shows a concrete test: on overrun with the injectors shut off, pure air should drive the signal well above its stoichiometric level, and if it stays below 1.7 V for 3 s the code sets as Type B. GM's 2005 V6 tables use the same fuel-cut check but book it under P2237.",["Pump-current wire chafed through to ground","Aged or contaminated sensor that no longer reads lean in fuel cut-off","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light after two drives","Lambda value does not rise during coasting in live data"],2,1,["P2237","P2239","P2241","P0131"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2239:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2239 is the high-side counterpart for the pump-current circuit of the bank 1 front wide-band sensor. On the Saab 9-5 2.0 turbo (2010) it sets when, in closed loop with the mixture deliberately enriched, the signal still sits at 1.48-1.51 V for 1 s, meaning the sensor ignores a change it should report; it is a Type B code.",["Pump-current wire shorted to heater supply or battery voltage","Wide-band sensor with internal short or stuck output","Damaged sensor interface in the ECM"],["Check engine light after two drives","Lambda reading frozen near 1.0 regardless of load","New sensor fails again quickly if the wiring short is not found"],2,1,["P2237","P2238","P2242","P0132"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P223A:["Reductant Heater E Control Circuit","P223A covers the control circuit of a fifth DEF heating element, heater E. Unlike heaters A to D, which each have four codes for open, performance, low and high, heater E gets only this one code, so any electrical fault of its driver or wiring ends up here. No maker documents P223A publicly.",["Open or shorted wiring or connector of heater E","Heating element E burnt out or shorted","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","DEF dosing delayed or blocked in freezing weather"],3,3,["P223B","P20C5","P20B9","P21C2"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ E — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P223B:["Reductant Heater F Control Circuit","P223B reports a fault in the control circuit of heater F, the sixth heating element of an SCR system. Like its neighbour P223A for heater E, it is a single catch-all code covering open lines and shorts alike.",["Damaged wiring or corroded connector of heater F","Heating element F open or shorted","Missing supply from the heater relay or fuse"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","Reduced power warning after a cold-weather DEF fault"],3,3,["P223A","P20C5","P20C1","P21C2"],"גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ F — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P223C:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Range/Performance (Bank 1)","P223C judges whether the pump current of the bank 1 wide-band sensor makes sense while the engine is coasting with fuel cut off. In that state the sensor sees almost pure air and, as Bosch's LSU 4.9 data show, must drive a clearly positive current. GM's tables (2016, 2018, 2019) start the test after 5 s of fuel cut-off and stop it at 12 s, with the reference cell above about 600 °C.",["Aged or poisoned wide-band sensor with wrong pump current in air","Open pump-current, reference-cell or reference-ground wire","Exhaust leak or misfire that distorts the gas at the sensor"],["Check engine light after two drives","Usually no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P223D","P223E","P2237","P2243","P2251"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P223D:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Range/Performance (Bank 2)","P223D applies the pump-current plausibility test to the front wide-band sensor of bank 2 on V engines. GM's 2016 and 2018 tables describe it for engines with a Continental interface chip: during a fuel cut-off window between 5 s and 12 s, a reading above 5.0 mA, within ±0.3 mA of zero, or below -0.10 mA is counted, and 40 hits in 160 samples in any window set the code as Type B.",["Worn bank 2 wide-band sensor that no longer pumps correctly in air","Interrupted pump-current or reference circuit of the bank 2 sensor","Sensor heater too weak to keep the element at temperature"],["Check engine light after two drives","Often no driveability complaint"],2,1,["P223C","P223F","P2240","P2247","P2254","P0155"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P223E:["O2 Sensor Reference Resistance Out Of Range (Bank 1)","P223E checks the internal resistance of the reference (Nernst) cell in the bank 1 wide-band sensor. That resistance falls as the ceramic heats up, so the ECM uses it as a thermometer; Bosch specifies 300 ohms nominal for the LSU 4.9 at operating temperature.",["Aged sensor whose reference cell resistance has drifted","Heater not holding the element at temperature (heater, wiring or control)","ECM calibration fault on GM 2.0 turbo LTG (bulletin 16-NA-266)"],["Check engine light after two consecutive drives","Remote start refuses to start the engine (GM LTG models)"],2,1,["P223F","P223C","P0135","P0030","P0132"],"התנגדות ייחוס חיישן חמצן — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 1)"],P223F:["O2 Sensor Reference Resistance Out Of Range (Bank 2)","P223F is the reference-cell resistance check for the front wide-band sensor of bank 2. GM's 2016 and 2018 tables translate the measured resistance into element temperature and count readings below 700 °C or above 1,000 °C; 64 of 80 samples (2018) or 128 of 160 (2016) at 25 ms set a Type B code.",["Bank 2 sensor ceramic aged and high-resistance","Weak heater supply or high resistance in the heater wiring","Sensor overheated by misfire or very high exhaust temperature"],["Check engine light after two drives","Bank 2 lambda control slow to become active after a cold start"],2,1,["P223E","P223D","P0050","P0155"],"התנגדות ייחוס חיישן חמצן — מחוץ לטווח (בנק 2)"],P2240:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2240 is the open pump-current circuit of the front wide-band sensor on bank 2, so it only exists on V engines and boxers. Ford's summaries (2012 and 2020-2023) introduced it to replace P0154; detection works as on bank 1, by lambda failing to react to reference-current pulses or by the NTK interface chip.",["Open pump-current wire or loose pin at the bank 2 sensor connector","Bank 2 front sensor damaged by water or thermal shock","PCM calibration that sets the code without a hardware fault (FCA 2025 Hurricane)"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 lambda value stuck at 1.0 in live data","Higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P2237","P2241","P2242","P2247","P2254","P0154"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2241:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2241 reports the pump-current circuit of the bank 2 front wide-band sensor at too low a level, typically a grounded wire or a sensor that cannot pump enough oxygen. No manufacturer publicly documents P2241 with thresholds. The bank 1 twin P2238 is described by Saab for its 2.0 turbo, where the signal must climb past 1.7 V on overrun with the injectors off; a V engine would run the same logic per bank.",["Bank 2 pump-current wire shorted to ground","Aged bank 2 front sensor with weak pump cell","Fault in the ECM sensor interface for bank 2"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 2"],2,1,["P2240","P2242","P2238","P0151"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2242:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2242 flags the pump-current circuit of the bank 2 front wide-band sensor as too high, usually a short to the heater feed or battery voltage, or a signal locked at its midpoint although the mixture is being changed. No manufacturer publicly documents P2242 with thresholds. Saab describes the bank 1 version P2239 for its 2.0 turbo: 1.48-1.51 V held for 1 s while closed loop enriches the mixture.",["Bank 2 pump-current wire shorted to heater supply or battery voltage","Internal short in the bank 2 wide-band sensor","Damaged sensor interface in the ECM"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 lambda value stuck near 1.0","Replacement sensor fails again if the short remains"],2,1,["P2240","P2241","P2239","P0152"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2243:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2243 flags an open reference voltage line on the front wide-band sensor of bank 1, i.e. the Nernst-cell lead (RE/UN on Bosch sensors, VS on NTK). Ford's OBD summaries set it on Bosch parts when the sensor voltage sits above 4.7 V or below 0.2 V for 10 s; on NTK parts the interface chip reports the break itself.",["Broken reference voltage (Nernst cell) wire or pushed-back pin between sensor and ECM","Sensing element cracked or tip broken off, for example by thermal shock","Corroded or loose sensor connector","Engine software that sets the code falsely (update available for some models)"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 1","Catalyst efficiency code P0420 alongside it if a sensor fragment damaged the converter"],2,1,["P2244","P2245","P2246","P2247","P2237","P2251","P0130","P0420"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2244:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2244 stands for a plausibility fault on the reference voltage side of the bank 1 upstream wide-band sensor: the Nernst-cell signal is electrically intact and within limits, but behaves in a way that does not fit the operating state, for instance offset or too slow. No manufacturer documents P2244 publicly. Ford treats this lead only as an open circuit (P2243) and books shorts on any sensor wire under P0131/P0132;",["Aged or contaminated wide-band sensor (oil ash, silicone, coolant)","High resistance in the reference voltage wire or connector","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensor distorting the reading"],["Check engine light","Slightly higher fuel consumption","Possible failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2243","P2245","P2246","P2248","P223C","P0133"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2245:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2245 reports that the reference voltage side of the upstream air-fuel sensor on bank 1 reads too low, usually because the wire touches ground or the sensor has shorted internally. GM's tables for the Saturn Vue 3.5 V6 (L66, 2004-05) define it precisely: with the engine running for over 85 s, the heater active and the element signal between 3.2 and 4.6 V, a pump-cell circuit voltage below 1.5 V for 0.5 s stores the…",["Reference voltage wire shorted to ground (chafed against exhaust or body)","Sensor element damaged internally, for example by water hitting the hot ceramic","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 1","Uneven idle or hesitation in some cases"],2,1,["P2243","P2244","P2246","P2249","P2238","P0131"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2246:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2246 means the reference voltage line of the bank 1 front wide-band sensor reads too high, typically from a short to battery or heater voltage or a short inside the sensor. No manufacturer publishes a threshold for P2246. GM's 2018 Duramax table 18OBDG04 names it, together with P2245, P2252 and P2253, as a fault that makes the front sensor signal unusable, but gives no setting criteria.",["Reference voltage wire shorted to heater supply or battery voltage","Internal short between heater and Nernst cell in the sensor","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption","Repeat failure of a new sensor if the wiring short remains"],2,1,["P2243","P2245","P2250","P2239","P0132"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2247:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2247 is the bank 2 version of P2243: the Nernst-cell reference line of the upstream wide-band sensor on the second cylinder bank is open. Ford's summaries trip it on Bosch sensors after 10 s outside 0.2-4.7 V and on NTK sensors via the interface chip, replacing the older P0150. VW's 2014 Touareg book names it an open Nernst-voltage circuit with limits of 0.25 and 4.80 V, while GM's 2005 V6 tables call it Type B.",["Broken reference voltage (Nernst cell) wire or loose pin on the bank 2 sensor","Cracked element or broken sensor tip after thermal shock","Engine software that sets the code falsely (update for some models)"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 2","Catalyst efficiency code P0430 if a sensor fragment damaged the converter"],2,1,["P2243","P2248","P2249","P2250","P2240","P2254","P0150","P0430"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2248:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2248 is meant for a reference voltage signal on the bank 2 upstream wide-band sensor that is present but implausible, as opposed to an open or shorted line. No manufacturer documents P2248 publicly, and the published diagnostic tables of Ford, GM, Saab and VW cover the bank 2 Nernst-cell line only with the open-circuit code P2247, while Ford routes shorts to P0151/P0152.",["Aged or contaminated wide-band sensor on bank 2","High resistance in the reference voltage wire or connector","Exhaust leak ahead of the bank 2 sensor"],["Check engine light","Slightly higher fuel consumption","Possible failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2244","P2247","P2249","P2250","P223D","P0153"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2249:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2249 indicates that the reference voltage circuit of the front air-fuel sensor on bank 2 is pulled too low, most often by a grounded wire in the harness or a fault inside the sensor. The only public manufacturer criteria come from GM's tables for the Saturn Vue 3.5 V6 (L66, 2004-05), a Honda-built engine: after more than 85 s of running with the sensor heater active and the element signal at 3.2-4.6 V, a pump-cell…",["Reference voltage wire shorted to ground on the bank 2 sensor harness","Internal short in the bank 2 air-fuel sensor","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 2","Possible failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2245","P2247","P2248","P2250","P2241","P0151"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P224A:["NOx Sensor Heater Resistance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P224A concerns the heater of the upstream NOx sensor on bank 1, the one before the SCR catalyst. Its electrical resistance rises with temperature, so the sensor electronics use it to hold the ceramic element at working heat. The code says that resistance is outside its allowed band, pointing to an aged or damaged element or a contact problem. No maker documents P224A publicly.",["Heating element of the NOx sensor aged or cracked","Corroded or loose contacts in the sensor connector","Unstable supply voltage to the sensor module"],["Check engine light","SCR efficiency or NOx plausibility codes may follow"],2,1,["P224B","P2209","P2205","P0053"],"התנגדות גוף חימום חיישן NOx (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P224B:["NOx Sensor Heater Resistance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P224B is the heater resistance fault of the second NOx sensor on bank 1, mounted after the SCR catalyst. This sensor tells the control unit how much NOx is left after dosing, so its readings feed the catalyst efficiency monitor and the closed-loop dosing correction. If the heater's resistance leaves its expected band, the element may be running too cold or too hot. No maker documents P224B publicly.",["Heating element of the downstream NOx sensor aged or damaged","Corrosion in the sensor connector exposed to road spray","Element cracked by water droplets hitting the hot sensor"],["Check engine light","SCR efficiency monitor delayed or failing"],2,1,["P224A","P22A7","P220F","P0054"],"התנגדות גוף חימום חיישן NOx (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P224C:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit/Open","P224C points to an open or otherwise faulty control circuit of shutoff valve A, the solenoid on a CNG or LPG tank that releases gas only when the engine runs on the alternative fuel. Such valves are normally closed. GM's 2015 bi-fuel Impala (bulletin PI1330) fits a high-pressure cut-off solenoid to the tank and energizes it in CNG mode while the engine cranks or runs;",["Broken wire or unplugged connector at the tank valve","Solenoid coil of the valve open","Supply interrupted by relay or tripped inertia switch"],["Check engine light","Vehicle will not switch to gas operation or falls back to gasoline"],3,1,["P224D","P224E","P224F","P2A22"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P224D:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P224D means tank shutoff valve A is electrically switched but the system behaves as if it stayed shut. Software can only infer that from a pressure response: once the valve is commanded open, line or rail pressure should climb toward the regulated value, which GM gives as 468-896 kPa for the bi-fuel Impala and Ford as about 724 kPa for its 2003 CNG trucks.",["Manual tank valve closed or tank nearly empty","Valve plunger stuck closed, e.g. by contamination","Supply voltage too low to pull the solenoid open","Faulty gas pressure sensor misreporting the response"],["Check engine light","Engine switches back to gasoline or will not run on gas","Gas fuel gauge shows content although no gas is delivered"],3,1,["P224C","P224E","P224F","P2A23"],"מעגל בקרת שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P224E:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit Low","P224E sets when the control line of tank shutoff valve A reads too low. The DTC list of CNG upfitter TransEco Energy for its alternative fuel control module (AFCM v1.4) blames the line touching ground or being interrupted, turns on the MIL in both dedicated and bi-fuel setups and lets the system keep operating normally rather than forcing a fallback. The same list uses P2A24 and related numbers for valves B to E.",["Control wire of the tank valve chafed through to ground","Open circuit, which some modules report under this code","Shorted solenoid coil in the valve"],["Check engine light","Gas operation unavailable or interrupted"],3,1,["P224C","P224D","P224F","P2A24"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P224F:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit High","P224F reports a control circuit of tank shutoff valve A that reads too high, typically a wire touching battery voltage. In TransEco Energy's AFCM fault list the cause is given as shorted to power, the MIL is lit and the gas system keeps working under the failure mode strategy.",["Control wire of the tank valve shorted to battery voltage","Output stage in the alternative fuel control module stuck on","Wiring mistake after a conversion or repair"],["Check engine light","Tank valve may stay open after switching off"],3,1,["P224C","P224D","P224E","P2A25"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2250:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2250 signals that the reference voltage line of the upstream wide-band sensor on bank 2 is too high, as happens with a short to the heater feed or battery voltage, or a breakdown inside the ceramic. No manufacturer documents P2250 publicly, and no bulletin in the NHTSA index names it.",["Reference voltage wire of the bank 2 sensor shorted to heater supply or battery voltage","Internal short between heater and Nernst cell","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption","Repeat failure of a new sensor if the wiring short remains"],2,1,["P2246","P2247","P2249","P2242","P0152"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2251:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2251 points to an open negative current control line, i.e. the reference or virtual ground (VM on Bosch, COM on NTK) of the bank 1 upstream wide-band sensor. Ford detects it on Bosch parts by a sensor voltage stuck in a narrow band, or by a reference-current pulse that still moves lambda; NTK chips report the break directly.",["Broken reference ground wire or pushed-back pin between sensor and ECM","Internal open circuit in the wide-band sensor","Engine software that sets the code falsely (reprogramming for some models)"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 1","Possible rough running or failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2252","P2253","P2254","P2243","P2237","P0130"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2252:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2252 means the negative current control side of the bank 1 front air-fuel sensor reads too low, typically because that line or the sensor cell is shorted to ground. GM's tables for the Honda-built 3.5 V6 in the Saturn Vue (L66, 2004-05) describe it as a sensor-cell short: once the engine has run for 85 s with the heater working and the element signal between 3.2 and 4.6 V, a sensor-cell voltage under 0.3 V for 0.5…",["Reference ground or sensor-cell wire shorted to ground (chafed against exhaust or body)","Internal short in the air-fuel sensor","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 1","Possible hesitation or uneven running"],2,1,["P2251","P2253","P2255","P2245","P0131"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2253:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2253 reports that the negative current control side of the bank 1 upstream air-fuel sensor reads too high. On the Honda-built 3.5 V6 of the 2004-05 Saturn Vue (L66), GM's tables treat it as an open sensor-cell circuit: with the heater operating and the element signal above 4.6 V, a sensor-cell voltage over 6.0 V for 5 s sets it, and P2256 does the same on bank 2.",["Open sensor-cell wire or connector contact, letting the signal float high","Wire shorted to heater supply or battery voltage","Internal defect in the air-fuel sensor"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 1","Repeat failure of a new sensor if a wiring short remains"],2,1,["P2251","P2252","P2256","P2246","P0132"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2254:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2254 concerns the negative current control line - also called reference ground, virtual ground or COM - of the wide-band air-fuel sensor ahead of the catalyst on bank 2. Ford's OBD summaries (2012 and 2020-2023) set it for an open line: with Bosch sensors the PCM briefly injects a reference current and flags the line if lambda barely moves, within about 10 s;",["Broken reference ground wire or pushed-out pin between sensor and ECM","Internal open circuit in the wide-band sensor","Corroded sensor connector with high contact resistance"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from open-loop fuelling on bank 2","Possible rough running or failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2251","P2255","P2256","P2247","P2240","P0150"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2255:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2255 reports that the negative current control line (reference ground) of the bank 2 upstream wide-band sensor reads too low, typically a short to ground. No manufacturer publicly documents P2255 with thresholds. Ford's OBD summaries assign shorts to ground on any wide-band sensor line to P0151 and use P2254 only for an open line, and VW's 2014 specification books likewise list only P2254.",["Reference ground wire shorted to ground (chafed against exhaust or body)","Internal fault in the wide-band sensor","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption","Possible hesitation or uneven running"],2,1,["P2252","P2254","P2256","P0151"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2256:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2256 means the negative current control line (reference ground) of the bank 2 upstream wide-band sensor reads too high, typically a short to battery or heater voltage. No manufacturer publicly documents P2256 with thresholds. Ford's OBD summaries send a short to battery on any wide-band sensor line to P0152 and reserve P2254 for the open line; VW's 2014 books also list only P2254 for this circuit.",["Reference ground wire shorted to heater supply or battery voltage","Internal short in the wide-band sensor","Fault in the sensor interface of the ECM"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption","Repeat failure of a new sensor if the wiring short remains"],2,1,["P2253","P2254","P2255","P0152"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2257:["AIR System Control A Circuit Low","P2257 concerns the control circuit of the secondary air (AIR) pump or its relay, which blows fresh air into the exhaust during cold starts so the catalyst lights off sooner. The code sets when that circuit reads low.",["Relay control wire shorted to ground","Secondary air relay with a shorted coil","Water ingress in the relay or pump connector"],["Check engine light","Secondary air pump silent during cold start","Secondary air flow codes such as P0411 may follow"],2,1,["P2258","P0418","P2259","P0411"],"בקרת מערכת האוויר המשני‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2258:["AIR System Control A Circuit High","P2258 reports that the line controlling secondary air (AIR) pump A or its relay sits at too high a level, usually because it is shorted to battery voltage or the driver cannot pull it down. The pump only runs briefly after a cold start to heat the catalyst faster, so the fault mainly raises warm-up emissions.",["Control wire of the AIR pump relay chafed through and touching a battery-voltage feed","Secondary air relay with shorted coil or welded contacts","Moisture or corrosion in the relay or pump connector bridging terminals","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["MIL on, often without any noticeable change in driving","Secondary air pump silent after a cold start","Higher hydrocarbon emissions during warm-up, possibly a failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2257","P0418","P0412","P2260","P0411"],"בקרת מערכת האוויר המשני‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2259:["AIR System Control B Circuit Low","P2259 is the low-level fault of the second secondary air control circuit, B. A second circuit exists where an engine uses two AIR pumps, two relays or a separately switched air valve; circuit A keeps its own codes P2257/P2258. A low reading usually means the control wire has contact with ground.",["Control wire of circuit B chafed against the body or engine and shorted to ground","Relay or air valve B with a shorted winding","Corroded connector at relay B or the air valve"],["MIL on","Secondary air pump audible for longer than usual or while warm","Blown fuse of the secondary air pump after a long run"],2,1,["P2260","P2257","P2258","P0411","P0418"],"בקרת מערכת האוויר המשני‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P225A:["NOx Sensor Calibration Memory (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P225A concerns the front NOx sensor of bank 1, the one ahead of the SCR catalyst. Modern NOx probes come with their own control unit that holds a sensor-specific calibration and reports finished values over CAN; this code means the stored calibration data of that unit cannot be read or fails its check. Ford's 2014 PCM code table carries P225A as a MIL code, but no manufacturer publishes the test or a threshold.",["Internal memory or checksum fault in the NOx sensor control unit","Replacement sensor with a part number or calibration that does not suit the vehicle","Supply voltage dropout or poor connector contact while the module was storing data","Engine or aftertreatment control unit software that misreads the sensor data"],["MIL on, usually without any change in how the engine runs","SCR dosing runs without valid feedback, so NOx emissions may rise","Follow-up NOx catalyst efficiency codes possible"],2,1,["P225B","P2200","P2201","P20EE"],"זיכרון כיול חיישן NOx (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P225B:["NOx Sensor Calibration Memory (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P225B is stored when the control unit of the downstream NOx sensor on bank 1 cannot provide valid calibration data from its memory. That sensor sits behind the SCR catalyst and is what the engine computer uses to judge how well urea dosing reduces NOx, so a sensor without trustworthy calibration leaves the catalyst monitor blind. Ford lists P225B as a MIL code in its 2014 PCM code table;",["Corrupted or unreadable calibration memory in the downstream NOx sensor module","Sensor installed with the wrong part number or an OEM calibration for another application","Moisture or corrosion at the sensor module connector disturbing its supply"],["MIL on with no driveability complaint","SCR efficiency monitor does not complete or reports P20EE","Possible emissions test failure because readiness stays incomplete"],2,1,["P225A","P229E","P22A1","P20EE"],"זיכרון כיול חיישן NOx (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P225C:["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P225C says the upstream NOx sensor of bank 1 reports more NOx than is plausible. Volvo describes its test on US17+OBD19 trucks: during engine motoring with zero fuel the engine makes no NOx, so the inlet sensor must fall below 50 ppm within about 10 s; each failure lights the MIL, which needs three clean drive cycles to go out. Volvo admitted false settings and told dealers not to replace the sensor.",["Engine or DEF control unit software that flags the sensor too eagerly","Leak in the charge air path or an EGR valve stuck partly open","Air mass or coolant temperature signal that skews the NOx model","Upstream NOx sensor with a genuine positive offset"],["MIL on, often without any noticeable driving fault","Code returns after the NOx sensor has been replaced","Higher DEF consumption or SCR efficiency codes in some cases"],3,1,["P225D","P225E","P2201","P221A","P20EE"],""],P225D:["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P225D is the opposite case to P225C: the upstream NOx sensor of bank 1 reads too little NOx or refuses to rise when the engine should be producing it. Volvo and Mack list P225D among NOx codes where the sensor is very unlikely to be at fault, because the probe is simply measuring fresh air; their guide says not to replace it.",["Charge air, intake or exhaust leak that lets the sensor see diluted gas","Sensor ports clogged with soot, for example after fuel contamination","Low-pressure EGR valve partly stuck open","Outdated engine control software that a published flash corrects"],["MIL on","Code persists after a new NOx sensor","Possible related intake, EGR or MAF codes"],3,1,["P225C","P225F","P2201","P2202","P20EE"],""],P225E:["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P225E points at the downstream NOx sensor of bank 1, behind the SCR catalyst, reading persistently high. Because that sensor sees what is left after urea dosing, a high value can be a sensor offset or genuine NOx slipping through a weak catalyst, poor DEF or a faulty dosing valve.",["Real NOx slip from a weak SCR catalyst, poor DEF quality or a faulty dosing valve","Downstream NOx sensor with a positive offset","Control software that evaluates the sensor incorrectly"],["MIL on, often together with P20EE","Increased DEF consumption or DEF quality warnings","Power reduction possible if SCR efficiency codes follow"],3,3,["P225F","P225C","P221A","P20EE","P229E"],""],P225F:["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P225F is set when the downstream NOx sensor of bank 1 reports less NOx than expected or does not move away from a low value. A sensor behind the SCR catalyst that reads too low makes the catalyst look better than it is, so the efficiency monitor can no longer be trusted.",["Exhaust leak upstream of the downstream sensor drawing in outside air","Chafed or corroded wiring between sensor module and probe","Downstream NOx sensor with reduced sensitivity"],["MIL on","SCR efficiency cannot be confirmed, readiness may stay open"],2,1,["P225D","P225E","P229E","P20EE"],""],P2260:["AIR System Control B Circuit High","P2260 flags secondary air control circuit B sitting at too high a level, as with a short to the supply or a driver output that cannot switch. Circuit B drives the second pump, second relay or a separate air valve, depending on the engine.",["Control wire of circuit B shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Relay or air valve B with an open coil, depending on how the driver is diagnosed","Output stage for circuit B in the engine control module defective"],["MIL on","Second secondary air pump or valve does not operate after a cold start","Increased cold-start emissions, possibly with a secondary air flow code on one bank"],2,1,["P2259","P2258","P2257","P0412","P0414"],"בקרת מערכת האוויר המשני‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2261:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A - Mechanical","P2261 means bypass valve A of the turbocharger or supercharger, also called the recirculation valve, does not work mechanically. When the throttle snaps shut it should let charge air flow back to the compressor inlet so the compressor does not surge.",["Bypass/recirculation valve sticking closed or with a torn diaphragm","Kinked, collapsed or wrongly routed recirculation or control hose","Electrical fault at the valve solenoid or its connector that prevents opening","Engine control module output reacting wrongly (software or hardware)"],["Fluttering, chuffing or rattling noise from the turbo when lifting off the throttle","MIL on","Slightly delayed boost after gear changes"],2,1,["P0033","P0034","P0035","P2263","P0299"],""],P2262:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Pressure A Not Detected - Mechanical","P2262 says boost pressure A does not appear at all although the charging system should be producing it, and the cause appears to be mechanical rather than a sensor fault. The control unit sees the pressure after the compressor stay near ambient or close to manifold pressure. VW's 2014 book for the supercharged Touareg 3.0 TSI uses the ratio of boost to manifold pressure and flags it below a band of 1 to 1.25.",["Intake or charge-air hose disconnected or split, so the compressor cannot build pressure","Wastegate or bypass stuck open, corroded or with a broken linkage","Damaged turbocharger or supercharger (bearing wear, broken drive, wheel damage)","Boost pressure sensor or its hose blocked or detached"],["Clear loss of power, no turbo or supercharger pull","MIL on, often with a reduced-power mode","Hissing or whistling from the intake if a hose has come off"],2,3,["P0299","P2263","P226B","P0234","P02CD"],""],P2263:["Turbocharger/Supercharger A Boost System Performance","P2263 means boost pressure measured in the intake manifold stays too far from the target set by the closed-loop boost control. CARB requires diesel OBD to detect underboost, overboost and slow response of the boost control. On the 2014 Cruze 2.0 diesel the allowed underboost deviation runs from 35 to 85 kPa with injection quantity and speed, and the code sets as Type A once the condition holds for 15 s;",["Charge-air hose or cooler duct leaking or pulled off","Variable-geometry vanes or actuator sticking","Restricted exhaust, for example a heavily loaded particulate filter","Boost pressure sensor reading wrong"],["Power loss or limp mode","Hissing or whistling from the charge-air system","Black smoke under load"],2,3,["P0299","P0234","P2563","P2002","P2463"],"מערכת לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2264:["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit","P2264 is the general circuit code for water-in-fuel sensor A, the probe in the diesel filter or separator that detects water by its conductivity. GM's 2018 diesel tables explain a neat self-test: after the ignition has been off for more than about 8 h, a healthy sensor briefly signals water during the first 0.3 to 1.8 s after power-up.",["Water-in-fuel sensor that no longer performs its power-up self-test","Corroded or loose connector at the filter housing, exposed to road spray","Open or damaged wire between sensor and ECM or tank zone module","Incompatible sensor fitted during a filter change"],["Service lamp or message on, engine runs normally","No warning if water actually collects in the separator"],1,0,["P2265","P2266","P2267","P2268","P2269"],""],P2265:["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2265 means the signal from water-in-fuel sensor A is electrically present but does not behave plausibly, for example a self-test response that comes at the wrong time or a value that sits between the expected dry and wet states. No manufacturer documents P2265 publicly.",["Sludge, emulsion or deposits coating the sensor electrodes","Sensor electronics drifting so the output lies between dry and wet","Corroded terminals adding resistance to the signal circuit"],["Water warning or service lamp that comes and goes","Water warning stays on even after the filter has been drained"],1,0,["P2264","P2266","P2267","P2268","P2269"],""],P2266:["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit Low","P2266 is set when the signal line of water-in-fuel sensor A stays below its valid range, typical of a grounded signal wire or of a conductive path that should not be there. Ford documents the code on 2017 and 2018 Super Duty trucks with the 6.7L diesel built up to 15 March 2018: bulletin 18-2133 links P2266, P2269 and P1140 with a lit water-in-fuel lamp to water entering connector C3080 at the sensor, which sits…",["Water intrusion into the sensor connector bridging signal and ground","Sensor with internal resistance outside specification","Signal wire chafed against the frame and shorted to ground"],["Water-in-fuel lamp on although no water is in the separator","Often stored together with P2269"],1,0,["P2267","P2264","P2268","P2269"],""],P2267:["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit High","P2267 reports that the signal of water-in-fuel sensor A sits above its valid range, which usually indicates an open signal or ground path, a disconnected sensor or a short to a voltage source. Stellantis has a case file for 2025 and 2026 Ram 2500 to 5500 trucks with the Cummins 6.7L: after the fuel filter module has been drained, the warning lamp may stay on with P2267 and P2269.",["Residual contamination on the probes after draining the filter","Unplugged sensor or open signal or ground wire","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Defective water-in-fuel sensor"],["Water-in-fuel lamp stays on after draining","Often appears together with P2269"],1,0,["P2266","P2264","P2268","P2269"],""],P2268:["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","P2268 is reserved for a water-in-fuel sensor A circuit whose signal drops out or jumps for short moments instead of staying at a fault level. No manufacturer documents P2268 publicly. The neighbouring codes show where such faults arise on real trucks: Ford traced P2266 on 6.7L Super Duty models to water entering the sensor connector, and Stellantis linked P2267 on Cummins Ram trucks to residue on the probes after…",["Loose or corroded connector at the filter housing losing contact under vibration","Wire chafing intermittently near the frame or filter bracket","Moisture in the plug that changes with temperature and spray"],["Water warning flickers or appears briefly while driving","Code stored as history with no fault present at the workshop"],1,0,["P2264","P2266","P2267","P2269"],""],P2269:["Water in Fuel Condition - Sensor A","P2269 is not a wiring fault but a statement about the fuel: sensor A has detected water. On diesels it means the separator is full; Ram's 2025-26 Cummins 6.7L trucks set it with the MIL, and Stellantis traced a persistent case to incomplete draining, fixed by draining and swapping the sensor's signal and ground pins (TSB 14-004-26).",["Water separator full and not drained at the service interval","Fuel from the tank or filling station containing water","Residual water after draining or a wet sensor connector faking the alarm","Engine control software needing an update"],["Water-in-fuel lamp or message, on some vehicles also the MIL","Rough running, power loss or hard starting if water reaches the injection system","Reduced power on some engines to protect the injection system"],1,3,["P2264","P2266","P2267","P226A","P0169"],""],P226A:["Water in Fuel Lamp Control Circuit","P226A concerns the output that switches the water-in-fuel warning lamp, not the sensor. The control unit drives the lamp circuit and checks it electrically; an open lamp, a broken wire or a shorted driver lets it set this code.",["Burnt-out warning lamp or corroded lamp socket","Open or shorted wire between control unit and lamp","Faulty lamp driver in the control unit"],["Water-in-fuel lamp does not light during the bulb check at ignition on","Lamp stays on permanently regardless of the filter state"],1,0,["P2269","P2264"],""],P226B:["Turbocharger/Supercharger A Boost Pressure Too High - Mechanical","P226B reports boost from turbocharger or supercharger A rising too high for a mechanical reason, for instance a wastegate or bypass that will not open or a seized actuator linkage, rather than a sensor or wiring fault. VW's 2014 book for the supercharged Touareg 3.0 TSI sets it when boost passes 250 kPa.",["Wastegate flap seized closed by corrosion or carbon","Seized or misadjusted wastegate or VGT actuator linkage","Vacuum or pressure line to a pneumatic actuator leaking or blocked","Supercharger bypass valve not opening"],["Sudden power cut or reduced-power mode under load","MIL on","Unusually strong surge of power just before the cut"],3,3,["P0234","P2262","P2263","P0299","P0243"],""],P226C:["Turbocharger Boost Control A Slow Response","P226C means the boost control actuator of turbocharger A does move, but too slowly, so boost lags behind changes in demand. Ford's 2023 diesel summary runs an intrusive check on the 3.0 L and 1.5 L at idle, once in each drive cycle: the variable vanes travel from closed to open, and within 7 s manifold pressure must change by at least 6.5 kPa at sea level (3.5 kPa at 8,000 ft).",["Variable vanes or turbine control valve sluggish from soot, varnish or corrosion","Worn electric or pneumatic boost actuator, or a weak control solenoid","Damaged wiring or connector between actuator and control module","Control module software that needs an update (cold-weather false sets)"],["Hesitant pull from low engine speed, turbo lag","MIL on, sometimes with a torque limit","More smoke on acceleration with diesel engines"],3,3,["P226F","P00AF","P2563","P0299","P2263","P0045"],"בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ A — תגובה איטית"],P226D:["Particulate Filter Deteriorated/Missing Substrate (Bank 1)","P226D means the bank 1 particulate filter offers so little flow resistance that its core is likely broken, burnt out or removed. CARB requires detection of a destroyed or missing substrate, or a filter replaced by a pipe.",["Filter core cracked, melted after an overheated regeneration, or removed","Differential pressure line disconnected, cracked, blocked or routed wrongly","Control software that sets the code without a hardware fault","Incorrect or faulty differential pressure sensor assembly"],["MIL on","Visible soot at the tailpipe if the filter core is damaged","Often no driveability change; regeneration behaviour may be affected"],3,1,["P226E","P2002","P2463","P2453","P244A"],""],P226E:["Particulate Filter Deteriorated/Missing Substrate (Bank 2)","P226E reports a damaged or missing particulate filter core on bank 2, which only exists where each cylinder bank has its own filter. Ford documents it in its 2024-2025 OBD summary for petrol engines: the gasoline particulate filter check runs once the filter has been above 250 °C for 30 s and exhaust flow lies between 300 and 850 m³/h;",["Bank 2 filter core cracked, melted or removed","Pressure sensing line of bank 2 loose, cracked or blocked","Back pressure sensor reading too low"],["MIL on","Usually no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],3,1,["P226D","P2003","P243B"],""],P226F:["Turbocharger Boost Control B Slow Response","P226F is the slow-response fault of boost control B, meaning the actuator of a second turbocharger or of the second stage on twin-turbo, bi-turbo or sequential layouts. Which unit the letter B denotes is up to the manufacturer. The monitoring principle mirrors P226C: the control unit commands a change in vane or wastegate position and expects boost or manifold pressure to follow within a set time.",["Boost actuator of turbocharger B sluggish or worn","Carbon or varnish restricting vanes or flap on turbocharger B","Leaking vacuum line or damaged wiring to actuator B"],["Delayed boost in the speed range where the second charger takes over","MIL on, possibly with reduced power"],3,3,["P226C","P0299","P2263","P0045"],"בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש טורבו‏ B — תגובה איטית"],P2270:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 1, Sensor 2)","P2270 concerns the oxygen sensor behind the catalyst on bank 1. When the mixture turns rich, this sensor should rise to a high voltage; if it stays low, the ECM treats it as biased or stuck lean and can no longer rely on it for catalyst monitoring or the post-catalyst trim.",["Rear oxygen sensor aged, contaminated or slow to reach rich voltage","Exhaust leak ahead of the rear sensor diluting the gas with air","Oil in the sensor connector or a bent terminal","Calibration issue fixed by an ECM update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Catalyst and oxygen sensor readiness not completing","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2271","P2272","P2096","P0136","P0137","P013E","P2195"],""],P2271:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 1, Sensor 2)","P2271 is the opposite fault of the same bank 1 rear sensor: its voltage refuses to fall when the exhaust should be lean. It is usually checked during a deceleration fuel cut, when almost pure air passes the sensor. GM's 2018 four-cylinders set it if the signal is still above 100 mV after 25 g of air in fuel cut-off (Type B);",["Rear oxygen sensor contaminated by coolant, oil or silicone","Faulty front A/F sensor making the rear sensor look stuck rich","Signal wire chafed against a voltage source"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Catalyst monitor not completing"],2,1,["P2270","P2273","P2097","P0138","P013A","P2196"],""],P2272:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 2, Sensor 2)","P2272 applies to V and flat engines with a separate catalyst and rear oxygen sensor on bank 2; that sensor fails to reach a rich reading when the ECM enriches bank 2. GM's 2016 tables (16OBDG05) set it if the voltage is still under 800 mV after 68 g of air during forced enrichment (Type B).",["Bank 2 rear oxygen sensor aged or contaminated","Engine oil in the sensor connector, for example from a leaking oil pressure switch","Exhaust leak on bank 2 ahead of the rear sensor"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Catalyst monitor for bank 2 not completing"],2,1,["P2273","P2270","P2098","P0156","P0157","P2A04","P2197"],""],P2273:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 2, Sensor 2)","P2273 means the rear oxygen sensor of bank 2 keeps a high voltage when the exhaust of that bank should be lean. GM's 2016 tables (16OBDG05) check this in fuel cut-off and set the code if the signal is above 100 mV after 9 g of air (Type B); GM's 2024 tables (24OBDG07) compare the lowest voltage during a commanded lean phase with 0.20 V over two trips.",["Bank 2 rear oxygen sensor fouled by oil or coolant","Signal wire touching a supply or heater line","Bank 2 front sensor misreading so that the bank actually runs rich"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Catalyst monitor for bank 2 not completing"],2,1,["P2272","P2271","P2099","P0158","P013C","P2198"],""],P2274:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 1, Sensor 3)","Sensor 3 exists only where a bank has a third oxygen sensor, usually behind a second catalyst, so that sensor 2 sits between two bricks. P2274 says this last sensor on bank 1 stays lean when it should swing rich. VW's 2014 data books for the CC, Passat and Tiguan 2.0 TSI define it as a rear signal that does not oscillate and stays under about 0.62 to 0.65 V even after the ECM enriches the mixture by 27.9 %.",["Third oxygen sensor aged or cracked by thermal shock from water","Exhaust leak ahead of sensor 3 drawing in air","Damaged wiring or connector of sensor 3"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2275","P2276","P2270","P0142","P0146","P0420"],""],P2275:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 1, Sensor 3)","P2275 is the rich-side fault of the third oxygen sensor on bank 1, the last one on systems with two catalysts in series: it keeps a high voltage while the exhaust should be lean. VW's 2014 data books for the CC, Passat and Tiguan check it in fuel cut-off, comparing the voltage with 0.15 V once 4500 mg of oxygen have passed, more than the 3000 mg used for sensor 2 because the extra catalyst stores oxygen first.",["Third oxygen sensor contaminated or damaged by water","Signal wire of sensor 3 touching a voltage source"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2274","P2277","P2271","P0142","P0144","P0420"],""],P2276:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 2, Sensor 3)","P2276 needs three oxygen sensors on bank 2, so it only occurs on V or flat engines whose second bank carries a front, a mid-catalyst and a post-catalyst sensor. It reports that the post-catalyst sensor of bank 2 does not reach a rich reading. No manufacturer publishes a threshold for this exact code;",["Bank 2 third oxygen sensor aged or cracked by water","Exhaust leak on bank 2 ahead of sensor 3","Damaged wiring or connector of sensor 3"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2277","P2274","P2272","P0162","P0163","P0430"],""],P2277:["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 2, Sensor 3)","P2277 is the rich-side counterpart of P2276: the third, post-catalyst sensor on bank 2 does not drop to a lean reading. On such layouts the check normally runs during a fuel cut, when the second catalyst must fill with oxygen before the sensor can respond, so a slow or fouled element shows up here. No manufacturer publishes a threshold for P2277 itself;",["Bank 2 third oxygen sensor contaminated or water-damaged","Signal wire of sensor 3 touching a voltage source"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2276","P2275","P2273","P0162","P0164","P0430"],""],P2278:["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped Bank 1 Sensor 3/Bank 2 Sensor 3","P2278 reports that the third oxygen sensors of the two banks are connected the wrong way round, so the ECM reads the bank 1 sensor as if it sat on bank 2 and vice versa. The check changes the exhaust of one bank only, for example by cutting its injectors or feeding air into one exhaust line, and watches which sensor answers.",["Sensor 3 connectors of both banks plugged in crosswise after a repair","Harness routed to the wrong side or pins swapped in a connector","Wrong harness, ECM or calibration after a replacement"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Catalyst or sensor codes reported for the wrong bank"],1,1,["P0040","P0041","P2274","P2276","P0142","P0162"],""],P2279:["Intake Air System Leak (Bank 1)","P2279 means the ECM has concluded that air enters the engine without being measured or expected, for example because the air mass sensor, manifold pressure and throttle position no longer agree with its air model. Volkswagen and Audi use it widely.",["Leaking crankcase breather or PCV pressure-regulating valve","Leak at intake manifold, hoses or seals after the air mass sensor","Camshaft timing offset","ECM calibration needing an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Whistling at idle, unstable or high idle speed","Limp mode on some engines"],2,3,["P0507","P2187","P0171","P2073","P0101"],"דליפת מערכת אוויר יניקה (בנק 1)"],P227A:["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit","P227A is the general circuit fault of barometric pressure sensor C, used when the control unit finds the signal missing or unusable without classifying it as too low or too high. Sensor C is not necessarily a separate ambient sensor: in GM's 2018 diesel tables the BARO C channel belongs to the turbocharger inlet pressure sensor, GM also uses it on the supercharged 6.2 L LT4, and on its 2023-2024 twin-throttle engine…",["Loose connector, corroded pins or damaged wiring at sensor C","Sensor C itself failed","5 V reference or sensor ground shared with other sensors disturbed"],["MIL on","Usually no noticeable change in driving; slight power loss at altitude possible"],2,1,["P227B","P227C","P227D","P227E","P2226","P222A"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P227B:["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P227B means sensor C supplies an electrically sound signal that does not agree with the other pressure readings. In GM's 2018 diesel tables sensor C is the turbocharger inlet pressure sensor: the ECM compares it with BARO and MAP at idle and in the window between key-off and the next start, and if only sensor C is out of line it gets the blame, as a Type B fault after 320 failures in 400 samples.",["Sensor C drifting or with an offset","Sensor port blocked by dirt, oil or ice, or sensor not seated in its bore","Heavily clogged air filter shifting the pressure ahead of the compressor or throttle"],["MIL on","Mostly no driveability change; occasionally reduced boost"],2,1,["P227A","P227C","P227D","P227E","P2227","P222B","P0106"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P227C:["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit Low","P227C flags a voltage from pressure sensor C that is too low. GM's 2018 tables show two variants. On the diesel, where sensor C measures turbocharger inlet pressure and the input has a pull-up, only a short to ground pulls it below 39.4 % of 5 V (about 50.2 kPa); 320 failures in 400 samples make it a Type B fault.",["Signal wire of sensor C shorted to ground","Open signal or 5 V supply line on inputs that read an open circuit as low","Replacement control module without the calibration that matches the fitted sensor","Sensor C internally defective"],["MIL on, on some engines immediately","Engine runs on a substitute value, at most slightly less power"],2,1,["P227D","P227A","P227B","P227E","P2228","P222C"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P227D:["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit High","P227D is the high-voltage counterpart of P227C. On GM's 2018 diesel the sensor C input has a pull-up, so both a short to the supply and a broken signal wire push it above 90.2 % of 5 V (about 115.4 kPa); after 320 failures in 400 samples it is a Type B fault.",["Signal wire of sensor C shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Broken signal wire or sensor ground on inputs with pull-up","Sensor C internally defective"],["MIL on","Little change in driving; possibly reduced boost or poorer altitude compensation"],2,1,["P227C","P227A","P227B","P227E","P2229","P222D"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P227E:["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P227E covers a sensor C signal that jumps although every single value is in range. GM measures this as a string length: the absolute difference between each reading and the one taken 12.5 ms earlier is summed over 80 consecutive readings, and a sum above 152 kPa (2018 diesel) or 150 kPa (supercharged LT4) counts as a failure.",["Loose or corroded terminals in the sensor C connector","Chafed wiring with intermittent contact","Interference from ignition or actuator wiring routed nearby","Sensor C with an unstable internal element"],["MIL on, possibly coming and going","Occasional brief hesitation or uneven boost"],2,1,["P227C","P227D","P227A","P227B","P2230","P222E"],"חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P227F:["Air Flow Restriction/Air Leak Between Air Filter and MAF (Bank 2)","P227F means the passage between the air filter and the mass air flow sensor of bank 2 is restricted or lets air in that has bypassed the filter. By today's wording the code belongs to engines with a separate air path and MAF per bank; P2280 is the bank 1 version.",["Air filter clogged with dust or soaked with too much oil","Intake opening blocked by snow, leaves or a collapsed duct","Loose clamp or cracked duct between filter box and MAF on bank 2","Faulty filter restriction or inlet pressure sensor"],["MIL on, on some trucks with an air filter service message","Reduced power and boost under load","More black smoke on diesel engines"],1,1,["P2280","P2281","P0299","P226C","P0101"],""],P2280:["Air Flow Restriction/Air Leak Between Air Filter and MAF (Bank 1)","P2280 is the bank 1 code for restricted airflow or an air leak between the air filter and the MAF sensor. A blocked filter lowers the pressure ahead of the sensor and limits the air the engine can take in. A leak in this section matters less for fuel metering, since the air still passes the MAF, but it lets unfiltered air and dust reach the engine.",["Air filter clogged or soaked with oil","Snow, ice or debris in the air inlet, or a collapsed intake duct","Cracked duct or loose clamp between filter box and MAF","Early software that flags the condition too readily"],["MIL on","Less power and slower boost build-up under load","More smoke from diesel engines when accelerating"],1,1,["P227F","P2281","P2282","P0101","P0299"],""],P2281:["Air Leak Between MAF and Throttle Body","P2281 points to air that escapes or enters between the MAF sensor and the throttle body, so the airflow the sensor reports no longer matches what reaches the cylinders. On turbocharged engines this section includes the compressor, the charge air cooler and their hoses: a loose clamp or split boot can blow off charge air under boost or draw in unmeasured air at idle.",["Loose clamp, split hose or leaking charge air cooler between MAF and throttle","Contaminated or drifting MAF sensor that misreports airflow","Engine software that sets the code without a real leak (update available)","Disconnected crankcase vent or other hose joined to this section"],["MIL on","Hissing under boost and less power","Black smoke on diesels or rough idle on petrol engines"],2,3,["P2280","P2282","P2279","P0101","P0299"],""],P2282:["Air Leak Between Throttle Body and Intake Valves","P2282 means air enters the intake behind the throttle, so it reaches the cylinders without passing the throttle. Ford uses it as its PCV monitor on turbo engines with speed density: airflow worked out from manifold pressure is compared with airflow through the throttle, and a calculated leak of 1 lb/min or more for at least 5 s, with the throttle at 4 degrees or less, sets the code (2012, 2020-2023 and 2024…",["Brake booster vacuum pipe detached or its check valve stuck open","Crankcase ventilation hose disconnected or cracked","Leaking intake manifold gasket, throttle body seal or vacuum hose","Iced manifold pressure sensor or software miscalculating the leak"],["High or unstable idle speed","MIL on, sometimes with a hissing noise from the engine bay","Harder brake pedal if the brake vacuum line is affected"],2,1,["P2281","P2279","P0106","P0507","P0171"],""],P2283:["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit","P2283 is the general circuit code for the injector control pressure (ICP) sensor. ICP describes the high-pressure engine oil that hydraulically actuated unit injectors (HEUI) use to pressurise fuel, as on Navistar-built Ford Power Stroke diesels; the sensor reports rail pressure so the injection pressure regulator can be closed-loop controlled. No manufacturer documents P2283 publicly.",["Failed ICP sensor, often with oil inside the connector","Damaged signal, reference or ground wire of the sensor","5-volt reference circuit pulled down by another sensor"],["Low power and hesitation","Hard or long cranking, especially when hot","MIL on"],2,3,["P2284","P2285","P2286","P2287","P2623"],"חיישן לחץ בקרת מזרק — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2284:["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2284 means the measured injector control pressure does not follow what the PCM commands. Ford's 6.0L Power Stroke summaries (2003 and 2004) run the check continuously every 8 ms with the engine running: a fault is recorded once measured pressure stays more than 3.0 MPa above the target for longer than 7 s, the reverse case being P2290.",["ICP sensor reading offset, including a shifted internal O-ring","Injection pressure regulator valve sticking or contaminated","Wrong, aerated or low engine oil disturbing pressure control","Oil wicking into the sensor connector"],["Reduced power and rough idle","Engine runs on a substitute pressure value","MIL on"],2,3,["P2285","P2286","P2288","P2290","P2283"],"חיישן לחץ בקרת מזרק — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2285:["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2285 is set when the ICP sensor voltage falls almost to zero. Ford's 6.0L Power Stroke summaries for 2003 and 2004 define it precisely: below 0.03 V, checked every 8 ms without entry conditions, decided in under one second. Such a value cannot come from a working sensor on a 5-volt reference, so it points to an open signal wire, a short to ground, a lost reference voltage or an unplugged sensor.",["Signal wire open or shorted to ground","Sensor disconnected or failed internally","Missing 5-volt reference supply"],["MIL on immediately","Hard starting and reduced power"],2,3,["P2286","P2284","P2283","P2287"],"חיישן לחץ בקרת מזרק — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2286:["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2286 means the ICP sensor voltage has risen to the top of the range. In Ford's 2004 summary for the 6.0L Power Stroke the limit is above 4.83 V, checked every 8 ms and confirmed in less than one second; the 2003 edition already names the code alongside P2285.",["Open sensor ground circuit","Signal wire shorted to the 5-volt reference or another voltage","ICP sensor failed with output stuck high"],["MIL on","Reduced power and possibly harsh running"],2,3,["P2285","P2284","P2283","P2287","P2288"],"חיישן לחץ בקרת מזרק — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2287:["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent","P2287 covers an ICP sensor signal that drops out or jumps for brief moments, too short or too irregular to be judged as a steady low or high fault. No manufacturer documents P2287 publicly; Ford's 6.0L summaries and its 2014 PCM table contain the steady electrical codes P2285 and P2286 but not this one.",["Engine oil creeping into the sensor connector","Fretting or loose terminals at sensor or PCM","Harness rubbing on engine parts and shorting briefly"],["Occasional stumble, surge or hesitation","Code returns without a fault visible in the workshop"],2,3,["P2283","P2285","P2286","P2284"],"חיישן לחץ בקרת מזרק — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2288:["Injector Control Pressure Too High","P2288 reports that the injector control pressure itself, not just its reading, has climbed above the allowed maximum while the engine runs. Ford's 6.0L Power Stroke summaries put the limit at 27.5 MPa in the 2003 edition and 29.5 MPa in 2004, sustained for more than 3 s. For comparison, Ford's high-pressure oil pump normally works between about 3 and 25 MPa on that engine.",["Injection pressure regulator valve stuck or contaminated","Fault in the regulator drive circuit holding it at high duty","ICP sensor reading higher than the actual pressure"],["Reduced power with fuel limit active","Loud injection noise or knocking","MIL on"],3,3,["P2289","P2290","P2284","P2623"],"לחץ בקרת מזרק — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2289:["Injector Control Pressure Too High - Engine Off","P2289 is a plausibility test carried out with the engine stopped. On a HEUI diesel the high-pressure oil pump is driven by the engine, so once it stops, injector control pressure should drop to almost nothing. Ford's 6.0L Power Stroke summaries check this in engine-off mode: if the ICP reading stays above 10 MPa for more than 10 s (2003) or 12 s (2004), P2289 is stored.",["ICP sensor with a positive offset or oil contamination","Partial short between signal and reference voltage","Faulty input stage in the PCM"],["MIL on, possibly after the engine was switched off","Hard starting if the PCM trusts the false pressure value"],2,1,["P2288","P2286","P2284","P2291"],""],P228A:["Fuel Pressure Regulator A - Forced Engine Shutdown","P228A is a protective shutdown code: the engine computer has stopped the engine because rail pressure could not be held even with fuel pressure regulator A at full authority. In GM's 2018 diesel tables regulator 1 (A) is the fuel metering unit on the high-pressure pump;",["Fuel supply starved (gelled or waxed diesel, clogged filter, failing in-tank pump)","Fuel metering unit on the high-pressure pump sticking or worn","High-pressure pump no longer reaching the required delivery","Leak in the high-pressure circuit or injector return"],["Engine stalls while driving or shuts off shortly after starting","Long cranking or no restart","Check engine light on, often with P0087","Whining in-tank fuel pump in cold weather"],3,3,["P228B","P228C","P0087","P0089","P229A"],""],P228B:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B - Forced Engine Shutdown","P228B mirrors P228A but concerns fuel pressure regulator B, which in GM's 2018 diesel calibration is the rail pressure regulator valve that spills surplus fuel from the rail. The ECM shuts the engine down when rail pressure stays more than 40 MPa below target although it already commands that valve fully closed, judged over 640 of 800 samples at 12.5 ms and stored as Type A.",["Rail pressure regulator valve not sealing when closed","Fuel starvation from gelled diesel or a blocked filter","High-pressure pump delivering too little","Excessive injector leak-off"],["Engine stops on its own and may not restart","Check engine light with low rail pressure codes","Loss of power just before the shutdown"],3,3,["P228A","P229A","P2293","P0087","P0089"],""],P228C:["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low","P228C means rail pressure has stayed below target long enough that regulator A, the path that sets pump delivery, is judged to have used up its correction. GM uses it widely on gasoline direct injection: in table 25OBDG03A the pump fails to keep up for 10 s within a 12.5 s window, logged as Type A;",["High-pressure pump or its control valve sticking or worn (e.g. after heavy E85 use)","Low-pressure supply too weak or contaminated fuel","Water or corrosion in the injector or pump wiring","Rail pressure sensor reading too low"],["Reduced engine power message","Hesitation under load","Check engine light, sometimes clearing after a key cycle"],3,3,["P228D","P229A","P0087","P0089","P2C9E"],""],P228D:["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High","P228D is the opposite of P228C: measured rail pressure stays above the setpoint for too long although regulator A should be cutting delivery. GM's gasoline table 25OBDG03A flags it when the high-pressure pump supplies more than requested for 10 of 12.5 s, as Type A; its 2018 diesel table uses minus 13 MPa with the metering unit in closed loop (Type B), and table 24OBDG07 minus 3 MPa for 7 s.",["Pump control or metering valve not reducing delivery","Engine control software needing an update","Rail pressure sensor reading too high","Defective unit or high-pressure pump (truck engines)"],["Check engine light","Louder injection noise or rough idle","Reduced power in some cases"],3,3,["P228C","P229B","P0088","P0089","P2C9D"],""],P228E:["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Learning Limits - Too Low","P228E reports that the self-learned correction of fuel pressure regulator A has reached its lower bound. Ford, which still calls the part regulator 1, explains the logic in its 2023 diesel summary for the 3.0 L and 6.7 L Power Stroke: whenever requested rail pressure is at least 600 bar, the PCM keeps adapting the pressure controller, and if the adaptation factor drifts beyond a limit equivalent to roughly a 20 %…",["Rail pressure sensor characteristic drifted","Pressure regulator or metering valve worn, characteristic changed","High-pressure pump delivery deviating from its model"],["Check engine light without noticeable drivability change","Occasional rough running or slower pressure response"],3,1,["P228F","P229C","P016D","P0191","P0089"],""],P228F:["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Learning Limits - Too High","P228F is the upper counterpart of P228E: the learned correction for fuel pressure regulator A has run into its maximum. Ford's 2023 diesel summary applies one test to both codes on the 3.0 L and 6.7 L engines, with a limit near a 20 % rail pressure sensor slope error and about 10 s of monitoring at 600 bar or more.",["Dirt in the high-pressure system, e.g. via a leaking fuel filter seal","High-pressure pump worn or noisy","Rail pressure sensor characteristic drifted","Low-pressure supply restricted"],["Check engine light","Noise from the high-pressure pump","Uneven running in some cases"],3,1,["P228E","P229D","P016F","P0087","P0094"],""],P2290:["Injector Control Pressure Too Low","P2290 belongs to the injector control pressure (ICP) family of hydraulically actuated unit injector (HEUI) diesels such as the Navistar-built Ford 6.0 L Power Stroke, where pressurised engine oil fires the injectors. Ford's 2003 and 2004 summaries run the check every 8 ms with the engine running and set it once actual ICP stays more than 3.0 MPa below the PCM's command for longer than 7 s;",["Injection pressure regulator (IPR) contaminated or not sealing","Leaking high-pressure oil rail fittings, stand pipes or O-rings","Worn high-pressure oil pump","Low, wrong or aerated engine oil"],["Hard starting, especially when hot","Lack of power and rough running","Check engine light"],3,3,["P2291","P2288","P2284","P2283","P2292"],"לחץ בקרת מזרק — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2291:["Injector Control Pressure Too Low - Engine Cranking","P2291 judges pressure build-up while the starter is turning. On HEUI diesels the injectors only fire once injector control pressure has reached a minimum, so any leak in the pressurised oil circuit shows up as a long crank or a no-start; Wikipedia's Power Stroke article names a contaminated injection pressure regulator and failed high-pressure oil seals as typical no-start causes on the 6.0 L.",["Leak in the high-pressure oil (HEUI) or fuel (common rail) circuit","Injection pressure regulator or rail pressure valve not sealing","High-pressure pump delivering too little at cranking speed","Low cranking speed from a weak battery or starter"],["Engine cranks long or does not start","Starts only after repeated attempts","Check engine light after the start attempt"],3,1,["P2290","P2284","P2288","P00C6","P0087"],""],P2292:["Injector Control Pressure Erratic","P2292 describes an injector control pressure that jumps around instead of sitting steadily below or above target. No manufacturer documents its detection logic publicly: Ford's 2014 PCM code table lists the code without a MIL marking, and the 6.0 L Power Stroke summaries only describe the steady checks P2284, P2288 and P2290.",["Air in the engine oil (foaming, wrong oil, overfill)","Injection pressure regulator sticking intermittently","ICP sensor or its connector making intermittent contact","High-pressure oil pump starting to fail"],["Surging or bucking under steady throttle","Intermittent power loss","Rough idle"],3,2,["P2283","P2287","P2284","P2290","P2288"],""],P2293:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Performance","P2293 checks whether fuel pressure regulator B really controls rail pressure. In GM's 2018 diesel table regulator B is the rail pressure regulator valve; the code sets when, with that valve in charge, rail pressure rises above a calibrated ceiling of 67 to 217 MPa in 160 of 229 samples at 6.25 ms, Type A.",["Rail pressure regulator valve sticking or worn (often replaced with the rail)","Rail pressure sensor reading wrong","Contaminated fuel affecting the valve","Engine control software issue"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or stalling in severe cases","Hard starting"],3,3,["P2294","P2295","P2296","P0089","P229B"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2294:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Control Circuit/Open","P2294 is the open-circuit check of the drive line to fuel pressure regulator B. GM's 2018 diesel ECM tests the low-side driver of the rail pressure regulator valve while the output is switched off: a voltage indicating more than 200 kΩ between signal and ground counts as open, and 44 failures in 88 samples at 6.25 ms set the code as Type B.",["Broken wire in the regulator harness","Loose, corroded or pushed-back connector pin","Open coil in the pressure regulator valve","Faulty output driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or emergency mode","Unstable idle or hard starting"],2,3,["P2293","P2295","P2296","P0090"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2295:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Control Circuit Low","P2295 stands for the control line of fuel pressure regulator B touching ground. GM's 2018 diesel ECM detects it with its low-side driver switched off: if the measured voltage corresponds to 0.5 Ω or less towards ground, the sample counts as failed, and 44 of 88 samples at 6.25 ms confirm the fault as Type B.",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Water or corrosion in the regulator connector","Shorted coil in the pressure regulator valve"],["Check engine light","Rail pressure too high or unstable, reduced power","Rough running"],2,3,["P2296","P2294","P2293","P0091"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2296:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Control Circuit High","P2296 is set when the control line of fuel pressure regulator B has contact with supply voltage. GM's 2018 diesel ECM checks this with its low-side driver switched on: if the line still shows a voltage equivalent to 0.5 Ω or less towards power, the sample fails, again with 44 of 88 samples and Type B.",["Control wire shorted to a voltage supply","Damaged or corroded regulator connector","Faulty output driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Hard starting or stalling","Reduced power"],2,3,["P2295","P2294","P2293","P0092"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2297:["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P2297 concerns the upstream oxygen sensor of bank 1 and the moment when fuel is cut on deceleration and the sensor should read almost pure air. Diesel calibrations compare the reading in overrun with a modelled value: GM's 6.6L LML faults a gap between measured and calculated value above 0.06 to 0.07, the 3.0L LZ0 a deviation beyond 5 percent (Type B).",["Upstream wide-band sensor aged or drifted (wrong reading in air)","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensor drawing in outside air","Air-mass or fuel model error (MAF, injector leakage, EGR) skewing the expected value","Engine software needing an update (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Usually no noticeable change in driving behaviour","Possibly stored with P0133 or fuel-quantity codes"],1,1,["P2298","P0130","P0133","P2195","P2196","P2A00","P2237"],""],P2298:["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","P2298 is the bank 2 version of P2297 and exists only on engines with two cylinder banks, each with its own upstream oxygen sensor. Three GM tables show the two readings of the code. The 2005 3.5L V6 (L66) tests during fuel cut-off with coolant above 69 °C and below 2,200 rpm, faulting a wide-band output above 4.5 V or below 2.9 V, over two drive cycles.",["Bank 2 upstream wide-band sensor aged or contaminated","Exhaust leak on bank 2 ahead of the sensor","Damaged sensor lead or connector on bank 2"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Usually no noticeable change in driving behaviour","Bank 2 fuel trim values may look unusual"],1,1,["P2297","P0150","P0153","P2197","P2198","P2A03","P2240"],""],P2299:["Brake Pedal Position/Accelerator Pedal Position Incompatible","P2299 means the vehicle has seen the brake and the accelerator pressed together in a way it treats as implausible; engine torque is usually cut as a brake-override measure. GM documents the check in the brake control module of 2020 models with a pedal travel sensor: the code sets when the travel signal is not zero while the accelerator is applied above 4.47 mph (7.2 km/h) for 0.12 s, Type A.",["Driver resting a foot on the brake while accelerating","Control module software needing an update","Brake light switch or pedal travel sensor misadjusted or sticking","Floor mat or object keeping a pedal partly pressed"],["Engine power drops while braking and accelerating together","Check engine light","Car does not respond to the accelerator for a moment"],1,3,["P0504","P0571","P0572","P0573","P2138"],""],P229A:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low","P229A is the low-pressure control-limit check for fuel pressure regulator B. In GM's 2018 diesel table regulator B is the rail pressure regulator valve; while it governs the rail in closed loop, the ECM compares setpoint and measured pressure and flags a deficit beyond about 13 MPa, using the same 640-of-800-sample window and Type B rating as the metering unit check P228C.",["Rail pressure regulator valve leaking internally","High-pressure pump delivering too little","Excessive injector leak-off","Restricted low-pressure supply or clogged filter"],["Check engine light","Lack of power under load","Longer cranking times"],3,3,["P229B","P228C","P228B","P2293","P0087"],""],P229B:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High","P229B flags rail pressure that stays above target while fuel pressure regulator B should be holding it. GM's 2018 diesel table, where regulator B is the rail pressure regulator valve, runs this check with the valve in closed-loop control and under the same enable conditions as P229A (fuel level, ambient pressure and temperature), mirroring the overpressure test P228D of the metering unit, and rates it Type B.",["Rail pressure regulator valve sticking closed","Rail pressure sensor reading too high","Valve drive signal stuck on (wiring or module)"],["Check engine light","Harder combustion noise","Reduced power in some cases"],3,3,["P229A","P228D","P2293","P0088"],""],P229C:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Learning Limits - Too Low","P229C means the learned correction for fuel pressure regulator B has reached its lower bound. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The matching check for regulator A is described by Ford for its 2023 diesels: the controller adapts at steady rail pressure of 600 bar or more and stores P228E or P228F when the adaptation would exceed roughly a 20 % sensor-slope error.",["Rail pressure regulator valve characteristic drifted","Rail pressure sensor characteristic drifted","Adaptation values not reset after a component replacement"],["Check engine light","Usually no noticeable change in driving"],3,1,["P229D","P228E","P229A","P2293"],""],P229D:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Learning Limits - Too High","P229D reports that the learned correction for fuel pressure regulator B has climbed to its upper bound, the opposite of P229C. No manufacturer documents the code publicly, so its logic can only be inferred from the regulator A equivalent P228F: Ford's 2023 diesel summary sets that code after about 10 s when the controller adaptation passes a limit near a 20 % sensor-slope error, and Volvo and Mack link P228F on…",["Rail pressure regulator valve worn or contaminated","Rail pressure sensor characteristic drifted","Contaminated fuel reaching the high-pressure side"],["Check engine light","Occasional unstable rail pressure or rough idle"],3,1,["P229C","P228F","P229B","P2293"],""],P229E:["NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P229E is the basic electrical fault of the second NOx sensor on bank 1, the one behind the SCR catalyst that shows how much NOx survives conversion. Its attached control unit checks the probe lines and passes the result to the engine computer over CAN. GM's 6.6L Duramax (LML) sets the code as Type A when an open or shorted status keeps arriving longer than 10 s, or 0.5 s in a later calibration.",["Internal failure of the outlet NOx probe or its control unit","Damaged lead between probe and sensor control unit (heat, chafing)","Water or corrosion in the sensor connector","Engine control software needing an update (Nissan Titan XD 2016, NTB16-048)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","No valid downstream NOx value in live data","SCR warning; catalyst efficiency check cannot complete"],2,3,["P229F","P22A0","P22A1","P22A2","P220B","P2200","U029E"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P229F:["NOx Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P229F says the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 is electrically sound but its reading fails a plausibility test. Methods vary. GM's 6.6L LML waits for a burst of engine-out NOx and faults the sensor if its own value moves by less than 3 ppm (Type B); the 3.0L LZ0 watches the stability of the internal pump currents, failing above 0.5 percent unstable time.",["Outlet NOx element drifted, slow or poisoned (e.g. sodium from cleaning fluids)","Poor DEF quality or faulty dosing that distorts downstream NOx","Harness or connector fault at the outlet sensor (Volvo/Mack P229F-64)","Engine or dosing software needing an update (several FCA, Hino, Mazda notices)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Often stored together with SCR efficiency code P20EE","Downstream NOx value implausible compared with the upstream sensor"],2,1,["P229E","P22A0","P22A1","P2201","P221A","P225E","P225F","P22FE"],"חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A0:["NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A0 reports that the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 sends a raw value below the smallest figure a healthy sensor can produce. Because the sensor talks over CAN, the test looks at the transmitted number rather than a wire voltage. GM uses minus 90 ppm on the 6.6L LML, on its 2017 small diesels (table 17OBDG04) and on the 3.0L LZ0, in each case Type B after two trips with dew point reached and supply in range;",["Outlet NOx element drifted low or internally faulty","Engine software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)","Damaged lead between probe and sensor module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Live data shows a negative downstream NOx value","SCR efficiency monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P229E","P229F","P22A1","P22A2","P2202"],"חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A1:["NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A1 flags a raw value from the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 that is higher than anything plausibly left behind the SCR catalyst. GM's 6.6L LML uses 1,500 ppm, or 2,500 ppm in table 14OBDG10; the 3.0L LZ0 and the 2017 small diesels also use 2,500 ppm, Type B after two trips. VW's 2014 Touareg TDI uses 1,655 ppm or a lambda signal above 1.54.",["Outlet NOx sensor reading high due to internal damage","DEF quality or dosing problem raising real tailpipe NOx","Engine software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Implausibly high downstream NOx value in live data","SCR efficiency code P20EE stored alongside"],2,1,["P229E","P229F","P22A0","P22A2","P2203","P20EE"],"חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A2:["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A2 describes a rear NOx sensor on bank 1 whose measuring circuit reports faults that come and go rather than staying present. Smart NOx sensors pass the state of that circuit (open wire, short or no error) to the engine computer over CAN, so brief, repeated fault reports fit this code. No manufacturer publicly documents a threshold for P22A2.",["Loose or corroded terminals at the outlet NOx sensor connector","Harness along the exhaust damaged by heat or vibration","Sporadic internal fault in the sensor module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp that may go out and return","Downstream NOx value dropping out briefly","Code remains stored after the root fault is fixed"],2,1,["P229E","P22A0","P22A1","P2204","U029E"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A3:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The ceramic element of a NOx sensor measures only after its built-in heater has brought it to several hundred degrees. P22A3 reports a break on the heater control side of the rear sensor on bank 1, behind the SCR catalyst. GM's 6.6L LML sets it when the sensor reports an open heater over CAN longer than 10 s, Type A.",["Heater element in the outlet NOx probe burnt through","Broken conductor between probe and sensor module","Software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after one trip","Outlet NOx sensor never reports ready","SCR warning on the display"],2,1,["P22A4","P22A5","P22A6","P220F","P2205"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A4:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A4 means the heater control line of the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 has a short to ground, so the sensor module can no longer drive the heater as commanded. GM documents it on the 3.0L LZ0 as a ground short on the heater control pin, judged once dew point is reached and sensor supply exceeds 9.9 V, 80 failures in 160 samples, Type B after two trips.",["Heater element or probe lead shorted to ground inside the sensor","Probe lead insulation chafed against the exhaust or body","Software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Outlet NOx sensor stays not ready","SCR warning on the display"],2,1,["P22A3","P22A5","P22A6","P2206"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A5:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A5 is the opposite of P22A4: the heater control line of the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 has a short to supply voltage. The sensor module then cannot switch or regulate the heater, and the element risks running too hot or the module shuts the heater off to protect it.",["Heater circuit inside the sensor shorted to supply voltage","Probe lead or connector touching a powered conductor","Software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Heater switched off, outlet NOx sensor not ready","SCR warning on the display"],2,1,["P22A3","P22A4","P22A6","P2207"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A6:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","Besides the heater supply, a NOx sensor has a sense line through which its module measures the resistance of the heated element and so infers its temperature. P22A6 reports an electrical fault on that feedback line of the rear sensor on bank 1. GM's 3.0L LZ0 sets it for an open circuit at the HTemp pin, 80 failures in 160 samples, Type A after one trip;",["Open heater sense conductor inside the outlet NOx probe or its lead","Water or corrosion in the probe connector","Software anomaly (GM 3.0L LZ0 2024, bulletin 24-NA-094)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after one trip","Outlet NOx sensor not ready, no downstream value","SCR warning on the display"],2,1,["P22A7","P22A8","P22A9","P22AA","P22A3","P2208"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A7:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A7 means the heater feedback of the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 shows a heater that does not reach or hold its target, although no open or short is found. GM's 3.0L LZ0 and 2017 small diesels compare the measured heater resistance with its target once supply has been in range for 45 s and dew point passed 180 s ago (Type B); the 6.6L LML fails the sensor if its heater never reports set-point temperature.",["Aged heater or element in the outlet NOx probe","Water in the NOx sensor connectors (Ford 6.7L 2017-2020, TSB 20-2067)","Harness chafed on the EGR cooler with blown supply fuse (Ford 6.7L 2023)","Weak supply to the sensor module limiting heater power"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Outlet NOx sensor becomes ready late or not at all","Often stored with U029E or other NOx sensor codes"],2,1,["P22A6","P22A8","P22A9","P22AA","P220F","P2209","U029E"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A8:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A8 means the heater sense line of the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 is shorted to ground; the sensor module uses that line to read the element temperature via its resistance. With that line pulled to ground, the module sees a temperature value it cannot trust and cannot regulate the heater properly.",["Heater sense conductor shorted to ground inside the probe","Probe lead insulation damaged against exhaust or body","Water bridging pins in the probe connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Outlet NOx sensor not ready","SCR efficiency check does not run"],2,1,["P22A6","P22A7","P22A9","P22AA","P2210"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22A9:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22A9 is the high-side twin of P22A8: the heater sense line of the rear NOx sensor on bank 1 has a short to supply voltage. The module then reads an element resistance that is far off and loses its temperature feedback, so it cannot hold the probe at working temperature.",["Heater sense conductor shorted to supply inside the probe","Probe lead touching another powered conductor","Water bridging pins in the probe connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Outlet NOx sensor not ready","SCR warning on the display"],2,1,["P22A6","P22A7","P22A8","P22AA","P2211"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22AA:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22AA covers a heater sense line on the rear NOx sensor of bank 1 that fails only now and then. The module uses this line to read the element temperature and keep the heater on target; if the reading drops out or jumps for short moments, the temperature control briefly loses its reference and the sensor may fall out of its ready state.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the probe connector","Lead near the exhaust cracked by heat or vibration","Intermittent internal contact fault in the probe"],["Malfunction indicator lamp that may come and go","Outlet NOx sensor intermittently not ready"],2,1,["P22A6","P22A7","P22A8","P22A9","P2212"],"חישת גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22AB:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22AB reports a break in the positive current control line of a wide-band probe mounted behind the catalyst or, on diesels, further down the aftertreatment on bank 1. On a Bosch-style five-wire probe this is the pump-current lead (IP/APE) through which the controller moves oxygen into or out of the pump cell.",["Corroded, loose or poorly crimped terminal in the sensor or sensor-module connector","Pump-current wire broken or chafed through along the exhaust","Internal open circuit in the downstream wide-band sensor"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen reading frozen or missing in live data","Related catalyst or aftertreatment monitors stay incomplete"],2,1,["P22AC","P22AD","P22AE","P22B2","P22B5","P22B8","P2237"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22AC:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22AC means the pump-current (positive current) line of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe reads below its allowed window, usually because the wire touches ground or its insulation has worn through. GM includes the code in bulletin 21-NA-149 for 2019-2022 light-duty trucks and SUVs with the 3.0 Duramax LM2, where chafed engine wiring triggers a long list of faults; no public GM table gives a threshold.",["Pump-current wire chafed against the body or exhaust and shorted to ground","Internal short in the downstream wide-band sensor","Water or contamination bridging the connector pins"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen value pinned at an extreme in live data","Possible failed emissions inspection because monitors are not ready"],2,1,["P22AB","P22AD","P22B9","P2238","P22B3"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22AD:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22AD is the high-side fault on the positive current control line of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe: the pump-current wire is pulled above its expected level, for example by contact with the heater feed or another supply wire. On Saab's 2010 9-5 the pump-current pins measure roughly 2.8 V at the plug, which gives a feel for the normal bias.",["Pump-current wire shorted to the heater supply or another positive feed","Internal short between heater and pump cell in the sensor","Faulty sensor interface in the ECM or sensor module"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen reading implausibly high or fixed","Readiness monitors for catalyst or aftertreatment not completed"],2,1,["P22AB","P22AC","P22BA","P2239","P22B4"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22AE:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22AE points to an open reference voltage line of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe, i.e. the lead of the Nernst (sensing) cell, called RE/UN by Bosch and VS by NTK. Through it the controller reads the cell voltage it regulates the pump current against, so a break leaves the oxygen value meaningless. Chrysler lists P22AE for 2010-2012 Ram 2500/3500 with the 6.7 Cummins;",["Corroded or wrongly plated terminals in the sensor or sensor-module connector","Broken Nernst-cell wire in the harness","Cracked or aged sensing cell with very high internal resistance"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen or lambda value invalid in live data","Other downstream sensor codes may be stored at the same time"],2,1,["P22AF","P22B0","P22B1","P22AB","P22B2","P22BB","P2243"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22AF:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22AF is a plausibility fault on the Nernst-cell (reference voltage) side of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe: the wiring is intact, but the cell signal does not behave as the controller expects, for instance it cannot be held at its set point or drifts.",["Aged downstream wide-band sensor with raised cell resistance","Soot, oil or coolant deposits on the sensing element","Weak heater or heater control that leaves the element too cold","High-resistance contact in the Nernst-cell circuit"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen reading sluggish or offset compared with the upstream sensor","Catalyst or aftertreatment monitor may report errors as a follow-up"],2,1,["P22AE","P22B0","P22B1","P22BC","P2244","P0141"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B0:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22B0 says the reference voltage (Nernst-cell) line of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe sits below its permitted range. On a Bosch LSU the Nernst cell is a high-impedance source that tolerates at most about 250 microamps, so a chafed wire touching ground drags it down at once. No maker documents this exact code publicly.",["Nernst-cell wire shorted to ground through damaged insulation","Internal short in the downstream wide-band sensor","Moisture in the connector creating a leakage path"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen value implausible or unavailable"],2,1,["P22AE","P22AF","P22B1","P22BD","P2245"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B1:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22B1 is set when the reference voltage (Nernst-cell) line of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe reads above its valid range. Because the cell delivers only a few hundred millivolts across about 300 ohms, any contact with the heater feed or another live wire overrides it. A cracked ceramic letting the heater circuit leak into the cell can do the same. No maker publishes this code with a threshold;",["Nernst-cell wire shorted to the heater supply or another live wire","Cracked sensor ceramic leaking heater voltage into the cell","Faulty sensor interface in the ECM or sensor module"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen reading stuck at a limit"],2,1,["P22AE","P22AF","P22B0","P22BE","P2246"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B2:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22B2 indicates an open negative current control line on the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe. This is the shared return of pump and sensing cell, the virtual ground (VM/IPN on Bosch, COM on NTK), which the controller holds at a mid-level bias of around 2.5 V. Chrysler lists the code for 2010-2012 Ram 2500/3500 with the 6.7 Cummins and repairs connectors and wiring first;",["Loose, corroded or pushed-back terminal on the return wire","Return (virtual ground) wire broken in the harness","Internal open circuit in the downstream wide-band sensor"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen reading frozen near a fixed value","Aftertreatment readiness not set"],2,1,["P22B3","P22B4","P22AB","P22AE","P22BF","P2251"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B3:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22B3 reports the negative current control line, i.e. the virtual ground of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe, as too low. Normally the controller lifts this common return to a bias near 2.5 V (Saab measures that at the plug of its 2010 9-5) so that pump current can flow in both directions; a short to chassis ground collapses the bias and with it the measuring range. No maker documents this exact code publicly.",["Return wire shorted to chassis ground through chafed insulation","Internal short inside the wide-band sensor","Faulty bias supply in the ECM or sensor module"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen value implausible or pinned"],2,1,["P22B2","P22B4","P22C0","P2252","P22AC"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B4:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22B4 is stored when the negative current control line (virtual ground) of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe climbs above its intended bias. Because this return sits at a mid-level voltage rather than at chassis ground, a short to the heater feed or battery voltage is the classic trigger, sometimes via moisture or a heat-damaged connector. No maker documents this exact code publicly;",["Return wire shorted to heater supply or battery voltage","Heat-damaged or wet connector bridging pins","Internal heater-to-cell leakage in the sensor"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen reading erratic or at a limit"],2,1,["P22B2","P22B3","P22C1","P2253","P22AD"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B5:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22B5 flags an open trim line on the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe. Bosch LSU probes carry a trimming resistor in the connector module, wired to pin 5 (RT/IA), that sets each sensor's individual characteristic; the controller reads it to scale the measured pump current. Lose that line and the oxygen value can still move, but with the wrong gain.",["Corroded or loose trim-line terminal in the sensor connector","Trim wire broken between sensor connector and ECM or sensor module","Open trimming resistor in the sensor's connector module"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen reading disagrees with the upstream sensor during fuel cut-off","Follow-up aftertreatment or catalyst faults possible"],2,1,["P22B6","P22B7","P22C2","P2626","P22AB"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B6:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","By its name P22B6 is the low fault on the trim line of the bank 1 downstream wide-band probe, i.e. the lead to the calibration resistor in a Bosch-style sensor connector. GM's diesel tables use the slot differently: they set it when the oxygen value reported by the second NOx sensor falls below its physical minimum, less than -4 % in 200 of 250 samples in the 2016 table, with the engine in combustion mode and no NOx…",["Faulty downstream NOx/oxygen sensor delivering an impossible oxygen value","Leaking charge-air cooler ducting (GM 6.6 L5P)","Trim or signal wire shorted to ground in the harness"],["Check engine light","Negative oxygen percentage shown for the downstream sensor in live data","Possible additional boost or air-flow codes when charge air leaks"],2,1,["P22B5","P22B7","P22C3","P2627"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B7:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22B7 is, going by its title, the high fault on the trim circuit belonging to bank 1's downstream wide-band probe. In GM's diesel tables (2016, 2018 and 2025 group 04) the code is a ceiling test on the oxygen value of the second NOx sensor: the 2016 table flags readings above 24 %, which is more oxygen than fresh air holds, in 100 of 200 samples.",["Faulty downstream NOx/oxygen sensor reporting excess oxygen","Chafed engine harness affecting the sensor lines (GM 3.0 LM2)","Trim or signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine light","Downstream oxygen value above 21 % in live data"],2,1,["P22B5","P22B6","P22C4","P2628"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P22B8:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22B8 is the bank 2 version of an open positive current control line on a downstream wide-band probe: the pump-current wire (IP/APE on Bosch) of the sensor behind the catalyst or aftertreatment on the second cylinder bank has lost continuity. It only exists on engines with two exhaust banks and a wide-band probe after each catalyst, which is rare. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Loose or corroded pump-current terminal in the sensor connector","Pump-current wire broken near the hot exhaust","Internal open circuit in the bank 2 downstream sensor"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen value missing or frozen"],2,1,["P22B9","P22BA","P22BB","P22AB","P2240"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22B9:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22B9 means the positive current control (pump-current) line of the bank 2 downstream wide-band probe reads below its allowed band, most often because the lead has worn through and touches ground.",["Pump-current wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Internal short in the bank 2 downstream sensor","Water in the connector"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen value at an extreme"],2,1,["P22B8","P22BA","P22AC","P2241"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22BA:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22BA is set when the pump-current (positive current control) wire of the bank 2 downstream wide-band probe is held above its normal bias, typically through contact with the heater supply or a damaged connector letting battery voltage in. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Pump-current wire shorted to the heater feed or battery voltage","Heater-to-pump-cell leakage inside the sensor","Faulty sensor interface in the ECM"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen value implausibly high"],2,1,["P22B8","P22B9","P22AD","P2242"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22BB:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22BB reports an open reference voltage line on the bank 2 downstream wide-band probe, meaning the controller has lost the Nernst-cell signal (RE/UN on Bosch, VS on NTK) it needs to regulate pump current and compute oxygen content. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Corroded or loose Nernst-cell terminal in the connector","Reference wire broken in the harness","Cracked sensing cell or internal open in the sensor"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen value invalid"],2,1,["P22BC","P22BD","P22BE","P22B8","P22AE","P2247"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22BC:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22BC concerns the plausibility of the Nernst-cell signal of the wide-band probe fitted after the bank 2 catalyst. The leads test fine, yet the cell voltage that the controller uses as its set point drifts, reacts slowly or cannot be held, so the computed oxygen value loses credibility. No maker documents this code publicly, and none publishes a limit for its upstream relative P2248 either.",["Aged downstream wide-band sensor on bank 2 with raised Nernst-cell resistance","Oil, coolant or additive deposits on the sensing element","Heater output too low to keep the cell at working temperature","Contact resistance in the Nernst-cell terminal"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen reading lags behind or is offset from the other sensors","Catalyst monitor for bank 2 does not complete"],2,1,["P22BB","P22BD","P22BE","P22AF","P2248"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22BD:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22BD reports that the Nernst-cell (reference voltage) lead of the bank 2 post-catalyst wide-band probe sits below its valid window. Bosch allows the cell a load of only about 250 microamps, so a lead whose insulation touches ground, or moisture bridging the plug, pulls the signal down quickly. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Nernst-cell lead chafed through and touching ground","Water or corrosion creating a leakage path in the connector","Sensing element cracked by water contact on the hot probe"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen value missing or at the lower end in live data"],2,1,["P22BB","P22BC","P22BE","P22B0","P2249"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22BE:["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22BE is stored when the reference voltage lead of the bank 2 downstream wide-band probe carries more voltage than a working Nernst cell can produce. A healthy cell produces well under one volt from a source of roughly 300 ohms, so contact with the heater feed, a 5 V line or battery voltage swamps it, and a cracked ceramic can let heater potential leak into the cell. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Nernst-cell lead shorted to the heater supply or another live wire","Cracked ceramic letting heater voltage into the sensing cell","Faulty sensor interface in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen reading pinned at the upper limit","Heater codes for the same sensor may appear alongside"],2,1,["P22BB","P22BC","P22BD","P22B1","P2250"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22BF:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22BF means the negative current control lead of the bank 2 post-catalyst wide-band probe has lost continuity. That lead is the common return of pump and Nernst cell (VM/IPN on Bosch, COM on NTK); without it neither cell has a reference and the signal freezes near its bias. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Loose, corroded or pushed-out terminal on the return wire","Return wire broken by heat or vibration near the exhaust","Internal break in the sensor lead or element"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream oxygen value frozen at a constant reading","Further codes for the same sensor may be stored together"],2,1,["P22C0","P22C1","P22BB","P22B2","P2254"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22C0:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22C0 flags the negative current control line (virtual ground) of the bank 2 downstream wide-band probe as too low. The controller deliberately lifts this return above chassis ground, around 2.5 V on Saab's 2010 9-5, which lets the pump cell be driven both ways; once the wire touches ground, that bias and the lean side of the measuring range disappear. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Return wire chafed against body or exhaust bracket, shorted to ground","Internal short from the sensor return to the housing","Faulty bias supply in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream reading cannot show lean values","Readiness for catalyst and oxygen sensor monitors stays open"],2,1,["P22BF","P22C1","P22B3","P2255","P2252"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22C1:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22C1 covers a return line (virtual ground) reading too high on the bank 2 post-catalyst wide-band probe: the line is pushed above the mid-level bias the controller sets, which in practice means contact with the heater supply or battery voltage, often via a melted or wet connector. With the reference raised, the rich side of the scale is lost and the oxygen value becomes useless.",["Return wire touching the heater feed or another positive supply","Heat-damaged or wet connector bridging the return to a live pin","Internal leakage from heater to sensing cells inside the probe"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream reading stuck high or implausible"],2,1,["P22BF","P22C0","P22B4","P2256","P2253"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22C2:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit/Open (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22C2 reports an open trim line on the bank 2 downstream wide-band probe. Every probe ships with a calibration resistor in its plug (pin 5, RT/IA on a Bosch LSU) that corrects for spread in its diffusion gap; on Bosch probes it sits in parallel with the controller's sense resistor.",["Corroded or loose trim-resistor terminal in the sensor plug","Trim resistor or its lead open inside the sensor connector","Trim wire broken between connector and control module"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream lambda reads slightly off, most visibly away from lambda 1"],2,1,["P22C3","P22C4","P22B5","P2629"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22C3:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22C3 is the low fault on the trim (label resistor) circuit of the bank 2 post-catalyst wide-band probe. Ford's 2012 OBD summary shows how makers can read this for NTK probes: at each key-on the controller switches the heater off, samples a voltage divider and estimates the label resistor; a value too high is taken as a broken or grounded lead and sets the trim-low code (P2630 for the bank 2 front probe).",["Trim wire chafed and shorted to ground","High-resistance or corroded trim terminal raising the measured resistance","Defective label resistor in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light","Code typically appears right after engine start"],2,1,["P22C2","P22C4","P22B6","P2630"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22C4:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P22C4 is the high fault on the trim circuit of the bank 2 downstream wide-band probe. In Ford's key-on check of NTK label resistors, an estimated resistance that is too low means the line is shorted to power, which sets the trim-high code (P2631 for the bank 2 front probe); the stored resistor rank then stays in use.",["Trim wire shorted to the heater supply or another positive feed","Heat- or water-damaged sensor plug bridging the trim pin","Internally shorted label resistor in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 downstream lambda slightly off; heater codes may accompany it"],2,1,["P22C2","P22C3","P22B7","P2631"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P22C5:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Valve Control Circuit/Open","P22C5 flags an open or broken drive circuit for the turbocharger compressor outlet valve. That valve sits in the charge-air path downstream of a compressor and decides whether this compressor feeds the engine, for example in register or two-stage charging or next to an electric auxiliary compressor.",["Valve connector loose, unplugged or corroded","Broken wire in the valve harness, often near hot turbo parts","Open actuator coil inside the compressor outlet valve","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power because boost is limited","Weak or delayed pull at the speed where the second boost path should join"],2,3,["P22C6","P22C7","P22C8","P22C9","P22CA"],"שסתום יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22C6:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Valve Control Circuit Low","P22C6 is stored when the control line of the compressor outlet valve sits at a voltage that is too low for the current command, which normally points to a short to ground somewhere between the module and the valve. Whether the valve then stays permanently energized or never moves depends on whether the engine control module switches the ground side or the supply side of the coil.",["Control wire chafed through and touching ground","Internal short in the valve actuator coil","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the connector","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on soon after starting","Boost limited, engine feels flat under load","Possible blown fuse if the short pulls heavy current"],2,3,["P22C5","P22C7","P22CB"],"שסתום יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22C7:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Valve Control Circuit High","P22C7 means the drive line of the compressor outlet valve reads higher than the module expects, typically because the wire has a short to battery voltage or the coil draws excessive current while the driver is on. Modern output stages notice the overcurrent and switch off to protect themselves, so the valve then stops responding even though nothing is open.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Shorted turns in the valve coil causing overcurrent","Replacement valve with unsuitable coil resistance","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Valve no longer switches, boost reduced","Code returns immediately after clearing"],2,3,["P22C5","P22C6","P22CC"],"שסתום יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22C8:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Valve Stuck Open","P22C8 is a functional fault: the compressor outlet valve stays open at a moment when the control strategy expects it shut, so pressure or airflow in the boost path does not follow the command. Mercedes-Benz uses it on the M256.8 inline six with its 48-volt electric auxiliary compressor.",["Check valve in the charge-air pipe jammed (Mercedes M256)","Oil film or deposits holding the valve flap open","Actuator or linkage no longer able to close the valve"],["Check engine light on","Little or poor power output","Boost builds poorly or unevenly"],2,3,["P22C9","P22C5","P22CD","P0299"],"שסתום יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P22C9:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Valve Stuck Closed","P22C9 says the compressor outlet valve did not open when commanded, so air from the compressor it controls cannot reach the engine and the expected boost is missing. Mercedes-Benz documents the code for the M256.8 six-cylinder: the first version of bulletin LI09.41-P-078735 (December 2024) covers P22C900 in the MRG3 engine control unit on models from 2019 to 2025 and traces it to a check valve in the charge-air pipe…",["Check valve in the charge-air pipe jammed shut (Mercedes M256)","Valve actuator, vacuum or pressure supply unable to open the valve","Valve seized by deposits or corrosion"],["Check engine light on","Noticeable loss of power under load","Boost malfunction, possibly with underboost code"],2,3,["P22C8","P22C5","P22CE","P0299"],"שסתום יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — תקוע במצב סגור"],P22CA:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Switching Valve Control Circuit/Open","P22CA reports an open drive circuit for the compressor outlet switching valve. In two-stage or register boost systems the outlet flap is often moved by vacuum or pressure, and this electrically driven switching valve decides when that actuating medium reaches it; Ford's two-stage patent notes such valves may be worked electrically or by vacuum.",["Switching valve connector loose or corroded","Broken wire between module and switching valve","Open coil in the switching solenoid","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Boost changeover no longer happens, power limited","Hesitation when accelerating through the switching speed"],1,3,["P22CB","P22CC","P22CD","P22CE","P22C5"],"שסתום מיתוג יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22CB:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Switching Valve Control Circuit Low","P22CB is set when the control line of the compressor outlet switching valve shows too little voltage for the present command, most often because the wire or the solenoid has a short to ground. On a low-side driven solenoid such a short can hold the valve energized all the time, so the outlet flap it supplies with vacuum or pressure stays in its switched position whatever the rpm and load.",["Control wire chafed and shorted to ground","Internal short in the switching solenoid","Water or corrosion in the solenoid connector"],["Check engine light on","Boost path stuck in one mode, uneven power across the rev range","Reduced power at low or high engine speed"],1,3,["P22CA","P22CC","P22C6"],"שסתום מיתוג יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22CC:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Switching Valve Control Circuit High","P22CC indicates that the drive line of the compressor outlet switching valve carries more voltage or current than allowed, usually a short to a battery feed or a solenoid with shorted windings. The output stage of the engine control module then tends to shut down for self-protection, which leaves the switching valve unpowered and the outlet flap in its rest position.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Shorted windings in the switching solenoid","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Outlet flap no longer switches, power reduced","Fault returns as soon as the valve is commanded"],1,3,["P22CA","P22CB","P22C7"],"שסתום מיתוג יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22CD:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Switching Valve Stuck Open","P22CD is a plausibility fault: the engine control module commanded the compressor outlet switching valve shut, yet boost pressure, airflow or a position signal behave as if the switched path were still open. Because the switching valve feeds the actuator of the outlet flap, a mechanically stuck solenoid, a leaking control hose or a flap held open by the actuator all lead to the same result.",["Switching solenoid mechanically stuck in the open position","Leaking, cracked or swapped control hose to the flap actuator","Outlet flap or its actuator unable to close"],["Check engine light on","Sluggish boost build-up at low engine speed","Hissing or whistling noise from the intake side"],2,3,["P22CE","P22CA","P22C8","P0299"],"שסתום מיתוג יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P22CE:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Switching Valve Stuck Closed","P22CE is set when the compressor outlet switching valve was told to open but the boost system shows no sign that the switched path changed over. Nissan documents the code as TC Outlet Switching Valve Stuck Closed for the 2016 Titan XD with the Cummins 5.0 litre V8 diesel and its two-stage turbocharger.",["Engine control software reacting wrongly in cold weather (Nissan Titan XD bulletin)","Collapsed, kinked or frozen control hose to the outlet flap actuator","Switching solenoid stuck in the closed position","Insufficient vacuum or pressure supply for the actuator"],["Check engine light on, mostly in cold weather","Hesitation when accelerating until the engine is warm","Weak pull in the speed range where the second stage should help"],2,3,["P22CD","P22CA","P22C9","P0299"],"שסתום מיתוג יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — תקוע במצב סגור"],P22CF:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Control Circuit/Open","P22CF points to an open drive circuit of the turbocharger turbine inlet valve, the exhaust-side valve that either lets gas skip the small first-stage turbine of a series two-stage system or isolates a second turbine in a parallel-sequential layout. GM's diesel OBD tables (17OBDG04 and 18OBDG04) group P22CF, P22D0 and P22D1 as the faults of the high-pressure turbine bypass actuator (HTB);",["Actuator connector loose, heat-damaged or corroded","Broken wire near the exhaust manifold or turbo","Open winding in the turbine valve actuator or its control solenoid","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, boost control in fallback mode","Turbo lag or a missing second-stage push"],2,3,["P22D0","P22D1","P22D2","P22D3","P22D4","P0033"],"שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22D0:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Control Circuit Low","P22D0 is logged when the drive circuit of the turbine inlet valve shows a voltage below the expected range, the classic sign of a short to ground in the wire or inside the actuator. GM lists P22D0 together with P22CF and P22D1 in the fault bundle of its high-pressure turbine bypass actuator in the 2017 and 2018 diesel OBD documents; any of them takes boost control out of closed loop.",["Heat-damaged wire rubbing through to ground","Internal short in the valve actuator or control solenoid","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Power limited, boost too low or uneven","Code sets right after start without a test drive"],2,3,["P22CF","P22D1","P22D6"],"שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22D1:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Control Circuit High","P22D1 tells you the drive circuit of the turbine inlet valve reads too high, which usually means a short to battery voltage or an actuator that draws overcurrent. GM assigns P22D1, along with P22CF and P22D0, to its high-pressure turbine bypass actuator in the 2017 and 2018 diesel OBD tables, and boost control drops out of closed loop when the fault is active.",["Actuator wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Actuator winding shorted or mechanically jammed, drawing overcurrent","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, boost control in fallback mode","Fault comes back as soon as the valve is driven"],2,3,["P22CF","P22D0","P22D7"],"שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22D2:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Stuck Open","P22D2 means the turbine inlet valve stays open after the module asked it to close. In a series two-stage system, an open valve lets exhaust skip the small high-pressure turbine, so low-speed boost and response suffer.",["Soot or corrosion seizing the valve shaft in the open position","Leaking or detached control line on a vacuum-operated actuator","Actuator or linkage unable to close the valve","Position sensor reporting open although the valve moved"],["Check engine light on","Noticeable turbo lag at low engine speed","Higher fuel consumption","Reduced power mode"],3,3,["P22D3","P22CF","P22D5","P0299"],"שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P22D3:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Stuck Closed","P22D3 is stored when the turbine inlet valve does not open on command. In a series two-stage layout all exhaust must then pass the small high-pressure stage even at high load, raising back-pressure and risking overboost or turbo overspeed, so the module caps power. In a parallel-sequential layout the second turbo never comes in.",["Valve seized closed by soot or corrosion","Engine software setting the code falsely (Jeep Cherokee 2026 bulletin)","Actuator, linkage or vacuum supply unable to open the valve"],["Check engine light on","Power capped at higher engine speed and load","Possible overboost code alongside"],3,3,["P22D2","P22CF","P22D5","P0234","P0299"],"שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — תקוע במצב סגור"],P22D4:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Position Sensor Circuit","P22D4 is the general circuit fault of the sensor that reports how far the turbine inlet valve is open. Engineering literature explains why this valve, unlike most compressor bypass valves, has feedback: a Ford two-stage patent calls the high-pressure turbine bypass valve emissions-critical and therefore actively controlled with a position sensor, and a GM patent uses the measured opening to run the valve in position…",["Loose, heat-damaged or corroded sensor connector","Damaged sensor wiring near the turbo","Failed position sensor, often integrated in the actuator"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, turbo valve held in a fallback position"],2,3,["P22D5","P22D6","P22D7","P22D8","P22CF"],"חיישן מצב שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P22D5:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P22D5 is a plausibility fault of the turbine inlet valve position signal. The voltage stays inside its electrical limits, yet it does not match what the module expects, for instance the reading lags the commanded position, fails to reach the learned end stops or does not change when the valve is moved. CARB requires input sensors of this kind to be checked for rationality as well as for circuit faults.",["Valve or linkage sluggish from soot, so position lags the command","Position sensor drifting or misaligned on the actuator","End positions not relearned after actuator replacement"],["Check engine light on","Jerky or delayed changeover between turbo stages","Boost fluctuates under steady throttle"],2,3,["P22D4","P22D2","P22D3","P22D6","P22D7"],"חיישן מצב שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P22D6:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Position Sensor Circuit Low","P22D6 is set when the position sensor signal of the turbine inlet valve falls below its lowest valid voltage. Position sensors on such actuators normally work on a 5-volt reference with a signal that never reaches the rails in normal use, so a reading near zero means a lost reference, a signal wire shorted to ground or an internal sensor fault rather than a real valve position.",["5-volt reference open or pulled down by another shorted sensor","Signal wire shorted to ground","Internal failure of the position sensor"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, valve in fallback position","Other sensor codes on the same reference circuit possible"],2,3,["P22D4","P22D7","P22D5","P22D8"],"חיישן מצב שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — אות נמוך במעגל"],P22D7:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Position Sensor Circuit High","P22D7 is logged when the position signal of the turbine inlet valve rises above its highest valid voltage. A reading pinned near the reference level usually comes from an open sensor ground, a signal wire touching the 5-volt reference or battery voltage, or a failed sensor element, not from the valve itself.",["Open or high-resistance sensor ground","Signal wire shorted to the 5-volt reference or battery voltage","Internal failure of the position sensor"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, valve held in fallback position"],2,3,["P22D4","P22D6","P22D5","P22D8"],"חיישן מצב שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — אות גבוה במעגל"],P22D8:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P22D8 covers short dropouts or jumps in the position signal of the turbine inlet valve: the value leaps faster than the valve could physically move, or briefly disappears and returns. Such patterns typically come from a connector with fretting contacts, a wire breaking inside its insulation near the vibrating, hot turbo, or a sensor that fails under heat.",["Loose or fretting contacts in the sensor connector","Wire breaking intermittently from heat and vibration","Position sensor dropping out when hot"],["Check engine light on, sometimes only now and then","Boost surging or hunting","Brief loss of power on rough roads"],2,3,["P22D4","P22D5","P22D6","P22D7"],"חיישן מצב שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P22D9:["Cylinder 1 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","P22D9 reports a broken control circuit at the gas injector of cylinder 1, the solenoid that meters CNG or LPG into the intake port whenever a bi-fuel or dedicated gas engine runs on the alternative fuel. The driver stage notices the break because no current flows when it switches on, or because the expected off-state voltage on its pin is missing.",["Open solenoid winding in the cylinder 1 gas injector","Loose, corroded or unplugged connector at the gas injector","Broken wire or failed splice in the gas system harness","Defective driver stage in the gas or engine control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Engine changes back to gasoline or refuses to switch to gas","Misfire on cylinder 1 in gas mode (dedicated engines)"],2,3,["P22DA","P22DB","P22DC","P22DD","P0201","P0301"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 1 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22DA:["Cylinder 1 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","P22DA means the cylinder 1 gas injector control wire reads too low. TransEco Energy's DTC list for its CNG control module (AFCM v1.4) blames either a grounded wire or an open line, turns on the MIL in bi-fuel installations and reacts the same way it would to the matching gasoline injector fault. Ford's 2014 OBD code list carries P22DA as a MIL code as well.",["Control wire of the cylinder 1 gas injector chafed through to ground","Interrupted control wire or connector (logged as Low by some modules)","Water or corrosion in the injector connector","Faulty output stage in the gas control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Very rough running on cylinder 1 in gas mode, possibly rich misfire","Gas system switches back to gasoline"],2,3,["P22D9","P22DB","P22DC","P22DE","P0261","P0301"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 1 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22DB:["Cylinder 1 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","P22DB flags a control circuit of the cylinder 1 gas injector that stays too high. TransEco Energy's AFCM fault list traces it to a short to battery voltage, lights the MIL for bi-fuel use and applies the same fallback as for the gasoline injector fault; Ford's 2014 code list also marks P22DB for the MIL.",["Control wire shorted to battery or injector supply voltage","Shorted turns in the cylinder 1 gas injector coil","Output stage of the gas control module damaged"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Lean misfire on cylinder 1 in gas mode, often with P0301","Engine runs normally on gasoline"],2,3,["P22D9","P22DA","P22DC","P22DF","P0262","P0301"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 1 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22DC:["Cylinder 1 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","P22DC is meant for a cylinder 1 gas injector whose circuit is electrically intact but whose response looks wrong, such as a current trace that never reaches its peak or does not fall back to the hold level, or a coil whose resistance has drifted.",["Cylinder 1 gas injector sticking from oil residue or debris in the gas","Injector coil resistance outside its specification","Weak supply voltage to the injector bank","Injector of the wrong type or impedance installed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Uneven running in gas mode, misfire counts on cylinder 1","Higher gas consumption or switch back to gasoline"],2,3,["P22D9","P22DA","P22DB","P22E0","P0201","P0301"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 1 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22DD:["Cylinder 2 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","P22DD signals an interruption in the circuit of the cylinder 2 gas injector. On many systems that circuit is not driven by the engine computer: Ford's 2003 bi-fuel CNG trucks used a separate alternative fuel control module holding drivers for both injector sets, with heavier stages for the gas injectors because they draw more current.",["Burnt-out or open coil in the cylinder 2 gas injector","Connector at the cylinder 2 injector loose or pulled off","Wire break between gas control module and injector","Failed injector driver in the separate gas control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Gas mode not available or ends shortly after switching","Misfire on cylinder 2 when running on gas"],2,3,["P22DE","P22DF","P22E0","P22D9","P0202","P0302"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 2 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22DE:["Cylinder 2 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","P22DE stands for a control line of the cylinder 2 gas injector whose voltage is too low. TransEco Energy's AFCM fault table blames a grounded or interrupted wire and turns on the MIL for bi-fuel vehicles; Ford's 2014 OBD code list includes P22DE as a MIL code too.",["Cylinder 2 injector control wire grounded on engine or body","Open wire or pin, reported as Low by modules like the TransEco AFCM","Shorted output transistor in the gas control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rich misfire or fouled spark plug on cylinder 2 in gas mode","Gas operation interrupted, engine runs on gasoline"],2,3,["P22DD","P22DF","P22E0","P22DA","P0264","P0302"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 2 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22DF:["Cylinder 2 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","P22DF indicates that the control circuit of the cylinder 2 gas injector reads high, which TransEco Energy's AFCM table attributes to a short to power; MIL on for bi-fuel use. Ford's 2014 code list likewise flags P22DF for the MIL. A line stuck at supply voltage keeps the injector closed, so cylinder 2 burns no gas and misfires lean, while running on gasoline is unaffected.",["Cylinder 2 control wire touching a live supply wire","Internal short in the cylinder 2 gas injector coil","Driver protection in the control module tripping due to a fault"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Cylinder 2 misfires only on gas","Unexpected return to gasoline"],2,3,["P22DD","P22DE","P22E0","P22DB","P0265","P0302"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 2 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22E0:["Cylinder 2 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","P22E0 covers a cylinder 2 gas injector circuit that passes the plain open and short checks yet responds outside its expected window. California's OBD regulation asks for output components to be checked not only for circuit faults but also for a proper functional response; for alternate-fueled vehicles from 2004 to 2018 the gasoline rules applied unchanged, and from 2019 the maker submits its own monitoring plan.",["Cylinder 2 gas injector opening or closing too slowly","Coil resistance of the injector out of tolerance","Driver stage or supply unable to provide the required current"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Uneven idle on gas, cylinder 2 misfire counts","Fuel trim drifts in gas mode"],2,3,["P22DD","P22DE","P22DF","P22DC","P0202","P0302"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 2 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22E1:["Cylinder 3 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","P22E1 marks an open control circuit at the cylinder 3 gas injector. Circuit continuity checks of this kind run all the time: California's OBD rule defines continuous monitoring as always enabled with at least two samples per second, so a break is caught within moments once the gas system is in use. No maker documents P22E1 openly.",["Cylinder 3 injector connector left off or not latched after service","Open coil in the cylinder 3 gas injector","Wire broken where the harness runs along the gas rail"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Gas mode switches off soon after changeover","Cylinder 3 misfire on dedicated gas engines"],2,3,["P22E2","P22E3","P22E4","P22DD","P0203","P0303"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 3 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22E2:["Cylinder 3 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","P22E2 is logged when the control circuit of the cylinder 3 gas injector reads low. In TransEco Energy's AFCM table the cause column says shorted to ground or open, the MIL comes on in bi-fuel systems and the reaction copies that for a gasoline injector fault. Ford's 2014 code list lists P22E2 as a MIL code. Because a grounded control wire can leave the injector energized, cylinder 3 may be flooded with gas;",["Cylinder 3 control wire rubbed through against a bracket or the manifold","Broken wire or terminal in the cylinder 3 injector circuit","Shorted driver output in the gas control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Cylinder 3 runs rich or misfires in gas mode","Smell of unburnt gas at the exhaust"],2,3,["P22E1","P22E3","P22E4","P22DE","P0267","P0303"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 3 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22E3:["Cylinder 3 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","P22E3 tells that the cylinder 3 gas injector circuit is held high. TransEco Energy's AFCM list names a short to power, MIL on for bi-fuel use, and Ford's 2014 code list also ties P22E3 to the MIL. With the line stuck at supply voltage the injector cannot be switched on, so cylinder 3 gets no gas and misfires lean.",["Cylinder 3 control wire shorted to a 12 V feed","Shorted turns in the cylinder 3 gas injector","Faulty output of the injector control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Lean misfire on cylinder 3 in gas mode, often with P0303","Noticeable loss of power on gas"],2,3,["P22E1","P22E2","P22E4","P22DF","P0268","P0303"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 3 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22E4:["Cylinder 3 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","P22E4 points to a cylinder 3 gas injector whose circuit works but whose electrical behaviour does not match the command. Peak-and-hold gas injectors first draw a high opening current and then a lower holding current; Ford's patent US 8,161,946 treats an injector that stays at peak or ignores commands as degraded and reports this back to the engine computer. No maker documents P22E4 publicly.",["Armature of the cylinder 3 gas injector gummed up by oil or debris","Injector coil aged or overheated, resistance out of range","Weak driver output or poor supply ground"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Intermittent cylinder 3 misfire on gas","Rising gas consumption"],2,3,["P22E1","P22E2","P22E3","P22E0","P01A5","P0303"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 3 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22E5:["Cylinder 4 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","P22E5 is the open-circuit code for the cylinder 4 gas injector; on four-cylinder gas engines it is the last injector of the set. The driver sees no current when it switches the injector on. No maker documents P22E5 in public sources: TransEco and Ford's 2014 list stop at the cylinder 4 Low/High codes P22E6 and P22E7, and TransEco files an open line under Low.",["Open coil in the cylinder 4 gas injector","Heat-damaged or brittle connector near the exhaust side","Broken wire in the cylinder 4 injector circuit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Gas mode unavailable, car runs on gasoline only","Cylinder 4 dead on a dedicated gas engine"],2,3,["P22E6","P22E7","P22E8","P22E1","P0204","P0304"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 4 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22E6:["Cylinder 4 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","P22E6 reports a low signal on the cylinder 4 gas injector control wire. TransEco Energy's AFCM table gives short to ground or open as the cause and turns the MIL on in bi-fuel installations, keeping the same failure response as for gasoline; Ford's 2014 code list carries P22E6 with the MIL as well.",["Cylinder 4 control wire grounded through damaged insulation","Separated terminal or broken wire in the cylinder 4 circuit","Damaged driver output in the gas control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Cylinder 4 runs rich or cuts out on gas","Engine stays on or returns to gasoline"],2,3,["P22E5","P22E7","P22E8","P22E2","P0270","P0304"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 4 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22E7:["Cylinder 4 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","P22E7 says the control circuit of the cylinder 4 gas injector reads high. TransEco Energy's fault table blames a short to power and lights the MIL for bi-fuel use; Ford's 2014 code list also marks P22E7 as a MIL code. The injector then cannot open and cylinder 4 misfires lean whenever gas is selected.",["Cylinder 4 control wire in contact with a 12 V circuit","Cylinder 4 injector coil with internal short","Output stage of the controlling module defective"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Cylinder 4 misfire only after the switch to gas","Reduced power in gas mode"],2,3,["P22E5","P22E6","P22E8","P22E3","P0271","P0304"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 4 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22E8:["Cylinder 4 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","P22E8 applies when the cylinder 4 gas injector circuit is complete but the measured response lies outside the plausible range, for instance an opening current that rises too slowly or a hold phase that never settles. No vehicle maker documents P22E8 openly; the published lists from TransEco and Ford end at Low/High.",["Cylinder 4 injector fouled by oil or liquids, often from a neglected gas filter","Aged injector coil with changed resistance","Low system voltage during cranking or at idle"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough idle on gas, smooth on gasoline","Gas mode ends after a while"],2,3,["P22E5","P22E6","P22E7","P22E4","P0204","P0304"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 4 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22E9:["Cylinder 5 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","P22E9 is the open-circuit code for the cylinder 5 gas injector and can only appear on engines with five or more cylinders, such as the V6 of GM's bi-fuel Impala or the 6.0-litre V8 of its bi-fuel Silverado and Sierra. The driver detects the break because current is missing when the injector is commanded on. No maker documents P22E9 publicly;",["Open coil in the cylinder 5 gas injector","Loose connector in the harness branch for this bank","Open driver output in the gas or injector control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Engine returns to gasoline after switching to gas","Cylinder 5 misfire if gas operation continues"],2,3,["P22EA","P22EB","P22EC","P22E5","P0205","P0305"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 5 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22EA:["Cylinder 5 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","P22EA stands for a low voltage on the cylinder 5 gas injector control wire, a code limited to engines with at least five cylinders. TransEco Energy's AFCM table points to a grounded wire or an open line, lights the MIL in bi-fuel use and applies the gasoline injector fault response; Ford's 2014 code list, written for V8 engines among others, keeps P22EA as a MIL code.",["Cylinder 5 control wire shorted to ground along the gas rail","Interrupted wire or terminal, flagged as Low by some modules","Shorted output stage in the gas control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Cylinder 5 runs rich or misfires in gas mode","Fouled spark plug on cylinder 5"],2,3,["P22E9","P22EB","P22EC","P22E6","P0273","P0305"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 5 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22EB:["Cylinder 5 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","P22EB reports that the cylinder 5 gas injector control circuit is too high, which TransEco Energy's AFCM list attributes to a short to power with the MIL on for bi-fuel use; Ford's 2014 code list likewise carries P22EB for the MIL. The injector stays closed, so cylinder 5 burns no gas and misfires lean, usually logged together with P0305.",["Cylinder 5 control wire chafed against a supply wire","Overheated cylinder 5 gas injector with shorted turns","Overloaded driver output in the gas control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Lean misfire on cylinder 5 in gas mode, often with P0305","Normal running on gasoline"],2,3,["P22E9","P22EA","P22EC","P22E7","P0274","P0305"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 5 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22EC:["Cylinder 5 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","P22EC is the plausibility code for the cylinder 5 gas injector circuit on engines with five or more cylinders: wiring and coil pass the basic checks, but the injector does not respond as commanded. California's OBD rule requires such output components to be checked for a proper functional response, and from model year 2019 the maker of an alternate-fueled vehicle submits its own plan for which monitors apply.",["Sticking armature in the cylinder 5 gas injector","Heat-aged coil with drifting resistance","Driver or supply not delivering the full opening current"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough cylinder 5 on gas or return to gasoline","Fuel trim on the affected bank drifts in gas mode"],2,3,["P22E9","P22EA","P22EB","P22E8","P0205","P0305"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 5 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22ED:["Cylinder 6 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","P22ED marks an open control circuit at the cylinder 6 gas injector, the last injector on six-cylinder engines like the 3.6-litre V6 of GM's 2015 bi-fuel Impala, where the ECM drives the CNG injectors directly. Current is missing when the injector should open, so the module records the break.",["Open coil in the cylinder 6 gas injector","Loose or corroded connector at cylinder 6","Broken wire between control module and cylinder 6 injector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Vehicle runs on gasoline although gas is selected","Cylinder 6 misfire on dedicated gas engines"],2,3,["P22EE","P22EF","P22F0","P22E9","P0206","P0306"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 6 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22EE:["Cylinder 6 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","On engines that burn natural gas or propane through their own gas injectors, the control module watches the drive line of each gas valve. This code means the line to the cylinder 6 gas injector sits at a lower voltage than the switching state allows.",["Control wire of the cylinder 6 gas injector chafed through to ground","Broken wire or loose plug at the gas injector (counted as Low by this system)","Gas injector coil burnt open","Faulty output stage in the PCM or gas control module"],["Check engine light on (bi-fuel versions)","Rough running or misfire on cylinder 6 in gas mode","System switches to gasoline or will not enter gas mode"],2,3,["P22ED","P22EF","P22F0","P22EA","P22F2","P0206","P0306"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 6 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22EF:["Cylinder 6 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","The counterpart to P22EE: the drive line of the cylinder 6 gas injector stays near battery voltage even when the output stage should pull it down. For Ford pickups and vans converted with the Altech-Eco/TransEco CNG kit, the installer sheet gives as cause is a short to power;",["Control wire of the cylinder 6 gas injector touching a battery-voltage feed","Gas harness spliced or pinned incorrectly during the conversion","Moisture bridging supply and control pins in the injector plug","Output stage in the control module no longer switches"],["Check engine light on (bi-fuel versions)","Lean misfire on cylinder 6 in gas mode","Automatic change to gasoline operation"],2,3,["P22EE","P22ED","P22F0","P22EB","P22F3","P0206"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 6 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22F0:["Cylinder 6 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","Unlike the pure wiring faults P22EE/P22EF, this code is meant for a cylinder 6 gas injector circuit that is electrically intact but behaves implausibly, for example a current rise or switching response that does not fit the command. No manufacturer documents this code publicly: neither the Ford 2014 code list nor the Altech-Eco/TransEco CNG table contains it; both stop at Low and High for this cylinder.",["Cylinder 6 gas valve sticking from oil or deposits carried in the gas","Coil resistance drifted out of the expected window","Corroded plug causing a slow current rise"],["Uneven idle or hesitation in gas mode","Cylinder 6 misfire count rising on gas only","Check engine light possible"],2,3,["P22ED","P22EE","P22EF","P22EC","P22F4","P0306"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 6 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22F1:["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","A general circuit or open-wire code for the gas injector of cylinder 7, which only exists on V8 and larger engines. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Ford and the Altech-Eco/TransEco CNG system for Ford V8 and V10 trucks report an open circuit at this valve under the Low code P22F2 instead, which CARB allows: for output circuit faults a maker need not store separate codes for open, shorted low and…",["Plug of the cylinder 7 gas injector loose or left off after service","Broken control or supply wire in the gas harness","Gas injector coil open internally"],["Misfire on cylinder 7 in gas mode","Fallback to gasoline on bi-fuel vehicles","Check engine light on"],2,3,["P22F2","P22F3","P22F4","P22ED","P22F5","P0207","P0307"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 7 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22F2:["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","Low voltage on the control line of the cylinder 7 gas injector. The code appears in Ford's 2014 code list with MIL and in the installer table of the Altech-Eco/TransEco CNG kits, which on Ford's V8 (F-150 5.0) and V10 (Super Duty 6.8) engines use the PCM to drive gas valves for all cylinders; cylinders 9 and 10 of the V10 get manufacturer codes there.",["Cylinder 7 injector control wire grounded on the engine or bracket","Open wire or poor pin contact (reported as Low)","Cylinder 7 gas injector coil failed"],["Check engine light on (bi-fuel versions)","Cylinder 7 misfire or rich running on gas","Gas mode blocked or ended"],2,3,["P22F1","P22F3","P22F4","P22EE","P22F6","P0207","P0307"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 7 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22F3:["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","Here the cylinder 7 gas valve drive line is held high, so the output stage cannot switch the valve on. Ford's 2014 list carries P22F3 with MIL; the Altech-Eco/TransEco table for its Ford V8 and V10 CNG systems names a short to power as cause, applies MIL only to bi-fuel trucks and notes that gas module version 1.4 cannot detect this fault itself.",["Cylinder 7 control wire shorted to a switched or battery feed","Wiring error at the splice between factory and gas harness","Output stage in the control module open"],["Lean misfire on cylinder 7 in gas mode","Check engine light on (bi-fuel versions)","Gas operation dropped in favour of gasoline"],2,3,["P22F1","P22F2","P22F4","P22EF","P22F7","P0207"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 7 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22F4:["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","Plausibility code for the cylinder 7 gas injector circuit: wiring passes the open/short checks, yet the electrical response of the valve does not match what the driver expects. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. For this cylinder, Ford's 2014 overview and the TransEco installer sheet for Ford V8/V10 engines contain just Low (P22F2) and High (P22F3) for this cylinder.",["Cylinder 7 gas valve slow or sticking from oil residue","Injector coil resistance shifted with heat or age","Weak supply voltage to the gas injector bank"],["Intermittent stumble in gas mode","Misfire code for cylinder 7 possible","Check engine light possible"],2,3,["P22F1","P22F2","P22F3","P22F0","P22F8","P0307"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 7 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22F5:["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","Open-circuit code for the gas injector of cylinder 8. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. In the two manufacturer-side lists found, the Ford overview from 2014 and TransEco's sheet for gas-converted Ford V8 and V10 trucks, cylinder 8 has only P22F6 and P22F7, and the TransEco table explicitly assigns an open line to P22F6. CARB permits this shortcut for output circuits.",["Cylinder 8 injector plug corroded or disconnected","Wire fatigued at a flex point of the gas harness","Coil of the cylinder 8 gas valve open"],["Cylinder 8 misfire whenever the engine runs on gas","Change to gasoline on bi-fuel vehicles","Check engine light on"],2,3,["P22F6","P22F7","P22F8","P22F1","P0208","P0308"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 8 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P22F6:["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","Cylinder 8 is the last cylinder with a generic gas injector code; beyond it the Altech-Eco/TransEco table for the Ford 6.8 V10 switches to manufacturer codes. P22F6 reports a control line for the cylinder 8 valve that is too low. That table counts a short to ground as well as an open line here, with MIL on bi-fuel vehicles only, and Ford's 2014 code list includes the code with MIL.",["Cylinder 8 control wire grounded through damaged insulation","Open wire or unplugged injector (reported as Low)","Cylinder 8 gas injector coil defective"],["Check engine light on (bi-fuel versions)","Misfire on cylinder 8 only in gas mode","Gas mode not available"],2,3,["P22F5","P22F7","P22F8","P22F2","P0208","P0308"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 8 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P22F7:["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","P22F7 means the drive line of the cylinder 8 gas injector cannot be pulled down and stays near supply voltage. Ford lists it with MIL in the 2014 code list; in the conversion data from Altech-Eco/TransEco the cause given is a short to power, keeps the MIL off on dedicated CNG engines and marks the fault as not detectable by gas module version 1.4.",["Cylinder 8 control wire pinched against a supply line","Supply and control pins swapped in the gas harness","Damaged output stage in the control module"],["Cylinder 8 lean misfire in gas mode","Check engine light on (bi-fuel versions)","Vehicle stays on gasoline"],2,3,["P22F5","P22F6","P22F8","P22F3","P0208"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 8 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P22F8:["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","Functional code for the cylinder 8 gas injector circuit, meant for cases where wiring is intact but the valve reacts outside the expected window. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Both at Ford (2014 list) and at Altech-Eco/TransEco the series stops at P22F6/P22F7 for this cylinder.",["Cylinder 8 gas valve opening late or partly due to contamination","Coil degraded by heat at the rear of the engine","Contact resistance in the injector plug"],["Hesitation under load in gas mode","Cylinder 8 misfire code possible","Check engine light possible"],2,3,["P22F5","P22F6","P22F7","P22F4","P0308"],"מזרק דלק חלופי צילינדר‏ 8 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P22F9:["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response Low to High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P22F9 concerns the NOx sensor ahead of the SCR catalyst on bank 1 and how fast it follows a rise in engine-out NOx. After a load step the control module times the sensor signal and compares it with the curve of its own NOx model. GM's 2025 diesel table starts both timers at 30 ppm and stops them at 220 ppm; a lag beyond 2 s or a relative delay above 10 % fails the check, rated Type B with the MIL after two trips.",["Front NOx sensor aged or contaminated (oil ash, silicone, cleaning agents), reacting slowly","ECM calibration error, fixed by reprogramming (GM 24-NA-058 for the 2024 L5P)","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensor diluting the gas sample","Soot or deposits covering the protective cap of the sensor"],["Check engine light on after two drives","Usually no noticeable change in driving","SCR efficiency codes may follow"],2,1,["P22FA","P22FB","P22FC","P2201","P2200"],""],P22FA:["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response High to Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P22FA mirrors P22F9 for the falling edge: when engine-out NOx drops, mostly as the driver lifts off into overrun, the front NOx sensor on bank 1 takes too long to come down. GM's 2014 Cruze 2.0 diesel fails it when the signal needs more than 1.8 s between 30 and 60 % of its starting value at 1320 rpm or more; the 6.6L LML allows 2.3 s for a drop from 70 to 40 %.",["Engine software anomaly, cured by reprogramming (GM PI1485, FCA 18-018-15, 18-008-21)","Front NOx sensor aged or contaminated, signal decays slowly","Exhaust leak near the sensor disturbing the measurement"],["Check engine light on","Warning about poor DEF quality on some GM diesels","Usually no change in engine behaviour"],2,1,["P22F9","P22FB","P22FD","P2201","P20EE"],""],P22FB:["NOx Sensor Performance - Sensing Element (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","P22FB questions whether the measuring element of the front NOx sensor on bank 1 still reads true. GM's 2025 diesel tables hold its filtered value against modelled engine-out NOx and fail it below minus 36 % or above plus 77 % (version A) or outside minus 51 to plus 100 % (version B), as a Type A fault with the MIL in one trip. Volvo and Mack count P22FB-92 among the codes that mean a damaged inlet sensor.",["Measuring cell of the front NOx sensor drifted or damaged (Volvo/Mack P22FB-92)","ECM or DEF control unit software, fixed by reprogramming (Isuzu SB22-L-001, GM 23-NA-159, Mazda 01-004-22)","Real engine-out NOx differs from the model, e.g. through an EGR fault (P0402)","Exhaust leak ahead of the sensor"],["Check engine light on, on GM's 2025 diesels already after one drive","Rough idle or surging if an EGR fault is behind it","Often no other noticeable effect"],2,1,["P22FE","P2201","P22F9","P22FA","P0402"],""],P22FC:["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response Low to High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22FC is reserved for the rear NOx sensor on bank 1, behind the SCR catalyst, when its signal climbs too slowly after NOx at that point increases. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and the NHTSA bulletin index has no entry for it. GM, whose tables describe the front-sensor version P22F9, files the dynamic check of the rear sensor under P229F instead (2018 diesel fault bundle for the NOx2 dynamic test).",["Rear NOx sensor aged or contaminated by urea deposits, oil ash or cleaning agents","Exhaust leak between SCR catalyst and sensor","Calibration of the test itself, check for software updates"],["Check engine light on","No change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P22FD","P22FE","P22F9","P229F","P20EE"],""],P22FD:["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response High to Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22FD stands for the falling edge at the rear NOx sensor on bank 1: after a NOx peak downstream of the SCR catalyst, the signal decays more slowly than permitted. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and no bulletin in the NHTSA index names it.",["Rear NOx sensor aged or coated, signal falls too slowly","Urea crystals around the sensor tip after dosing faults","Exhaust leak close to the outlet sensor"],["Check engine light on","SCR efficiency code may appear as well"],2,1,["P22FC","P22FE","P22FA","P229F","P23C0","P20EE"],""],P22FE:["NOx Sensor Performance - Sensing Element (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P22FE tests the measuring cells of the rear NOx sensor on bank 1. On GM diesels the check runs after the engine is switched off: the sensor alters its internal pump currents so that about 1000 ppm of oxygen sits in the second cavity, and the result is compared with a reference written into its memory at the supplier. Blocked cavities lower NOx sensitivity.",["Measuring cavities of the rear NOx sensor clogged or cells drifted","ECM or DEF control unit software (GM PIP5615A, 23-NA-193, Isuzu SB22-L-001)","Contamination by urea residue, oil ash or additive cleaners"],["Check engine light on","Code sets after shutdown, so it often appears at the next start","Driving behaviour unchanged"],2,1,["P22FB","P22FC","P22FD","P229F","P23C1"],""],P22FF:["SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too Low","Diesel engines raise exhaust temperature on purpose so the SCR catalyst can reduce NOx; this code reports that the gas entering the SCR stays too cold despite that. Ford describes it for the 6.7L and 3.2L diesels under its monitoring of the exhaust temperature controller: the measured SCR inlet value is compared with the setpoint, and the fault sets when it lags more than 80 °C behind for 300 s (2015 model year,…",["Long idling or light-load operation keeps exhaust cold","Exhaust leak ahead of the SCR cools the gas or skews the reading","Exhaust temperature sensor reading too low while still in range","Engine software with overly strict monitor (update available on some makes)"],["Check engine light on","Reduced NOx conversion, possible further SCR efficiency codes","Code returns after extended idling"],2,1,["P05EB","P214A","P20EE","P2080","P2084","P249C"],"טמפרטורת כניסת ממיר קטליטי NOx SCR — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2300:["Ignition Coil A Primary Control Circuit Low","P2300 reports that the control line to ignition coil A is pulled towards ground. GM, Saab and VW assign coil A to cylinder 1. GM's 2019 engine tables check the low-side driver while it is switched off: if the line voltage lies in the band of a short below 100 ohms to ground in 50 of 63 samples (taken every 100 ms, battery above 11 V), the Type A fault turns on the MIL in the first trip.",["Coil A (cylinder 1) with an internal fault pulling the control input to ground","Control wire of coil A chafed through and touching engine ground","Water or corrosion in the coil A connector","Engine module driver or software fault (FCA 2023: PCM reflash)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire and rough running on cylinder 1","Noticeable loss of power","Fuel to cylinder 1 cut off by the engine module"],2,3,["P2301","P2302","P0351","P2303","P0301","P0300"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2301:["Ignition Coil A Primary Control Circuit High","P2301 is the mirror image of P2300: the control line of coil A, i.e. cylinder 1, carries voltage at a moment when the engine module is trying to pull it low. Saab's Trionic 8 in the 2003 9-3 sets it if the line stays above 2 V for longer than 1 s while the module grounds it;",["Coil A with an internal short feeding supply voltage onto the control input","Control wire of coil A rubbing against a 12 V line in the harness","Broken control line or loose pin (counts as P2301 on Saab Trionic 8)","Faulty output stage in the engine module"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 1 misfires, engine shakes at idle","Jerking and loss of power under load"],2,3,["P2300","P2302","P0351","P2304","P0301"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2302:["Ignition Coil A Secondary Circuit","P2302 looks at the high-voltage side of coil A – the secondary winding, the boot and the spark plug of cylinder 1 – rather than at the control line covered by P2300 and P2301. Only a few makers use it.",["Worn or fouled spark plug in cylinder 1, gap too wide","Cracked coil boot letting the spark jump to the cylinder head","Secondary winding of coil A breaking down","Ion-sense evaluation in the PCM (FCA 18-069-16: PCM replaced)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 1, often together with P0301","Rough idle and hesitation"],2,3,["P2300","P2301","P2305","P0301","P0300","P0351"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2303:["Ignition Coil B Primary Control Circuit Low","P2303 tells you that the trigger wire of coil B – cylinder 2 in GM, Saab and VW documentation – has found a path to ground. On the Saab 9-5 2.0 turbo (GM LDK engine, 2010) the check runs continuously below 6,000 rpm with 9–18 V on the ignition feed and sets after 4 s of uninterrupted short or 50 s added up; as a Type B code it turns on the MIL only after a second failing trip.",["Coil B (cylinder 2) faulty, pulling the control line low","Insulation damage on the coil B control wire touching ground","PCM software assigning the code to the wrong cylinder (Ford Bronco, FCA 2.0 turbo)","Engine module output stage defective"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 2","Engine runs on fewer cylinders, less power"],2,3,["P2304","P2305","P0352","P2300","P0302"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2304:["Ignition Coil B Primary Control Circuit High","P2304 means the control line of coil B (cylinder 2) is held at too high a voltage – usually a short to a supply line, sometimes an internal coil fault. In VW's 2014 tables a primary control circuit counts as high once its signal voltage exceeds about 5.1–7.0 V, while the low code reacts to a current above 24 mA; the Touareg six-cylinder petrol table (engine code CGRA) names the coils directly by cylinder number.",["Coil B control wire shorted to a voltage-carrying line","Internal fault in coil B or its built-in driver","Engine module fault (Polaris Slingshot 2026: ECM replaced)","Interrupted control line on systems that report it here (Saab Trionic 8)"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 2 misfiring","Shaking at idle, weak acceleration"],2,3,["P2303","P2305","P0352","P2301","P0302"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2305:["Ignition Coil B Secondary Circuit","P2305 is about coil B's output side: the secondary winding, the connection to the plug and the spark plug of cylinder 2. Where a maker uses it, the module does not just watch whether the coil was switched, but whether a usable spark happened.",["Spark plug of cylinder 2 worn, oily or with the wrong gap","Coil B boot cracked or damp, spark leaking away","Coil B secondary winding weak","Faulty ion-current evaluation in the PCM"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 2, sometimes only under load","Rough running, raised fuel consumption"],2,3,["P2303","P2304","P2302","P0302","P0352"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2306:["Ignition Coil C Primary Control Circuit Low","With P2306 the engine module has seen the output for coil C, cylinder 3 at GM, Saab and VW, dragged down to ground. Ford explains where such a fault can sit on engines whose coils carry their own driver: the coil-driver chip in the PCM watches current and voltage at its output, so the culprit may be the PCM, the harness, the plug-in connection at the coil or the driver electronics inside the coil – but not the…",["Driver electronics inside coil C defective","Coil C control wire grounded through chafing or a pinched harness","Corroded or bent pins at the coil C connector","PCM output or software (FCA 2023 reflash)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 3","Uneven idle, possibly cylinder shut-off"],2,3,["P2307","P2308","P0353","P2303","P0303"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2307:["Ignition Coil C Primary Control Circuit High","P2307 sets when the coil C control line, cylinder 3 in most layouts, is shorted to a voltage source. On GM's 3.6-litre LLT V6 (2008) the check is a continuity test against voltage that runs below 6,000 rpm with the battery between 9.99 and 18.1 V and needs 4 s at a stretch or 50 s in total.",["Coil C control wire touching a battery-voltage line","Coil C with an internal short to its supply","Code filed against the wrong cylinder by PCM software (Ford Bronco SSM 52342)","Broken control wire on systems reporting opens here (Saab Trionic 8)"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 3 misfires","Power loss, engine runs rough"],2,3,["P2306","P2308","P0353","P2304","P0303"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2308:["Ignition Coil C Secondary Circuit","P2308 points at the high-voltage path of coil C, normally cylinder 3: winding, boot and plug. The code is uncommon. FCA's 3.6 V6 in the 2015–2016 Caravan and Town & Country calls it coil 3 secondary circuit with insufficient ionization.",["Spark plug of cylinder 3 worn or fouled","Boot of coil C leaking high voltage","FCA vans built 27 July–11 September 2015: PCM fault (bulletin 18-069-16)","Coil C secondary winding faulty"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 3 with P0303 stored","Engine runs rough"],2,3,["P2306","P2307","P2311","P0303","P0300"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2309:["Ignition Coil D Primary Control Circuit Low","P2309 stands for a grounded control lead to coil D – cylinder 4, which on a four-cylinder engine is the last coil in the row. In 2023 FCA released bulletins 18-022-23 and 18-023-23 for the Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio with the 280 hp 2.0 turbo: P2300-00, P2303-00, P2306-00 and P2309-00 could set together with an EVAP purge code, and the remedy was PCM software rather than parts.",["Coil D (cylinder 4) defective","PCM software fault setting several coil low codes (FCA 2.0 turbo 2023)","Damaged harness section carrying several coil lines","Poor contact or moisture at the coil D connector"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 4","Auto stop-start no longer works (Ford)","Reduced power"],2,3,["P2310","P2311","P0354","P2306","P0304"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P230A:["Cylinder 1 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P230A belongs to a second series of cylinder imbalance codes. P219C reports that cylinder 1 runs a mixture unlike the others; P230A goes a step further and says the balancing function has already moved the fuel correction for cylinder 1 to its end stop without evening it out.",["Injector of cylinder 1 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 1","Valve of cylinder 1 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 1"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 1","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P219C","P230B","P0301","P0201","P219A"],""],P230B:["Cylinder 2 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P230B singles out cylinder 2: its individual fuel correction has reached the limit during cylinder balancing and the imbalance remains. Audi is one of the few makers whose use of the code is on record. Its 2020 bulletin 2060348 for the A6 2.0 TFSI of the third EA888 generation explains that a calibration mistake filed a cylinder 2 imbalance under P230E, the cylinder 5 code, instead of the correct P230B;",["Injector of cylinder 2 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 2","Valve of cylinder 2 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Calibration error in the cylinder assignment (Audi 2.0 TFSI Gen 3, bulletin 2060348)"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 2","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P219D","P230A","P230C","P230E","P0302","P0202","P219A"],""],P230C:["Cylinder 3 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P230C is the balance-limit code for cylinder 3. On three-cylinder engines this is the last cylinder of the row; on fours and larger engines it sits further inside. The engine control trims the fuel of each cylinder separately to even out mixture differences, and P230C means the trim for cylinder 3 is used up. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly and the NHTSA index lists no bulletin for it.",["Injector of cylinder 3 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 3","Valve of cylinder 3 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 3"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 3","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P219E","P230B","P230D","P0303","P0203","P219A"],""],P230D:["Cylinder 4 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P230D flags cylinder 4, so the engine needs at least four cylinders. The balancing function has run the individual fuel trim for that cylinder to its limit and the mixture still deviates. Audi's 2020 bulletin for the 2.0 TFSI (third-generation EA888) shows that this four-cylinder reports imbalance through the P230 series, which gives the code a real home, although the bulletin itself only names P230B and P230E.",["Injector of cylinder 4 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 4","Valve of cylinder 4 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 4"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 4","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P219F","P230C","P230E","P0304","P0204","P219A"],""],P230E:["Cylinder 5 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P230E concerns cylinder 5 and is genuine only on engines with five or more cylinders, such as inline fives, sixes and V8s. The balancing logic has exhausted the individual fuel trim for cylinder 5.",["Injector of cylinder 5 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 5","Valve of cylinder 5 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Calibration error in the cylinder assignment (Audi 2.0 TFSI Gen 3, bulletin 2060348)"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 5","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A0","P230D","P230F","P230B","P0305","P0205","P219A"],""],P230F:["Cylinder 6 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P230F is the balance-limit code for cylinder 6 and can only appear on engines with six or more cylinders, inline sixes, V6 units and larger. On a V6, cylinder 6 shares its bank and front oxygen sensor with two others, so its individual trim has to be estimated from that bank signal or from crankshaft speed. No maker documents P230F publicly, and no NHTSA bulletin mentions it.",["Injector of cylinder 6 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 6","Valve of cylinder 6 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 6"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 6","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A1","P230E","P231A","P0306","P0206","P219A","P219B"],""],P2310:["Ignition Coil D Primary Control Circuit High","P2310 sets when the coil D control line, belonging to cylinder 4, carries voltage while the engine module tries to switch it to ground. Saab's Trionic 8 (9-3, 2003) uses a 2 V limit held for over 1 s and evaluates cylinder 4 together with cylinder 2 for its ion-based combustion signal; the injector of the affected cylinder is shut off.",["Coil D control wire shorted to a voltage source","Internal fault in coil D","Interrupted line reported as high on Saab Trionic 8","Defective driver in the engine module"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 4 misfiring, injector shut off","Rough idle"],2,3,["P2309","P2311","P0354","P2307","P0304"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2311:["Ignition Coil D Secondary Circuit","P2311 concerns the secondary side of coil D, usually cylinder 4. The secondary winding has thousands of turns of fine wire and delivers roughly 15–40 kV, so insulation that is merely tired can let the spark escape to ground instead of crossing the plug gap. Few control units watch this side as a circuit of its own;",["Aged insulation in coil D or its boot letting the spark leak to ground","Spark plug of cylinder 4 worn, gap grown","Oil in the plug well softening the boot","PCM ion-sense fault (FCA bulletin 18-069-16)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 4, worse in damp weather or under load","Flashing MIL at heavy misfire"],2,3,["P2309","P2310","P2308","P0304","P0300"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2312:["Ignition Coil E Primary Control Circuit Low","P2312 is the first code of this series that only engines with five or more cylinders can set: it flags the control lead of coil E, i.e. cylinder 5, as shorted to ground. Examples with documented coil E checks are VW's 2.5-litre five-cylinder in the 2014 Passat (low above a current of 24 mA), the Saab 9-5 2.8 V6 (LAU) and GM's LT5 Corvette V8, whose 2019 table rates it Type B after two trips in 50 of 63 samples.",["Coil E (cylinder 5) defective","Short in the coil supply shared by one bank (Saab LAU: coils 1, 3, 5)","Coil E control wire chafed against ground","Wrong cylinder assignment in PCM software (Ford SSM 52455)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 5","Rough running, less power"],2,3,["P2313","P2314","P0355","P2309","P0305"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2313:["Ignition Coil E Primary Control Circuit High","P2313 reports that the control line of coil E, cylinder 5, is shorted to positive, and therefore needs an engine with at least five cylinders. Saab spells out the conditions for its 9-5 2.8 V6 (LAU, 2011): engine running at 400–5,000 rpm with 10–18 V, a check on every crank revolution once 20 have passed, and a fault after more than 4 s or 30 s in total; P2313 is a Type B code.",["Coil E internally shorted to supply","Aftermarket device spliced into the coil wiring (Saab LAU note)","Coil E control wire touching a 12 V line","PCM cylinder mapping error (Ford Bronco 3.0, TSB 24-2406)"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 5 misfiring","Hesitation and jerking under load"],2,3,["P2312","P2314","P0355","P2310","P0305"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2314:["Ignition Coil E Secondary Circuit","P2314 reports a fault on the high-voltage side of coil E, which only five-cylinder and larger engines have; it normally fires cylinder 5. The control line may be perfectly sound; what failed is the energy reaching the plug or the combustion that should follow.",["Spark plug of cylinder 5 worn or fouled","Coil E secondary winding or boot damaged","PCM fault on FCA vans from the 2015 build window"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 5","Rough idle, slight vibration"],2,3,["P2312","P2313","P2317","P0305","P0355"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ E — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2315:["Ignition Coil F Primary Control Circuit Low","P2315 indicates that the switching line of coil F – cylinder 6 – is grounded, so six-, eight- and larger engines only. Several makers name the cylinder outright: VW's 2014 Touareg table for the six-cylinder petrol engine CGRA speaks of the ignition coil of cylinder 6, Saab's 9-5 2.8 V6 of coil 6, and GM's 2008 3.6 V6 (LLT) lists P2315 with the other five ground-short codes.",["Coil F (cylinder 6) faulty","Fault in the bank 2 coil supply affecting coils 2, 4 and 6 (Saab LAU)","Coil F control wire chafed to ground near the rear of the engine","Engine module output defective"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 6","Engine shakes, power down"],2,3,["P2316","P2317","P0356","P2312","P0306"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ F — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2316:["Ignition Coil F Primary Control Circuit High","P2316 means the coil F control line, cylinder 6, sits at a voltage it should not have while the module switches it – a short to supply or a fault inside the coil. In VW's 2014 Touareg tables the high threshold is a signal voltage above about 5.1–7.0 V.",["Coil F control wire shorted to a supply line","Internal short in coil F","Intermittent contact in the harness near coil F","Engine module driver defective"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 6, P0306 may also be stored","Intermittent stumbling"],2,3,["P2315","P2317","P0356","P2313","P0306"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ F — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2317:["Ignition Coil F Secondary Circuit","P2317 concerns the high-voltage side of coil F, which serves cylinder 6 on engines with six or more cylinders. With coil-on-plug designs there is no separate lead any more – Ford notes that individual coils did away with plug wires – so a secondary fault lies in the coil, its boot or the plug.",["Spark plug of cylinder 6 worn or wrongly gapped","Coil F boot cracked or contaminated","Coil F secondary winding failing","PCM ion-current evaluation defective (FCA)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 6","Uneven running, especially under load"],2,3,["P2315","P2316","P2314","P0306","P0300"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ F — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2318:["Ignition Coil G Primary Control Circuit Low","P2318 says the command wire of coil G, cylinder 7, is touching ground, so it only occurs on V8, V10 or V12 engines. GM's 2019 table for the 5.3-litre L84 truck V8 lists it as a Type B code (50 of 63 failed samples, battery above 11 V, MIL after two trips). Ford covers the series up to P2327 for its V10 and adds that the PCM cuts the injector of the affected cylinder;",["Coil G (cylinder 7) defective","Water or corrosion at the coil G connector","Control wire of coil G grounded by heat or chafing damage","PCM cylinder mapping error on Ford 6.8/7.3 (SSM 52455)"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 7","V8 runs noticeably rough, power reduced"],2,3,["P2319","P0357","P2315","P2321","P0307"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ G — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2319:["Ignition Coil G Primary Control Circuit High","P2319 sets when the coil G control line, belonging to cylinder 7 of a V8 or larger engine, shows a short to voltage. GM's 2019 tables include it for the LT5 Corvette V8 as a Type B code with 50 of 63 failed samples. Ford describes the protective reaction in detail: after a coil-driver fault the injector of that cylinder stays off for 30 s;",["Coil G control wire shorted to a supply line","Internal fault in coil G","Code assigned to the wrong cylinder by PCM software (Ford SSM 52455)","Engine module output stage defective"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 7 shut off for periods of 30 s (Ford)","Rough running and loss of power"],2,3,["P2318","P0357","P2316","P2322","P0307"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ G — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P231A:["Cylinder 7 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P231A takes the series to cylinder 7; since P2310 to P2319 are ignition coil codes, the versions for cylinders 7 to 12 start at P231A. Only engines with eight or more cylinders can set it. Mercedes-Benz documents it for the 2022 to 2024 SL with the AMG M177 V8 (LI07.61-P-077382): the ME control unit reports irregular mixture formation at cylinder 7 and disables the injector quantity adjustment.",["Injector of cylinder 7 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 7","Valve of cylinder 7 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","ME engine software (Mercedes M177, LI07.61-P-077382)"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 7","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A2","P230F","P231B","P0307","P0207","P219A","P219B"],""],P231B:["Cylinder 8 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P231B is the balance-limit code for cylinder 8, the last cylinder of a V8 and an inner one on V10 and V12 engines. The fuel trim for that cylinder has hit its stop while balancing. No maker documents P231B publicly;",["Injector of cylinder 8 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 8","Valve of cylinder 8 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 8"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 8","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A3","P231A","P231C","P0308","P0208","P219A","P219B"],""],P231C:["Cylinder 9 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P231C points to cylinder 9 and therefore exists only on ten- and twelve-cylinder engines, a small group of mostly high-performance and heavy-duty petrol units. The balancing logic has pushed the fuel trim for cylinder 9 to its limit. No manufacturer documents the code publicly and the NHTSA index has no bulletin for it.",["Injector of cylinder 9 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 9","Valve of cylinder 9 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 9"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 9","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A4","P231B","P231D","P0309","P0209","P219A","P219B"],""],P231D:["Cylinder 10 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P231D is the cylinder 10 code of the balance-limit series. On a V10 it marks the last cylinder, on a V12 one of the inner ones; smaller engines cannot set it. The individual fuel correction for cylinder 10 has reached its end stop while the controller tried to equalise the mixture. No maker publishes a description, and no NHTSA bulletin lists it.",["Injector of cylinder 10 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 10","Valve of cylinder 10 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 10"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 10","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A5","P231C","P231E","P0310","P0210","P219A","P219B"],""],P231E:["Cylinder 11 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P231E belongs to cylinder 11 and can only come from twelve-cylinder engines, V12 or W12. The per-cylinder fuel trim for cylinder 11 sits at its limit during balancing. There is no public manufacturer description and no NHTSA bulletin. On such engines six cylinders share each bank, so one deviating cylinder shifts the bank sensor signal only slightly;",["Injector of cylinder 11 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 11","Valve of cylinder 11 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 11"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 11","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A6","P231D","P231F","P0311","P0211","P219A","P219B"],""],P231F:["Cylinder 12 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance - Adjustment At Limit During Balance","P231F closes the balance-limit series at cylinder 12, the last cylinder of a twelve-cylinder engine. It says the balancing routine has used up the fuel trim for that cylinder without matching it to the rest. Public manufacturer documentation is missing, and the NHTSA index contains no bulletin naming it.",["Injector of cylinder 12 delivering too much or too little (deposits, wear)","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 12","Valve of cylinder 12 not sealing (worn seat or guide), low compression","Poor contact at the connector of injector 12"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 12","Higher fuel consumption or exhaust smell"],2,1,["P21A7","P231E","P0312","P0212","P219A","P219B"],""],P2320:["Ignition Coil G Secondary Circuit","P2320 points at the high-voltage half of coil G, normally the coil on cylinder 7, so only engines with seven or more cylinders can log it. FCA is the maker on record: STAR case S2118000002 from March 2021 for the 2020–2021 Ram 1500 names P2320 as coil 7 secondary circuit with insufficient ionization.",["Coil 7 connector not fully seated or latched (FCA)","Spark plug of cylinder 7 worn, fouled or with wrong gap","Coil G secondary winding or boot breaking down","Ion-current evaluation in the PCM faulty"],["Check engine light on","Misfire felt on cylinder 7, often with P0307","Engine shakes at idle or under load"],2,1,["P2318","P2319","P2323","P2317","P0357","P0307"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ G — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2321:["Ignition Coil H Primary Control Circuit Low","With P2321 the engine module has seen the switching line of coil H pulled to ground; on a V8 coil H is the final one, on a V10 it is number eight. GM's 2019 tables, which label the code as cylinder 8, carry it for the LT5 Corvette and the L84 5.3-litre truck engine: a Type B fault after 50 bad readings in 63 samples taken every 100 ms with the system above 11 V.",["Water ingress or corrosion in the coil H connector (GM PIP5147)","Coil H with internal short","Coil H control wire chafed through to ground","Coil driver stage in the engine module damaged"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 8 misfires or drops out","Rough idle and weaker pulling power"],2,3,["P2322","P2323","P0358","P2318","P2324","P0308"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ H — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2322:["Ignition Coil H Primary Control Circuit High","P2322 is the counterpart to P2321: the coil H control line, cylinder 8 on most V8 layouts, reads as if it were tied to voltage. GM monitors it the same way on the 2019 LT5 and L84 engines, as a Type B code, flagged once 50 of 63 samples fail.",["Coil H control wire shorted to a voltage-carrying line","Coil H defective internally","PCM assigns the code to the wrong cylinder (Ford SSM 52455/52342)","Output stage in the engine module faulty"],["Check engine light on","One cylinder repeatedly shut off for about 30 s (Ford)","Noticeable vibration and loss of power"],2,3,["P2321","P0358","P2319","P2325","P0308"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ H — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2323:["Ignition Coil H Secondary Circuit","P2323 concerns the spark side of coil H, the coil on cylinder 8. It is the last code of FCA's ion-sensing series: STAR case S2118000002 (2021) for the 2020–2021 Ram 1500 reads it as coil 8 secondary circuit with insufficient ionization, and an older FCA parts review lists it together with the cylinder misfire codes P0301–P0308.",["Coil 8 connector loose or not latched (FCA)","Worn or fouled spark plug on cylinder 8","Coil H boot cracked or tracking to the head","PCM ion-sense circuit faulty"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 8 misfire, frequently stored with P0308","Rough running when accelerating"],2,1,["P2321","P2322","P2320","P0358","P0308"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ H — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2324:["Ignition Coil I Primary Control Circuit Low","Coil I is the ninth coil, so P2324 only appears on ten- or twelve-cylinder petrol engines. The documented user is Ford: its OBD system summaries (2012 and 2020–2023) group P2324 with the other codes for a coil driver shorted to ground, monitored continuously from 200 rpm with the battery between 11 and 16 V, and Ford's 2014 code interpretation list marks it as a MIL code.",["Coil I (cylinder 9) shorted internally","Coil I control wire grounded on the engine or exhaust side","Moisture or corroded pins at the coil I plug","PCM coil driver for cylinder 9 failed"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 9 cuts out, rough running","Reduced towing or climbing power"],2,3,["P2325","P2326","P0359","P2321","P2327","P0309"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ I — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2325:["Ignition Coil I Primary Control Circuit High","P2325 flags a short to voltage on the trigger line of coil I, the ninth ignition output. Ford is again the only maker that lists it publicly: in its OBD summaries P2325 sits among the codes for a coil driver shorted high, and the 2014 Ford code list shows it as a MIL-lighting code checked with the engine running. The PCM judges current and voltage on the driver against open and short limits;",["Coil I control wire touching a 12 V feed","Coil I primary winding damaged","PCM driver stage for coil I faulty"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 9 drops out in roughly 30 s cycles","Uneven idle and vibration"],2,3,["P2324","P0359","P2322","P2328","P0309"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ I — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2326:["Ignition Coil I Secondary Circuit","P2326 would report a fault in the high-voltage output of coil I – coil, boot or plug of the ninth cylinder. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. FCA's ion-sensing secondary codes, the closest analogue, end at coil 8 (P2323), and Ford, the one maker with public coil I codes, monitors that coil only on its driver side (P2324/P2325).",["Spark plug on cylinder 9 worn or bridged","Coil I boot perforated or oil-soaked","Coil I secondary winding weak"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 9 (P0309)","Hesitation under heavy load"],2,1,["P2324","P2325","P2329","P0359","P0309"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ I — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2327:["Ignition Coil J Primary Control Circuit Low","P2327 is the highest ground-side coil code Ford publishes: its driver short-circuit-low list in the 2012 and 2020–2023 OBD summaries runs from P2300 up to P2327 and stops there, matching a ten-coil engine such as the 6.8-litre Modular V10. Coil J serves the tenth cylinder in Ford's count. The check runs continuously between 200 rpm and about 3,200 rpm under positive torque and finishes in under a second;",["Coil J (cylinder 10) failed with internal short","Coil J signal wire shorted to ground near the rear of the engine","Corroded or water-filled coil J connector","PCM driver for coil J defective"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 10 missing, engine shakes","Higher fuel consumption from cylinder shut-off cycles"],2,3,["P2328","P2329","P0360","P2324","P0310"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ J — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2328:["Ignition Coil J Primary Control Circuit High","P2328 marks the end of Ford's published coil list: it is the last entry in the driver short-circuit-high group of the 2012 and 2020–2023 OBD summaries, and the 2014 Ford code list puts it directly before the evaporative codes with a MIL flag.",["Coil J control wire shorted to battery voltage","Coil J drawing abnormal current","PCM output for coil J damaged"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 10 switched off at intervals","Engine runs rough and pulls weakly"],2,3,["P2327","P0360","P2325","P06D1","P0310"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ J — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2329:["Ignition Coil J Secondary Circuit","P2329 covers the secondary side of coil J, meaning the spark path to the plug of cylinder 10. No public manufacturer source assigns it. Ford, whose V10 is the obvious ten-cylinder candidate, lists coil J only on the primary side (P2327/P2328) and in its 2014 code list skips every secondary code of the series. FCA's insufficient-ionization codes stop after coil 8. The code therefore stays a reserved SAE slot;",["Eroded spark plug on cylinder 10","Carbon tracking on the coil J boot","Coil J high-voltage winding deteriorating"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 10 (P0310)","Jerking under acceleration, worse when damp"],2,1,["P2327","P2328","P2326","P0360","P0310"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ J — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P232A:["TCM Request - Forced Engine Shutdown","P232A is stored by the engine module when the transmission control module has demanded that the engine be switched off. A TCM sends such a request over the vehicle network when it decides that keeping the engine running could harm the transmission or the vehicle, typically after a serious internal transmission or module fault; the root cause then sits as a separate code in the TCM.",["Serious transmission fault detected by the TCM (stored there as its own code)","Disturbed CAN communication between TCM and engine module","Low battery voltage or poor supply/ground at the TCM","Mismatched or outdated TCM/engine software after repair or replacement"],["Engine shuts off while driving or at idle","Engine cranks but does not stay running until the fault is cleared","Transmission warning and further codes in the TCM"],3,3,["P06AF","P0700","P0613","U0101","P2105","P241D"],""],P232B:["Cylinder 11 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit","Common-rail diesels keep a small-quantity correction for every injector. During overrun fuel cut the module fires one injector alone with a tiny known amount (GM: about 1.5 mm³), judges the torque from crankshaft acceleration and records how much the energizing time has to change at each rail pressure level.",["Injector of cylinder 11 leaking or delivering too much at small quantities","Injector correction code not or wrongly entered after replacement","Disturbed crankshaft speed signal falsifying the torque evaluation","Engine software calibration issue"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable change; possibly louder combustion noise or rough idle","Possibly smoke or higher fuel consumption"],3,1,["P232C","P232D","P02DE","P0211","P01E0","P0311"],""],P232C:["Cylinder 11 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit","P232C is the upper-limit partner of P232B for injector A in cylinder 11. The small-quantity learning has found that this injector needs far more energizing time than the nominal map to produce the expected torque pulse, and the stored correction has hit its maximum at one or more rail pressure levels. Typical reasons are coking, wear or a sticking needle, so the injector delivers too little or opens late.",["Injector of cylinder 11 coked, worn or sticking (delivers too little)","Injector correction code missing or wrong after replacement","Poor fuel quality or contamination promoting deposits","Disturbed crankshaft speed signal"],["MIL on after two trips","Rough idle or uneven running at low load","Possibly harder starting or more smoke"],3,1,["P232B","P232E","P02DF","P0211","P01DF","P0311"],""],P232D:["Cylinder 12 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit","The offset-learning codes for injector A of cylinders 1 to 10 sit at P02CC to P02DF; cylinders 11 and 12 were placed separately at P232B to P232E, and P232D is the lower limit for cylinder 12, the last cylinder of a V12. The engine module calibrates each injector in overrun with small test injections and crankshaft-acceleration feedback (GM: test quantity around 1.5 mm³, values kept per rail pressure level).",["Injector of cylinder 12 leaking or opening early","Correction code not programmed after fitting a new injector","Crankshaft signal disturbed (tone wheel, sensor, flywheel)"],["Check engine light on","Possibly harsher combustion noise or knocking at idle","Possibly more smoke or consumption"],3,1,["P232E","P232B","P02DE","P0212","P01E2","P0312"],""],P232E:["Cylinder 12 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit","P232E closes the row of injector A offset-learning codes: cylinder 12, upper limit. The learned extra energizing time for this injector has run to the top of its range for at least one rail pressure level, meaning the injector needs much longer activation than its nominal map to give the expected small-quantity torque – it under-delivers or opens late, often from coking or wear.",["Injector of cylinder 12 coked or worn (delivers too little)","Injector correction code missing or wrong","High resistance in the injector wiring slowing the opening"],["MIL on after two trips","Uneven idle, possibly harder starting","Often no other noticeable change"],3,1,["P232D","P232C","P02DF","P0212","P01E1","P0312"],""],P232F:["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P232F checks the downstream oxygen signal of bank 1 while fuel is cut on deceleration and the exhaust holds almost pure air. GM uses it on the 2023 6.6L L5P Duramax (Silverado HD, Sierra HD): the O2 value of sensor 2, the downstream NOx sensor, is compared with that of sensor 1 once the latter is stable in overrun; if the filtered difference leaves the window of +3.01 % to −3.18 %, a Type B fault is stored.",["Downstream sensor drifting or aged (on GM diesels the O2 signal of NOx sensor 2)","Exhaust leak near the downstream sensor","Damaged sensor wiring or connector (chafing, corrosion)","Leaking injector or upstream sensor fault distorting the overrun comparison"],["Check engine light on","Usually no change in driving behaviour","MIL only after two trips with the fault (GM Type B)"],1,1,["P2379","P239E","P2297","P2C65","P013A","P013E","P2270","P0136"],""],P2330:["Ignition Coil K Primary Control Circuit Low","P2330 belongs to coil K, the eleventh coil, which only twelve-cylinder petrol engines have – V12 units such as those built by BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Lamborghini or Ferrari, or the VW group's W12. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the published coil lists stop earlier (Ford at J, GM at H).",["Coil K shorted internally","Coil K control wire damaged and grounded in the bank harness","Coil K driver in the engine module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 11 not firing","Slight roughness, often hard to feel on a V12"],3,3,["P2331","P2332","P0361","P2333","P0311"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ K — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2331:["Ignition Coil K Primary Control Circuit High","P2331 is the short-to-power version for coil K, cylinder 11 in a straightforward count. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; neither Ford nor GM, whose OBD descriptions explain the primary codes in detail, build engines with eleven or more coils.",["Coil K signal wire shorted to a supply wire","Coil K with internal leakage","Engine module output for coil K defective"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 11 may be fuel-cut temporarily","Slightly uneven idle"],3,3,["P2330","P0361","P2334","P2328","P0311"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ K — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2332:["Ignition Coil K Secondary Circuit","P2332 reserves a code for trouble between coil K and the plug of cylinder 11. No manufacturer documents it publicly: the only published secondary-circuit series, FCA's ion-current codes, covers coils 1 to 8, and twelve-cylinder makers do not release their code lists. Ion-current sensing, known from Saab's Direct Ignition, would be one way to detect such a fault; another is evaluating the secondary voltage.",["Coil K boot perforated","Oil in the plug well of cylinder 11","Spark plug of cylinder 11 worn out"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 11 (P0311)","Faint vibration at idle"],3,1,["P2330","P2331","P2335","P0361","P0311"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ K — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2333:["Ignition Coil L Primary Control Circuit Low","P2333 is the ground-short code for coil L, the twelfth and final coil letter in the SAE scheme. It fits only V12 or W12 engines. There is no public manufacturer documentation for it; the published lists of Ford and GM end at coils J and H.",["Coil L shorted internally","Coil L control wire chafed to ground","Damaged or corroded coil L connector","Coil L output stage in the engine module failed"],["Check engine light on","One cylinder (usually 12) not firing","Mild roughness at idle"],3,3,["P2334","P2335","P0362","P2330","P0312"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ L — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2334:["Ignition Coil L Primary Control Circuit High","P2334, the last primary-side coil code of the series, reports a short to voltage on the coil L trigger line. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; it can only occur on engines with twelve individual coils.",["Coil L control wire shorted to a voltage source","Coil L internally faulty","Engine module output for coil L defective"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder 12 intermittently dead","Hardly noticeable loss of smoothness"],3,3,["P2333","P0362","P2331","P0312"],"ראשי סליל הצתה‏ L — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2335:["Ignition Coil L Secondary Circuit","P2335 closes the ignition coil block of J2012: a fault on the high-voltage side of coil L, the twelfth coil. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and none of the reviewed ion-sensing or secondary-monitoring documents reaches past coil 8. Its practical relevance is therefore small;",["Spark plug of cylinder 12 worn","Coil L boot cracked","Coil L secondary winding weak"],["Check engine light on, possibly flashing with heavy misfire","Misfire on cylinder 12 (P0312)"],3,1,["P2333","P2334","P2332","P0362","P0312"],"משני סליל הצתה‏ L — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2336:["Cylinder 1 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","The engine module listens to the knock sensors and assigns each vibration burst to the cylinder whose combustion falls into that crank-angle window, so it can retard spark on one cylinder alone. P2336 means the knock intensity attributed to cylinder 1 has exceeded the calibrated threshold.",["Engine damage from machining debris or casting sand (Stellantis 2.0L PHEV, bulletin 09-009-26)","Carbon deposits or hot spots in cylinder 1","Fuel with too low octane rating","Cylinder 1 running lean (injector delivering too little)"],["Check engine light on","Knocking or pinging noise from the engine","Less power because spark is retarded"],3,1,["P2337","P2338","P2339","P0324","P0325","P0301"],""],P2337:["Cylinder 2 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2337 is the cylinder 2 entry of the per-cylinder knock series P2336–P2347. Using crank position, the engine module splits the knock sensor signal into one window per combustion event and compares the vibration level in cylinder 2's window with its threshold; above it the code is stored and spark for that cylinder is pulled back.",["Internal damage from debris left in the engine (Stellantis 2.0L PHEV)","Deposits on piston or valves of cylinder 2","Wrong or worn spark plug in cylinder 2","Mechanical noise falling into cylinder 2's knock window"],["MIL on","Audible knocking, especially under load","Reduced power or sluggish acceleration"],3,1,["P2336","P2338","P2339","P0324","P0326","P0302"],""],P2338:["Cylinder 3 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2338 sets when the knock signal assigned to cylinder 3 rises above its threshold. Because one or two knock sensors serve several cylinders, the module relies on the crank-angle window to tell which cylinder knocked; a code for just one cylinder therefore suggests something local: carbon build-up, a hot spot, a lean-running injector, a wrong spark plug, or mechanical noise that happens to fall into that window.",["Carbon build-up or a hot spot in cylinder 3","Injector of cylinder 3 delivering too little (lean, hot combustion)","Engine damage from casting sand or chips (Stellantis 2.0L PHEV)","Knock sensor loose or wrongly torqued, picking up noise"],["Check engine light on","Pinging under acceleration","Noticeably less power"],3,1,["P2336","P2337","P2339","P0324","P0327","P0303"],""],P2339:["Cylinder 4 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2339 covers cylinder 4. On a four-cylinder engine this is the last cylinder of the series, which is why Stellantis bulletin 09-009-26 lists exactly P2336 to P2339 for the 2.0L turbo PHEV (sales code ECX, Jeep Wrangler 4xe 2024–2025, Grand Cherokee 2023–2025): any of the four codes with the MIL on, often together with a knocking noise, qualifies for an engine replacement under an extended warranty because of…",["Machining debris or casting sand damaging the engine (Stellantis bulletin 09-009-26)","Low-octane fuel or high intake temperature","Deposits raising compression in cylinder 4"],["MIL on","Knocking noise from the engine compartment","Reduced power"],3,1,["P2336","P2337","P2338","P2340","P0324","P0331","P0304"],""],P233A:["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Control Circuit/Open","Fuel pressure regulator C is a third pressure actuator that only a few high-pressure systems have; which valve carries the letter is up to the manufacturer. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B assigns C to a second fuel metering unit valve on the pump, driven by the ECM through a high-side and a low-side switch. P233A is logged when, with the valve commanded on, almost no current flows between the two drivers, i.e.",["Valve connector loose, corroded or a terminal pushed back","Engine harness wire broken where it rubs on brackets or clamps","Coil of the metering valve interrupted","Output driver in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine light on in the first trip","Rail pressure deviates, hesitation or reduced power","Possibly hard starting or stalling"],2,3,["P233B","P233C","P2C00","P0090","P2294"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P233B:["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Control Circuit Low","P233B points to the ground side of fuel pressure regulator C: the line between valve and low-side driver has contact with ground. In GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B, regulator C is the second fuel metering unit valve, and the ECM checks this line while the driver is switched off. If the voltage there is too low, meaning less than about 0.5 Ohm towards ground, the sample counts as failed;",["Insulation of the control wire worn through against engine or bracket","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the valve connector","Metering valve winding shorted to its housing","Low-side driver in the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine light on immediately","Rail pressure too high or unstable, rough running","Reduced engine power possible"],2,3,["P233A","P233C","P2C00","P0091","P2295"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P233C:["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Control Circuit High","With P233C the ECM sees the control line of fuel pressure regulator C pulled towards battery voltage. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B runs this test while the low-side driver of the second metering unit valve is switched on: if the voltage across the driver stays high, the line evidently has a path to power of less than about 0.5 Ohm.",["Control wire chafed against a battery-fed wire in the harness","Damaged valve connector with pins touching","Shorted turns in the metering valve coil","Low-side driver in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine light on immediately","Long cranking or no start","Reduced power, sometimes stalling"],2,3,["P233A","P233B","P2C00","P0092","P2296"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P233D:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Solenoid Supply Voltage Control Circuit/Open","Where the ECM switches the solenoid of fuel pressure regulator B on both sides, the ground-side line is checked under P2294 to P2296 and the feed from the high-side driver under P233D to P233F. P233D is the open-circuit code for that feed.",["Supply wire to the regulator solenoid broken or terminal loose","Corrosion at the regulator connector","Regulator solenoid winding open","High-side driver in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Rail pressure not controllable, reduced power","Possibly hard starting or stalling"],2,3,["P233E","P233F","P2294","P2293","P00C8"],"מתח אספקה סולנואיד וסת לחץ דלק‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P233E:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Solenoid Supply Voltage Control Circuit Low","P233E concerns the feed side of fuel pressure regulator B: the line from the ECM's high-side driver to the solenoid is shorted to ground. GM documents it for its 2025 diesels (table 25OBDG04A); there, regulator B means the rail pressure regulator valve. The ECM looks at the voltage across the high-side driver while it is switched on;",["Supply wire to the regulator rubbed through to ground","Regulator solenoid shorted internally or to its housing","Water or corrosion in the regulator connector","High-side driver in the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine light on in the first trip","Reduced power, rail pressure deviation","Hard starting or stalling possible"],2,3,["P233D","P233F","P2295","P2293","P00C9"],"מתח אספקה סולנואיד וסת לחץ דלק‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P233F:["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Solenoid Supply Voltage Control Circuit High","P233F is set when the feed line of the fuel pressure regulator B solenoid carries voltage even though the ECM has its high-side driver switched off. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04A describes this test for the rail pressure regulator valve: in the off state the voltage across the driver should be large; if it is low, the line is fed from elsewhere, as if tied to power through less than half an ohm.",["Regulator supply wire touching a battery or ignition feed","Bent or bridged pins in the regulator connector","High-side driver in the engine control module stuck on"],["Check engine light on in the first trip","Rail pressure too high or unstable","Reduced engine power possible"],2,3,["P233D","P233E","P2296","P2293","P00CA"],"מתח אספקה סולנואיד וסת לחץ דלק‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2340:["Cylinder 5 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2340 reports knock above threshold for cylinder 5, so it can only occur on engines with at least five cylinders – inline-five, six-cylinder, V8 or larger. The principle matches the rest of the series: the module evaluates the knock sensor signal in the crank-angle window of each combustion and retards spark individually when one cylinder knocks. No manufacturer was found that documents P2340 publicly;",["Carbon deposits or glowing particles in cylinder 5","Injector of cylinder 5 delivering too little","Wrong heat range or damaged spark plug","Mechanical damage in cylinder 5 (piston, valve)"],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Less power, higher consumption"],2,1,["P2341","P2339","P2342","P0324","P0330","P0305"],""],P2341:["Cylinder 6 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","Cylinder 6 is the last cylinder of inline-six and V6 engines, and P2341 reports that its share of the knock sensor signal has crossed the limit. Modern knock control adjusts ignition timing for every cylinder on its own, so a single cylinder can run retarded while the others keep optimum spark; the code tells which one keeps knocking.",["Fuel octane too low for the engine","Deposits in the combustion chamber of cylinder 6","Loose component or valve train noise read as knock","Lean mixture in cylinder 6 from a restricted injector"],["MIL on","Knocking at full throttle or uphill","Reduced power"],2,1,["P2340","P2342","P0324","P0326","P0331","P0306"],""],P2342:["Cylinder 7 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2342 applies only to engines with seven or more cylinders, in practice V8s and larger. It says the vibration picked up by the knock sensor during cylinder 7's combustion window has exceeded the threshold. On a V8 each bank usually has its own sensor, so the module has to combine sensor choice and crank angle to blame the right cylinder; noise from a loose bracket or the valve train in that window can mimic knock.",["Loose bracket, heat shield or valve train noise in cylinder 7's window","Deposits or hot spots in cylinder 7","Knock sensor of that bank loose or wrongly torqued","Low-octane fuel (usually affects several cylinders)"],["Check engine light on","Possibly audible knocking under load","Less power from retarded ignition"],2,1,["P2341","P2343","P0324","P0330","P0332","P0307"],""],P2343:["Cylinder 8 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2343 belongs to cylinder 8, the last cylinder of a V8, and is stored when the knock intensity measured in that cylinder's crank-angle window stays above the calibrated limit. The knock control first answers with spark retard for cylinder 8 alone, and on turbocharged engines it may also lower boost; the code marks that this cylinder keeps knocking.",["Carbon build-up in cylinder 8","Fuel grade below the requirement","Wrong plug type or gap in cylinder 8","Cylinder 8 running lean from low injector delivery"],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking, mostly under load","Reduced power, possibly less boost on turbo engines"],2,1,["P2342","P2341","P2344","P0324","P0332","P0308"],""],P2344:["Cylinder 9 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","A ninth cylinder exists only on V10 and V12 engines, so P2344 is confined to a small group of vehicles: V10s such as Ford's 6.8L Triton in E-Series vans, Super Duty pickups and the Excursion, the Dodge Viper and Ram SRT-10, and performance cars from BMW, Audi and Lamborghini, plus the V12s.",["Deposits or hot spots in cylinder 9","Fuel of too low octane for a high-output engine","Wrong or fouled spark plug in cylinder 9"],["MIL on","Knocking or pinging under heavy load or towing","Reduced power"],2,1,["P2345","P2343","P2346","P0324","P0325","P0309"],""],P2345:["Cylinder 10 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2345 is the knock code for cylinder 10, the last cylinder of a V10, so it appears mainly on engines such as Ford's 6.8L Triton truck V10, the Viper V10 used by Dodge, and the V10s of BMW M5/M6, Audi and Lamborghini. It sets when the knock signal belonging to cylinder 10's firing window stays over the calibrated limit; the module then keeps that cylinder's spark retarded.",["High load, towing or high intake temperature with marginal fuel","Carbon deposits in cylinder 10","Valve train noise interpreted as knock"],["Check engine light on","Pinging when towing or climbing","Loss of power"],2,1,["P2344","P2346","P0324","P0330","P0310"],""],P2346:["Cylinder 11 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","Cylinders 11 and 12 exist only on V12 engines, for example BMW's V12 in the 7 and 8 Series, Mercedes-Benz's M120 and its successors, and the V12s of Ferrari, Lamborghini and Aston Martin. P2346 reports that cylinder 11 has knocked above the threshold that the knock control allows in its crank-angle window.",["Deposits or hot spots in cylinder 11","Fuel below the required octane rating","Disturbed crank or knock sensor signal shifting the cylinder assignment"],["MIL on","Slight loss of power","Possibly audible pinging"],2,1,["P2345","P2347","P0324","P0325","P0311"],""],P2347:["Cylinder 12 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","P2347 ends the per-cylinder knock series that starts with P2336 for cylinder 1; it is the code for cylinder 12 and thus appears only on V12 engines such as those from BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Ferrari or Lamborghini. The engine module has found that the vibration in cylinder 12's combustion window exceeds the threshold and is holding back that cylinder's spark.",["Carbon deposits in cylinder 12","Low-octane or contaminated fuel","Cylinder 12 running lean (restricted injector)","Mechanical noise near the sensor of that bank"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power","Possibly knocking under load"],2,1,["P2346","P2345","P2336","P0324","P0330","P0312"],""],P2348:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit","A cylinder pressure sensor, usually built into the glow plug of a diesel, reports the combustion pressure of one cylinder so the ECM can trim injection for it. P2348 is the general circuit code for the sensor of cylinder 9, meant for modules that do not split faults into low and high.",["Sensor or glow plug connector of cylinder 9 loose or corroded","Reference, signal or ground wire damaged","Pressure sensor electronics faulty"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable change in driving","Possibly slightly harsher combustion noise"],2,1,["P2349","P234A","P234B","P234C","P0395","P2352"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2349:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2349 is the plausibility code for the combustion pressure sensor of cylinder 9: the signal is electrically valid but does not match what the ECM expects for the operating point. CARB requires input sensors to be checked for rationality where feasible, in both directions. A natural test point is overrun, when no fuel burns and the peak pressure should match the pure compression pressure;",["Sensor drift from combustion deposits","Glow plug seat leaking or plug tightened to wrong torque","Genuinely low compression in cylinder 9 distorting the comparison"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable driveability change"],2,1,["P2348","P234A","P234B","P234D","P0396","P2353"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P234A:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P234A means the signal of the cylinder 9 combustion pressure sensor stays below its permitted minimum. No published manufacturer document covers cylinder 9; the closest pattern is the GM-built 2.0 CDTI diesel of the Saab 9-5, whose cylinder 1–4 low codes (P0397 for cylinder 1) set after more than 2 s below threshold with the engine running, checked once per operating cycle, as Type B – the MIL comes on after the…",["5 V reference interrupted or shorted to ground","Signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor in the glow plug defective"],["Check engine light after two trips","Peak pressure reads 0 kPa on the scan tool","Driving behaviour mostly unchanged"],2,1,["P234B","P2348","P2349","P234C","P0397","P2354"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P234B:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P234B is stored when the cylinder 9 combustion pressure sensor signal sits above its upper limit. Nobody documents this cylinder-9 code openly, so the description borrows from the Saab 9-5 diesel (GM 2.0 CDTI): its high codes for cylinders 1–4 (P0398 for cylinder 1) need more than 2 s above threshold with the engine running, are tested once per operating cycle and are Type B.",["Connector at the cylinder 9 glow plug not plugged in","Sensor ground or signal wire interrupted","Reference or signal wire shorted to voltage"],["Check engine light after two trips","Peak pressure shows an implausibly high fixed value","No obvious drivability complaint"],2,1,["P234A","P2348","P2349","P234C","P0398","P2355"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P234C:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P234C covers a cylinder 9 combustion pressure signal that jumps or briefly drops out instead of staying permanently low or permanently high. As an analogue only the Saab 9-5 diesel (a GM 2.0 CDTI) is published: its erratic codes for cylinders 1–4 (P0399 for cylinder 1) react much faster than the low/high codes, already once the signal has left its window for longer than 0.2 s while the engine runs, and they are Type…",["Intermittent contact at the glow plug connector","Harness rubbing on the cylinder head, breaking contact under vibration","Sensor electronics unstable at high temperature"],["Check engine light, often coming and going","Fault stored but hard to reproduce in the workshop"],2,1,["P2348","P234A","P234B","P2349","P0399","P2356"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P234D:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Too Low","Unlike the sensor circuit codes, P234D judges the pressure itself: the value measured or modelled for cylinder 9 stays below what the ECM expects, while the sensor is electrically in order. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and the cylinder-1 analogue P039A is equally undocumented by code;",["Injector of cylinder 9 delivering too little or clogged","Compression loss from valve or piston ring wear","Combustion gas escaping at the glow plug seat","Pressure sensor reading too low"],["Check engine light on","Rough running, especially at idle","More smoke and higher fuel consumption"],3,1,["P234E","P2349","P2351","P0309","P039A","P2357"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — ערך נמוך מדי"],P234E:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Too High","P234E reports that the pressure determined for cylinder 9 exceeds the expected maximum. No manufacturer documents the cylinder-9 code publicly. The sibling codes for cylinders 1–4 appear in two Audi bulletins for the 2015 S3, a petrol engine: they lit the EPC lamp together with misfire codes and turned out to be a software fault that misjudged combustion, cured by a software update.",["Engine software misjudging combustion (update available at some makers)","Injector of cylinder 9 leaking or injecting too much","Pressure sensor reading too high"],["Warning lamp on, sometimes with misfire codes","Harsh, knocking combustion noise","Loss of power if the cylinder is shut off"],2,3,["P234D","P2349","P2351","P0309","P039B","P2358"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — ערך גבוה מדי"],P234F:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Variation Low","P234F flags that the pressure signal of cylinder 9 changes too little: the rise and fall the ECM expects across each combustion cycle is missing or very small. For cylinder 9 there is no manufacturer documentation. In the Saab 9-5 with GM's 2.0 CDTI, the cylinder-1 analogue is P039C, labelled pressure variation too low, with three sub-faults;",["Sensing element of the glow plug stuck by carbon","Sensor lost sensitivity through ageing","Cylinder 9 builds up little pressure (compression or injection fault)"],["Check engine light on","Usually no change in engine behaviour"],2,1,["P2350","P234C","P2349","P039C","P2359"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — ערך נמוך"],P2350:["Cylinder 9 Pressure Variation High","P2350 is the opposite of P234F: the cylinder 9 pressure signal swings more than plausible, with peaks or steps that do not fit the engine's operating state. No manufacturer publishes the code for cylinder 9.",["Interference or chafing on the sensor signal wire","Poor sensor ground connection","Sensor electronics in the glow plug failing","Injector of cylinder 9 dribbling after closing"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable symptoms"],2,1,["P234F","P234C","P2349","P039D","P235A"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 9 — ערך גבוה"],P2351:["Cylinder 9 Combustion Performance","P2351 does not concern the sensor but the quality of combustion in cylinder 9, as judged from the pressure trace: the energy released per cycle, or its balance against the other cylinders, falls outside the permitted window. No manufacturer documents the code publicly, nor its cylinder-1 analogue P039E.",["Injector of cylinder 9 coked, leaking or sticking","Partial compression loss in cylinder 9","Poor fuel quality or water in the fuel","Pressure sensor distorting the evaluation"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running and vibration","Increased smoke and fuel consumption"],3,1,["P234D","P234E","P2349","P0309","P039E","P235B"],"בעירת צילינדר‏ 9 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2352:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit","P2352 is the catch-all code for the electrical circuit of the cylinder 10 combustion pressure sensor, meant for engine computers that make no distinction between low and high. A tenth cylinder exists only on V10 and V12 engines. Under the bank-by-bank numbering of Ford and Audi it is the rearmost cylinder of the second bank;",["Glow plug/sensor connector of cylinder 10 not fully latched or corroded","Harness branch to the rear cylinder of the bank chafed or heat-damaged","Electronics in the pressure-sensing glow plug failed"],["Check engine light on","Engine usually runs as before","Combustion noise may become slightly harder"],2,1,["P2353","P2354","P2355","P2356","P2348","P235C","P0395"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2353:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2353 means the cylinder 10 pressure sensor delivers a signal that is electrically within limits but not believable for the current operating point – the reading is skewed, not cut off. CARB expects input sensors to be checked for such rationality faults, not just for open or shorted circuits.",["Sensor offset drifted with age and heat","Carbon on the heater rod hampers pressure transfer to the diaphragm","Replacement glow plug with calibration for another engine"],["Check engine light on","No noticeable change in engine behaviour"],2,1,["P2352","P2354","P2355","P2357","P2349","P235D","P0396"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2354:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2354 reports that the signal of the cylinder 10 pressure sensor stays below its lower limit. The pattern known for this fault type comes from Saab's 9-5 diesel with its GM 2.0 engine: its low codes for the four cylinders (P0397 on cylinder 1) demand that a running engine sees the signal under the threshold for longer than 2 s, run once per trip and are Type B, so the MIL waits for a second failed trip.",["Signal wire shorted to ground, e.g. chafed on the cylinder head","5 V reference interrupted or shorted to ground","Internal fault of the pressure-sensing glow plug"],["Check engine light after the second faulty trip","Scan tool shows peak pressure near zero for cylinder 10","Driving behaviour normally unchanged"],2,1,["P2355","P2352","P2353","P2356","P234A","P235E","P0397"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2355:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2355 means the cylinder 10 pressure signal is stuck above its upper limit. Taking the Saab 9-5 diesel with GM's 2.0 engine as the model, the Type B high codes for its four cylinders (P0398 on cylinder 1) wait until the signal has stayed above the threshold for over 2 s with the engine running.",["Signal or low reference wire open, connector pulled off","Signal or reference shorted to a voltage source","Sensor electronics driving the output high"],["Check engine light after two trips","Peak pressure for cylinder 10 frozen at a very high value","No obvious driveability complaint"],2,1,["P2354","P2352","P2353","P2356","P234B","P235F","P0398"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2356:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2356 points to a cylinder 10 pressure signal that drops out or jumps for moments instead of failing permanently. No manufacturer covers cylinder 10 publicly. For four-cylinder TDI engines, a 2014 Volkswagen bulletin lays out a sensible order: first push and pull the glow plug connector – a felt click or a plug that comes off easily is already the fault – then swap the plug with a neighbouring cylinder to see…",["Connector not fully seated, contact lost under vibration","Wire break inside the insulation or chafe point that opens intermittently","Glow plug sensor electronics failing intermittently"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Fault hard to reproduce in the workshop"],2,1,["P2352","P2354","P2355","P2353","P234C","P2360","P0399"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2357:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Too Low","P2357 is not about the wiring: the pressure measured or modelled for cylinder 10 itself is below expectation while the sensor circuit tests fine. No manufacturer publishes this code, and the cylinder-1 counterpart P039A is equally undocumented.",["Injector of cylinder 10 delivering too little fuel","Compression loss from valve leakage or worn rings","Combustion gas leaking past the glow plug seal","Pressure sensor reading too low"],["Check engine light on","Rough running, mainly at idle","More smoke and higher fuel consumption"],3,1,["P2358","P2353","P235B","P0310","P234D","P2361","P039A"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2358:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Too High","P2358 indicates that the pressure determined for cylinder 10 exceeds its upper expectation. No manufacturer documents this cylinder-10 code. The closest published cases are Audi bulletins for the 2015 S3 with the 2.0 TFSI engine code CYFB: there the pressure-too-high codes of cylinders 1 to 4 (P039B00 to P03B900) showed up with misfire codes and P130A00, the entry for a cylinder the ECM has hidden, that is, switched…",["Engine control software misjudging combustion (update available)","Injector of cylinder 10 leaking or over-delivering","Pressure sensor reading too high"],["Warning lamp on, sometimes together with misfire codes","Hard, knocking combustion noise","Reduced power if the cylinder is switched off"],2,3,["P2357","P2353","P235B","P0310","P234E","P2362","P039B"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2359:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Variation Low","P2359 means the pressure trace of cylinder 10 changes too little: the build-up through compression and combustion is flatter than the ECM expects. No manufacturer documents this code for cylinder 10. Saab's 9-5 diesel lists the cylinder-1 analogue P039C with three sub-types, 00, 01 and 02, and counts it as a signal performance fault that reacts after 0.2 s out of range;",["Heater rod stuck in carbon, pressure no longer reaches the diaphragm","Sensing element has lost sensitivity","Cylinder 10 builds up hardly any pressure"],["Check engine light on","Engine behaviour usually unchanged"],2,1,["P235A","P2356","P2353","P234F","P2363","P039C"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — ערך נמוך"],P235A:["Cylinder 10 Pressure Variation High","P235A is the counterpart to P2359: the cylinder 10 pressure signal swings more than the combustion can explain, with spikes or steps from one cycle to the next. A public manufacturer description of this tenth-cylinder code does not exist. In the Saab 9-5 diesel the cylinder-1 version P039D belongs to the signal performance group; it is Type B and responds within 0.2 s of leaving its window.",["Interference on a damaged or poorly shielded signal wire","Poor engine ground or corroded ground point","Sensor electronics delivering an unstable signal","Injector dribbling after closing, combustion varies"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable symptoms"],2,1,["P2359","P2356","P2353","P2350","P2364","P039D"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 10 — ערך גבוה"],P235B:["Cylinder 10 Combustion Performance","P235B rates how well cylinder 10 burns, derived from its pressure curve – for instance from the energy each working cycle releases or from how it compares with the other nine cylinders of a V10. No manufacturer documents this code, nor the cylinder-1 equivalent P039E.",["Coked or worn injector of cylinder 10","Partial compression loss in cylinder 10","Air leak in the intake tract","Poor or contaminated fuel"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running and vibration","Increased smoke and fuel consumption"],3,1,["P2357","P2358","P2353","P0310","P2351","P2365","P039E"],"בעירת צילינדר‏ 10 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P235C:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit","P235C stands for a fault in the circuit of the cylinder 11 combustion pressure sensor without saying whether the signal is too low or too high. A V10 ends at cylinder 10, so only twelve-cylinder engines have an eleventh one. With bank-wise numbering, cylinder 11 is the second-to-last of the second bank, between 10 and 12.",["Connector at the cylinder 11 glow plug loose or corroded","Reference, low reference or signal wire damaged","Sensor electronics in the glow plug failed"],["Check engine light on","No change in how the engine runs"],2,1,["P235D","P235E","P235F","P2360","P2352","P2366","P0395"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P235D:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P235D is set when the combustion pressure reported for cylinder 11 is electrically valid yet does not fit the engine's state – for example a compression peak that is clearly off while no fuel is being injected. Only engines with twelve cylinders have a cylinder 11, and none of them is publicly documented with pressure sensors, so no manufacturer describes this code.",["Deposits on the heater rod distort the reading","Glow plug with calibration for another engine application fitted","Seal at the glow plug seat leaking"],["Check engine light on","Driving behaviour practically unchanged"],2,1,["P235C","P235E","P235F","P2361","P2353","P2367","P0396"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P235E:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","With P235E the signal of the cylinder 11 combustion pressure sensor is too low, typically close to zero. No manufacturer documents this code, as twelve-cylinder engines with pressure sensors are not described publicly; the analogue is P0397 for cylinder 1 in Saab's 9-5 diesel, where a low signal must persist beyond 2 s with the engine running before the Type B code is logged.",["5 V reference interrupted or shorted to ground","Signal wire chafed through to ground","Sensor glow plug outside its 3–12 Ohm specification"],["Warning lamp after the second faulty trip","Peak pressure of cylinder 11 shown as zero"],2,1,["P235F","P235C","P235D","P2360","P2354","P2368","P0397"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P235F:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P235F is logged when the cylinder 11 pressure sensor signal remains above its plausible maximum. Only twelve-cylinder engines have this cylinder, and no maker documents the code; the Saab 9-5 diesel serves as the model with P0398 for cylinder 1, a Type B code that needs more than 2 s over the threshold.",["Low reference (ground) wire of the sensor open","Signal wire interrupted or connector off","Reference or signal shorted to battery voltage","Insulation failure between sensor terminals and plug body"],["Check engine light after two trips","Implausibly high fixed pressure value for cylinder 11"],2,1,["P235E","P235C","P235D","P2360","P2355","P2369","P0398"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2360:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2360 records a cylinder 11 combustion pressure signal that is unsteady – brief dropouts or spikes that do not last long enough for a low or high code. Since only twelve-cylinder engines have cylinder 11, and none is documented with pressure sensors, the code has no public manufacturer description.",["Fretting corrosion or loose fit at the connector terminals","Harness touching hot engine parts","Sensor electronics in the plug head failing when warm"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Fault stored without a lasting complaint"],2,1,["P235C","P235E","P235F","P235D","P2356","P236A","P0399"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2361:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Too Low","P2361 says the combustion pressure of cylinder 11 is too low although the sensor works electrically. No manufacturer documents this code, since no twelve-cylinder engine with combustion pressure sensing is publicly described. What the code judges is the cylinder itself: if its peak stays clearly below that of comparable cylinders or below the expected value, combustion or compression is lacking.",["Injector of cylinder 11 with reduced flow or clogged nozzle","Worn piston rings or burnt valve lowering compression","Leak at the glow plug seat","Pressure sensor drifting low"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running, especially at idle","Possibly misfire code for cylinder 11 as well"],3,1,["P2362","P235D","P2365","P0311","P2357","P236B","P039A"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2362:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Too High","P2362 is stored when cylinder 11 shows more combustion pressure than the ECM considers plausible. No manufacturer publishes it, because no twelve-cylinder engine with cylinder pressure monitoring is documented. On a diesel, excess pressure usually comes from the fuel side: an injector that leaks or hangs open adds fuel, injection timed too early raises the peak, and a sensor drifting upward fakes the effect.",["Injector of cylinder 11 leaking or hanging open","Engine control software misjudging the pressure","Injection timing too early for this cylinder","Pressure sensor drifting high"],["Warning lamp on","Harsh combustion noise","Loss of power if the cylinder is shut off"],2,3,["P2361","P235D","P2365","P0311","P2358","P236C","P039B"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2363:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Variation Low","P2363 flags a cylinder 11 pressure signal with too little swing between its low point and the combustion peak. No manufacturer documents this code; cylinder 11 only exists on twelve-cylinder engines, none of which is publicly known with pressure-sensing glow plugs. Saab's 9-5 diesel files the related P039C for cylinder 1 as a Type B signal fault.",["Piezo-resistive sensing element has lost sensitivity","Deposits holding the heater rod in place","Genuinely low compression in cylinder 11"],["Check engine light on","Engine runs normally in most cases"],2,1,["P2364","P2360","P235D","P2359","P236D","P039C"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — ערך נמוך"],P2364:["Cylinder 11 Pressure Variation High","P2364 is stored when the pressure signal of cylinder 11 varies too strongly, from cycle to cycle or within one cycle. No maker publishes this code. Saab's 9-5 diesel has the analogous P039D for cylinder 1, a Type B signal fault reacting to 0.2 s outside its window.",["Interference coupling into the signal line","Ground connection with changing contact resistance","Moisture in the glow plug connector","Injector with unstable spray pattern"],["Check engine light on","No noticeable effect on driving"],2,1,["P2363","P2360","P235D","P235A","P236E","P039D"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 11 — ערך גבוה"],P2365:["Cylinder 11 Combustion Performance","P2365 means the ECM judges combustion in cylinder 11 to be poor, based on the pressure signal rather than on crankshaft speed alone. No manufacturer publishes this code; twelve-cylinder engines with pressure-sensing glow plugs are not documented. BorgWarner names the purpose of such sensors: letting the controller adjust injection quantity and timing per cylinder in closed loop.",["Fouled or leaking injector of cylinder 11","Compression loss in cylinder 11","Intake air leak","Contaminated fuel"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running and vibration","More smoke from the exhaust"],3,1,["P2361","P2362","P235D","P0311","P235B","P236F","P039E"],"בעירת צילינדר‏ 11 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2366:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit","P2366 is the general circuit code for the combustion pressure sensor of cylinder 12; it does not tell whether the signal sits too low or too high. Twelve is the highest number on a V12 or W12. Whether a maker counts bank by bank or along the crankshaft, number 1 is normally the front cylinder, which places 12 at the opposite end of the engine.",["Glow plug connector not fully latched or loose","Damaged wire in the harness branch to the rearmost cylinder","Pressure-sensing glow plug faulty"],["Check engine light on","Pressure reading for cylinder 12 missing or fixed in live data"],2,1,["P2367","P2368","P2369","P236A","P235C","P2352","P0395"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2367:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","With P2367 the cylinder 12 pressure signal is electrically within its limits but makes no sense for the operating point. A natural yardstick is the motored cycle: on overrun nothing burns, so the curve has to peak at top dead centre.",["Sensor zero point or gain drifted","Combustion gas escaping at the glow plug seat","Glow plug of a different calibration fitted"],["Check engine light on","Implausible peak pressure value for cylinder 12 compared with the others"],2,1,["P2366","P2368","P2369","P236B","P235D","P2353","P0396"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2368:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2368 is stored when the voltage coming from the cylinder 12 pressure sensor stays below its lower limit. As the last cylinder of a V12 or W12, it has no publicly documented application, so Saab's 9-5 diesel code P0397 serves as the template. There, the scan tool shows peak combustion pressure in a normal band of 0 to 9,000 kPa; a signal wire touching ground or a missing 5 V reference pins the value at the bottom.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference open or shorted to ground","Sensor electronics in the glow plug head failed low"],["Warning lamp after two trips with the fault","Peak pressure of cylinder 12 stuck near zero"],2,1,["P2369","P2366","P2367","P236A","P235E","P2354","P0397"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2369:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2369 means the cylinder 12 pressure input reads above its upper limit. Like the rest of the cylinder-12 family, it is not documented publicly by any maker. On Saab's 9-5 diesel the matching cylinder-1 code P0398 is set after more than 2 s above the threshold and is evaluated once per operating cycle.",["Signal or low-reference wire open","Signal shorted to a voltage source","Glow plug sensor electronics outputting a fixed high value"],["Check engine light after the second trip","Cylinder 12 shows an impossibly high pressure in live data"],2,1,["P2368","P2366","P2367","P236A","P235F","P2355","P0398"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P236A:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P236A covers brief, irregular disturbances of the cylinder 12 pressure signal – faults that come and go without settling into a lasting low or high state. Its model is the Saab 9-5 diesel code P0399, which responds as soon as the signal stays outside its band longer than 0.2 s. No manufacturer publishes P236A itself, since no twelve-cylinder engine with pressure glow plugs is documented.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the plug connector","Harness rubbing through under engine vibration","Glow plug sensor with intermittent internal fault"],["Warning lamp that switches on and off over several days","Pressure value of cylinder 12 jumps when the harness is moved"],2,1,["P2366","P2368","P2369","P2367","P2360","P2356","P0399"],"חיישן לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P236B:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Too Low","P236B reports that cylinder 12 builds too little combustion pressure while its sensor circuit itself is in order. No manufacturer documents the code, because no V12 or W12 with cylinder pressure measurement has been made public.",["Intake or exhaust valve of cylinder 12 not sealing","Worn piston rings or head gasket leak","Injector delivering too little fuel","Gas leaking past the glow plug seal"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle and vibration","Misfire code for cylinder 12 stored as well"],3,1,["P236C","P2367","P236F","P0312","P2361","P2357","P039A"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — ערך נמוך מדי"],P236C:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Too High","P236C flags combustion pressure in cylinder 12 above its allowed value. A public twelve-cylinder application does not exist. That a code of this kind need not involve a pressure sensor at all is shown by its cylinder-1 to -4 relatives P039B, P03A5, P03AF and P03B9 on Audi's 2015 S3 with the CYFB petrol engine: faulty ECM software logged misfires in its primary detection window, switched on the EPC lamp and shut a…",["Engine control software error (update available)","Injector dripping or delivering too much pilot fuel","Pressure sensor drifting upward"],["EPC or check engine lamp on","Loss of power when the cylinder is switched off","Harder combustion noise"],2,3,["P236B","P2367","P236F","P0312","P2362","P2358","P039B"],"לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — ערך גבוה מדי"],P236D:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Variation Low","P236D is stored when the cylinder 12 pressure trace swings too little – the curve stays flatter than compression and combustion ought to make it. No manufacturer documents this code for a twelve-cylinder engine. In Saab's 9-5 diesel the comparable cylinder-1 code P039C exists in three sub-variants, 00, 01 and 02, a sign that the ECM tells apart several ways in which a signal can be too weak.",["Carbon deposits restricting the heater rod","Sensor electronics with reduced gain","Actual low compression in cylinder 12"],["Check engine light on","Flat pressure curve for cylinder 12 in live data"],2,1,["P236E","P236A","P2367","P236B","P2363","P2359","P039C"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — ערך נמוך"],P236E:["Cylinder 12 Pressure Variation High","P236E means the pressure signal of cylinder 12 scatters more than the ECM tolerates, either within one cycle or from one cycle to the next. No manufacturer publishes the code; the reference is Saab's P039D for cylinder 1, a Type B fault that needs only 0.2 s outside its window. Two groups of causes are possible.",["Interference on the signal wire","Low-reference contact with changing resistance","Injector delivery varying from shot to shot","Air in the fuel supply"],["Check engine light on","Occasional slight roughness"],2,1,["P236D","P236A","P2367","P236F","P2364","P235A","P039D"],"סטיית לחץ צילינדר‏ 12 — ערך גבוה"],P236F:["Cylinder 12 Combustion Performance","P236F is the ECM's verdict that combustion in cylinder 12 falls short, judged from the evaluated pressure curve rather than from a single limit. No manufacturer documents it, as no twelve-cylinder engine with cylinder pressure sensing is public. BorgWarner states that its pressure glow plug lets the controller correct, cylinder by cylinder, how much fuel is injected and when, with the measured pressure as feedback.",["Injector of cylinder 12 coked or worn","Weak compression in cylinder 12","Contaminated or poor-quality fuel","Restricted intake path"],["Check engine light on","Rough running","More visible exhaust smoke"],3,1,["P236B","P236C","P2367","P0312","P2365","P235B","P039E"],"בעירת צילינדר‏ 12 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2370:["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit/Open","A fuel volume regulator is the solenoid valve at the high-pressure pump that decides how much of the pump's stroke reaches the rail. Regulator B only exists where a second valve or second pump is fitted – the 5.2 litre V10 of Audi and Lamborghini, for instance, has two cam-driven high-pressure pumps for its two rails. No manufacturer documents P2370 publicly;",["Connector at regulator B loose or corroded","Regulator coil burnt open","Broken high-side or low-side wire"],["Check engine light on","Rail pressure deviation and possible reduced power","Hard starting"],2,3,["P2371","P2372","P2373","P0001","P0087","P0088"],"וסת נפח דלק‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2371:["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit Performance","P2371 is a functional fault of the second fuel volume regulator: the control circuit works electrically, but the valve does not achieve what the ECM asks of it. No manufacturer publishes a definition for regulator B, so the A side helps.",["Regulator B valve sticking from dirt or wear","High-pressure pump B worn","ECM driver stage overheating"],["Check engine light on","Rail pressure fluctuates or misses its target","Reduced power under load"],3,3,["P2370","P2372","P2373","P0002","P0087","P0088","P0089"],"וסת נפח דלק‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2372:["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit Low","P2372 says the line driving fuel volume regulator B is pulled too low, as a rule by contact with ground. No manufacturer documents this B code publicly; it mirrors P0003 on regulator A. Ford's 2023 diesel detects that condition with the valve switched off: the voltage reported by the driver chip then falls below 2.8 V, where about 5 V would be normal.",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Moisture in the regulator connector","Internal short in the regulator coil"],["Check engine light on","Rail pressure too high or too low depending on the affected side","Limp-home with reduced power"],2,3,["P2373","P2370","P2371","P0003","P0087"],"וסת נפח דלק‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2373:["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit High","P2373 points to too much voltage or current in the control circuit of fuel volume regulator B, typically from a short to battery voltage or a shorted coil. No manufacturer publishes the B version; P0004 on regulator A is the model. Ford's 2023 diesel sets that code when the energised valve draws more than 3.7 A, while 2.2 A is the normal maximum.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Regulator coil with shorted turns drawing excess current","ECM output stage faulty"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power or limp-home mode","Rail pressure deviation codes stored as well"],2,3,["P2372","P2370","P2371","P0004","P0088"],"וסת נפח דלק‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2374:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit","P2374 covers any wiring or sensor-side failure of a second pressure sensor mounted upstream of a compressor. Where the letter B belongs is the manufacturer's choice; on parallel twin-turbo V engines, where each turbocharger serves one cylinder bank, a second inlet sensor for the other compressor is the obvious candidate.",["Connector or wire of sensor B open, corroded or shorted","Sensor B reports an internal error","Sensor supply voltage missing"],["Check engine light on","Reduced boost or power"],1,3,["P2375","P2376","P2377","P2378","P012A"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת מגדש‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2375:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","With P2375 the signal of compressor inlet pressure sensor B is electrically valid but implausible – stuck, offset or out of step with the other pressure values. No manufacturer publishes the B code; GM's 2018 table for the supercharged LT4 V8 describes the A counterpart P012B in detail.",["Sensor B drifted or stuck","Air filter on the side of compressor B clogged","Leaking or collapsed duct ahead of compressor B"],["Check engine light after two trips","Uneven boost between the two turbochargers","Reduced power"],1,3,["P2374","P2376","P2377","P2378","P012B","P0106"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת מגדש‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2376:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","P2376 is set when the output voltage of compressor inlet pressure sensor B drops below its lower limit. No maker documents the B code publicly; GM's A version P012C on the supercharged LT4 gives an idea of the scale. There the threshold is 3 % of the 5 V reference, equal to roughly 6 kPa – a value no intake can reach in reality.",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","5 V reference to sensor B open","Sensor B failed"],["Check engine light on","Live data show an inlet pressure far below ambient","Possible boost limitation"],1,3,["P2377","P2374","P2375","P2378","P012C"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת מגדש‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2377:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","P2377 means sensor B ahead of the compressor delivers a voltage above its upper limit. Publicly no manufacturer defines this B code, so GM's P012D for the supercharged LT4 serves as a reference: it trips above 97 % of the 5 V reference, which equals about 124 kPa at that sensor, again with 320 failed samples out of 400 at 12.5 ms intervals and Type B.",["Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor ground of sensor B open","Moisture bridging terminals in the connector"],["Check engine light on","Implausibly high inlet pressure in live data"],1,3,["P2376","P2374","P2375","P2378","P012D"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת מגדש‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2378:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2378 records a signal from compressor inlet pressure sensor B that jumps or briefly drops out without staying beyond a limit. No manufacturer documents it publicly, and even for the A sensor a dedicated erratic code is rare: GM's LT4 table catches short spikes only through the counting window of its low and high checks (320 of 400 samples), and Ford's 2023 diesels fold faults of their digital sensor into P012A.",["Loose terminals at sensor B","Harness damaged by heat from the turbocharger","Moisture in the sensor connector"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Brief hesitation under boost"],2,3,["P2374","P2376","P2377","P2375","P012E"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת מגדש‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2379:["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P2379 covers the oxygen sensor behind the catalyst on bank 2 at the moment the injectors are shut off on a closed throttle: the exhaust is then close to fresh air, and a sensor whose reading stays outside the expected lean window is suspect. No manufacturer documents P2379 publicly.",["Bank 2 downstream sensor aged or contaminated, reacting too little to fuel cut","Exhaust leak near the bank 2 rear sensor diluting or distorting the sample","Chafed sensor lead or corroded connector on the bank 2 rear sensor","Leaking injector on bank 2 keeping fuel in the exhaust during overrun"],["Check engine light on","No noticeable change in how the car drives","Downstream O2 reading on bank 2 stays high during coasting in live data"],1,1,["P232F","P239F","P239E","P2298","P013C","P014A","P2272","P2273"],""],P237A:["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","P237A says the rear oxygen sensor of bank 1 is not getting, or not reporting, a representative sample of exhaust: its reading does not fit the gas that should be flowing past it after the catalyst, typically because outside air enters through a leak or the sensing element is no longer exposed properly. No manufacturer documents P237A publicly.",["Leak at a flange, joint or cracked pipe ahead of the bank 1 rear sensor drawing in air","Rear sensor element damaged, coated or loose in its boss","Contaminated or blocked reference air path of the sensor (wiring or connector)"],["Check engine light on","Catalyst monitor not completing or reporting implausible results","Possible ticking exhaust noise from a leak"],2,1,["P237B","P23A0","P2414","P0136","P232F"],""],P237B:["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","P237B is the bank 2 version of the sample check on the post-catalyst oxygen sensor and therefore only appears on engines with two exhaust banks, mostly V6 and V8 units with a separate downstream sensor on each side. The ECM decides that what the sensor reports cannot be genuine exhaust from that bank, for example because a leak at the second-bank pipe lets air in or the probe is mounted badly.",["Air leak in the bank 2 exhaust between catalyst and rear sensor","Bank 2 rear sensor damaged, poisoned or not seated correctly","Rear sensors of bank 1 and bank 2 swapped at the connectors after a repair"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 catalyst monitor incomplete or failing","Engine runs as usual"],2,1,["P237A","P23A1","P2415","P0156","P2379"],""],P237C:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Control Circuit/Open","Some hybrids route the exhaust through a coolant heat exchanger after a cold start to warm the engine and cabin sooner, and flap A sends the gas around it once heat is no longer wanted. P237C is set when the drive circuit of that bypass actuator shows an open or a general circuit fault.",["Water inside the heat exchanger assembly or actuator (Ford Maverick SSM 51921)","Bypass valve actuator with open winding or failed electronics","Broken wire or loose connector in the hot area under the vehicle"],["Check engine light on","Engine and cabin may warm up more slowly in cold weather","Further heat exchanger codes such as P2C22 stored alongside"],3,1,["P237D","P237E","P237F","P23A2","P2C22","P2C23"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P237D:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Control Circuit Low","P237D concerns the same drive line as P237C, the one that operates bypass flap A of an exhaust heat recovery unit, but here the module measures a voltage that sits too low – the usual picture of a control wire touching ground or an actuator shorted internally. Moisture in a connector under the car can produce exactly that.",["Water in the heat exchanger or its actuator shorting the drive (Maverick)","Actuator internally shorted to ground","Control wire chafed through against the body or exhaust bracket"],["Check engine light on","Slower heater response after a cold start","Car otherwise drives normally"],3,1,["P237C","P237E","P237F","P23A3","P2C22"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P237E:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Control Circuit High","P237E is logged when the driver for exhaust bypass flap A on a heat recovery unit sees a control voltage above its expected range. The likely story is a short from the control wire to a supply feed or an actuator whose internal driver has failed in a way that pulls the line up. The flap then no longer follows the warm-up strategy.",["Heat exchanger bypass actuator with failed internal driver (Ford F-150 SSM 53003)","Control wire shorted to a supply circuit in the harness","Heat-damaged connector with bridged pins"],["Check engine light on","Cabin heat may build up later on cold days"],3,1,["P237C","P237D","P237F","P23A4","P2C23"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P237F:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Control Performance","P237F is not about wiring of the drive but about the result: the bypass flap A of the exhaust heat recovery unit was commanded, yet the effect the module expects does not appear. Ford judges this partly by temperatures, which is why SSM 52543 for the full hybrids F-150 3.5L (from 2021), Explorer 3.3L and Escape 2.5L (from 2020) and Maverick 2.5L (from 2022), all through 2024, first sends technicians to the…",["Water, corrosion or torn seal at the exhaust coolant temperature sensor 3/4 connectors (Ford SSM 52543)","PCM calibration setting the code falsely (2024 Maverick, TSB 24-2173)","Bypass actuator or flap sluggish, sticking or worn"],["Check engine light on","No effect on drivability","Often stored together with P2C23"],2,1,["P237C","P237D","P237E","P23A5","P2C23","P2C22"],"בקרת שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2380:["EGR Sensor D Circuit","P2380 is the general circuit code for EGR sensor D. Which sensor carries the letter D is up to the maker. Ford's 2024–2025 petrol OBD summary assigns it to the EGRP sensor, a smart EGR pressure sensor with a digital output covering 0.1 to 408.8 kPa: P2380 is stored when the sensor itself reports an internal malfunction, checked continuously while the EGR monitor runs, with 5 seconds to register the fault;",["Internal fault reported by the smart EGR pressure sensor","Corroded or loose connector at the sensor","Unstable supply or ground to the sensor"],["Check engine light on","EGR monitor not completed","Possibly slight knock tendency or higher NOx with EGR reduced"],2,1,["P2381","P2382","P2383","P2384","U0669","P0409"],"חיישן EGR‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2381:["EGR Sensor D Circuit High","P2381 means the signal of EGR sensor D is stuck at the top of its electrical range. GM's 2025 diesel ECM tables use it for the differential pressure sensor of the low-pressure EGR loop: if the raw voltage exceeds 99.83 % of the scale in 480 out of 600 samples, taken every 6.25 ms after cranking and with the powertrain relay above 11 V, GM records a Type A fault, lighting the MIL in the first trip.",["Open sensor ground or reference return","Chafed engine harness shorting the signal to a supply (GM 21-NA-149)","Differential pressure sensor failed with output at full scale"],["Check engine light on immediately","Low-pressure EGR disabled, NOx emissions rise","Other harness-related codes possible at the same time"],2,1,["P2380","P2382","P2383","P2384","P0406"],"חיישן EGR‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2382:["EGR Sensor D Circuit Low","P2382 reports that EGR sensor D delivers almost no signal voltage. In GM's 2025 diesel ECM tables this sensor measures the pressure difference across the low-pressure EGR path, and the code sets once the raw value drops below 0.02 % of range in 480 of 600 samples, sampled every 6.25 ms once the engine is out of cranking and the relay supply exceeds 11 V; it is a Type A fault with MIL on the first trip.",["Conductor broken right at the sensor connector (GM 21-NA-149)","Open 5 V reference or signal shorted to ground","Differential pressure sensor without output"],["Check engine light on in the first trip","Low-pressure EGR switched off","Fault may come and go with engine vibration"],2,1,["P2380","P2381","P2383","P2384","P0405"],"חיישן EGR‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2383:["EGR Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","P2383 flags an EGR sensor D whose signal is electrically fine but makes no sense. Two published strategies show how differently makers test it. GM's 2025 diesel ECM tables check the low-pressure EGR differential pressure sensor at key-off, when there should be no pressure difference: if the averaged reading exceeds 6 %, a Type A fault is set at once, provided no circuit or intermittent fault is present.",["Sensor hoses swapped, cracked or disconnected (Ford EGRP)","Sensor drifted so that it reads a pressure difference with the engine off (GM)","Sensing lines blocked by soot or condensate","Intermittent wire break at the sensor connector (GM 21-NA-149)"],["Check engine light on","EGR rate reduced or switched off","Often appears after work on the EGR or exhaust system"],2,1,["P2380","P2381","P2382","P2384","P0401","P0409"],"חיישן EGR‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2384:["EGR Sensor D Circuit Intermittent","P2384 marks an EGR sensor D signal that jumps or drops out for brief moments without staying at a fixed fault level. GM's 2025 diesel ECM tables apply it to the differential pressure sensor of the low-pressure EGR loop: when two successive raw readings differ by more than 10 % in 300 out of 600 samples, taken every 6.25 ms with the relay supply above 11 V and no high or low circuit fault present, a Type A fault is…",["Loose or corroded terminals at the EGR sensor D connector","Harness chafing intermittently on engine or exhaust parts","ECM software anomaly (GM 3.0L LM2 2020, bulletin 20-NA-039)","Sensor with an internal contact fault"],["MIL on, often without noticeable driving change","Code stored, cleared and returning after some drives","EGR operation reduced as a precaution"],2,1,["P2380","P2381","P2382","P2383","P2389"],"חיישן EGR‏ D — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2385:["EGR Sensor E Circuit","P2385 is the general circuit code for a fifth EGR-related sensor, labelled E. The letter is assigned by each manufacturer, so the code only makes sense on engines with an extensive set of EGR sensors, such as diesels that pair high- and low-pressure loops with several pressure and temperature probes. No manufacturer documents P2385 publicly.",["Connector of EGR sensor E unplugged, damaged or corroded","Open or shorted wire between sensor and engine control unit","Sensor electrically failed","Shared 5 V reference supply faulty"],["MIL on","EGR monitor not completing, readiness stays open","Possibly higher NOx and slightly changed engine response under load"],2,1,["P2386","P2387","P2388","P2389","P2380"],"חיישן EGR‏ E — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2386:["EGR Sensor E Circuit High","P2386 says the signal of EGR sensor E sits at or above the upper end of its electrical range. With a typical three-wire 5 V pressure or position sensor that happens when the ground is open or the signal line touches a supply voltage; on a temperature sensor wired as a pull-up, an open circuit shows the same picture. No manufacturer documents P2386 publicly.",["Open sensor ground wire or ground terminal","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor output stuck high internally"],["MIL on","EGR shut off or reduced","Scan data shows sensor E at full scale"],2,1,["P2385","P2387","P2388","P2381"],"חיישן EGR‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2387:["EGR Sensor E Circuit Low","P2387 is stored when the signal of EGR sensor E falls below its valid electrical range. On a pressure sensor with a 5 V reference that typically points to a lost reference feed, a signal wire shorted to ground or a sensor that no longer drives its output; a shorted thermistor would produce the same result on a temperature input. No manufacturer documents P2387 publicly.",["5 V reference open or pulled down by another sensor","Signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor without output signal"],["MIL on","Further low-voltage codes on sensors sharing the same reference","EGR in fallback mode"],2,1,["P2385","P2386","P2388","P2382"],"חיישן EGR‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2388:["EGR Sensor E Circuit Range/Performance","P2388 covers an EGR sensor E whose signal is electrically valid but does not agree with what the engine controller expects from the operating state. Typical tests compare the reading with a known condition, such as zero pressure difference with the engine off, or with a modelled value from other sensors. No manufacturer documents P2388 publicly.",["Sensing hoses blocked, cracked or swapped","Soot deposits at the sensor port","Sensor drifted out of calibration"],["MIL on","EGR monitor readiness not set","Sensor E reading implausible at engine off"],2,1,["P2385","P2389","P2383","P0401"],"חיישן EGR‏ E — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2389:["EGR Sensor E Circuit Intermittent","P2389 points to an EGR sensor E signal that is mostly plausible but now and then jumps, spikes or drops out. Engine controllers detect this by watching the rate of change between consecutive readings rather than absolute limits. No manufacturer documents P2389 publicly;",["Weak pin tension or unlatched connector","Harness damaged by heat or rubbing near the exhaust","Moisture in the connector","Sensor with an intermittent internal fault"],["MIL on, sometimes going out again","Fault cannot be reproduced at the workshop","Jumps visible in the sensor E data stream"],2,1,["P2385","P2386","P2387","P2384"],"חיישן EGR‏ E — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P238A:["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit","P238A is the general circuit code for water-in-fuel sensor B, used where a diesel has two water-detecting points, for example a frame-mounted primary filter and a second separator. Stellantis case file S2214000004 for 2022 Ram 2500 to 5500 trucks shows that on these vehicles the B sensor is part of the fuel filter mounted on the frame; P238A itself is not named there. No manufacturer documents P238A publicly.",["Water or corrosion in the sensor B connector at the chassis filter","Damaged harness along the frame rail","Water-in-fuel sensor B failed"],["Water-in-fuel lamp or message on","No warning for real water in the chassis filter"],1,0,["P238B","P238C","P238D","P238E","P238F","P2264"],""],P238B:["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P238B means water-in-fuel sensor B delivers a signal that is electrically valid but implausible, for instance a value stuck between the clear dry and wet states, or a self-test answer that arrives at the wrong moment. No manufacturer documents P238B publicly. On 2022 Ram heavy-duty diesels sensor B is fitted to the frame-mounted filter, exposed to road spray (Stellantis case S2214000004).",["Dirt film or deposits on the sensor electrodes","Residual water or emulsion around the probe after incomplete draining","Corroded or aged sensor"],["Water-in-fuel warning without water being found","Warning that persists after draining"],1,0,["P238A","P238F","P2265"],""],P238C:["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit Low","P238C is set when the signal line of water-in-fuel sensor B stays below its valid range. Because the sensor reads conductivity, anything that bridges its terminals or pulls the signal to ground can cause it: a chafed wire, a wet connector or a sensor body full of water. No manufacturer documents P238C publicly.",["Water bridging the terminals in the sensor connector","Signal wire chafed through to ground on the frame","Sensor resistance out of specification"],["Water-in-fuel lamp on","Fault appears after washing or rain"],1,0,["P238D","P238A","P238F","P2266"],""],P238D:["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit High","P238D reports that the signal of water-in-fuel sensor B sits above its valid range, usually from an open circuit, a disconnected sensor or a short to voltage. Stellantis case file S2214000004 documents it for 2022 Ram 2500, 3500, 4500 and 5500 trucks: the water warning lamp or message comes on at low mileage, and the cause is water that a pressure washer or similar spray drove into the plug of the filter housing on…",["Spray water in the connector at the chassis-mounted fuel filter","Corroded terminals on harness or filter housing side","Sensor in the filter housing failed","Open signal or ground wire"],["Water-in-fuel lamp or message on at low mileage","No water found when draining"],1,0,["P238C","P238A","P238F","P2267"],""],P238E:["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P238E is meant for a water-in-fuel sensor B circuit whose signal flickers or drops out for short periods instead of staying at one fault level. No manufacturer documents P238E publicly. The one published case for the same sensor explains well why such faults come and go: on 2022 Ram heavy-duty trucks Stellantis found water from road spray or pressure washing inside the plug of the frame-mounted filter, logged there…",["Moisture entering and drying out in the connector","Loose terminals losing contact on rough roads","Broken harness clips letting the wire rub on the frame"],["Water-in-fuel lamp flickering or coming and going","Fault not present when tested at the workshop"],1,0,["P238A","P238C","P238D","P2268"],""],P238F:["Water in Fuel Condition - Sensor B","P238F is no wiring fault: it states that water-in-fuel sensor B has detected water, meaning the separator at that point has collected enough to bridge the probe. Ram's 2022 heavy-duty pickups (2500 to 5500) are covered by Stellantis case S2214000004, which keeps it apart from the circuit code P238D: with P238F stored, the filter on the frame has to be emptied completely and the fuel tested for water before any…",["Water collected in the chassis filter separator","Fuel contaminated with water from tank or filling station","Separator drained incompletely after an earlier warning"],["Water-in-fuel lamp or message on","Rough running or power loss if water reaches the injection system","MIL on some vehicles"],1,1,["P238D","P238A","P2269"],""],P2390:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Circuit/Open","P2390 concerns the drive circuit of the second electronically operated intake throttle that some diesel engines carry; which flap a maker labels A or B is its own choice. With the driver switched off, the engine module checks whether the motor circuit is closed; an open wire, a pulled connector or a burnt motor winding sets this code. No manufacturer publishes P2390 with thresholds.",["Connector at the B throttle unplugged, loose or with pushed-back terminals","Broken motor lead in the harness between module and throttle","Open motor winding inside the throttle unit","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["MIL on, often without a noticeable change in driving","Particulate filter regeneration delayed or blocked","Engine may shake more when switched off because the flap no longer closes"],2,3,["P2392","P2393","P239B","P2391","P02E0"],"זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2391:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Performance","P2391 compares where the B intake throttle should be with where its position sensor says it is. If the gap stays too large under a steady command, the module concludes that the flap is sluggish or obstructed, typically by soot and oil deposits from EGR and crankcase gases, a worn gear stage or a weak motor. No published manufacturer table covers P2391.",["Soot and oil deposits making the B flap stiff","Worn plastic gears or shaft bearing in the throttle unit","Weak motor or high resistance in the drive circuit","Position sensor reporting an offset angle"],["MIL on","Regeneration of the particulate filter does not complete","Occasionally reduced power or uneven response"],2,3,["P2394","P2395","P2397","P239B","P02E1"],"בקרת זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2392:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Circuit Low","P2392 is set when the module finds the motor output for the B intake throttle pulled towards ground, for example by a chafed wire touching the engine, water inside the connector or a shorted motor. The output stage protects itself and switches off. No manufacturer documents P2392 publicly.",["Motor lead chafed through and touching engine or body ground","Water or corrosion in the throttle connector","Internal short of the throttle motor to its housing","Damaged H-bridge in the engine control module"],["MIL on, code returns immediately after clearing","Regeneration blocked or aborted","Little or no change in driving"],2,3,["P2393","P2390","P239B","P02E2"],"זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2393:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Circuit High","P2393 is the counterpart of P2392: one of the B-throttle motor leads has contact with battery voltage, for example through a pinched harness or a bridged pin in the connector, so the output stage sees an overcurrent as soon as it switches. No manufacturer publishes P2393.",["Motor lead pinched against a live wire or terminal","Bridged pins in the connector (moisture, corrosion)","Shorted turns in the throttle motor","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["MIL on","Filter regeneration not carried out","Possibly blown fuse or further circuit codes on the same supply"],2,3,["P2392","P2390","P239B","P02E3"],"זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2394:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Stuck Open","P2394 means the B intake throttle remains wider open than requested even though the module drives its motor hard towards closing. A flap that cannot throttle fails to create the manifold depression that strong exhaust recirculation and regeneration heating depend on. No manufacturer documents P2394 openly.",["Deposits holding the flap in an open position","Broken gear tooth or stripped drive between motor and shaft","Motor too weak to overcome the return spring","Foreign object or broken part blocking the flap"],["MIL on","Frequent or failing particulate filter regenerations","Engine shakes when switched off"],2,3,["P2395","P2391","P239C","P02E4","P0401"],"בקרת זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2395:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Stuck Closed","P2395 reports a B intake throttle that remains nearer to its closed stop than the module asks for. Of the two stuck faults this is the more serious one, because a flap jammed near its seat starves the engine of air. No manufacturer publishes thresholds for P2395.",["Deposits locking the flap near its closed stop","Broken return spring, flap no longer opens when unpowered","Jammed gear train or seized shaft bearing","Ice on the shaft or flap after cold, damp conditions"],["Marked loss of power, limp mode","Black smoke under load","Rough running or stalling in severe cases"],2,3,["P2394","P2391","P239D","P02E5","P0299"],"בקרת זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2396:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit","P2396 is the general electrical fault of the sensor that reports the angle of the B intake throttle, a potentiometer or, on newer units, a contactless Hall sensor with analogue or SENT output. The code says only that the signal is electrically implausible, without telling whether the reading sits under or over its window; makers that separate the two would set P2398 or P2399 instead.",["Corroded or loose sensor connector","Damaged reference, ground or signal wire","Failed position sensor in the throttle unit"],["MIL on","Flap switched off, EGR runs with limited control","Regeneration postponed"],2,3,["P2397","P2398","P2399","P239A","P02E6"],"חיישן מצב זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2397:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Range/Performance","P2397 covers a B-throttle position signal that stays inside its electrical window but does not make sense, for instance a reading that does not move when the motor is driven, or one that disagrees with the commanded angle. CARB asks for such rationality checks on inputs wherever feasible. No published manufacturer table covers P2397.",["Sticking flap that lags behind the command","Worn potentiometer track or drifting sensor","Contact resistance in connector or signal wire","Play between gear and flap shaft"],["MIL on","Displayed flap angle does not follow the command","Occasionally reduced power"],2,3,["P2391","P2396","P2398","P2399","P02E7"],"חיישן מצב זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2398:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2398 is logged when the position signal of the B intake throttle falls below its lower limit. Likely reasons are a signal lead shorted to ground, a lost 5 V supply, or a broken signal wire that the module input pulls low; on SENT sensors the transmitted raw value can also leave its range. No manufacturer documents P2398 itself.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Open 5 V reference or open signal wire","Shared 5 V reference pulled down by another faulty sensor","Internally failed position sensor"],["MIL on","Further 5 V sensor codes at the same time","Regeneration suspended"],2,3,["P2399","P2396","P2397","P239A","P02E8"],"חיישן מצב זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2399:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit High","P2399 is the upper-limit counterpart of P2398: the B-throttle position signal reads higher than any real flap angle can produce. That usually points to a lost sensor ground, a signal wire touching the 5 V reference or battery voltage, or water bridging the terminals in the connector. No manufacturer is known to publish P2399.",["Open or high-resistance sensor ground","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Moisture bridging terminals in the connector","Failed position sensor"],["MIL on","Flap stays at spring position","Regeneration suspended"],2,3,["P2398","P2396","P2397","P239A","P02E9"],"חיישן מצב זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P239A:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P239A describes a B-throttle position signal that keeps jumping or dropping out for short moments, too briefly to set the low or high code. Loose terminals, a harness that cracks as the engine rocks, corrosion or a worn potentiometer track are typical; on digital SENT sensors corrupted messages have the same effect.",["Loose or corroded terminals in the sensor connector","Wire breaking or rubbing intermittently with engine movement","Worn potentiometer track or faulty SENT sensor electronics","Electrical interference on the signal line"],["MIL that comes and goes","Short-lived jerks or EGR interruptions","Code stored without a permanent fault on testing"],2,3,["P2396","P2398","P2399","P2397","P02EA"],"חיישן מצב זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P239B:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Motor Current Range/Performance","P239B checks the current the B-throttle motor draws while its H-bridge is switched on. A blocked or very stiff flap, a partly shorted winding or the two motor leads touching each other push the current beyond what the module expects. No manufacturer publishes P239B with values.",["Flap blocked or very stiff, motor running at stall current","Partly shorted motor winding","Short between the two motor leads in harness or connector","Faulty current measurement in the control module"],["MIL on","Flap switched off and resting at spring position","Often stored together with P2391 or the stuck codes"],2,3,["P2390","P2392","P2393","P2391","P02EB"],"זרם מנוע בקרת זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P239C:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control System - High Air Flow Detected","P239C belongs to the air-mass control loop rather than to the throttle alone: with the B intake throttle taking part in that control, the module sees more fresh air than its target and cannot bring the reading down even at the limit of its authority.",["EGR valve stuck closed or EGR cooler clogged","B throttle unable to close far enough","Air-mass meter reading too high","Boost higher than intended"],["MIL on","No noticeable driving change in most cases","Often stored together with EGR flow codes"],3,1,["P239D","P2394","P02EC","P0401","P0101"],""],P239D:["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control System - Low Air Flow Detected","P239D is the mirror image of P239C: the measured fresh-air mass remains below target although the control loop involving the B intake throttle is already at its limit. Candidates are an EGR valve that will not close and floods the intake with exhaust gas, a B flap stuck partly shut (often together with P2395), a restricted air filter or charge-air path, a turbocharger delivering too little, or an air-mass meter…",["EGR valve stuck open","B throttle stuck partly closed","Clogged air filter or restricted charge-air path","Contaminated air-mass meter reading too low","Turbocharger delivering too little boost"],["Loss of power, possibly limp mode","Black smoke","Frequent particulate filter regenerations"],3,3,["P239C","P2395","P02ED","P0402","P0299"],""],P239E:["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 1 Sensor 2) - Duplicate Listing of P232F","P239E carries in common code lists exactly the same wording as P232F: a downstream oxygen sensor on bank 1 reading outside its expected window while fuel is cut on deceleration. No manufacturer, OBD summary or service bulletin on record uses P239E, and no source gives it a meaning of its own.",["Scan tool code table showing the duplicate number instead of the maker's code","Aged or drifting rear oxygen sensor on bank 1","Exhaust leak ahead of the rear sensor"],["MIL on without noticeable driving change","Code text in the scan tool contradicts the manufacturer's documentation"],2,1,["P232F","P239F","P2379"],""],P239F:["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 2 Sensor 2) - Duplicate Listing of P2379","P239F appears in code lists with the identical title already given to P2379: the post-catalyst oxygen sensor of bank 2 is out of range while the injectors are switched off on a closed throttle. Neither code has a published manufacturer application; the only documented member of this deceleration check is GM's bank 1 code P232F on the single-bank 2023 L5P diesel, so a second bank never occurs there.",["Scan tool listing the duplicate number for a maker-specific fault","Aged rear oxygen sensor on bank 2","Air leak in the bank 2 exhaust ahead of the sensor"],["MIL on, engine runs normally","Catalyst monitor may not complete"],2,1,["P2379","P239E","P232F"],""],P23A0:["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error (Bank 1 Sensor 2) - Duplicate Listing of P237A","P23A0 repeats, word for word, the title of P237A in the usual code lists: the rear oxygen sensor of bank 1 does not see, or does not report, a representative sample of post-catalyst exhaust. No manufacturer uses P23A0 in any published OBD table or service bulletin, and no source defines it differently, so it is a duplicate listing of P237A. Even P237A has no public manufacturer application;",["Scan tool code table using the duplicate number","Air leak in the exhaust ahead of the rear sensor on bank 1","Sensor mounted poorly or element contaminated"],["MIL on, no drivability change","Catalyst diagnosis unreliable or incomplete"],2,1,["P237A","P23A1","P2414"],""],P23A1:["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error (Bank 2 Sensor 2) - Duplicate Listing of P237B","P23A1 is listed with the same title as P237B: the bank 2 oxygen sensor behind the catalyst reports something that cannot be genuine exhaust from that bank. Only engines with two exhaust banks and a downstream sensor on each side could produce it. No published OBD summary or bulletin assigns P23A1, and no source gives it its own meaning; it is thus a duplicate listing of P237B, itself without public manufacturer use.",["Scan tool reporting the duplicate number","Leak in the bank 2 exhaust pipe ahead of the rear sensor","Damaged wiring or connector of the bank 2 rear sensor"],["MIL on, engine runs normally","Readiness for catalyst monitor stays open"],2,1,["P237B","P23A0","P2415"],""],P23A2:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve B Control Circuit/Open","P23A2 reports an open or otherwise broken drive circuit for the second exhaust bypass flap, valve B, of an exhaust heat exchanger. Such units route the exhaust through a coolant heat exchanger after a cold start and send it past once engine and cabin are warm; a valve B only exists where the layout needs two flaps. No manufacturer documents P23A2 publicly.",["Connector at the valve B actuator loose, corroded or unplugged","Control wire broken near the hot exhaust or at a harness clip","Actuator coil or internal electronics of valve B open"],["Check engine light on","Slower engine and cabin warm-up in cold weather","No change in how the vehicle drives"],2,1,["P23A3","P23A4","P23A5","P237C","U066C"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23A3:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve B Control Circuit Low","With P23A3 the module sees the control line of exhaust bypass valve B sitting lower than its commanded state allows, which usually means that the wire or the driver stage of the actuator has found a path to ground. Water or road salt in a connector under the vehicle is a typical trigger. P23A3 itself appears in no public manufacturer document.",["Control wire chafed through and touching body or exhaust ground","Moisture or salt bridging pins in the actuator connector","Internal short in the valve B actuator"],["Check engine light on","Heater output builds up slowly after a cold start","Fault may reappear after rain or washing"],2,1,["P23A2","P23A4","P23A5","P237D"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23A4:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve B Control Circuit High","P23A4 is stored when the control circuit of exhaust heat exchanger bypass valve B reads higher than expected – a short to a battery feed, a chafed wire touching another supply, or an actuator whose electronics pull the line up. Because the flap no longer obeys, the warm-up strategy has to run without it. There is no public manufacturer documentation for P23A4.",["Control wire shorted to a 12 V feed in the harness","Failed electronics inside the valve B actuator","Output stage in the controlling module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Bypass flap does not respond to an actuator test","Driving behaviour unchanged"],2,1,["P23A2","P23A3","P23A5","P237E"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23A5:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve B Control Performance","Unlike the circuit codes, P23A5 judges the result: the module commanded valve B, the second exhaust bypass at the heat exchanger, but it does not see the response it expects, for example in position feedback or in how the exhaust-side coolant temperatures change. No manufacturer publishes P23A5.",["Flap of valve B sluggish from soot or corrosion","Exhaust coolant temperature sensor connector wet or corroded, distorting the plausibility check","Worn actuator gearing or linkage","Overly strict calibration, fixed by a software update"],["Check engine light on","Cabin heat slow to arrive in winter","No effect on drivability"],2,1,["P23A2","P23A6","P23A7","P23A8","P237F"],"בקרת שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P23A6:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve B Stuck Open","P23A6 says that bypass valve B of the exhaust heat exchanger stays open while the module wants it closed. In the usual layout the exhaust then keeps taking the bypass route, so the heat exchanger adds little or no heat after a cold start – noticeable as a slow engine warm-up and a weak cabin heater in cold weather, and on hybrids as the engine running longer just to make heat.",["Flap seized in the open position by carbon or corrosion","Linkage between actuator and flap broken or detached","Actuator no longer able to move the flap"],["Check engine light on","Engine and heater take noticeably longer to warm up","Hybrid engine runs more often in cold weather"],3,1,["P23A7","P23A5","P23A8","P00E3"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P23A7:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve B Stuck Closed","P23A7 is the opposite of P23A6: the second bypass valve (B) on the exhaust heat exchanger does not open on command and stays closed. Depending on the layout, all exhaust is then forced through the heat exchanger even when the engine is fully warm, which adds heat to the coolant and some back pressure – most relevant under load and in hot weather.",["Flap stuck closed by deposits or corrosion","Actuator motor or gearing failed","Damaged or water-filled heat exchanger obstructing the flap"],["Check engine light on","Coolant temperature higher than usual under load","Possibly reduced power or a changed exhaust note"],3,1,["P23A6","P23A5","P23A8","P00E4"],"שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P23A8:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Stop Performance","P23A8 concerns the position feedback of exhaust bypass valve B at its mechanical end stops. Systems with a position sensor learn the readings at the fully open and the fully closed stop and compare later readings with them; if a stop value drifts out of its window, or the flap no longer reaches the stop at all, this code is set. Causes range from a carbon-fouled or bent flap to a slipping sensor or a worn actuator.",["Deposits or a bent flap keep valve B from reaching its end stop","Position sensor in the actuator drifted or loose","Play in the actuator gearing","End stops not relearned after a repair"],["Check engine light on","Valve position in live data does not reach the expected end value"],2,1,["P23A5","P23A6","P23A7","P25D6","P2C23"],"עצירת חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P23A9:["Communication Fault - Forced Engine Shutdown","P23A9 records that the engine was stopped, or kept from running, because the engine module lost contact with a control unit whose messages it needs to operate the engine safely. The title names only the consequence; which data link is meant is defined by each manufacturer, and none publishes P23A9. The underlying network fault normally shows up as a separate U code in the same or another module.",["Damaged CAN wiring, connector or termination","Partner module without power or ground, or low battery voltage","Failed or wrongly programmed partner module","Software versions of the modules not matching after repair"],["Engine stops while driving or does not start","Several U codes and warning messages from other modules","MIL or other warning lights on"],3,3,["P06AF","P232A","P0600","P2105","P241D"],""],P23AA:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Stuck","P23AA concerns bypass valve A of a turbocharger or supercharger, which opens a path around the compressor to relieve boost when the throttle closes or at part load. The code means the valve no longer follows its command and sits fixed.",["Valve or actuator mechanically seized (deposits, wear)","Faulty electric actuator or position sensor of the valve","Damaged linkage or valve plate","High resistance in wiring or connector"],["Reduced boost and power","Fluttering or surging noise when lifting off","MIL on, possibly limited power mode"],3,3,["P0033","P0034","P0035","P2261","P0299","P0234"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ A — תקוע"],P23AB:["NOx Sensor Processor Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","A NOx sensor is a smart part: the probe in the exhaust is wired to a small control unit with its own processor, which runs the heater, evaluates the cell currents and reports over CAN. P23AB means that this electronics in sensor 3 of bank 1 – usually the one behind a second SCR catalyst – reports an internal error or fails its self-checks. No manufacturer documents P23AB publicly.",["Internal electronics of the sensor 3 control unit defective","Supply voltage dips or poor ground resetting the sensor electronics","Sensor control unit damaged by heat or water ingress"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 values missing or frozen in live data","SCR or emissions warning on the display"],2,1,["P06EA","P06EB","P23AC","P23B6"],"מעבד חיישן NOx — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23AC:["NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23AC is the general electrical fault reported for NOx sensor 3 on bank 1. The sensor's own control unit watches the leads between its electronics and the ceramic probe and tells the engine computer over CAN whether a measuring circuit is open or shorted; the user manual of Drivven's NOx sensor module kit, published by NI, lists these status states for the NOx and O2 circuits.",["Lead between probe and sensor control unit damaged by heat or chafing","Corroded or loose terminals at the sensor 3 connectors","Probe or sensor electronics failed internally"],["Check engine light on","No NOx reading from sensor 3 in live data","SCR system warning"],2,1,["P23AD","P23AE","P23AF","P23B0","P2200","P229E"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23AD:["NOx Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23AD flags the third NOx sensor on bank 1 as electrically intact but not trustworthy. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B describes the check for its post-second-catalyst NOx sensor: the internal stability flags of the NOx and lambda current control are watched, and a flag counts as off when, for instance, the V2 cell voltage leaves a 40 mV band around its set point or the pump currents Ip1 and Ip2 change faster than…",["Aged or poisoned sensing cell giving unstable pump currents","High contact resistance in the sensor 3 wiring","Exhaust leak near the sensor upsetting the measurement"],["Check engine light after two trips","Sensor 3 NOx value jumps in live data","SCR efficiency monitor may not complete"],2,1,["P23AC","P23AE","P23AF","P2201","P229F"],"חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23AE:["NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23AE is set when the third NOx sensor on bank 1 reports a concentration below anything physically possible. GM's 25OBDG04B table for its 2025 diesels requires the raw NOx value of the sensor behind the second catalyst to fall under −90 ppm in 100 of 200 samples, taken every 25 ms once dew point is reached, supply exceeds 9.9 V and no CAN fault is present; it is rated Type B with the MIL after two trips.",["Engine harness chafed, disturbing the sensor 3 supply or signal","Sensor 3 with a negative offset from ageing or damage","Water in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light after two trips","Negative or zero NOx value for sensor 3 in live data","Other harness-related codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P23AF","P23AD","P23AC","P2202","P22A0"],"חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23AF:["NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","With P23AF the third NOx sensor on bank 1 delivers a value above its measuring range. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B sets the code when the raw reading of the post-second-catalyst sensor exceeds 2,990 ppm in 120 of 240 samples, provided the air system control is active or DEF dosing is ready; the rating is Type B, so the MIL follows on the second trip.",["Wire broken inside the insulation near a connector in the exhaust sensor harness","Sensor 3 failed with a reading stuck high","Short between sensor lines in the harness"],["Check engine light after two trips","Sensor 3 shows implausibly high NOx even at idle","SCR efficiency code may follow"],2,1,["P23AE","P23AD","P23AC","P2203","P22A1","P20EE"],"חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B0:["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23B0 is meant for a third NOx sensor on bank 1 whose circuit faults come and go instead of staying present, so the status the sensor module reports over CAN keeps toggling between valid and faulty. No manufacturer documents P23B0 publicly, and none publishes a threshold for it; GM's 2025 diesel table, which details several other sensor 3 codes, does not list it.",["Loose or fretting terminal in a sensor 3 connector","Harness rubbing or flexing near the exhaust, breaking contact under vibration","Moisture entering a connector in wet weather"],["Check engine light that goes out and returns","Sensor 3 value drops out briefly in live data"],2,1,["P23AC","P23AD","P2204","P22A2"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B1:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","A NOx sensor only measures once its built-in heater has brought the ceramic element up to temperature. P23B1 reports that the heater control side of the third sensor on bank 1 is open. GM's 2025 diesel calibration (table 25OBDG04B) looks for a missing load on the heater control pin of the post-second-catalyst sensor and fails after 80 of 160 samples at a 25 ms rate, with powertrain relay voltage above 11 V and the…",["Heater element in the sensor 3 probe burnt through","Broken heater conductor between probe and sensor module","Probe connector not fully engaged after a repair"],["Check engine light after one trip","Sensor 3 never reports operating temperature","SCR warning on the display"],2,1,["P23B2","P23B3","P23B4","P23B7","P2205","P22A3"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B2:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23B2 points to the heater control line of bank 1's NOx sensor 3 being pulled to ground. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B checks that pin on the sensor downstream of the second catalyst for a short to ground and, unlike the open-circuit test, waits until the dew point has been reached, so that the heater is actually allowed to run; 80 failed out of 160 samples set the code.",["Heater control wire chafed against ground","Internal short in the heater of sensor 3","Water bridging the heater pins in the connector"],["Check engine light after two trips","Sensor 3 slow or unable to become ready"],2,1,["P23B1","P23B3","P23B7","P2206","P22A4"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B3:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","If, on NOx sensor 3 of bank 1, the heater control pin sits at supply voltage when the electronics expect it to switch, P23B3 is stored. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B describes it, for the sensor behind the second catalyst, as a battery short at the heater drive pin, evaluated every 25 ms with sensor supply above 9.9 V and dew point reached, and failing at 80 of 160 samples; Type B with the MIL on the second trip.",["Heater control wire shorted to a supply line","Heater driver inside the sensor 3 electronics failed","Heat-damaged connector with pins touching"],["Check engine light after two trips","Sensor 3 heater status shows an error in live data","SCR warning"],2,1,["P23B1","P23B2","P23B7","P2207","P22A5"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B4:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","Besides its drive line, the heater of a NOx sensor has a sense connection through which its resistance, and with it the element temperature, is measured. P23B4 reports a fault in that sense path for the third sensor on bank 1. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B checks the HTemp pin of the post-second-catalyst sensor for an open circuit: 80 of 160 samples, Type A, MIL after one trip.",["Heater sense lead broken between probe and module","Backed-out or corroded terminal at the probe connector","Internal break in the sensor 3 probe"],["Check engine light after one trip","Sensor 3 temperature status invalid"],2,1,["P23B5","P23B8","P23B9","P23BA","P2208","P22A6"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B5:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23B5 says the heater feedback from NOx sensor 3 (bank 1) is present but implausible: the element does not reach or hold the resistance that matches its target temperature. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B compares the raw heater resistance of the post-second-catalyst sensor with its target and fails it outside a relative band of 0.06, after waiting 200 s from supply in range and from dew point;",["NOx sensor harness chafing on a hot component such as the EGR cooler (Ford 2023 6.7L)","Aged heater element whose resistance no longer matches the target","Blown fuse in the NOx sensor supply after a short","High contact resistance in the heater connector"],["Check engine light after one trip","Several NOx sensor and communication codes at once","SCR warning, sensor 3 not ready"],2,1,["P23B4","P23B7","P2209","P22A7","U029D"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B6:["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23B6 concerns the power feed of the third NOx sensor on bank 1, the smart probe behind the second SCR catalyst. Its built-in control unit needs a stable supply, and when the voltage it reports leaves the allowed range the engine module stores this code. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B fails it below 9.90 V while the engine runs, the powertrain relay delivers more than 11 V and the dew point has been passed;",["Blown fuse in the NOx sensor supply after a short elsewhere in the harness","Supply or ground wire chafed through on the engine or frame (GM 3.0L LM2)","Corroded or loose pins in the sensor 3 connector under the vehicle","Weak battery or charging fault pulling the sensor supply down"],["Check engine light after two trips","Sensor 3 shows no NOx value in live data","Further NOx sensor or communication codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P23AB","P23AC","P220A","P220B"],"חיישן NOx — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B7:["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23B7 is set when the heater drive of NOx sensor 3 on bank 1 looks electrically sound but does not behave as the control strategy expects, for instance a heater duty cycle far from what the element should need to reach operating temperature. No manufacturer documents P23B7 publicly; GM's 2025 table covers sensor 3 only with the plain heater circuit codes P23B1-P23B3 and the resistance check P23B5.",["Aged heater element that needs far more or less power than expected","High resistance in heater supply or ground contacts","Sensor supply voltage at the lower limit, so the heater cannot keep up"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 takes long to become ready or drops out of its active state","SCR efficiency monitor not completing"],2,1,["P23B1","P23B2","P23B3","P23B5","P220E","P220F"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B8:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","Smart NOx sensors report heater temperature through a separate sense connection, which GM calls the HTemp pin. P23B8 means this line on sensor 3 of bank 1 is pulled to ground. GM's 2025 table 25OBDG04B looks for the ground short on the post-second-catalyst sensor once the powertrain relay is above 11 V, the relay feeding the sensor bus is switched on, the supply exceeds 9.90 V and the dew point is reached;",["Sense wire chafed through and touching body, frame or exhaust ground","Water or salt bridging the sense pin to ground in the connector","Internal short in the sensor or its control unit"],["Check engine light after two trips","Sensor 3 does not report valid NOx values","Often stored together with other wiring-related codes"],2,1,["P23B9","P23B4","P23BA","P2210","P22A8"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות נמוך במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23B9:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23B9 is the counterpart of P23B8: the temperature feedback wire of NOx sensor 3 on bank 1 carries a voltage that only a short to battery or to another live wire can explain. The sensor then cannot report a trustworthy heater temperature, so it withholds its NOx output.",["Sense wire shorted to the heater supply or another battery-fed wire","Harness insulation melted by contact with hot exhaust parts","Internal fault in the sensor or its control unit"],["Check engine light after two trips","No NOx reading from sensor 3","Possibly a blown fuse in the sensor supply"],2,1,["P23B8","P23B4","P23BA","P2211","P22A9"],"גוף חימום חיישן NOx — אות גבוה במעגל החישה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23BA:["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","With P23BA, the heater feedback signal from the third NOx sensor of bank 1 keeps vanishing or leaping for a moment and then recovers, rather than staying broken. P23BA itself is not described in any public manufacturer document.",["Terminal in the sensor 3 connector with weak contact pressure","Sense lead cracked by vibration or heat and opening only at times","Moisture entering the plug through a damaged seal"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Sensor 3 briefly leaves its ready state","Fault often cannot be reproduced in the workshop"],2,1,["P23B4","P23B8","P23B9","P2212","P22AA"],"חישת גוף חימום חיישן NOx — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23BB:["NOx Sensor Heater Resistance (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23BB says the heater element of NOx sensor 3 on bank 1 has a resistance outside its permitted band. Because the resistance of the ceramic heater climbs with temperature, it doubles as the thermometer of the probe, so an aged or cracked element heats poorly and reports a false temperature as well. No manufacturer publishes P23BB.",["Heater element aged by long service at high exhaust temperature","Element cracked by water droplets hitting the hot ceramic","Added resistance from a corroded heater contact"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 slow to become ready after a cold start","Implausible NOx readings from the rear sensor"],2,1,["P23B5","P23B7","P224A","P224B"],"התנגדות גוף חימום חיישן NOx (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23BC:["NOx Sensor Calibration Memory (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","Every smart NOx sensor carries its own control unit with a memory holding trim and reference data written for that individual probe at the factory. P23BC means this memory in sensor 3 on bank 1 cannot be read or fails its integrity check, so the engine module can no longer trust the readings. No manufacturer documents P23BC publicly.",["Memory inside the sensor control unit corrupted or failed","Voltage dips or spikes on the sensor supply disturbing the memory","Replacement sensor with a calibration that does not match the vehicle"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 readings ignored by the engine module","SCR monitoring cannot complete"],1,1,["P23AB","P23C1","P225A","P225B"],"זיכרון כיול חיישן NOx (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P23BD:["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck High (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23BD means NOx sensor 3 on bank 1, the last probe downstream of the second SCR catalyst, reports more NOx than the operating state allows, or its value no longer comes down from a high level. A common test is engine overrun without fuel, when the exhaust contains no NOx at all: Volvo, for its inlet-sensor counterpart P225C, expects the reading to fall below 50 ppm within roughly 10 s.",["Measuring cell drifted upward with age or contamination","Sensor element damaged by thermal shock or poisoning","Monitor calibration too strict, fixed by an engine software update"],["Check engine light on","SCR efficiency code may follow although the catalyst is fine","Sensor 3 reading stays high in overrun"],2,1,["P23BE","P23AD","P225C","P225E"],""],P23BE:["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck Low (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23BE is the low-side mirror of P23BD: NOx sensor 3 on bank 1 shows less NOx than is plausible, or it stays near zero while the engine is clearly producing some. Behind a working SCR system the true value is small anyway, which makes a low-stuck sensor the more dangerous error for monitoring, because it can hide a failing catalyst. No manufacturer documents P23BE publicly.",["Exhaust leak or air drawn in ahead of sensor 3, diluting the gas","Measuring cell lost sensitivity and reads too low","Sensor not seated correctly so it samples too little exhaust"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 reads near zero under load","Possibly an audible exhaust leak at the rear section"],2,1,["P23BD","P23AD","P225D","P225F"],""],P23BF:["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response Low to High (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23BF concerns how quickly NOx sensor 3 on bank 1 follows a rise in NOx. The control module waits for an increasing transient and times the climb of the sensor signal against what a model predicts. No manufacturer publishes P23BF.",["Soot, oil ash or urea residue blocking the gas inlet of the sensor","Measuring cells aged beyond their response specification","Element running too cold because the heater is weak"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 signal trails the front sensor during acceleration","No change in how the engine runs"],2,1,["P23C0","P23C2","P22F9","P22FC"],""],P23C0:["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response High to Low (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","With P23C0 the third NOx sensor on bank 1 is too sluggish when NOx falls, for instance when the driver lifts off and the engine goes into fuel cut-off. The module measures how long the reading takes to come down between two levels. No manufacturer documents P23C0 publicly.",["Deposits from condensate, fuel or oil on the sensor element","Holes in the protective tube partly blocked by soot or urea crystals","Sensor aged and no longer able to release its reading quickly"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 value stays raised for seconds after lifting off","Driveability unaffected"],2,1,["P23BF","P23C2","P22FA","P22FD"],""],P23C1:["NOx Sensor Performance - Sensing Element (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23C1 asks whether the measuring cells of NOx sensor 3 on bank 1 have lost sensitivity, for example because deposits clog the internal cavities. GM's 2025 table 25OBDG04B runs the test on the post-second-catalyst sensor during afterrun: the sensor shifts its internal pump currents so that oxygen in the second cavity rises to a target, and the outcome is set against a value the supplier recorded on the new part and…",["Internal measuring cavities clogged by ash or other deposits","Sensing cells worn out after high mileage","Wiring fault upsetting the sensor supply during the test (GM 3.0L LM2)"],["Check engine light after one trip","SCR monitoring results become unreliable","No noticeable change in engine behaviour"],2,1,["P23BC","P23BD","P23BE","P22FB","P22FE"],""],P23C2:["NOx Sensor Delayed Response - High to Low (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","P23C2 targets the dead time of NOx sensor 3 on bank 1 when NOx drops: the reading only starts to fall too long after the exhaust has changed, even if it then moves at a normal pace. CARB separates these two failure types in its oxygen sensor definitions, calling the time before a sensor first reacts delayed response and a sluggish transition slow response. No manufacturer documents P23C2 publicly.",["Protective tube partly blocked, so new exhaust gas reaches the cell late","Aged sensing cells reacting late to a change","Condensate in the sensor housing after many short trips"],["Check engine light on","Sensor 3 value holds briefly before dropping in overrun","Engine runs normally"],2,1,["P23C0","P23BF","P24F4","P24F5"],""],P23C3:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Position Sensor Circuit","P23C3 is the general electrical fault on the feedback sensor that tells the engine module how far the third coolant bypass valve has turned. On modern thermal management modules this valve is a motor-driven rotary part, so without a valid angle the module loses its closed-loop positioning. No manufacturer documents P23C3 publicly.",["Loose, corroded or coolant-contaminated connector at the valve module","Damaged signal, 5 V reference or ground wire of the position sensor","Internal failure of the position sensor built into the valve actuator","Faulty sensor input or reference supply in the engine control module"],["Engine warning lamp","Engine takes longer to reach operating temperature","Coolant temperature gauge reads unusually high or unsteady"],2,3,["P23C4","P23C5","P26BB","P26B7","P26A4","P2AA7"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P23C4:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Position Sensor Circuit Low","P23C4 says the angle reported by the bypass valve C position sensor has dropped below anything the sensor can produce in normal use, which GM traces to the signal line touching ground. GM's 2025 tables use the code on both its 3.0L Duramax diesel (25OBDG04B) and a gasoline family (25OBDG03B): the SENT sensor value must fall under 27 or under 50 counts respectively, for 4 seconds within a 5-second window, while SENT…",["Position sensor signal wire chafed against ground","Coolant or water in the valve connector bridging the signal to ground","Defective position sensor inside the valve actuator","Missing sensor supply so the output stays at its lowest value"],["Engine warning lamp after two drives","Bypass valve C position shown as implausibly low in live data","Slow warm-up or unusual engine temperature"],2,3,["P23C3","P23C5","P26BB","P26A6","P2AA9"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P23C5:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Position Sensor Circuit High","With P23C5 the position feedback of coolant bypass valve C sits at the top end of its digital range, a reading GM explains as the signal line touching a voltage source. In GM's 2025 summaries for the 3.0L Duramax (25OBDG04B) and a gasoline engine family (25OBDG03B) the limit is identical: a SENT value above 4,050 counts present for 4 seconds within 5 seconds, checked only when the SENT link reports no error and the…",["Position signal wire shorted to a supply or reference wire","Open ground wire of the position sensor","Position sensor in the valve actuator reporting a stuck maximum value","Bent or spread terminals in the valve connector"],["Engine warning lamp on the second faulty trip","Live data shows bypass valve C near full scale regardless of command","Heater output or engine temperature behaves unusually"],2,3,["P23C3","P23C4","P26BB","P26A7","P2AAA"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P23C6:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P23C6 is set by the output stage itself: the H-bridge that drives the motor of coolant bypass valve C reports more current, or more heat, than it can tolerate. GM labels it a motor overcurrent in two 2025 summaries, the diesel table 25OBDG04B (3.0L Duramax) and the gasoline table 25OBDG03B;",["Valve rotor stiff or seized by deposits or worn seals, so the motor stalls","Shorted windings in the valve motor drawing excess current","Motor wires partly shorted to each other or to ground","Overheated or faulty H-bridge driver in the engine control module"],["Engine warning lamp after two trips","Bypass valve C no longer moves and stays in its last position","Engine runs too cold or too warm depending on where the valve stopped"],3,3,["P26B7","P26B8","P26B9","P26BB","P23C3"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P23C7:["Fuel Heater Control Module Power Control Circuit/Open","Flex-fuel engines that must start on high-ethanol blends in the cold warm the fuel before injection, and a separate heating control unit switches the high heater currents on command of the engine module. P23C7 reports that the power control line to this unit is open or electrically faulty, so the heaters cannot be enabled. No manufacturer documents P23C7 publicly.",["Broken or disconnected power control wire between engine module and heater unit","Blown fuse or failed relay feeding the heater control circuit","Corroded or loose connector at the fuel heater control module","Internal fault in the fuel heater control module"],["Hard or failed cold starts on high ethanol blends","Rough running right after a cold start","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23C8","P23C9","P23CD","P23CA","U01B6"],"כוח מודול בקרת גוף חימום דלק — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23C8:["Fuel Heater Control Module Power Control Circuit Low","P23C8 covers the case where the engine module finds the heater unit's power control line pulled to ground. The likely culprit is a chafed wire touching the body or engine, or a short inside the heater unit. Because the line is held low, the heating unit either never receives its enable or, depending on the circuit design, the fuse protecting it may blow. No manufacturer documents P23C8 publicly;",["Power control wire chafed through to ground","Moisture in the heater unit connector creating a path to ground","Shorted control input inside the fuel heater control module","Faulty output driver in the engine control module"],["Long cranking in cold weather on ethanol","Blown fuse in the fuel heater circuit","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23C7","P23C9","P23CF","P23CB"],"כוח מודול בקרת גוף חימום דלק — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23C9:["Fuel Heater Control Module Power Control Circuit High","P23C9 is stored when the power control line to the fuel heater control unit shows battery voltage although the engine module has it switched off, pointing to a short to a live wire. The real risk here is the reverse of the low case: the heater stage may be enabled without being asked, warming the fuel after it is no longer needed and loading the electrical system. No manufacturer documents P23C9 publicly.",["Power control wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Welded relay contact keeping the circuit energized","Internal leakage in the fuel heater control module","Engine module output that does not switch off"],["Fuel heating active when not needed, possible battery drain","Heater unit or wiring gets unusually warm","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23C7","P23C8","P23D0","P23CC"],"כוח מודול בקרת גוף חימום דלק — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23CA:["Fuel Rail Heater Control Circuit/Open","Some flex-fuel engines heat the fuel directly in the injector rail: a heating element in the rail brings ethanol up to temperature just before a cold start. P23CA flags the control circuit of that rail heater as open or otherwise faulty, so no heating current flows. No manufacturer documents P23CA publicly.",["Burnt-out heating element in the fuel rail","Broken wire or unplugged connector at the rail heater","Corroded high-current terminals at the heater","Failed output stage in the fuel heater control module"],["No start or long cranking on ethanol below about 13 °C","Misfiring or stumbling in the first seconds after a cold start","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23CB","P23CC","P23C7","P23D1"],"גוף חימום מסילת דלק — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23CB:["Fuel Rail Heater Control Circuit Low","P23CB means the control side of the fuel rail heater reads too low, normally a short to ground between the switching stage and the heating element. Since a rail heater draws a high current, a ground short on its feed can blow the fuse or trip the protection in the driving stage before the fuel gets warm. No manufacturer documents P23CB publicly.",["Heater feed wire chafed to ground near the intake manifold","Heating element shorted to the rail body","Fuel or water in the heater connector","Shorted output stage in the fuel heater control module"],["Difficult cold start with ethanol","Fuel heater fuse blows repeatedly","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23CA","P23CC","P23C8"],"גוף חימום מסילת דלק — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23CC:["Fuel Rail Heater Control Circuit High","With P23CC the fuel rail heater control circuit sits at supply voltage when it should not, most often because the line has shorted to a battery feed or the switching element is stuck conducting. The concern is uncontrolled heating: if the element keeps running, the fuel in the rail can get hotter than intended once the engine is warm. No manufacturer documents P23CC publicly.",["Heater control wire shorted to a battery feed","Switching transistor in the heater unit stuck conducting","Internal fault in the fuel heater control module","Damaged terminals letting adjacent pins touch"],["Rail heater stays on after start","Hard restart when the engine is hot","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23CA","P23CB","P23C9"],"גוף חימום מסילת דלק — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23CD:["Fuel Heater Control Module Feedback Signal/Open","Besides being commanded, a fuel heater control unit reports back to the engine module, so the engine knows whether heating actually took place. P23CD indicates that this feedback line carries no usable signal or is open.",["Broken feedback wire between heater unit and engine module","Loose or corroded pin for the feedback signal","Heater unit without supply or ground, so it sends nothing","Failed feedback output in the fuel heater control module"],["Cold-start fuel heating disabled or unconfirmed","Harder starts on ethanol in cold weather","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23CE","P23CF","P23D0","P23C7"],""],P23CE:["Fuel Heater Control Module Feedback Signal Performance","Unlike the open and short codes, P23CE concerns a feedback signal that is electrically present but does not fit what the engine module expects. The heater unit may, for example, report no temperature rise during a commanded heating phase, a rise that is far too slow, or values that contradict the command state.",["Aged heating element delivering less heat than commanded","High resistance at heater power or ground terminals","Drifting temperature or current measurement inside the heater unit","Weak battery reducing heating power during cranking"],["Slow or rough cold starts on ethanol without a wiring fault","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],3,1,["P23CD","P23CF","P23D0","P23D4"],"אות משוב מודול בקרת גוף חימום דלק — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P23CF:["Fuel Heater Control Module Feedback Signal Circuit Low","P23CF is logged when the feedback line from the fuel heater control unit stays near ground, below its valid signal range. Mostly the wire is chafed against ground or the feedback output inside the unit is shorted. Depending on how the signal is coded, a permanently low level can also look like a heater that never reports a result, which is why the engine module treats it as a circuit fault rather than as real data.",["Feedback wire shorted to ground","Moisture in a connector of the feedback circuit","Shorted feedback output in the fuel heater control module","Faulty input stage in the engine control module"],["Fuel heating not used for cold starts","Long cranking with ethanol in cold weather","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23CD","P23CE","P23D0","P23C8"],"אות משוב מודול בקרת גוף חימום דלק — אות נמוך במעגל"],P23D0:["Fuel Heater Control Module Feedback Signal Circuit High","P23D0 applies when the return signal from the fuel heater control unit is stuck above its plausible maximum. A short to a voltage source on the feedback wire is the usual explanation; with a pull-up input in the engine module an open ground at the heater unit can produce the same picture.",["Feedback wire shorted to a voltage supply","Missing ground at the fuel heater control module","Feedback output of the heater unit stuck high","Faulty input stage in the engine control module"],["Fuel heating switched off as a precaution","Poor cold starts on high ethanol blends","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23CD","P23CE","P23CF","P23C9"],"אות משוב מודול בקרת גוף חימום דלק — אות גבוה במעגל"],P23D1:["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Control Circuit/Open","Instead of one heater for the whole rail, some flex-fuel systems give every cylinder its own heating path, either a heated injector or an element at each rail outlet. P23D1 is the open or general circuit fault on the path for cylinder 1, so that cylinder gets unheated ethanol during a cold start.",["Burnt-out heater at cylinder 1 (heated injector or rail element)","Broken wire or unplugged heater connector at cylinder 1","Corroded terminals in the cylinder 1 heater connector","Failed channel 1 output in the fuel heater control module"],["Cylinder 1 misfire right after a cold start on ethanol","Rough idle until the engine warms up","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D2","P23D3","P23D4","P23D5","P23CA"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 1 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23D2:["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Control Circuit High","P23D2 is the high-voltage fault on the cylinder 1 heater circuit; note that in this series the high code comes before the low code (P23D3). The control side of the heater shows supply voltage while it should be switched off, so the switching stage has lost control: a short to a positive wire or a switching element that no longer turns off are the usual reasons.",["Cylinder 1 heater control wire shorted to a positive feed","Channel 1 switching element stuck on in the heater unit","Damaged connector letting the heater pin touch a supply pin"],["Cylinder 1 heater stays on, higher current draw","Possible hot-restart problems","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D1","P23D3","P23D4","P23D6"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 1 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23D3:["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Low","P23D3 reports that the control circuit of the cylinder 1 fuel heater is pulled toward ground. It follows the high code P23D2 in the numbering, not the other way round. A ground short on a heater path rated at a few hundred watts lets far too much current flow, so the heater unit or a fuse cuts the channel and cylinder 1 starts with cold fuel while the other heaters still work.",["Cylinder 1 heater wire chafed to ground on the intake or engine","Heater at cylinder 1 shorted to its housing","Fuel or water in the cylinder 1 heater connector","Shorted channel 1 output in the heater unit"],["Single-cylinder misfire on cold ethanol starts","Blown fuse in the fuel heater circuit","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D1","P23D2","P23D4","P23D7"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 1 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23D4:["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Performance","P23D4 is not about wiring at all: the cylinder 1 heater circuit is electrically intact, yet it fails to heat as it should. The heater unit measures what each heat circuit delivers, so a heater that draws too little current, warms too slowly or reaches a lower temperature than its neighbours stands out.",["Aged cylinder 1 heater with reduced heating power","High-resistance connection in the cylinder 1 heater circuit","Deposits reducing heat transfer at a heated injector","Low battery voltage during the heating phase"],["Cylinder 1 runs rough for a while after a cold start on ethanol","Longer cranking in cold weather","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],3,1,["P23D1","P23D2","P23D3","P23D8","P23CE"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P23D5:["Cylinder 2 Fuel Heater Control Circuit/Open","Cylinder 2 has its own fuel heating path on flex-fuel engines that warm the fuel per cylinder, and P23D5 says this path carries no current although the heater is commanded on, or the control line shows a general fault. To the heater unit the open simply looks like a missing load on channel 2.",["Heater at cylinder 2 burnt through (open element)","Cylinder 2 heater plug loose or not latched after intake work","Broken conductor in the cylinder 2 heater lead","Channel 2 output of the heater control unit failed"],["Cylinder 2 misfires briefly after a cold start on ethanol","Uneven idle in the first minute when cold","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D6","P23D7","P23D8","P23D1","P23D9"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 2 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23D6:["Cylinder 2 Fuel Heater Control Circuit High","P23D6 flags the control circuit of the cylinder 2 fuel heater as high. A heater driver typically checks the line both with the channel off and with it on; a level that stays near supply voltage in both states points to a control wire touching a positive feed or to a driver that no longer pulls the circuit down. Depending on the wiring, the heater then either stays energized or cannot be switched at all.",["Cylinder 2 heater control wire touching a positive feed","Switching FET of channel 2 failed in the conducting state","Bent connector pin touching a supply terminal"],["Heater at cylinder 2 runs on or does not switch","Cylinder 2 starts cold on ethanol","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D5","P23D7","P23D8","P23D2","P23DA"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 2 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23D7:["Cylinder 2 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Low","For P23D7 the module reads the cylinder 2 heater control line as low, which on these power circuits nearly always means a path to ground: a chafed wire, a heater element shorted to its body, or fuel or water bridging the connector pins. The short draws more than the channel is meant to carry, so the heater unit protects itself;",["Cylinder 2 heater wire chafed through to ground","Heating element at cylinder 2 shorted to its housing","Fuel or water bridging pins in the cylinder 2 heater plug"],["Rough cold start on one cylinder","Fuel heater fuse blown","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D5","P23D6","P23D8","P23D3","P23DB"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 2 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23D8:["Cylinder 2 Fuel Heater Performance","P23D8 concerns how well the cylinder 2 heater works, not its wiring. According to Bosch, the Flexstart heated rail warms pure ethanol fuel at rates of as much as 30 °C a second, so a system of this kind knows roughly how quickly each heating point ought to warm up.",["Cylinder 2 heater element with reduced output","Varnish or scale on the heated surface at cylinder 2","Corroded contact dropping voltage under heater load"],["Cylinder 2 runs rough for about a minute after a cold ethanol start","Longer cranking below freezing","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],3,1,["P23D5","P23D6","P23D7","P23D4","P23DC"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P23D9:["Cylinder 3 Fuel Heater Control Circuit/Open","P23D9 is the open-circuit or general circuit fault of the heating path for cylinder 3. The fuel heater control unit drives each heater through a channel of its own; when channel 3 is switched on but no load current appears, the connection to the heater is considered broken.",["Open heating element at cylinder 3","Terminal pushed out of the cylinder 3 heater connector","Wire broken where the harness flexes near the rail","Failed channel 3 output in the heater unit"],["Stumble on cylinder 3 after a cold ethanol start","Harder starting below about 13 °C","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23DA","P23DB","P23DC","P23D5","P23DD"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 3 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23DA:["Cylinder 3 Fuel Heater Control Circuit High","P23DA tells that the control side of the cylinder 3 heater sits at a high level. The likely pictures are a control wire touching a positive feed, so voltage stays on the line when the channel is off, or an output stage that has failed conducting, so heater 3 runs without command.",["Channel 3 output stage failed conducting","Cylinder 3 control wire shorted to a positive feed","Heater supply relay contacts welded"],["Flat battery after the car has stood for some hours","Heater at cylinder 3 warm long after switch-off","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D9","P23DB","P23DC","P23D6","P23DE"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 3 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23DB:["Cylinder 3 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Low","With P23DB the cylinder 3 heater control circuit is too low, meaning the line or the heater itself has found a path to ground. Because a single heat circuit is sized for several hundred watts, such a short trips the current limit at once; Bosch describes short detection per circuit and an integrated current relay in its Flexstart unit, which then cuts only the affected channel.",["Water in the cylinder 3 heater connector","Harness chafed through at a damaged clip near the rail","Heated injector at cylinder 3 shorted internally"],["One-cylinder roughness when starting cold","Other cylinders start normally","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23D9","P23DA","P23DC","P23D7","P23DF"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 3 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23DC:["Cylinder 3 Fuel Heater Performance","P23DC is set when the heating at cylinder 3 works electrically but delivers too little effect. Bosch writes that its heater unit follows the heat output of all four circuits and hands a temperature reading to the engine controller, so a channel that warms more weakly than the others can be singled out.",["Cylinder 3 heating element below its rated output","High-resistance crimp or plug in the cylinder 3 heater circuit","Deposits insulating the heated surface"],["Misfire on cylinder 3 during warm-up on ethanol","Lean running in the first minutes","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],3,1,["P23D9","P23DA","P23DB","P23D8","P23E0"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P23DD:["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Control Circuit/Open","P23DD reports an open or general fault on the fourth and last heating channel. Bosch builds its heater unit with exactly four heat circuits and its heated rail for either three- or four-cylinder operation, so this code belongs to four-cylinder layouts. There the usual culprit is a heater at cylinder 4 that has burnt through or a plug that came loose during work on the intake manifold;",["Burnt-through heater at cylinder 4","Heater plug at cylinder 4 left loose after intake work","Dead channel 4 in the heater control unit"],["Uneven running on one cylinder for the first seconds after a cold start","Worse with high ethanol content","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23DE","P23DF","P23E0","P23D9","P23D1"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 4 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23DE:["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Control Circuit High","P23DE means the cylinder 4 heater control circuit is at a high level where the module expects otherwise. Either the line has contact with a voltage source, or the driving stage no longer switches off, so heater 4 may keep running.",["Channel 4 driver no longer switching off","Cylinder 4 heater line touching a voltage source","Connectors swapped or mismated after repair"],["Hard restart when the engine is hot","Uneven idle after hot soak","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23DD","P23DF","P23E0","P23DA","P23D2"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 4 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23DF:["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Low","P23DF marks the cylinder 4 heater control circuit as low, which in practice is a short to ground between the control unit and the heater. The channel then stays off until the next start. On four-cylinder engines cylinder 4 is the outermost rail outlet, where the harness often passes brackets and hot components;",["Chafed insulation on the cylinder 4 heater lead at the rail end","Heating element at cylinder 4 shorted to its housing","Moisture in the cylinder 4 heater plug","Shorted channel 4 output in the heater unit"],["Rough cold start on one cylinder","Tripped fuel heater fuse","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P23DD","P23DE","P23E0","P23DB","P23D3"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 4 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23E0:["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Performance","P23E0 judges the effect of the cylinder 4 heater rather than its wiring: the circuit is intact, but the heat delivered or the temperature reached falls short of what the conditions call for. One factor specific to resistive heaters is supply voltage. Bosch specifies 260 W per heating element at 12 V;",["Aged heater at cylinder 4 with reduced output","Poor contact in the cylinder 4 heater circuit","Weak battery or low system voltage during heating"],["Rough start in cold weather on high-ethanol fuel","Longer cranking","Engine warning lamp, depending on manufacturer"],3,1,["P23DD","P23DE","P23DF","P23DC","P23D4"],"גוף חימום דלק צילינדר‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P23E1:["EGR C Control Circuit/Open","P23E1 covers the electrical drive of EGR valve C, a third exhaust gas recirculation actuator next to valves A and B. Which valve carries the letter C is up to the manufacturer; no carmaker documents P23E1 publicly. The code means the module has found the control circuit open or otherwise faulty.",["Unplugged or corroded connector at EGR valve C","Open motor winding or solenoid coil in valve C","Broken drive wire between engine module and valve C"],["Warning lamp with otherwise normal driving","Raised NOx at emissions testing"],2,1,["P23E2","P23E3","P23E4","P0403","P045A"],"EGR‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P23E2:["EGR C Control Circuit Performance","P23E2 is raised when the drive circuit of EGR valve C is electrically intact but the valve does not respond to it as expected: commanded and measured position, or drive current and movement, drift apart.",["Soot and lacquer making valve C sluggish","Worn gears or linkage in the valve C actuator","Actuator motor of valve C losing torque"],["Warning lamp after warm-up drives","Occasional hesitation when EGR is cut"],2,1,["P23E1","P23E5","P23E6","P0404","P045B"],"EGR‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P23E3:["EGR C Control Circuit Low","P23E3 says the control circuit of EGR valve C reads low. On motor or solenoid driven EGR valves this mostly means one of the drive lines has a short to ground, so the output stage would draw excessive current or sees a level it cannot produce by itself. The module then switches the driver off to protect it, and the valve falls back to its spring position, usually closed.",["Drive wire of valve C shorted to ground","Internal short in the valve C motor or coil","Faulty output stage in the engine module"],["Warning lamp, little change in driving","EGR path C switched off"],2,1,["P23E1","P23E4","P23E2","P0489","P045C"],"EGR‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P23E4:["EGR C Control Circuit High","P23E4 is the high counterpart: the control circuit of EGR valve C carries a level that is too high. Typical are a drive line touching a battery feed, a connector pin bent onto a supply terminal, or an output stage that no longer pulls its side low. Unlike a ground short, a short to voltage can leave the actuator partly energized, so depending on the design the valve may move unexpectedly or not at all.",["Drive wire of valve C touching a battery feed","Bent pin in the valve C connector","Engine module output stage not pulling low"],["Warning lamp on","Valve C moves unexpectedly or not at all"],2,1,["P23E1","P23E3","P23E2","P0490","P045D"],"EGR‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P23E5:["EGR C Control Stuck Open","P23E5 means EGR valve C stays open although it is commanded closed. The 2018 GM diesel calibration decides the A-side code P042E like this: once the driver is switched off, the return spring should bring the valve to its closed default within 2 s; if the measured position is still above 5 % after that, the code sets at once as Type A, MIL on the first trip. Comparable logic would suit valve C.",["Carbon deposits holding valve C open","Broken return spring in valve C","Jammed shaft or linkage"],["Rough idle or stalling","Misfire and lack of power","Smoke on diesel engines","Warning lamp on the first trip"],2,3,["P23E6","P23E8","P23E2","P042E","P045E"],"בקרת EGR‏ C — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P23E6:["EGR C Control Stuck Closed","With P23E6 the module concludes that EGR valve C does not open when commanded and stays at or near its closed stop. The consequence is the reverse of P23E5: the engine runs smoothly, but the exhaust share from this path is missing, combustion temperature and NOx go up, and a petrol engine may knock more readily.",["Valve C glued shut by soot","Seized shaft or stripped drive gear","Actuator motor too weak to break the valve free"],["No change in driving, but higher NOx","Possible knocking on petrol engines","Warning lamp"],2,1,["P23E5","P23E7","P23E2","P042F","P045F"],"בקרת EGR‏ C — תקוע במצב סגור"],P23E7:["EGR C Flow Insufficient Detected","P23E7 means the module calculates less recirculated exhaust through path C than it expects for the current operating point. The valve may well move correctly; the gas simply does not get through, for example because the passage, cooler or valve seat is choked with soot.",["Soot-choked EGR passage or valve seat on path C","Clogged EGR cooler in path C","Air mass or pressure sensor reading off, skewing the calculation"],["Warning lamp after steady cruising","Raised NOx at emissions testing"],3,1,["P23E8","P23E6","P23E2","P0401","P049B"],""],P23E8:["EGR C Flow Excessive Detected","P23E8 reports that more exhaust gas passes through the third recirculation path, C, than the module allows for the current operating point – the reverse of P23E7. A valve C that does not seat fully, a leaking bypass or a flow sensor reading too high are the usual explanations. CARB requires the OBD system to recognise EGR flow so high that the system can no longer bring it down to the commanded rate.",["EGR valve C held partly open by carbon deposits","Worn valve seat or leaking bypass in path C","Air-mass or EGR flow sensor reading off, so flow is overestimated","Control software needing an update"],["Rough or unstable idle","Engine stalls when coming to a stop","Hesitation or misfire under load","Visible smoke on diesel engines"],2,3,["P23E7","P23E5","P23E2","P0402","P049C"],""],P23E9:["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","P23E9 concerns a signal the engine control module sends out rather than one it receives: on some engines the ECM passes a conditioned copy of the bank 2 camshaft A position signal on to another module that needs engine phase information. The code flags a broken or otherwise faulty output line, typically an open circuit found when the driver stage is switched. No manufacturer documents P23E9 publicly.",["Broken wire in the output line to the receiving module","Terminal pushed back or corroded in a connector","Receiving module unplugged or without its load resistor","Faulty output driver inside the engine control module"],["Stored code with no noticeable change in engine running","Fault entries in the module that receives the camshaft signal","Start-stop or shift functions may be restricted"],2,2,["P23EA","P23EB","P23EC","P23EF","P2614","P0345"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P23EA:["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P23EA sets when the ECM's output line that relays the bank 2 camshaft A position signal to another control unit is pulled toward ground. The check is blocked during cranking: the module commands the output high and expects the line to rise; if it stays low, the wire is chafed against ground or the receiver has an internal short.",["Output wire chafed through to ground on the engine or body","Receiving module with an input shorted to ground","Moisture or dirt bridging terminals in a connector","Output stage in the engine control module failed"],["Code stored, engine running normally","Harsher shifts or delayed engagement if the transmission module uses the signal","Start-stop function switched off"],2,2,["P23E9","P23EB","P23ED","P23F0","P2615"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P23EB:["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit High (Bank 2)","P23EB is the opposite fault to P23EA: the bank 2 camshaft A output line, which the ECM drives as a switched low-side signal for another module, stays high when it should be pulled low. Typical reasons are a wire touching a supply circuit, moisture in a connector or a defective driver in the ECM.",["Output wire shorted to a battery or 5 V supply wire in the harness","Water ingress bridging terminals","ECM output transistor no longer switching to ground"],["Code present without drivability complaint","Related fault codes in the receiving control module","Comfort functions such as start-stop deactivated"],2,2,["P23E9","P23EA","P23EE","P23F1","P2616"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P23EC:["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit/Open (Bank 1)","P23EC belongs to the camshaft B group – on most layouts the exhaust camshaft – and refers to bank 1, the side with cylinder 1. The ECM rebroadcasts the phase signal of that camshaft on a dedicated output wire, and P23EC reports that this wire, or the driver stage feeding it, shows an open or undefined circuit condition. No manufacturer publishes P23EC;",["Open circuit in the camshaft B output wire","Connector at the ECM or receiver not fully latched","Input stage of the receiving module defective"],["Stored code, often found during a routine scan","Receiving module runs on substitute values"],2,2,["P23ED","P23EE","P23EF","P23E9","P2614","P0365"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P23ED:["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Low (Bank 1)","With P23ED the ECM detects that its camshaft B output for bank 1 reads low although it has released the line to go high. Most often a harness section rubbing through to the engine block, a crushed connector pin or a shorted input in the receiving module is to blame.",["Harness rubbed through against the engine block","Crushed or bent connector pin touching ground","Shorted input in the receiving module","ECM output stage damaged"],["Code stored, engine performance unaffected","Downstream module reports missing camshaft signal","Possible fallback behaviour in transmission or hybrid functions"],2,2,["P23EC","P23EE","P23EA","P23F0","P2615"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P23EE:["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit High (Bank 1)","P23EE flags a camshaft B, bank 1 output line that the ECM cannot pull low: the voltage stays near supply level, pointing to a short to a battery-fed or 5 V wire, a faulty pull-up in the receiving unit or a failed ECM driver transistor.",["Output line shorted to a battery or sensor supply wire","Faulty pull-up circuit in the receiving module","ECM driver transistor burnt out"],["Code logged while the engine runs normally","Faults or reduced functions in the module fed by the signal"],2,2,["P23EC","P23ED","P23EB","P23F1","P2616"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P23EF:["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","P23EF covers the last combination of this series: camshaft B, usually the exhaust shaft, on bank 2, the cylinder bank without cylinder 1. On V-engines with four camshafts the ECM can provide a separate phase output per shaft, and P23EF says the bank 2 exhaust output has lost circuit continuity – a broken wire, a terminal backed out of its connector or a missing load at the receiving end.",["Wire break in the bank 2 camshaft B output line","Terminal backed out of the connector housing","Receiving module disconnected or with failed input"],["Code stored without warning lamp on many vehicles","Module relying on the signal sets its own fault codes"],2,2,["P23F0","P23F1","P23EC","P23E9","P2614","P0390"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P23F0:["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Low (Bank 2)","P23F0 is stored when the bank 2 camshaft B output stays at ground potential while the ECM expects it to float high. A low reading can come from insulation damage near the exhaust side, where heat makes harness sleeves brittle, or from a receiving module whose input has failed shorted. Following GM's published logic for P2615, the module samples every 100 ms and sets the fault after 40 bad samples out of 50;",["Heat-damaged insulation on the exhaust side grounding the wire","Receiving module input failed short to ground","Defective output stage in the ECM"],["Code stored, engine itself unaffected","Harsher shifts or delayed gear changes","Features such as start-stop disabled"],2,2,["P23EF","P23F1","P23ED","P23EA","P2615"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P23F1:["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit High (Bank 2)","P23F1 means the camshaft B output for bank 2 sits at a high level that the ECM did not command. Its driver switches the line to ground to form the pulses; if the line stays high while switched, current is coming in from elsewhere – typically a short to a supply wire in a shared harness bundle, sometimes water bridging terminals.",["Short to a supply wire within a shared harness bundle","Water bridging connector terminals","Receiving module feeding voltage back into the line","ECM driver no longer switching"],["Code present, no change in engine behaviour","Communication or plausibility faults in the receiving module"],2,2,["P23EF","P23F0","P23EE","P23EB","P2616"],"יציאת אות מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P23F2:["Cylinder 1 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F2 says that the mixture in cylinder 1 has drifted away from the other cylinders and that the control unit holds the second injector of that cylinder, injector B, responsible. Only engines that feed each cylinder through two injectors can produce it. Toyota first paired a port and a direct injector in each cylinder with D-4S on the 2005 2GR-FSE V6.",["Injector B (usually the port injector) of cylinder 1 clogged or dripping","Leaking injector O-ring or intake runner gasket at cylinder 1","Loose connector on injector B of cylinder 1 (often with P21CF)","Poor valve sealing on cylinder 1"],["Check engine light on","Often no noticeable drivability change","Slightly rough idle or a misfire count on cylinder 1"],2,1,["P219C","P21CF","P0301","P23FE","P23F3","P219A"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 1 B"],P23F3:["Cylinder 2 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F3 points to cylinder 2 and to its injector B, the second of two injectors feeding that cylinder. The smallest engines able to raise it have three cylinders, for example Ford's 1.5 EcoBoost, which pairs port and direct injection and can switch one cylinder off at light load.",["Injector B of cylinder 2 delivering too much or too little fuel","Air leak at the intake port or injector seal of cylinder 2","Work done on the wrong cylinder because of the maker's numbering scheme","Chafed wire to injector B of cylinder 2 (check P21D0)"],["Check engine light on","Shaking at idle, most noticeable on small three- or four-cylinder engines","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P219D","P21D0","P0302","P23F2","P23F4","P23FE","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 2 B"],P23F4:["Cylinder 3 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F4 refers to cylinder 3: the control unit has found that this cylinder burns leaner or richer than the others and traces the deviation to injector B. On a three-cylinder engine with port and direct injection, such as the Ford 1.5 EcoBoost, cylinder 3 is the last one; on four- and six-cylinder engines it lies in the middle of the block or bank.",["Port injector (injector B) of cylinder 3 dripping or partly blocked","Leaking seal at the intake port of cylinder 3","Low compression or leaking valves on cylinder 3"],["Check engine light on","Possible misfire code P0303 at the same time","Uneven idle when the engine is warm"],2,1,["P219E","P21D1","P0303","P23F3","P23F5","P23FE"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 3 B"],P23F5:["Cylinder 4 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F5 concerns cylinder 4, the end cylinder of a four-cylinder engine. Many four-cylinder units now carry two injectors per cylinder: Toyota's 8AR-FTS turbo (D-4ST) and its Dynamic Force engines such as the M20A (D-4S), Hyundai's Smartstream G2.5 GDi and T-GDi, and the updated Ford 2.3 EcoBoost of the 2024 Mustang. With a single bank, all cylinders share one wide-band sensor ahead of the catalyst;",["Deposits or wear in injector B of cylinder 4","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 4","Low-pressure (port) fuel rail problem showing first at cylinder 4 (look for P2BF0/P2BF1)"],["Check engine light on","Slight vibration at idle","Fuel trim shifted on the single bank"],2,1,["P219F","P21D2","P0304","P2BF0","P2BF1","P23F4","P23FE"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 4 B"],P23F6:["Cylinder 5 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F6 flags cylinder 5 and is the first code in this row that a four-cylinder engine can never set. Engines with port plus direct injection and at least five cylinders are mostly V6 and V8 units: Ford's second-generation 3.5 EcoBoost V6, first shown in the 2017 Ford GT, Toyota's 2GR-FKS V6 with D-4S, and the V8s named at P23F8.",["Port injector of cylinder 5 out of tolerance","Intake manifold gasket leaking near cylinder 5","Intermittent contact in the injector B wiring of cylinder 5 (P21D3)"],["Check engine light on","Usually no change in performance","Fuel trim of the affected bank drifts"],2,1,["P21A0","P21D3","P0305","P23F5","P23F7","P23FE","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 5 B"],P23F7:["Cylinder 6 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F7 belongs to cylinder 6, the highest-numbered cylinder on a V6 or straight six. Toyota's GR V6 family is a typical carrier: the 2GR-FSE in the Lexus IS and GS and the later 2GR-FKS both use D-4S, in which the port injector supplies part of the fuel next to the direct injector, its share depending on load and engine speed. Ford's PFDI V6 engines follow the same idea.",["Port injector of cylinder 6 deviating in the ranges where it carries most of the fuel","Air leak at the intake runner or injector seat of cylinder 6","Injection split calibration needing a software update"],["Check engine light on","Fault comes and goes depending on driving style","Occasional roughness at low or medium load"],2,1,["P21A1","P21D4","P0306","P23F6","P23F8","P23FE","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 6 B"],P23F8:["Cylinder 7 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F8 identifies cylinder 7 and its injector B, so it needs at least seven cylinders, in practice a V8 or V10. Three V8 families using a pair of injectors in every cylinder are on record: Ford's 5.0 Coyote, which gained direct injection on top of port injection for the 2018 Mustang GT and F-150; Toyota's 2UR-GSE with D-4S in Lexus F models and the LC 500;",["Port injector of cylinder 7 clogged or leaking","Intake leak at cylinder 7","Fault in the separate injector B driver module, where fitted (e.g. GM LT5)"],["Check engine light on","Fuel trim of one bank off while the other bank is normal","Rarely a perceptible misfire"],3,1,["P21A2","P21D5","P0307","P23F7","P23F9","P23FE","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 7 B"],P23F9:["Cylinder 8 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23F9 points to cylinder 8, the highest number on any V8. GM's 2019 tables for the LT5 Corvette show how far a V8 with port and direct injection resolves imbalance in practice: only bank by bank. For bank 2 the monitor samples the front oxygen sensor once per cylinder event, normalises the variance against a map and fails when the filtered ratio exceeds 0.75, a Type A fault that turns on the MIL after one trip.",["Injector B of cylinder 8 with wrong flow rate","Leak at the intake runner or PCV connection near cylinder 8","Front oxygen sensor of the bank giving a distorted signal"],["Check engine light on","Bank-level imbalance code (P219A/P219B) stored as well","Normal drivability in most cases"],3,1,["P21A3","P21D6","P0308","P219B","P23F8","P23FA","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 8 B"],P23FA:["Cylinder 9 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23FA concerns cylinder 9, which among passenger-car engines fitted with dual injection realistically means a V10. The best-known example is the 5.2 litre V10 of the Lamborghini Huracán, described as the first V10 to combine direct and multi-point injection. Its firing order 1-6-5-10-2-7-3-8-4-9 alternates between cylinders 1 to 5 and 6 to 10, so cylinder 9 belongs to the second group and fires last.",["Multi-point (port) injector of cylinder 9 deviating","Leak in the intake path of cylinder 9","Valve seat or compression problem on cylinder 9"],["Check engine light on","Little or no effect on the high-revving engine's behaviour","Bank trim of the second cylinder group shifted"],4,1,["P21A4","P21D7","P0309","P23F9","P23FB","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 9 B"],P23FB:["Cylinder 10 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23FB marks cylinder 10, the highest cylinder number of a V10. Among dual-injection engines, the Huracán's 5.2 litre unit is the documented case; it adds multi-point injection to direct injection. In its firing order cylinder 10 follows directly after cylinder 5.",["Port injector of cylinder 10 dirty or worn","Injector seal leaking air at cylinder 10","Heat-damaged wiring to injector B of cylinder 10 (check P21D8)"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 or misfire code stored alongside","Mostly no noticeable change"],4,1,["P21A5","P21D8","P0310","P219B","P23FA","P23FC","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 10 B"],P23FC:["Cylinder 11 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23FC is reserved for cylinder 11, so it can only belong to twelve-cylinder engines that add an extra injector in every cylinder. Such a pairing is hard to find in public engine data. Volkswagen's W12 illustrates the point: its early versions used twelve injectors in the intake manifold, one per cylinder, while the 6.3 FSI of the Audi A8 L W12 switched to direct injection with six-hole high-pressure injectors, again…",["Second injector of cylinder 11 delivering a wrong quantity","Intake leak at cylinder 11","Code read from an engine that has no injector B (scan tool or software issue)"],["Check engine light on","Hardly any change in smoothness on a twelve-cylinder engine"],4,1,["P21A6","P21D9","P0311","P23FB","P23FD","P23FE","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 11 B"],P23FD:["Cylinder 12 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23FD closes the cylinder series at number 12. It states that the twelfth cylinder runs out of step with the rest and that the cause lies with its injector B. A matching engine needs twelve cylinders and two injectors in each, a combination that public engine references do not show: the VW W12, for instance, appeared with port injection and later as the 6.3 FSI with direct injection only.",["Second injector of cylinder 12 out of tolerance","Intake leak or valve sealing fault at cylinder 12","Code reported by a tool on an engine without a second injector"],["Check engine light on","Bank or misfire code stored at the same time"],4,1,["P21A7","P21DA","P0312","P23FC","P23FE","P23FF"],"חוסר איזון יחס אוויר-דלק מזרק צילינדר‏ 12 B"],P23FE:["Bank 1 System B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23FE reports a cylinder-to-cylinder imbalance on bank 1 that the control unit attributes to fuel system B, without naming a cylinder. Ford's 2024 OBD summary explains the letter for its dual-injection engines: the port path is Fuel Control System B with its own lean and rich codes (P2BF0/P2BF1 for bank 1), while direct injection forms system A.",["Several port injectors on bank 1 fouled by deposits","Port fuel rail pressure or low-pressure supply wrong on bank 1","Intake manifold leak on the bank 1 side","Front oxygen sensor of bank 1 responding poorly"],["Check engine light on","Lean or rich fuel trim on bank 1, possibly P2BF0 or P2BF1","Slightly increased fuel consumption"],2,1,["P219A","P23FF","P2BF0","P2BF1","P23F2"],""],P23FF:["Bank 2 System B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","P23FF mirrors P23FE for bank 2 and can only occur on V, W or boxer engines, because inline engines have no second bank. It means the cylinders on the side without cylinder 1 deviate from each other and the fault is assigned to injection system B, which on Ford's PFDI engines is the port path (lean and rich codes P2BF2/P2BF3).",["Several port injectors on bank 2 with deposits or wear","Intake manifold gasket leaking on bank 2","Supply problem in the port fuel rail feeding bank 2","Front oxygen sensor or its wiring on bank 2 distorting the signal"],["Check engine light on","Fuel trims of the two banks clearly apart","Possibly P2BF2 or P2BF3 as well"],2,1,["P219B","P23FE","P2BF2","P2BF3","P23F9"],""]};export{e as default};
